window.lessonPageData = {"1":{"lesson":1,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":39,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 1\n\nGuidelines\n\n[Note to Teacher: Please review the guidelines\nbefore the start of the lesson]\n\nA. This is a study of the Bible, not a study of a\nparticular Christian denomination.\nB. Each lesson will last approximately 1 hour to\n1.5 hours.\nC. All scripture text is taken from the New King\nJames Version - unless noted otherwise.\nD. Please wait until the end of the class with\nany questions as these questions could be\nanswered throughout the course of the\nlesson.\nE. Let us open our hearts and minds as we open\nthe Word of God.\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will be able to explain what the\nBible is\n\n•\n\nThe student will be able to list the benefits of\nstudying the Word of God\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will examine evidences and\nconclude that the Bible is reliable and true\n\n•\n\nThe student will demonstrate an attitude of\nwanting to know and understand the Word of\nGod"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 1\n\nLesson Outline\nA. The Journey of the Bible\n\n3\n\nB. Arrangement of the Bible\n\n4\n\nC. The Bible is God’s Word\n\n5\n\nD. Facts about this Amazing Book\n\n6\n\nE. Faith\n\n12\n\nF. How does God view His Word\n\n13\n\nG. Benefits of the Word of God\n\n14\n\nH. How Should I Respond to the Word of God\n\n15"},{"page":3,"text":"A\nLesson 1\n\nTHE JOURNEY OF THE BIBLE\nI. The Start of God’s Communication\nThe written Word of God began after\napproximately 2500 years of Man’s history. Prior\nto that, God spoke to humanity in various ways\nsuch as nature, dreams, visions, angels, and\nsymbols.\n\nHebrews 1:1\nGod, who at various times and in various ways spoke in time past to\nthe fathers by the prophets\n\nII. The Beginnings of the Written Word\nThe written Word of God started with Moses who\nreceived the Covenant of God on Mount Sinai.\nThe Covenant or Law was inscribed on tablets of\nstone by the finger of God. These tablets were\nthen placed inside a holy sacred box called the\nArk of the Covenant. Over time, scribes would\ncarefully copy these words onto leather, clay\ntablets, wood, and other surfaces.\nDeuteronomy 31:9-11\nSo Moses wrote this law and delivered it to the priests, the sons of\nLevi, who bore the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and to all the\nelders of Israel. And Moses commanded them, saying: “At the end\nof every seven years, at the appointed time in the year of release, at\nthe Feast of Tabernacles, when all Israel comes to appear before the\nLORD your God in the place which He chooses, you shall read this\nlaw before all Israel in their hearing.\n\n3"},{"page":4,"text":"B\nLesson 1\n\nARRANGEMENT OF THE BIBLE\nRefer to Chart L1.1-5\nThe English word, Bible, is from the Latin word\n- biblia, which means “books”. It is essentially a\ncollection of books, and has been referred to as\nthe “Book of books”.\nThe Bible is divided by translators into two\nsections – the Old and the New Testament\nThe Old Testament – a collection of books\nthat cover almost 3,600 years of human history\nconsisting of 39 books.\nLaw: Genesis to Deuteronomy\nHistory: Joshua to Esther\nPoetry: Job to Song of Solomon\nProphecy:\n• Major Prophets: Isaiah to Daniel\n• Minor Prophets: Hosea to Malachi\nThe New Testament – a collection of books\nthat cover about 2,000 years of human history\nconsisting of about 27 books. This portion\nof the Bible covers the details of a person\nnamed Jesus Christ. We will learn more\nabout Jesus in future lessons.\nGospels: Matthew to John\nActs of the Apostles: Acts\nEpistles: Romans to Jude\nProphecy: Revelation\n\n4"},{"page":5,"text":"How do I use the Bible?\nThe Books in the Bible is further divided by\ntranslators into Chapters and Verses for referencing\npurposes.\n\nLesson 1\n\nChapter\n\nGenesis 1:1\nBook\n\nC\n\nVerse\n\nTHE BIBLE IS THE INSPIRED WORD OF GOD\n2 Timothy 3:16\nAll Scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for\ndoctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness\n\nInspiration – “God Breathed”\nThe Bible said over 3,800 times, “The Lord said”,\n“the Lord spoke” and “God said”.\nHere are two examples of men of God writing\nwhat God spoke to them:\nI. Paul [Writing to the church in Corinth]:\n1 Corinthians 14:37\n“…the things that I write are the commandments of the Lord.”\n\n5"},{"page":6,"text":"II. Jeremiah:\nJeremiah 30:1-2\n\nLesson 1\n\n“The word that came to Jeremiah from the Lord saying, Thus speaks\nthe Lord God of Israel, saying: Write in a book for yourself all the\nwords that I have spoken to you.”\n\nKey #1: The Bible is the inspired Word of God.\n\nD\n\nFACTS ABOUT THIS AMAZING BOOK\n[Note to Teacher: Please choose your examples\nselectively according to your student’s interest and\ncomprehension abilities]\n\nHere are some examples of evidence to show the\nBible’s relevance and validity in our world today:\nI. Scientific Evidence\nRefer to Chart L1.2-5\nA.) Spherical Earth verses Flat Earth\nThere were ancient cultures and civilizations\nincluding Greece (until the Classical period),\nthe Bronze Age and Iron Age civilizations of\nthe near East (until the Hellenistic period),\nIndia (until the Gupta period), and China until\nthe 17th century that subscribed to a flat\nearth belief.\nSource: Lucien Levy-Bruhl, Primitive Mentality\n(repr. Boston: Beacon, 1966) 353, H. B.\nAlexander, The Mythology of All Races 10:\nNorth American (repr. New York: Cooper\nSquare, 1964) 249.\n\nIsaiah 40:22\nIt is He who sits above the circle of the earth\n\n6"},{"page":7,"text":"Lesson 1\n\nB.) Number of stars in the sky\nThe standard star catalogue in the Middle\nAges was the one published by Ptolemy in the\n2nd century (part of his Almagest) and it listed\n1022 stars. Tycho Brahe, who completed his\n”thousand-star” catalogue in 1598, contain\n965 stars. Johannes Hevelius published the\nlast major catalogue based on naked eye\nobservations in 1687, the Catalogus Stellarum\nFixarum, which contains 1,564 stars. It was\nnot until the 1600s that they found out by\nusing a telescope that they were innumerable.\nYet, Jeremiah had it written many years\nbefore that the host of Heaven, which are the\nstars, cannot be numbered.\n\nJeremiah 33:22\nAs the host of heaven cannot be numbered, nor the sand of the sea\nmeasured, so will I multiply the descendants of David My servant and\nthe Levites who minister to Me.\n\nC.) Earth hung upon nothing\nThe question of what the earth was hanging\nupon was not answered until Newton’s\ndiscovery of the law of universal gravitation in\n1687. Job discusses the fact that the earth has\nan invisible support and hangs on nothing.\n\nJob 26:7\nHe stretches out the north over empty space; He hangs the earth on\nnothing.\n\n7"},{"page":8,"text":"II. Medical Evidence\n\nLesson 1\n\nA.) Bloodletting\nDoctors believed they could cure George\nWashington’s pain and shortness of breath\nby removing blood from his body in a process\ncalled “bloodletting”. He died that very night.\nWe know today, and the Bible had it written\nmany years ago, that blood is needed to\nsustain life.\nSource: PBS News hour, 15 December 2014,\n<www.pbs.org/newshouse>\n\nLeviticus 17:11\nFor the life of the flesh is in the blood, and I have given it to you upon\nthe altar to make atonement for your souls; for it is the blood that\nmakes atonement for the soul.\n\nIII. Historical Evidence\nRefer to Chart L1.3-5\nA.) Accounts of worldwide flood\nPresence of multiple flood narratives in\nancient literature supports the Biblical story\nof a worldwide flood (Noah’s Ark).\n“The Great Flood had such a profound\nimpact that it became part of various ancient\ncultures. The early aborigines of nearly every\ncountry of the world have preserved records\nof the universal flood. Anthropologist Dr.\nRichard Andree has collected 46 different\nflood accounts from North and South\nAmerica, 20 from Asia, 5 from Europe, 7 from\nAfrica, and 10 from the South Sea Islands and\nAustralia.”\nSource: Willmington, Willmington’s Guide to\nthe Bible, 950.\n8"},{"page":9,"text":"B) Archaeological findings of locations and\nartefacts\nExample:\nLesson 1\n\nTel Dan Stela—the ninth-century B.C.\ninscription that furnished the first historical\nevidence of King David outside the Bible\nSiloam pool in Jesus time - Archaeologists\nexcavated part of a monumental pool\nwhere Jesus performed the miracle of\nrestoring sight to a blind man in the Gospel\nof John\nSource: http://www.biblicalarchaeology.org\nC) Discovery of the Dead Sea Scrolls\nScrolls of approximately 2000-year-old\nmanuscripts were found in 1947 by Arab\nBedouins who tended their flocks in the\nregion.\nThese scrolls contain representations of\nevery book of the traditional Hebrew canon,\nexcept Esther.\nUpon comparing these manuscripts with\nour modern Bible, they found them to\nbe 95% identical (word for word) with 5%\nvariation consisting primarily obvious slips\nof the pen and spelling alterations.\nSource: Collins, John J. (1992b), “Dead\nSea Scrolls,” The Anchor Bible Dictionary,\ned. David Noel Freedman (New York:\nDoubleday), 2:85-101.\nArcher, Gleason, Jr. (1974), A Survey of\nOld Testament Introduction (Chicago, IL:\nMoody).\n\n9"},{"page":10,"text":"IV. Textual Preservation Evidence\nLesson 1\n\nThe accuracy and reliability of an ancient\ndocument is dependent on the “time gap”\nbetween the time the original author wrote it, and\nthe first copy written. The number of available\nmanuscripts also increases its credibility.\nTime Gap: The gap of time from when the author\nwrote the original to the time the first copy was\nwritten.\nAUTHOR\n\nFIRST COPY\n\nTIME GAP\n\nThese handwritten documents, originals and\ncopies, were called manuscripts.\nThe smaller the time gap between the original\nand copy, the less room for error.\nHere is a table comparing how widely accepted\nancient writings measure up with the Bible.\nContrast: New Testament with Other Books of Antiquity\n\n10\n\nAuthor\n\nNo. of\nManuscripts\n\nTime Gap\n\nCaesar\n\n10\n\n1,000 years\n\nPlato (Tetralogies)\n\n7\n\n1,200 years\n\nTacitus (Annals)\n\n20\n\n1,000 years\n\nPliny the Younger (History)\n\n7\n\n750 years\n\nSuetonius\n(De Vita Caesarum)\n\n8\n\n800 years\n\nHomer (Iliad)\n\n643\n\n500 years\n\nNew Testament\n\nOver 24,000\n\n25 years"},{"page":11,"text":"V. Prophetic Evidence\nLesson 1\n\nThe Bible contains numerous prophecies. Prophecy is literally\nhistory written in advance (before it happens). Because no man\ncan see the future but God alone, prophecies that are fulfilled\nfurther show that the Bible is a supernatural book.\nExample:\nA) The Rebirth of Israel as a Nation\n• The nation of Israel (both Northern and Southern) was\ndestroyed and overthrown by 587 B.C.\n• Ever since then, Israel was in captivity by foreign empires.\n• God sent prophets to tell Israel that there will come a day\nthat the nation will be rebirthed and Jews will gather back\nin their land again (see Amos 9:14-15, Isaiah 66:7-8)\nThis prophecy was fulfilled in 1948, 15 May when the United\nNations announce Israel as a sovereign nation. Till this day,\nIsrael is the only country that is born again.\nB) The Coming of Messiah\nRefer to Chart L1.4-5\nPrior to the time of Jesus, Jews were given over 100\nprophecies describing the coming of a Messiah (a king who\nwould deliver Israel and set up the kingdom of God).\nAn expert in mathematical probabilities, Peter Stoner, wrote\nin Science Speaks that if only 8 of the prophecies in the Old\nTestament concerning Messiah were fulfilled, the probability\nof their actually coming to pass would be 1 in 10 to the 17th\ndegree – that probability is 1 in 100,000,000,000,000,000.\nThat’s one in one hundred quadrillion!\nThe point is that when people say that the fulfilment of\nprophecy in the life of Jesus was accidental, they do not\nknow what they are talking about. Keep in mind that Jesus\ndid not just fulfil 8 prophecies, He fulfilled 108.\n\n11\n\nNumber of Prophecies\n\nProbability\n\n8\n\n1 in 1017\n\n16\n\n1 in 1045\n\n48\n\n1 in 10157\n\n108\n\n1 in 10???"},{"page":12,"text":"Key #2: The Bible is accurate and true.\nLesson 1\n\nE\n\nFAITH\nAlthough there is evidence to show us that the\nBible can be trusted, it is ultimately a book that\nrequires faith.\n\nRomans 10:17\nSo then faith comes by hearing, and hearing by the word of God.\nHebrews 11:6\nBut without faith it is impossible to please Him, for he who comes to\nGod must believe that He is, and that He is a rewarder of those who\ndiligently seek Him.\n\nGod rewards those who put their faith in His Word.\n\nHebrews 4:2\nFor indeed the gospel was preached to us as well as to them; but the\nword which they heard did not profit them, not being mixed with\nfaith in those who heard it.\nMark 16:20\nAnd they went out and preached everywhere, the Lord working with\nthem and confirming the word through the accompanying signs.\nAmen.\n\nKey #3: God will confirm His Word when\nwe have faith.\nThe world says, “Prove it to me and then I’ll believe\nit,” but God says the opposite, “Believe Me and I’ll\nprove it.”\n12"},{"page":13,"text":"F\n\nHOW DOES GOD VIEW HIS WORD?\nHe magnifies His Word above His name\n\nLesson 1\nPsalm 138:2\nI will worship toward Your holy temple, And praise Your name For\nYour lovingkindness and Your truth; For You have magnified Your\nword above all Your name.\n\nHis Word is alive, powerful, active and sharp\nHebrews 4:12\nFor the word of God is living and powerful, and sharper than any\ntwo-edged sword, piercing even to the division of soul and spirit, and\nof joints and marrow, and is a discerner of the thoughts and intents\nof the heart.\n\nHis Word does not return void\n\nIsaiah 55:11\nSo shall My word be that goes forth from My mouth; It shall not\nreturn to Me void, But it shall accomplish what I please, And it shall\nprosper in the thing for which I sent it.\n\nHis Word is Truth\n\nJohn 17:17\nSanctify them by Your truth. Your word is truth.\n\nHis Word is everlasting\nMatthew 24:35\nHeaven and earth will pass away, but My words will by no means\npass away.\n\n13"},{"page":14,"text":"G\nLesson 1\n\nBENEFITS OF THE WORD OF GOD\nAble to make us wise\nPsalm 119:98-99\nYou, through Your commandments, make me wiser than my\nenemies; For they are ever with me. 99 I have more understanding\nthan all my teachers, For Your testimonies are my meditation.\n\nProvides a guide for life\nPsalm 119:133\nDirect my steps by Your word, and let no iniquity have dominion over\nme.\n\nProverbs 3:5-6\nTrust in the Lord with all your heart, and lean not on your own\nunderstanding; in all your ways acknowledge Him, and He shall direct\nyour paths.\n\nReveals God’s plan for humanity and the world\nJohn 3:16\nFor God so loved the world that He gave His only begotten Son, that\nwhoever believes in Him should not perish but have everlasting life.\n\nUltimately, it allows us to know and\nexperience its author, God\n\nJohn 5:39\nYou search the Scriptures, for in them you think you have eternal life;\nand these are they which testify of Me.\n\n14"},{"page":15,"text":"To preach the Bible as ‘the handbook for life,’ or as the\nanswer to every question, rather than as the revelation of\nChrist, is to turn the Bible into an entirely different book.\nThis is how the Pharisees approached Scripture, as we can\nsee clearly from the questions they asked Jesus. For the\nPharisees, the Scriptures were a source of trivia for life’s\ndilemmas.\n\nLesson 1\n\n—Michael Horton\n\nKey #4: The Bible is given to us to know\nand experience God.\n\nH\n\nHOW SHOULD I RESPOND TO THE\nWORD OF GOD\nRevelation 1:3\nBlessed is he who reads and those who hear the words of this\nprophecy, and keep those things which are written in it; for the time\nis near.\n\n1. READ (KNOW THE WORD)\n\nPsalm 119:33\nTeach me, O LORD, the way of Your statutes, And I shall keep it to the\nend.\n\nFamiliarize yourself with the Bible by being\nopen to learn from it. Allow God to speak to you\nthrough His Word.\n\n15"},{"page":16,"text":"2. HEAR (UNDERSTAND THE WORD)\nLesson 1\n\nProverbs 2:1-5\nMy son, if you receive my words, and treasure my commands within\nyou, 2 So that you incline your ear to wisdom, and apply your heart to\nunderstanding; 3 Yes, if you cry out for discernment, and lift up your\nvoice for understanding, 4 If you seek her as silver, And search for her\nas for hidden treasures; 5 Then you will understand the fear of the\nLORD, And find the knowledge of God.\n\nGod wants us to understand His Word. To do so,\nwe need to know how to study and interpret the\nWord accurately.\n\n2 Peter 1:20\nknowing this first, that no prophecy of Scripture is of any private\ninterpretation\n\nGod never intended for anyone to make up\ntheir own interpretation. Therefore, we must\ninterpret the Bible using the Bible and not our\npersonal opinion.\nHow do I understand the Word of God?\nRead its context (two or three witnesses)\nSometimes, to seek out the true meaning\nof what the writer is trying to communicate,\nit would require you to read surrounding\npassages of Scripture.\nDeuteronomy 19:15\n“One witness shall not rise against a man concerning any iniquity or\nany sin that he commits; by the mouth of two or three witnesses the\nmatter shall be established.\n2 Corinthians 13:1\nThis will be the third time I am coming to you. “By the mouth of two or\nthree witnesses every word shall be established.”\n\n16"},{"page":17,"text":"Do not add or subtract from it\nLesson 1\n\nDeuteronomy 4:2\nYou shall not add to the word which I command you, nor take from\nit, that you may keep the commandments of the Lord your God\nwhich I command you.\nProverbs 30:6\nDo not add to His Words, Lest He rebuke you, and you be found a\nliar.\nRevelation 22:18-19\nFor I testify to everyone who hears the words of the prophecy of\nthis book: If any- one adds to these things, God will add to him the\nplagues that are written in this book; and if anyone takes away from\nthe words of the book of this prophecy, God shall take away his part\nfrom the Book of Life, from the holy city, and from the things which\nare written in this book.\n\nInvest time to study it\n\n2 Timothy 2:15 (KJV)\nStudy to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth\nnot to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth.\n\nSincerely seek the Lord using His Word and let the\nHoly Spirit illuminate your understanding\n\nJohn 14:26 (KJV)\nBut the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will\nsend in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to\nyour remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.\n\n17"},{"page":18,"text":"3. KEEP (APPLY THE WORD)\nLesson 1\n\nJames 1:22\nBut be doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving yourselves.\nJoshua 1:8\nThis Book of the Law shall not depart from your mouth, but you shall\nmeditate in it day and night, that you may observe to do according to\nall that is written in it. For then you will make your way prosperous,\nand then you will have good success.\n\nKey #5: The Bible is to be read, understood\nand applied.\n\n18"},{"page":19,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 1\n\nRefer to Chart L1.5-5\n1. The Bible is the inspired Word of God.\n2. The Bible is accurate and true.\n3. God will confirm His Word when we have faith.\n4. The Bible is given to us to know and experience\nGod.\n5. The Bible is to be read, understood and applied.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n19"},{"page":20,"text":"Charts\nLesson 1\n\n20"},{"page":21,"text":"Charts\nLesson 1\n\n21"},{"page":22,"text":"Charts\nLesson 1\n\n22"},{"page":23,"text":"Lesson 1\n\nModular Section\n1. Interesting Facts about the Bible\n2. Additional facts on Scientific Evidence\n3. Additional facts on Textual Preservation\nEvidence\n4. Facts on Universal Influence of the Bible"},{"page":24,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nI. Interesting Facts about the Bible\nThe following list is not designed to discuss\ndoctrine, or provide in-depth teaching.\nIt is merely a resource center for factual\ninformation on the Bible. Many of these\nquestions have been addressed in various\nlocations throughout our website; however,\nas many people do not have the time to\ncomb through the entire website to find\nthe answers they are looking for, we have\ncompiled the following list.\n\nHOW MANY BOOKS\nARE IN THE BIBLE?\n\nThe Bible contains 66 books, divided\namong the Old and New Testaments.\n\nHOW MANY BOOKS\nARE IN THE OLD\nTESTAMENT?\n\nThere are 39 books in the Old\nTestament.\n\nHOW MANY BOOKS\nARE IN THE NEW\nTESTAMENT?\n\nThere are 27 books in the New\nTestament.\n\nWHAT DOES\n“TESTAMENT” MEAN?\n\nTestament means “covenant” or\n“contract.”\n\nWHO WROTE THE\nBIBLE?\n\n24\n\nThe Bible was written under the\ninspiration of the Holy Spirit by over\n40 different authors from all walks of\nlife: shepherds, farmers, tent-makers,\nphysicians, fishermen, priests,\nphilosophers and kings. Despite these\ndifferences in occupation and the\nspan of years it took to write it, the\nBible is an extremely cohesive and\nunified book.\n\nWHICH SINGLE\nAUTHOR CONTRIBUTED\nTHE MOST BOOKS TO\nTHE OLD TESTAMENT?\n\nMoses. He wrote the first five books\nof the Bible, referred to as the\nPentateuch; the foundation of the\nBible.\n\nWHICH SINGLE\nAUTHOR CONTRIBUTED\nTHE MOST BOOKS TO\nTHE NEW TESTAMENT?\n\nThe Apostle Paul, who wrote 14 books\n(over half) of the New Testament."},{"page":25,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nWHEN WAS THE BIBLE\nWRITTEN?\n\nIt was written over a period of some\n1,500 years, from around 1450 B.C.\n(the time of Moses) to about 100 A.D.\n(following the death and resurrection\nof Jesus Christ).\n\nWHAT IS THE OLDEST\nBOOK IN THE OLD\nTESTAMENT?\n\nMany scholars agree that Job is the\noldest book in the Bible, written by\nan unknown Israelite about 1500\nB.C. Others hold that the Pentateuch\n(the first five books of the Bible) are\nthe oldest books in the Bible, written\nbetween 1446 and 1406 B.C.\n\nWHAT IS THE\nYOUNGEST BOOK IN\nTHE OLD TESTAMENT?\n\nThe book of Malachi, written about\n400 B.C.\n\nWHAT IS THE OLDEST\nBOOK OF THE NEW\nTESTAMENT?\n\nProbably the book of James, written as\nearly as A.D. 45.\n\nWHAT IS THE\nYOUNGEST BOOK IN\nTHE NEW TESTAMENT?\n\nThe Book of Revelation is the\nyoungest book of the New Testament,\nwritten about 95 A.D.\n\nWHAT LANGUAGES\nWAS THE BIBLE\nWRITTEN IN?\n\n25\n\nThe Bible was written in three\nlanguages: Hebrew, Aramaic, and\nKoine Greek.\n\nWHEN WAS THE BIBLE\nCANONIZED?\n\nThe entire New Testament as we\nknow it today, was canonized before\nthe year 375 A.D. The Old Testament\nhad previously been canonized long\nbefore the advent of Christ.\n\nWHAT DOES “CANON”\nMEAN?\n\n“Canon” is derived front the Greek\nword “Kanon,” signifying a measuring\nrod. Thus, to have the Bible\n“canonized” meant that it had been\nmeasured by the standard or test\nof divine inspiration and authority.\nIt became the collection of books or\nwritings accepted by the apostles\nand leadership of the early Christian\nchurch as a basis for Christian\nbelief. It is the standard by which all\nChristians throughout the ages live\nand worship.\n\nWHEN WAS THE FIRST\nTRANSLATION OF THE\nBIBLE MADE INTO\nENGLISH?\n\n1382 A.D., by John Wycliffe."},{"page":26,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nWHEN WAS THE BIBLE\nPRINTED?\n\nThe Bible was printed in 1454 A.D. by\nJohannes Gutenberg who invented\nthe “type mold” for the printing press.\nIt was the first book ever printed.\n\nWHAT IS THE OLDEST\nALMOST-COMPLETE\nMANUSCRIPT OF\nTHE BIBLE NOW IN\nEXISTENCE?\n\nThe Codex Vaticanus, which dates\nfrom the first half of the fourth\nCentury. It is located in the library of\nthe Vatican in Rome. There are older\nfragments of the Bible that are still\npreserved however-- the oldest being\na tiny scrap of the Gospel of John was\nfound in Egypt, dating back to the\nbeginning of the second century. (It\nis currently in the Rayland’s Library in\nManchester, England).\n\nWHAT IS THE LONGEST\nBOOK IN THE BIBLE?\n\nThe book of Psalms.\n\nWHAT IS THE SHORTEST\nBOOK IN THE BIBLE?\n\n2 John.\n\nWHAT IS THE LONGEST\nCHAPTER IN THE BIBLE?\n\nPsalm 119\n\nWHAT IS THE SHORTEST\nCHAPTER IN THE BIBLE?\n\nPsalm 117\n\nWHAT IS THE LONGEST\nVERSE IN THE BIBLE?\n\nEsther 8:9\n\nWHAT IS THE SHORTEST\nVERSE IN THE BIBLE?\n\nJohn 11:35\n\nWHICH BOOK IN THE\nBIBLE DOES NOT\nMENTION THE WORD\n“GOD?”\n\n26\n\nThe book of Esther.\n\nWHO WAS THE OLDEST\nMAN THAT EVER LIVED?\n\nMethuselah who lived to be 969 years\nold (Genesis 5:27).\n\nWHO WERE THE TWO\nMEN IN THE BIBLE\nWHO NEVER DIED BUT\nWERE CAUGHT UP TO\nHEAVEN?\n\nEnoch, who walked with God and was\nno more (Genesis 5:22-24). Elijah, who\nwas caught up by a whirlwind into\nheaven (II Kings 2:11).\n\nWHO DOES THE BIBLE\nSAY WAS THE MEEKEST\nMAN IN THE BIBLE\n(NOT INCLUDING\nJESUS)?\n\nMoses (Numbers 12:3)."},{"page":27,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nHOW MANY\nLANGUAGES HAS\nTHE BIBLE BEEN\nTRANSLATED INTO?\n\nIS THE BIBLE STILL THE\nBEST-SELLING BOOK IN\nTHE WORLD?\n\nThe Holy Bible has been translated\ninto 2,018 languages, with countless\nmore partial translations, and audio\ntranslations (for unwritten languages).\n(This is an enormous amount\nof translations. In comparison,\nShakespeare, considered by many to\nbe the master writer of the English\nlanguage, has only been translated\ninto 50 languages.)\nYes, indeed!\n\nII. Additional Facts on Scientific Evidence\n1. Geophysics – The Earth is round (Isaiah\n40:22)\nFor many thousands of years, common\npeople believed the earth was flat. Until\n16th century astronomers Copernicus\nand Kepler claimed otherwise.\nWith the invention of the compass and\nMagellan’s voyage in 1521. Magellan\nwas the first person to circle the globe,\ndemonstrating that a ship could travel\naround the world without falling off the\nedge.\nHowever, this scientific truth had been\nrevealed in the Bible more than 3,100\nyears before Magellan by the 8th\ncentury BC prophet Isaiah. Obviously,\nIsaiah did not get his wisdom from the\nscience of his day, which taught that the\nearth was flat, for he proclaimed…\n\nIsaiah 40:22\nIt is he that sitteth upon the circle of the earth\n\n27\n\nHenry M. Morris, Science and the Bible,\nrev. and updated ed. (Chicago: Moody,\n1986), 13–14."},{"page":28,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\n2. Planetology – The Earth is suspended\nin space (Job 26:7)\nMany ancient people believed “planet\nearth” was flat and there were various\ntheories on how the earth was held up:\n• On the back of a gigantic turtle\n• On the back of a tiger or an\nelephant. (The shaking of\nthe elephant accounted for\nearthquakes.)\nOnly in the 17th century AD did the\nscientific community, with Newton’s\ngravitational theory, discover the force\nthat propels celestial bodies through\nspace.\nHowever, this scientific truth had been\nrevealed in the Bible much earlier in the\nBook of Job, written around the 15th\ncentury BC.…\n\nJob 26:7\nHe stretcheth out the north over the empty place,\nAnd hangeth the earth upon nothing.\n\nLynn Waller, How Do We Know the Bible Is\nTrue? Reasons a Kid Can Believe It (Grand\nRapids: Zondervan, 1991), 4–5; Morris,\nScience and the Bible, 14.\n\n28"},{"page":29,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\n3. Earth Science – Mountains and canyons\nexist in the sea (2 Samuel 22:16)\nFor thousands of years, until the 20th\ncentury, the scientific assumption was\nthat the ocean was bowl-shaped—\nshallow around the edges and deepest\nin the middle. Yet today researchers\nhave discovered that some of the\nhighest mountains and deepest valleys\nexist in the middle of oceans, seen in\nthe Atlantic range. In the Pacific Ocean,\nthe Mariana Trench near the Philippines\nis over 7 miles deep.\nHowever, this scientific truth had been\nrevealed in the Bible several thousand\nyears earlier.\n• In the 10th century BC, David spoke\nof “the valleys of the sea” (2 Samuel\n22:16).\n• In the 8th century BC, rebellious\nJonah, described sinking to the\nbottom of a submerged mountain\nafter being thrown overboard …\n\nJonah 2:6 (NIV)\nTo the roots of the mountains I sank down.\n\nWaller, How Do We Know the Bible Is\nTrue? 8–9 and Henry M. Morris, The\nBiblical Basis for Modern Science (Grand\nRapids: Baker, 1984), 289.\n\n29"},{"page":30,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\n4. Oceanography – Water paths/ocean\ncurrents exist in the sea (Psalm 8:8)\nFor thousands of years scientists knew\nnothing about sea lanes and ocean\ncurrents. Therefore, they drew no water\ncharts for sailing lanes.\nThen in 1839, when Dr. Matthew Maury,\nthe father of modern oceanography,\nbecame ill, one of his children began\nreading the Bible to him. Astonished at\nhearing Psalm 8:8, he asked to hear it\nagain.\nAs a result, he spent several years\ncharting the paths of the seas—the\ncurrents of the ocean—which became\nthe basis for the first textbook of\nmodern oceanography, Physical\nGeography of the Sea.\nHowever, this scientific truth had been\nrevealed in the Bible much earlier by\nDavid in the 10th century BC.…\n\nPsalm 8:8\nAnd whatsoever passeth through the paths of the seas.\n\nWaller, How Do We Know the Bible Is\nTrue? 10–11 and Morris, Biblical Basis,\n289; Answers in Genesis, “Matthew\nMaury’s search for the secret of the\nseas,” first published in Creation\nMagazine, 11(3):30 June 1989, http://\nwww.answersingenesis.org/creation/\nv11/i3/maury.asp.\n\n30"},{"page":31,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\n5. Genetics – All living things reproduce\nafter their own kind (Genesis 1:21)\nIn 350 BC Aristotle presented the\ntheory of “spontaneous generation”—\nlife appears out of nonlife—a theory\nthat the scientific world accepted for\nthousands of years.\nScientists theorized that frogs originated\nout of slime pools and insects out of rot.\nThen in 1862, with the invention of\nthe microscope, Louis Pasteur totally\ndisproved spontaneous generation.\nThen 3 years later, Johann Mendel\ndeveloped what is now the universal law\nof heredity.\nHowever, thousands of years earlier\nin the 15th century BC, the 1st book of\nthe Bible presented the same law of\nheredity verifying that all living things\nwere created according to their own\nkind.…\n\nGenesis 1:21\nSo God created the great sea creatures and every living creature\nthat moves, with which the waters swarm, according to their\nkinds, and every winged bird according to its kind.\n\nSee Morris, Biblical Basis, 372–379.\n\n31"},{"page":32,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\n6. Haematology – Life is in the blood (Leviticus\n17:14)\nFor some 3,000 years, “bloodletting” was a\nwidespread, medical procedure practiced among\nmany ancient peoples up until the early 20th\ncentury.\n• By removing a sizable amount of blood from a\npatient, the medical community believed that\nany disease could be treated.\n• Scientists and surgeons believed that\nbloodletting would remove stagnate blood\nbuilding up in the extremities.\n• The more severe the problem, the more blood\nwould be “let”—whether by lances or leeches.\nBut the truth is, bloodletting caused many\nillnesses to escalate in severity, even to the\npoint of death.\n• Suffering with a throat infection in 1799,\nGeorge Washington, the 1st president of the\nUnited States, had approximately 4 pints (1.7\nliters) of blood removed from his body, a\nprocess that contributed to his death.\nHundreds of years after Moses penned Leviticus,\nHerophilos, the celebrated Alexandrian physician\nof the 3rd century BC, identified blood as the\ncarrier of disease.\nHowever, notice the irony. Centuries earlier,\nthe Bible had presented blood as the carrier of\nlife. And nowhere in the Bible is one mention of\nthe weakening, sometimes deadly practice of\nbloodletting.…\nLeviticus 17:14\nFor the life of every creature is its blood: its blood is its life.\n\nWillmington, Willmington’s Guide to the\nBible, 817–818.\n\n32"},{"page":33,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\n7. Hydrology – Precipitation and evaporation cycles\nexist (Job 26:8, 36:27-28, 38:25-27)\nFor thousands of years, scientists understood\nthe reality of rain clouds that resulted in rain. Yet\nhydrology—the science of water and the water\ncycle—was not understood. Unknown was the\n“hydrologic cycle.”\n• Then, in the 1st century BC, Marcus Vitruvius\ndescribed a philosophical theory—though\nlimited—in which rain falling in the mountains\ninfiltrated the earth’s surface, which led to\nstreams and springs in the lowlands.\n• Yet it wasn’t until the 15th century that\nLeonardo da Vinci presented an accurate\npicture of the hydrologic cycle. In essence,\nwater on earth moves in a cycle through\ndifferent pathways and at different rates.\nFor example, the evaporation of ocean water\nproduces clouds … clouds drifting over land\nproduce rain … rainwater flows into lakes and\nrivers … water in lakes and rivers evaporates\nback into the atmosphere or eventually flows\nback into the ocean. And the cycle continues.\nHowever, this scientific cycle had been revealed\nin the Bible approximately 3,000 years prior. The\nBook of Job explains the work of God in this way …\n\nJob 26:8, 36:27-28; 38:25-27\n“He wraps up the waters in his clouds, yet the clouds do not burst under\ntheir weight.… He draws up the drops of water, which distill as rain to the\nstreams; the clouds pour down their moisture and abundant showers fall\non mankind.… Who cuts a channel for the torrents of rain, and a path for\nthe thunderstorm, to water a land where no man lives, a desert with no one\nin it, to satisfy a desolate wasteland and make it sprout with grass?”\n\nThe “Who” in the last sentence is the One who\ninvented the cycle in the first place—the One who\nactually recorded the cycle in His Word.\nMorris, Science and the Bible, 14–15.\n\n33"},{"page":34,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nIII. Additional Facts on Textual Preservation\nEvidence\n1. HONESTY TEST\nTo see if the authors wrote any\nembarrassing thing about themselves.\nThe writers of the Bible were more\nconcerned with writing truth than\nwriting an awesome biography.\n• Adam and Eve’s disobedience\n• Moses smiting the rock out of anger,\nthus not able to enter the promise\nland\n• King David’s act of adultery and\nmurder\n• Israel’s backsliding and God’s\njudgment on Israel\n• Jesus called Peter satan\n• Jesus rebuked the disciples for\nfalling asleep when they should be\npraying\n• The disciples of Jesus deserted Him\n• Peter denied Jesus thrice\n• God’s rebuke of the 7 churches in\nthe book of revelation\n• The list goes on\nThe Bible is full of accounts of the\nfailures of people.\ne.g. the Japanese government textbook\nauthorization system has been criticised\nfor being used to reject textbooks that\ndepict Imperial Japan in a negative\nlight. Such as the description of the\nNanking Massacre and other war crimes\ncommitted by the Japanese military\nbefore and during World War II.\n\n34"},{"page":35,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\n2. CORROBORATION TEST\nDo other historical materials confirm or\ndeny the testimony of the Bible?\n• There are 9 non-Christian sources\nthat mention Jesus within 150 years\nof His death\no Roman Historians\n• Tacitus (AD 55-120) the\ngreatest early Roman\nhistorian, wrote that Christus\n(Greek for Christ) had lived\nduring the reign of Tiberius\nand “suffered under Pontius\nPilate, that Jesus’ teachings\nhad already spread to Rome;\nand that Christians were\nconsidered criminals and\ntortured in a variety of ways,\nincluding crucifixion.”\n• Suetonius (AD 69-130) wrote\nof “Chrestus” as an instigator.\nMost scholars believe this is a\nreference to Christ. Suetonius\nalso wrote of Christians having\nbeen persecuted by Nero in\na.d. 64.11\no Roman Officials\n• Pliny the Younger was an\nimperial magistrate under\nEmperor Trajan. In a.d. 112,\nPliny wrote to Trajan of his\nattempts to force Christians to\nrenounce Christ, whom they\n“worshiped as a god.”\n• Emperor Trajan (a.d. 56-117)\nwrote letters mentioning Jesus\nand early Christian origins.\n• Emperor Hadrian (a.d. 76-136)\nwrote about Christians as\nfollowers of Jesus.\n• Plus 33 Christian sources\n\n35"},{"page":36,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nIV. Facts on Universal Influence of the Bible\nNo other book has influenced humanity as\nthe Bible has.\n• The Bible has impacted every culture it\nhas touched\n• The traditional BC\\AD date indicators\nreflect a biblical perspective. BC = Before\nChrist, AD = Anno Domini (Latin for in the\nyear of our Lord)\n• The fine arts have been heavily\ninfluenced by the Bible\nArt: Rembrandt, Da Vinci, Raphael,\nMichaelangelo\nMusic: Bach, Mendelssohn, Brahms,\nBeethoven, Handel\nLiterature: Milton, Shakespeare,\nLongfellow, Kipling, Hawthorne\n• Legal systems are rooted in biblical\nprinciples\nU.S. PRESIDENTS\nGeorge Washington (1732–1799)\nThe 1st president of the United States.\n“It is impossible to rightly govern the world without the Bible.”\n\nThomas Jefferson (1743–1826)\n3rd president of the United States,\nprincipal author of the Declaration of\nIndependence.\n“The Bible makes the best people in the world.”\n\nAbraham Lincoln (1809–1865)\n16th president of the United States.\nIn 1863 he abolished slavery with his\nEmancipation Proclamation.\n“But for this Book, we could not know right from wrong. I believe the Bible is\nthe best gift God has ever given to man.”\n\n36"},{"page":37,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nWORLD LEADERS\nWinston C hurchill (1874–1965)\nEnglish statesman, author, and\nstrategic prime minister of the United\nKingdom during World War II.\n“We rest with assurance upon the impregnable rock of Holy Scripture.”\n\nDouglas MacArthur (1880–1964)\nAmerican General of the U.S. Army,\nSupreme Commander of the Allied\nPowers in Japan, overseeing the\noccupation of Japan during World War\nII and credited for making democratic\nchanges in that country.\n“Never a night goes by, be I ever so tired, but I read the Word\nof God before I go to bed.”\n\nNapoleon (1769–1821)\nA general during the French\nRevolution, the first consul of the\nFrench Republic and emperor of\nFrance.\n“The Bible is no mere book but a living creature with a power that conquers\nall that oppose it.”\n\n37"},{"page":38,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nLAWYERS\nDaniel Webster (1782–1852)\nA leading American statesman and\norator who compiled the widely-used\nWebster’s Dictionary.\n“I believe the Scriptures of the Old and New Testament to be the will and\nthe Word of God.”\n\nBenjamin Franklin (1706–1790)\nScientist, inventor, famous diplomat,\nphilosopher, author, publisher,\npolitician, civic activist, and one of the\nfounding fathers of the United States.\n“Young men, my advice to you is that you cultivate an\nacquaintance with, and a firm belief in, the Holy Scriptures.”\n\nSCIENTISTS\nSir Isaac Newton (1642–1727)\nEnglish physicist, mathematician,\nastronomer, philosopher, and\nalchemist, regarded as the greatest\nfigure in the history of science.\n“We account the Scriptures of God to be the most sublime philosophy.\nI find more sure marks of authenticity in the Bible than in any profane\nhistory whatsoever.”\n\nGalileo Galilei (1564–1642)\nItalian physicist, astronomer,\nastrologer, and philosopher who is\nclosely associated with the scientific\nrevolution.\n“I believe that the intention of Holy Writ was to persuade men\nof the truths necessary to salvation.…”\n\n38"},{"page":39,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 1\n\nWRITERS\nCharles Dickens (1812–1870)\nOne of the best known English\nnovelists, who wrote such classics\nas A Tale of Two Cities, A Christmas\nCarol, Great Expectations, David\nCopperfield, and, Oliver Twist.\n“It is the best Book that ever was or ever will be in the world.”\n\nH. G. Wells (1866–1946)\nEnglish historian, teacher, futurist,\nessayist, and author of The War of the\nWorlds.\n“The Bible has been the Book that held together the fabric of Western\ncivilization. It has been the handbook of life to countless millions of men\nand women. The civilization we possess could not have come into existence\nand could not have been sustained without it.”\n\nMark Twain (1835–1910)\nAmerican humorist, journalist, and\nauthor who acquired international\nfame for his novel The Adventures of\nHuckleberry Finn.\n“Most people are bothered by those passages of Scripture they do not\nunderstand, but the passages that bother me are those I do understand.\n\nHelen Keller (1880–1968)\nAmerican blind and deaf author,\ninspirational lecturer.\n“Unless we form the habit of going to the Bible in bright moments as\nwell as in trouble, we cannot fully respond to its consolations because\nwe lack equilibrium between light and darkness.”\n\n39"}]},"2":{"lesson":2,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":60,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 2\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will be able to list the\ncharacteristics of God from creation, judgment\nand redemption\n\n•\n\nThe student will be able to define sin and its\nconsequences\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will be able to distinguish the\ndifference between Man’s way of dealing with\nsin and God’s way\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence\n\nAge of Conscience\n\nRefer to Chart L2.1-6\n\nCast (Characters)\nGod, Angels, Adam, Eve, Serpent (Devil)\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 2\n\nLesson Summary\nIn this lesson, we will explore God and His work of\ncreation. God made Man (Male and Female) and placed\nthem in the garden with one commandment to follow.\nMan, however, chose to disobey God when tempted by\nthe devil - resulting in sin entering humanity. Sin came\nwith consequences in the form of judgment, but God in\nHis mercy, gave Man a plan for future salvation.\n\nLesson Outline\nA. God\n\n3\n\nB. What Creation teaches us about God\n\n5\n\nC. Creation of Angels\n\n9\n\nD. Creation of Man\n\n10\n\nE. Innocence to the Fall of Man\n\n12\n\nF. Consequences of Sin\n\n15\n\nG. Man’s Way of Dealing with Sin\n\n18\n\nH. God’s Way of Saving Man\n\n19\n\nI. Judgment\n\n20\n\nJ. Promise of a Future Savior\n\n21\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"A\nLesson 2\n\nGOD\nGenesis 1:1\nIn the beginning God created the heavens and the earth.\n\nKey #1: God is the grand subject of the Bible\n\nGod is the Beginning, Source, Initiator, Author\nand Origin of all things. The universe did not\njust come into being by chance; it was created\nby God. The Bible declares to us the truth about\nGod.\n\nI. God is Spirit\nGenesis 1:2\nThe earth was without form, and void; and darkness was on the face\nof the deep. And the Spirit of God was hovering over the face of the\nwaters.\nJohn 4:24\n“God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship him in spirit\nand in truth.”\n\nThe Webster’s Dictionary’s definition of spirit: “A\nsupernatural, rational being usually invisible to\nhuman beings but having the power to become\nvisible at will.”\nTo distinguish God’s Spirit from other spirits, the\nWord of God refers of Him to be the Holy Spirit\n(see Psalm 51:11)\n\n3\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"II. God is Infinite\nLesson 2\n\nPsalm 90:2\nBefore the mountains were brought forth, Or ever You had formed\nthe earth and the world, Even from everlasting to everlasting, You are\nGod.\n\nMan dwells in matter, space and time. God does\nnot. He is not limited to space and time. No one\nand nothing is like God.\n\nIsaiah 40:25-26\n“To whom then will you liken Me, Or to whom shall I be equal?” says\nthe Holy One.\n\nIII. God is the Creator of the World\nIsaiah 44:24\nThus says the LORD, your Redeemer, And He who formed you from\nthe womb: “I am the LORD, who makes all things, Who stretches out\nthe heavens all alone, Who spreads abroad the earth by Myself\n\nCreation reveals and gives glory to God. Creation\nis also God’s design expressed.\n\nPsalms 19:1-4\nThe heavens declare the glory of God; And the firmament shows\nHis handiwork. 2 Day unto day utters speech, And night unto night\nreveals knowledge. 3 There is no speech nor language Where their\nvoice is not heard. 4 Their line has gone out through all the earth, And\ntheir words to the end of the world.\nRomans 1:20\nFor since the creation of the world His invisible attributes are clearly\nseen, being understood by the things that are made, even His eternal\npower and Godhead, so that they are without excuse.\n\n4\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"B\nLesson 2\n\nWHAT CREATION TEACHES US ABOUT GOD\nRefer to Chart L2.2-6\nGod created the world in six days and rested on\nthe seventh.\nDay One: God spoke Light into Existence\n\nGenesis 1:2-3\nThe earth was without form, and void; and darkness was on the face\nof the deep. And the Spirit of God was hovering over the face of the\nwaters. 3 Then God said, “Let there be light”; and there was light.\n\nIV. God is a God of order\nGod is a God of order and has a plan and pattern\nfor everything that He does.\n\n1 Corinthians 14:33\nFor God is not the author of confusion but of peace…\n\nGod lays the foundation of the earth in a\nsystematic manner.\nFor example:\n• God opened the earth to His light before\nhe appointed the sun, moon and stars to\nregulate light on Day 4.\n• God brought forth waters on the earth\nand firmament in the sky in Day 2 before\nHe created sea creatures and birds in the\nair (Day 5).\n\n5\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"V. God is a God of separation\nLesson 2\n\nGenesis 1:4-5\nAnd God saw the light, that it was good; and God divided the light\nfrom the darkness. 5 God called the light Day, and the darkness He\ncalled Night. So the evening and the morning were the first day.\n\nFrom here, you can see that God continues to\nseparate things throughout the whole creation\nprocess.\nDay Two: God Separated Atmosphere and Water\n\nGenesis 1:6-8\n“Then God said, “Let there be a firmament in the midst of the waters,\nand let it divide the waters from the waters.” 7 Thus God made the\nfirmament, and divided the waters which were under the firmament\nfrom the waters which were above the firmament; and it was so.\n8\nAnd God called the firmament Heaven. So the evening and the\nmorning were the second day.\n\nFirmament – expanse, atmosphere\nDay Three: God Separated Seas and Lands\n\nGenesis 1:9-13\nThen God said, “Let the waters under the heavens be gathered\ntogether into one place, and let the dry land appear”; and it was\nso. 10 And God called the dry land Earth, and the gathering together\nof the waters He called Seas. And God saw that it was good. 11 Then\nGod said, “Let the earth bring forth grass, the herb that yields seed,\nand the fruit tree that yields fruit according to its kind, whose seed is\nin itself, on the earth”; and it was so. 12 And the earth brought forth\ngrass, the herb that yields seed according to its kind, and the tree\nthat yields fruit, whose seed is in itself according to its kind. And God\nsaw that it was good. 13 So the evening and the morning were the\nthird day.\n\n6\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Refer to Chart L2.3-6\nLesson 2\n\nDay Four: God created the Sun, moon and stars;\nSeparation of seasons\n\nGenesis 1: 14-19\nThen God said, “Let there be lights in the firmament of the\nheavens to divide the day from the night; and let them be for\nsigns and seasons, and for days and years; 15 and let them be for\nlights in the firmament of the heavens to give light on the earth”; and\nit was so. 16 Then God made two great lights: the greater light to rule\nthe day, and the lesser light to rule the night. He made the stars also.\n17\nGod set them in the firmament of the heavens to give light on the\nearth, 18 and to rule over the day and over the night, and to divide the\nlight from the darkness. And God saw that it was good. 19 So the\nevening and the morning were the fourth day.\n\nVI. God is a God of blessing\nDay Five: God blessed the water creatures and the birds\n\nGenesis 1:20-23\nThen God said, “Let the waters abound with an abundance of living\ncreatures, and let birds fly above the earth across the face of the\nfirmament of the heavens.” 21 So God created great sea creatures\nand every living thing that moves, with which the waters abounded,\naccording to their kind, and every winged bird according to its kind.\nAnd God saw that it was good. 22 And God blessed them, saying,\n“Be fruitful and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and let\nbirds multiply on the earth.” 23 So the evening and the morning\nwere the fifth day.\n\n7\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"Day Six: God blessed Man\nLesson 2\n\nGenesis 1:24-31\nThen God said, “Let the earth bring forth the living creature\naccording to its kind: cattle and creeping thing and beast of the\nearth, each according to its kind”; and it was so. 25 And God made the\nbeast of the earth according to its kind, cattle according to its kind,\nand everything that creeps on the earth according to its kind. And\nGod saw that it was good. 26 Then God said, “Let Us make man in\nOur image, according to Our likeness; let them have dominion over\nthe fish of the sea, over the birds of the air, and over the cattle, over\nall the earth and over every creeping thing that creeps on the earth.”\n27\nSo God created man in His own image; in the image of God He\ncreated him; male and female He created them.28 Then God blessed\nthem, and God said to them, “Be fruitful and multiply; fill the\nearth and subdue it; have dominion over the fish of the sea,\nover the birds of the air, and over every living thing that moves\non the earth.” 29 And God said, “See, I have given you every herb\nthat yields seed which is on the face of all the earth, and every tree\nwhose fruit yields seed; to you it shall be for food.30 Also, to every\nbeast of the earth, to every bird of the air, and to everything that\ncreeps on the earth, in which there is life, I have given every green\nherb for food”; and it was so. 31 Then God saw everything that He had\nmade, and indeed it was very good. So the evening and the morning\nwere the sixth day.\n\nMan was placed in charge of God’s creation and\ngiven dominion in verse 28.\nGod gave rulership over creation to Man. This\nauthority was a delegated authority for which\nman would be accountable.\n\nVII. God is a God of perfection and excellence\nThe word “good” appears seven times (vs. 4, 10,\n12, 18, 21, 25, 31). A better translation of the\nword “good” would be “excellent”.\n\nDeut. 32:3-4\nFor I proclaim the name of the LORD: Ascribe greatness to our God.\nHe is the Rock, His work is perfect; for all His ways are justice, a God\nof truth and without injustice; righteous and upright is He.\n\n8\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"Everything God does is stamped with perfection.\nMan was inspected by God and found to be “very\ngood” in verse 31. Everything else was declared to\nbe “good”. Man was declared to be “very good” or\nvery excellent!\n\nLesson 2\n\nDay Seven: God blessed the day.\nVIII. God is Holy\n\nGenesis 2:2-3 (NIV)\nBy the seventh day God had finished the work he had been doing; so\non the seventh day he rested from all his work. 3 And God blessed\nthe seventh day and made it holy, because on it he rested from all\nthe work of creating that he had done.\n\nC\n\nCREATION OF ANGELS\nAngels are spiritual beings created to serve God\nand His purposes.\n\nHebrews 1:14 (NLT)\nTherefore, angels are only servants—spirits sent to care for people\nwho will inherit salvation.\nHebrews 12:22\n22 But you have come to Mount Zion and to the city of the living God,\nthe heavenly Jerusalem, to an innumerable company of angels,\n\n9\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"Lesson 2\n\nGod has millions and millions of angels. In fact,\nPaul tells us in Hebrews 12:22 that God’s angels\nare innumerable--that is, they can’t be numbered.\nGod had three chief angels. Michael, who is\ncalled “the archangel” (Jude 9), is the warring\nangel. Gabriel is known as the messenger angel,\nbecause he was most often used to deliver\nmessages (Luke 1: 19-26)\n\nLucifer, the Fallen Angel who became Satan\nSatan, or Lucifer as he was called before his\nfall, was perhaps the most beautiful of all Gods\nangels, but he became proud and rebellious. We\nread of this in Ezekiel 28:13-17 and Isaiah 14:1215.\nProbably each of the chief angels were given\nauthority over one third of the angels of God.\nSatan was not satisfied with his high position. He\nsaid, “I will be like the most High“ But God said,\n“Thou shalt be brought down to hell.“ When Satan\nwas cast out of heaven, his angels were cast out\nalso, because they evidently joined him in his\nrebellion against God. These fallen angels are\nthe demon spirits all over the world today. These\nspirits are all a part of the organized kingdom of\nSatan (Matthew 12:26).\n\nEzekiel 28:15\nYou were perfect in your ways from the day you were created, Till\niniquity was found in you.\nIsaiah 14:14\nI will ascend above the heights of the clouds, I will be like the Most\nHigh.\n\n10\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"The desire to be like God demonstrates Satan’s\nrebellion in not submitting to God’s authority and\nlaws.\nLesson 2\n\nThe chief purpose of Satan and the millions of\ndemons under his control is to defeat the plan\nand purpose of God. That is, to keep people from\nsurrendering their lives fully to God, and having a\nbeautiful love relationship with Him. That is why\nwhen you and I want to live for God, Satan or one\nof his demons try to hinder us.\n\nKey #2: The purpose of Satan is to try\nand defeat God’s plan to have a beautiful\nrelationship with Man.\n\nD\n\nCREATION OF MAN\nRefer to Chart L2.4-6\n\nMan was created in the image of God\n\nGenesis 1:27\nSo God created man in His own image; in the image of God He\ncreated him; male and female He created them.\n\nMan was created by God for God.\n\nRevelation 4:11 (KJV)\n“You are worthy, O Lord, To receive glory and honor and power; For\nYou created all things, And by Your will they exist and were created.”\nColossians 1:16\n“For by Him all things were created that are in heaven and that are\non earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or\nprincipalities or powers. All things were created through Him and for\nHim.”\n\n11\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"Man was delegated authority and responsibility\nto rule earth with God.\nLesson 2\nPsalm 8:3-6\nWhen I consider Your heavens, the work of Your fingers, The moon\nand the stars, which You have ordained, 4 what is man that You are\nmindful of him, And the son of man that You visit him? 5 For You have\nmade him a little lower than the angels, And You have crowned him\nwith glory and honour. 6 You have made him to have dominion over\nthe works of Your hands; You have put all things under his feet,\nPsalm 115:16\nThe heaven, even the heavens, are the LORD’S; But the earth He has\ngiven to the children of men.\n\nMan was given a help meet, a Woman\n\nGenesis 2:21-23\nAnd the LORD God caused a deep sleep to fall on Adam, and he\nslept; and He took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh in its place.\nThen the rib which the LORD God had taken from man He made\ninto a woman, and He brought her to the man. And Adam said: “This\nis now bone of my bones and flesh of my flesh; she shall be called\nWoman, because she was taken out of Man.”\n\nAdam had everything he needed in the garden\nof Eden: food, a beautiful home, a wife - and\nmost important, fellowship with God. God would\ncome walking in the garden in the cool of the day\n(Genesis 18).\nThere was also an absence of negative things. No\nweeds, thorns, thistles, because God had not yet\ncursed the ground (Genesis 3:17). No sickness,\nsorrow, guilt, fear, because man still had a perfect\nrelationship with his Creator. The only negative\nfactor in the garden was - Satan.\n\n12\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"IX. God is love\nLesson 2\n\n1 John 4:8\nHe who does not love does not know God, for God is love.\n\nBecause God is love, He created Man to manifest\nHimself by loving Man. He wants to have a\nrelationship with us.\nMan was given a commandment and choice\n\nGenesis 2:15-17\nThen the LORD God took the man and put him in the garden of Eden\nto tend and keep it. 16 And the LORD God commanded the man,\nsaying, “Of every tree of the garden you may freely eat; 17 but of the\ntree of the knowledge of good and evil you shall not eat, for in the\nday that you eat of it you shall surely die.”\n\nForced love and obedience is not love and\nobedience at all! God did not make man to be as\na puppet or robot. God’s plan was to bring into\nexistence a group of people who would willingly\nchoose to love and serve him.\nThe presence of the tree of life and the tree of\nknowledge of good and evil in the middle of the\ngarden gave man the power of choice. Adam\nwas warned that if he made the wrong choice, he\nwould die.\n\nKey #3: God’s plan was to bring into\nexistence a group of people who would\nwillingly choose to love and serve Him.\n\n13\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"E\nLesson 2\n\nINNOCENCE TO THE FALL OF MAN\nMan was created in innocence and without shame.\nGod also had unbroken fellowship with Man in the\ngarden. The only negative factor in the garden was\nSatan who disguised himself in the form of a serpent\nto tempt Man to disobey God.\n\nGenesis 3:1-5\nNow the serpent was more cunning than any beast of the field which\nthe LORD God had made. And he said to the woman, “Has God indeed\nsaid, ‘You shall not eat of every tree of the garden’?” 2 And the woman\nsaid to the serpent, “We may eat the fruit of the trees of the garden; 3\nbut of the fruit of the tree which is in the midst of the garden, God has\nsaid, ‘You shall not eat it, nor shall you touch it, lest you die.’ “4 Then the\nserpent said to the woman, “You will not surely die. 5 For God knows\nthat in the day you eat of it your eyes will be opened, and you will be\nlike God, knowing good and evil.”\n\n• Satan planted the first question (doubt) about God’s\nWord to the woman (v1)\n• Satan then planted a lie and contradicted the truth of\nGod’s Word (v4)\n• Satan made the woman question God’s character (v5)\n• Satan offered the woman to be like God, defining good\nand evil for themselves rather than trust the Word of\nGod (v5)\n\nQuestion: What do you think the woman could have\ndone after her encounter with the serpent?\n\n14\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"Sin entered into humanity\n\nLesson 2\n\nGenesis 3:6\n”So when the woman saw that the tree was good for food, that it was\npleasant to the eyes, and a tree desirable to make one wise, she took\nof its fruit and ate. She also gave to her husband with her, and he ate.”\n\nInstead of obeying God, the woman reasoned with\nherself and chose to eat the fruit.\n\nProverbs 14:12\nThere is a way that seems right to a man, But its end is the way of\ndeath.\n\nAdam (the man) chose to obey his wife instead of\nGod. As a result of Man’s disobedience, sin entered\ninto humanity.\n\nDefining Sin\n• Sin is falling short of God’s glory\nRomans 3:23\nfor all have sinned and fall short of the glory of God,\n\nCreation gives glory to God when they walk in God’s\noriginal design for them. When we step out of God’s\nintended will for us, we fall short of His glory.\n\n15\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"• Sin occurs when we decide to do things our way\nrather than God’s way.\n1 John 3:4 (ESV)\nEveryone who makes a practice of sinning also practices lawlessness;\nsin is lawlessness.\n\nLesson 2\n\n• Sin is disobedience to God\n\nJames 2:10 (NLT)\nFor the person who keeps all of the laws except one is as guilty as a\nperson who has broken all of God’s laws.\n\nF\n\nCONSEQUENCES OF SIN\nRefer to Chart L2.5-6\n\nGenesis 3:7-13\nThen the eyes of both of them were opened, and they knew that\nthey were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together and made\nthemselves coverings. And they heard the sound of the LORD God\nwalking in the garden in the cool of the day, and Adam and his wife\nhid themselves from the presence of the LORD God among the trees\nof the garden. Then the LORD God called to Adam and said to him,\n“Where are you?” So he said, “I heard Your voice in the garden, and I\nwas afraid because I was naked; and I hid myself.” And He said, “Who\ntold you that you were naked? Have you eaten from the tree of which\nI commanded you that you should not eat?” 12Then the man said,\n“The woman whom You gave to be with me, she gave me of the tree,\nand I ate.” 13 And the LORD God said to the woman, “What is this you\nhave done?” The woman said, “The serpent deceived me, and I ate.”\n\n• Sin breaks our communion with God\nIsaiah 59:2\nBut your iniquities have separated you from your God; And your sins\nhave hidden His face from you, So that He will not hear.\n\n16\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"We are robbed from the righteousness, peace and joy\nthat comes with His presence.\nLesson 2\n\n• Sin introduces guilt, fear and shame\nProverbs 28:1\nThe wicked flee when no one pursues, But the righteous are bold as\na lion.\n1 John 3:20\nFor if our heart condemns us…\n\nGuilt is the feeling that says, “I made a mistake”\nShame says “I am a mistake”\nOne of the titles given to Satan is “the accuser”\n(Revelation 12:10)\n• Sin enslaves us\nJohn 8:34\nJesus answered them, “Most assuredly, I say to you, whoever commits\nsin is a slave of sin.\n\nMan lost the authority God gave them and became slaves.\n• Sin leads to death\nRomans 6:23\nFor the wages of sin is death…\n\n17\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"This death represents both a spiritual death (separation\nfrom God) and physical death (sickness, diseases)\nLesson 2\n\n• Sin will affect the next generation\nExodus 20:5\n…For I, the LORD your God, am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of\nthe fathers on the children to the third and fourth generations of those\nwho hate Me,\n\nThe next generation can inherit the consequences of\nour sins.\n• Sin destroys our relationship with people around us\nAdam started blaming his wife for the choices he made\nby himself. The woman was deceived by the serpent but\nAdam willfully disobeyed God by heeding the voice of\nhis wife.\nKey #4: Sin separates us from God and will\neventually lead to death.\n\n18\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"G\nLesson 2\n\nMAN’S WAY OF DEALING WITH SIN\nBlame\n“the woman whom You gave to be with me”\nAdam blamed God for his disobedience. The\nwoman blamed the serpent for deception.\nHide\n“Adam and his wife hid themselves from the\npresence of God”\n\n1 John 1:8 (KJV)\nIf we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is\nnot in us.\n\nCover up\n“Sewed fig leaves together…”\n\nIsaiah 64:6 (NLT)\nWe are all infected and impure with sin. When we display our\nrighteous deeds, they are nothing but filthy rags. Like autumn leaves,\nwe wither and fall, and our sins sweep us away like the wind.\n\nFilthy rags – “menstrual cloth”, “cloth soiled with\ndirty blood”\nSelf-righteousness is basically Man’s attempt to\natone for his own sin by good deeds.\n\n19\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"H\nLesson 2\n\nGOD’S WAY OF DEALING WITH SIN\nTaking responsibility\nPsalm 51:3\nFor I acknowledge my transgressions, And my sin is always before me.\n\nConfess\n“Where are you”\nProverbs 28:13\nHe who covers his sins will not prosper, But whoever confesses and\nforsakes them will have mercy.\n\nCovered by God’s mercy\nGenesis 3:21\n“Also for Adam and his wife the Lord God made tunics of skin and\nclothed them”\n\nGod could have destroyed them but instead an\ninnocent animal became a substitute for them. God\nmade the animal skins to cover Adam and Eve.\nThis is also the start of a substitutionary system\nin the Old Testament where innocent animals are\nsacrificed to atone the sin of Man temporarily.\n\nHebrews 9:22\n“...without shedding of blood there is no remission.”\n\n(You will learn later in the Bible study that the blood\nof animals cannot fully atone for Man. Rather, the\ndeath of an innocent Man was necessary to bring\nhumanity into salvation)\n20\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"X. God is Merciful\nLesson 2\n\nKey #5: Salvation from sin can only come\nfrom God’s way\n\nI\n\nJUDGMENT\nBecause of sin, the time period of innocence ends with\njudgment.\nXI. God is Just\n1. Judgment on the serpent\n\nGenesis 3:14\nSo the LORD God said to the serpent: “Because you have done this,\nYou are cursed more than all cattle, And more than every beast of the\nfield; On your belly you shall go, And you shall eat dust All the days of\nyour life.\n\n2. Judgment on the woman\n\nGenesis 3:16\n“To the woman He said: “I will greatly multiply your sorrow and your\nconception; In pain you shall bring forth children; Your desire shall be\nfor your husband, And he shall rule over you.”\n\n3. Judgment on the ground of the earth\n\nGenesis 3:17-18\n“Then to Adam He said, “Because you have heeded the voice of your\nwife, and have eaten from the tree of which I commanded you, saying,\n‘You shall not eat of it’:” Cursed is the ground for your sake; in toil you\nshall eat of it all the days of your life. Both thorns and thistles it shall\nbring forth for you, and you shall eat the herb of the field.”\n\n21\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"4. Judgment on the man\nLesson 2\n\nGenesis 3:19 (NKJV)\nIn the sweat of your face you shall eat bread Till you return to the\nground, For out of it you were taken; For dust you are, And to dust you\nshall return.”\n\nIt was after the judgments that Adam named his wife\nEve, which means “life”.\n\nJ\n\nHOPE OF A FUTURE SAVIOR\nWhile God in His mercy provided an innocent animal\nas a temporary substitute, the blood of animals cannot\nfully atone for Man’s sin.\nHebrews 10:4\nFor it is not possible that the blood of bulls and goats could take\naway sins.\n\nGod’s plan of restoring back to innocence and\nfellowship with God would later come from a promised\nchild.\nGenesis 3:15\nAnd I will put enmity Between you and the woman, And between your\nseed and her Seed; He shall bruise your head, And you shall bruise\nHis heel.”\n\nEnmity – “hostility”\nSeed – “descendant”\nThis promised Child (seed) will ultimately destroy\nthe work of Satan and save humanity. Until then,\nMan had to struggle with life outside of God’s rule\nand protection.\n22\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"Genesis 3:23-24\n“Therefore the Lord God sent him out of the garden of Eden to till\nthe ground from which he was taken. So He drove out the man; and\nHe placed cherubim at the east of the garden of Eden, and a flaming\nsword which turned everyway, to guard the way to the tree of life.\n\nLesson 2\n\nDeuteronomy 30:19-20 (NLT)\n“Today I have given you the choice between life and death, between\nblessings and curses. Now I call on heaven and earth to witness the\nchoice you make. Oh, that you would choose life, so that you and your\ndescendants might live! 20  You can make this choice by loving the\nLORD your God, obeying him, and committing yourself firmly to him.\nThis is the key to your life….\n\nEleven Attributes of God in this Lesson\nI.\n\nGod is Spirit\n\nII.\n\nGod is infinite\n\nIII.\n\nGod is the Creator of the world\n\nIV.\n\nGod is a God of order\n\nV.\n\nGod is the God of separation\n\nVI.\n\nGod is the God of blessing\n\nVII.\n\nGod is the God of perfection and excellence\n\nVIII.\n\nGod is holy\n\nIX.\n\nGod is love\n\nX.\n\nGod is merciful\n\nXI.\n\nGod is just\n\n23\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":24,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 2\n\nRefer to Chart L2.6-6\n\n1. God is the grand subject of the Bible.\n2. The purpose of Satan is to defeat the plan and\npurpose of God – which is to have a beautiful\nrelationship with God.\n3. God’s plan was to bring into existence a group of\npeople who would willingly choose to love and\nserve Him.\n4. Sin separates us from God and will eventually lead\nto death.\n5. Salvation from sin can only come from God’s way.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n24\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":25,"text":"Charts\nLesson 2\n\n25\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":26,"text":"Charts\nLesson 2\n\n26\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":27,"text":"Charts\nLesson 2\n\n27\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":28,"text":"Lesson 2\n\nModular Section\n1.  Does God Exist?\na. Science vs Faith\nb.  Types of Evolution claimed to be present\ntoday\n2.  Where did the Universe come from?\na.  The Origin of our Universe\nb.  The Big Bang Theory\nc. Evidence of Intelligent Design\nd.  Natural Selection\ne.  Old Earth Theory\n3.  Evil and Suffering\nDM Lab Videos\n-\n\nDoes Science Argue for or against\nGod? https://www.youtube.com/\nwatch?v=UjGPHF5A6Po\n\n-\n\nGod vs. Atheism: Which is more\nRational? https://www.youtube.com/\nwatch?v=4T_P14JjMcM\n\n-\n\nDoes God Exist?\nhttps://www.youtube.com/\nwatch?v=gIorXcloIac\n\n-\n\nWhere Do Good and Evil Come From?\nhttps://dmlab.tabjoy.org/topic/wheredo-good-and-evil-come-from\n\nFor additional resources:\nCreation Ministries International – www.\ncreation.com\nAnswers in Genesis - https://\nanswersingenesis.org/\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":29,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nI. Does God Exist?\na. Science vs. Faith\nDefinition of science: the intellectual\nand practical activity encompassing the\nsystematic study of the structure and\nbehaviour of the physical and natural world\nthrough observation and experiment.\nIn theory, it is the job of science to observe\nthe natural world and seek to understand\nthe natural world through that observation.\nIt can often say, “This happens,” or “This is\nthe value of such-and-such event or process.”\n“Why” and “value” are usually terms more\nproperly associated with philosophy or\nreligion rather than with science. In practice,\nscientists often overstep science’s domain\nand attempt to deliver pronouncements on\nsubjects with which science by definition is\nunable to deal. Biologist Jack Wood Sears\nnotes:\n\n“Science deals only with that which is timeless, repeatable\nat will, dependable, and universal. By this I mean that\na scientist doing an experiment works only with those\nphenomena that are the same today as they were yesterday\nand as they will be tomorrow. He cannot deal with the\nunique, the thing that happens only once, for science\nrelies for verification not upon one experiment but on\nrepeated experiments. A scientist in the laboratory does\nhis experiment today and expects to be able to do it again\ntomorrow with the same results.”\nJack Wood Sears, Conflict and Harmony in Science and the\nBible (Grand Rapids: Baker, 1969), pp. 22–23.\n\nIs evolution a science? Can it be\nsystematically studied, with observation and\nexperiment?\nIf evolution is a science, it must be able to be\nsystematically studied, with observation and\nexperiment.\n29\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":30,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nAdaptation and mutation of genes within\na species is not evolution as Darwin has\nproposed. That is only micro-evolution.\n- Evolution is not a “science”.\n- Evolution vs. Creation is not Science vs\nFaith.\n- Our faith is not blind and evolution is not\nmere fact.\nIt is faith versus faith.\nQuestions to ask:\n• Are we able to observe evolution?\n• Can we make an experiment of it? We have\nobserved adaptation within a species but\nno one has seen cross-species evolution.\n• Has the universe created new planets\nsimilar to ours since the Big Bang?\nIn essence, you could say that both are\n“theories” because we cannot recreate it\ntoday. Which is more plausible? Creation or\nevolution? We all have a belief on how we\ngot here today. The question is - what do we\nbelieve?\nIn other words, it’s natural selection or a\nCreator. There is no middle ground. George Sim\nJohnston\nOther major religions of the world and their\nview on creation/evolution:\n• Buddhism: Creation occurs repeatedly\nthroughout time. At the beginning of\neach kalpa (cycle) land forms, in darkness,\non the surface of the water. Spiritual\nbeings who populated the universe in the\nprevious kalpa are reborn; one of them\ntakes the form of a man and starts the\nhuman race. Unhappiness and misery\nreigns. This is the interval that we are\nexperiencing today. Eventually, the\nuniverse dissolves; all living creatures\nreturn to the soul life, and the cycle\nrepeats.\n\n30\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":31,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\n• Hinduism: The Puranas, ancient Vedic\nbooks, states that universes form from the\nbreath of the God Vishnu’s breath. They\nlast for the duration of one exhalation and\ninhalation. “With each breath, countless\nuniverses emanate from Vishnu in seedlike forms that expand. Then Vishnu\nmultiplies Himself in as many forms as\nthere are universes and enters into each\nuniverse.”\n• Islam: Similar to Bible version of creation.\nHowever, more Islamic scholars have\nallowed for theistic evolution in modern\nday context.\n\nLiving Beings\n\nBeliefs of\nCreationists\n\nBeliefs of\nEvolutionists\n\n-\n\nCreated by Creator\n\n-\n\nIntelligent Design\n\nEvolution by means of\nNatural Selection.\n\nUniverse\n\nSpoken into existence.\n\nBig Bang Theory.\n\nTheism (Is there\na God?)\n\n-\n\n-\n\nScientific\n\nWell-known\nProponents\n\nYes (Theistic)\n\nNature and complexity\nof life declares the\nhandiwork of God.\nHowever, creation\ncannot be re-created.\nGalileo Galilei\nBlaise Pascal\nIsaac Newton\nJohannes Kepler\nAndre Marie Ampere\nLouis Pasteur\nLeonardo Da Vinci\nJames Cleark Maxwell\nGeorge Washington\nCarver\nGuglielmo Marconi\nAntony Flew\nWilliam Lane Craig\n\nNo (Atheist)\n\nObservable through\nnature, fossils and\nscientific study. Able to\nbe re-created or seen.\nCharles Darwin\nStephen Hawkings\nRichard Dawkins\nStephen Jay Gould\nCarl Sagan\n\n31\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":32,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nGalileo – Italian astronomer, inventor of\ntelescope, pendulum\nPascal – Pascal’s law (physics), Pascal’s\ntheorem (math)\nNewton – laws of gravity, motion, and calculus\nKepler – Prominent astronomer of the\nScientific Revolution, discovered Kepler’s law\nof planetary motion\nAmpere – One of the founders of classical\nelectromagnetism. The unit of electric current,\nAmpere, named after him.\nPasteur – pasteurization (pasteurized milk),\nvaccination, microbial fermentation\nDa Vinci – painter (Mona Lisa, Last Supper),\ninventor (hydraulics)\nGeorge Washington Carver – Scientist,\nbotanist, educator, inventor\nMarconi – Italian inventor and electrical\nengineer. Pioneering work on long-distance\nradio transmission and his development of\nMarconi’s law and a radio telegraph system.\nAntony Flew – one of the world’s most famous\natheists who converted to Christianity\nWilliam Lane Craig – one of today’s most\nrenowned Christian apologists\nJames Clerk Maxwell – Electromagnetism,\nwhich was later worked on by Albert Einstein,\nleading to his theory on special relativity.\nWork on chemical kinetic theory of gases.\n• Under the direction of James Clerk\nMaxwell, the Cavendish Laboratory was\nopened in 1874.\n• The Cavendish Laboratory is the\nDepartment of Physics at the University\nof Cambridge, and is part of the School of\nPhysical Sciences.\n• The oak door of the Cavendish Laboratory\nis known for its inscription from the Book\nof Psalms in the Bible: “The works of the\nLord are great, sought out of all them that\nhave pleasure therein.” – Psalm 111:2\n\n32\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":33,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nAccording to 100 Years of Nobel Prizes of\nNobel prizes award between 1901 and 2000\nreveals that (65.4%) of Nobel Prizes Laureates,\nhave identified Christianity in various forms as\ntheir religious preference. Overall, Christians\nhave won a total of 72.5% of all the Nobel\nPrizes in Chemistry, 65.3% in Physics, 62% in\nMedicine, 54% in Economics.\n\nEvolution: Claims and Reasonings\nIdea of Evolution (“On The Origin of\nSpecies” by Charles Darwin, 1859)\nPrior to 1859, most people held to the\nCreationist worldview. History records that\nmost of the great scientists of the 17th and\n18th centuries concur with this viewpoint.\n\n“The central idea of biological evolution is that all life on Earth\nshares a common ancestor, just as you and your cousins share\na common grandmother. Through the process of descent with\nmodification, the common ancestor of life on Earth gave rise to\nthe fantastic diversity that we see documented in the fossil record\nand around us today. Evolution means that we’re all distant\ncousins: humans and oak trees, hummingbirds and whales.”\nThe University of California Museum of Paleontology, Berkeley\nhttp://evolution.berkeley.edu/evolibrary/article/evo_02\n\nThere were writings before Darwin but\nDarwin today is credited with the recognition\nof proposing this theory. Darwin studied\ntheology at Cambridge University, after not\nsuccessfully completing a degree in medicine.\n\n33\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":34,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nHe was on his way to become a minister in England before\n“he received a letter from Captain Fitzroy. This noted Christian\ncommander offered Darwin the position of naturalist on an\nupcoming five-year, round-the-world ocean voyage. Darwin\nsigned up for the journey on the sailing vessel Beagle. During\nthe years away, Darwin in particular recorded observations of\nisland natives, varieties of birds, and geographic landmarks.”\nExcerpt From: Nicholas Comninellis. “Creative Defense.”\n\nIn summary, evolution according to Darwin is:\n• Organisms compete for resources.\n• Therefore the organisms favour traits\nthat aid survival, increasing chances of\nreproduction and more offspring.\n• The increase of favourable traits leads\nto production of new species, therefore\nevolution.\n• This theory of “Natural Selection” is also\nknown as the survival of the fittest.\nThe theory of evolution relies on the following\nmechanisms:\n• Random mutation (spontaneous changes\nwithin the genetic code of all living beings)\n• Natural selection (modification of traits for\nincreased survival chances)\n• Enormous amount of time (rare to have\nrandom mutations and spontaneous\ngeneration, therefore a large amount of\ntime is necessary)\n• Genetic drift and gene flow (new genes\nbrought to new environment, therefore\nnew genetic combinations arise)\nSpontaneous generation – disproven by Louis\nPasteur.\n**Spontaneous generation (arisal of life from non-life\nmatter, and the presence of a pond of such matter;\nknown as the pre-biotic soup) has been long proven\nuntrue (Louis Pasteur) so it is not in question anymore.\n\n34\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":35,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nb. Types of Evolution Claimed To Be Present\nToday\n• Cosmic evolution: the origin of time,\nspace, and matter from nothing in the “big\nbang”\n• Chemical evolution: all elements “evolved”\nfrom hydrogen\n• Stellar evolution: stars and planets formed\nfrom gas clouds\n• Organic evolution: life begins from\ninanimate matter/unicellular to complex\ncells\n• Macro-evolution: animals and plants\nchange from one type into another\n• Micro-evolution: variations form within\nthe “kind”\nNote: Only micro-evolution does exist. It is\ncalled different species. Different breeds of\ndogs, but they are all still dogs.\n\n35\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":36,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nII. Where did the universe come from?\na. The Origin of our Universe\nEvolutionists say…\n\nCreationists say…\n\nOur universe came from\nthe Big Bang\n\nGod spoke the universe\ninto existence\n\nThe origins of the universe can be narrowed down\nto three alternatives:\n1. The universe is not eternal but just popped into\nexistence with no pre-existent cause;\n2. The universe is itself eternal, although it may\nhave changed forms at various times; or\n3. The universe is not eternal but came into\nexistence at a point in time and was caused by\nsomething or someone other than itself.\nPossibilities 1 and 3 are variations of the same\nidea, so we can narrow the possibilities to\ntwo: the universe is either ETERNAL or NOT\nETERNAL.\nScience and the Bible both agree that a\nthing cannot cause itself or have a finite (not\neternal) existence without any cause at all.\nSo did the universe cause itself?\nReturning to our three viable options for the\norigin of the universe, option 1 assumes the\nunscientific and unbiblical hypothesis that\nsomething (the universe) can come from nothing\n(self-caused). By taking on this hypothesis,\nis to say that something came from nothing.\nTherefore, we can remove this option as a viable\napproach to the origin of the universe.\n\n36\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":37,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nIs the universe eternal?\nScientific research is mounting in support of\na clear beginning to our present universe. But\nbefore we deal with that evidence, on what basis\ndo some still postulate an eternal universe? Such\npeople are usually of one of two persuasions:\nthey have a religious presupposition that\nassumes an eternal universe, or, they mistakenly\nthink that scientific evidence supports an eternal\nuniverse theory.\nThose who accept an eternal universe because of\na misunderstanding of scientific evidence show\nignorance of the two most fundamental laws of\nphysics: the law of conservation of energy (“The\nsum total of mass and energy in this universe is\nneither created nor destroyed”) and the law of\nentropy (“Every process in the universe tends\ntoward nonrecoverable energy loss”).\n\n1. The First Law of Thermodynamics (the science\nof energy): Energy can be neither created nor\ndestroyed, but can only be converted from one\nform to another.\na. Examples of the First Law of Thermodynamics:\nLight bulbs transform electrical energy\ninto light energy, and gas stoves transform\nchemical energy from natural gas into heat\nenergy. Plants perform one of the most\nbiologically useful transformations of energy\non Earth: they convert the energy of sunlight\ninto the chemical energy stored within organic\nmolecules.\n\n37\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":38,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\n2. The second law of thermodynamics: In any\nenergy transfer or change, although the total\namount of energy remains unchanged, the\namount of usefulness and availability that the\nenergy possesses is always decreased. The same\nprinciple applies to all the stars of the universe,\nso that the physical universe is, beyond\nquestion, growing old, wearing out and running\ndown.\na. This law certainly testifies equally to the\nnecessary truth that the universe had a\ndefinite beginning. If it is growing old, it must\nonce have been young; if it is wearing out,\nit must once have been new; if it is running\ndown, it must first have been wound up.\nTherefore, the assumption that the universe is\neternal is not a viable option for the origin of the\nuniverse. This leaves us with only option 3, that\nthe universe is not eternal but came into existence\nat a point in time and was caused by something or\nsomeone other than itself.\n\n38\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":39,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nb. The “Big Bang” Theory\nModern scientific cosmology centers on the Big\nBang theory for the origin of the universe. This\ntheory, which says that the universe began with\na huge explosion, which provides convincing\nexplanations for certain observable evidences:\n1. The red shifts in the light coming from\ndifferent galaxies indicate (via the Doppler\neffect) that those more distant are\ntraveling away from us at a faster speed\nthan closer ones. When one calculates\nthese speeds backwards, it appears that\nall the galaxies originated from the same\npoint in space and time.\n2. In 1965 astronomers detected faint radio\nwaves coming equally from all directions\nof the universe. This is now thought to be\nthe “echo” of the Big Bang.\nNoted agnostic astronomer Robert Jastrow said\nthe evidence points to one conclusion: “The\nuniverse had a beginning.”\nRobert Jastrow, God and the Astronomers (New\nYork: W. W. Norton and Company, Inc., 1978), p.\n111.\nWe have just discussed the scientific reasoning\nbehind a rejection of the eternal universe theory.\nWe are left finally with the alternative that makes\nscientific and biblical sense: the universe was\ncreated (had an origin), and was created by\nsomething or someone outside itself.\nThe “Big Bang” is not a CAUSAL theory. It is a\ndescription or an affirmation that the first event\ntook place at a finite time in the past. But does\nnot tell you what caused that first event. It is a\ntheory of the first EFFECT.\n\n39\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":40,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nWhat initiated the “Big Bang”?\n• Evolution says that the Big Bang started\nwith atoms and particles.\nSo how did the atoms and particles get\nthere? Who created these particles? How\ndid they get there?\nIf an evolutionist says that the atoms and\nparticles got there by itself, then we need\nto ask, how can nothing create something?\nExamples: 0x1=0. Zero x anything is always\nzero. An empty room full of air particles\nwill not create a rabbit or grass.\n• Evolution says that an incredible\namount of energy combusted to cause\nthe Big Bang. Evidence is found in the\never-expanding universe, and the\nplanets in motion in the same direction.\nThe First Law of Thermodynamics\nsay that energy cannot be created or\ndestroyed, only converted from form to\nform. How do you explain the Big Bang\ncreating energy and defying this Law?\nNothing in this world has ever defied this\nLaw, so is it possible that the Big Bang did?\nIt will not be a law if it is not universally\napplied.\nIf the Big Bang theory is true, then we have\nto assume the universe is a closed system\n(no God) with a constant amount of energy\n(zero). (Remember the room full of air particles\nmentioned above? Closed sealed room.)\n• But zero energy cannot combust into a\nknown Universe, because it violates the\nfirst Law of Thermodynamics.\n• Zero cannot result in a non-zero output.\n\n40\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":41,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nHowever, the law of thermodynamics will hold\nwith an open system.\n• The Universe therefore must be an\nopen system that was created by a nonphysical force (not composed of mass/\nmatter/energy) outside of the physical\nboundary of this Universe (above nature,\nor supernatural) with the capability of\nbringing it into existence out of nothing.\nThat Force can be none other than the\nsupernatural God of the Bible. – Dr. Jeff\nMiller\n   (http://apologeticspress.org/apcontent.\naspx?category=9&article=2106)\n“The actual point of creation lies outside the\nscope of presently known laws of physics.” –\nStephen Hawking\nTheism provides a better explanation of the\norigin of the universe. There has to be a Finetuner or a Designer behind the origin of the\nuniverse.\n\nIs there a Designer behind the universe?\nRemember, science observes, it does not\nanswer why questions, and so science can\nnever really prove the existence of God. If we\nassume that there is a God, however, and that\nhe did create the universe, and that he is the\ninfinite, intelligent, powerful, and benevolent\nGod the Bible says he is, then he would leave\njust such “traces” or “evidences” in his world\nas we find in our universe. We could almost\nsay that the universe bears the “signature” of\nGod.\nThe universe is expanding at a precisely\ncalibrated rate. If the universe were expanding\nfaster, then there would be no structure in\nthe universe. If the universe were expanding\nslower, it would collapse back in on itself.\n\n41\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":42,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nTake the expansion rate of the universe, which is fine-tuned\nto one part in a trillion trillion trillion trillion trillion. That is, if\nit were changed by one part in either direction--a little faster,\na little slower--we could not have a universe that would be\ncapable of supporting life.”\n~Stephen C. Meyer, PHD (Lee Strobel, The Case for Creator)\n\nThe universe is fine-tuned for human life.\nThis is called the Antrhopic Principle (Perfect\nconditions to sustain life on Earth).\n• When comparing the electromagnetic\nforce to gravity, electromagnetism is 39\ntimes stronger. – Victor J. Stenger, Physicist\n• If the two powers were more evenly\nmatch, the stars would not burn long\nenough for life to develop on an orbiting\nplanet.\n• Scientists refer to this as an anthropic\ncoincidence.\nEvolutionist and astronomer Carl Sagan said\nthat the odds that such an explosion could\nproduce the highly organized structures we\nsee in the universe is 1 to 102,000,000,000\n(that is 1 followed by 2 billion zeros).\nJohn Billingham and Rudolf Pe, editors, Communications\nWith Extra-Terrestrial Intelligence (New York, NY: Pergamon\nPress, 1979)\n\nStatisticians point out that anything beyond\n10(50) is beyond reason. Jesus fulfilling 8 OT\nprophecies is already 10 to the power of 17.\nBelieving the Big Bang takes even more faith\nthan to believe in the fact that Jesus Christ\nis Messiah! And evolutionists still say that\nChristians have blind faith? Who has more\nblind faith?\nIt is not possible to say that a random\nunplanned collision results in today’s highly\nintricate design of an Earth and Earth life.\nThe facts point to intricate creation with an\nIntelligent Designer.\n\n42\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":43,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nWould it not be strange if a universe without purpose\naccidentally created humans who are so obsessed with\npurpose?\n- Sir John Templeton (Lee Strobel, The Case for Creator)\n\nWe cannot recreate the creation of the\nuniverse. We have to look at the proofs and\nsee which is more plausible.\n\nEvolution say that the Big Bang created the Earth and\nit’s environment, as well as all complex cells and living\nbeings of today.\n\nHow did a random, unorganized collision\ncaused such Intelligent Design?\nc. Evidence of Intelligent Design:\n- Anthropic Principle (Perfect conditions to\nsustain life on Earth)\n\n“When you compare the electromagnetic force to gravity, we\nfind that electromagnetism is 39 times stronger, according\nto physicist and author Victor J. Stenger. And that’s handy\nbecause if the two powers were more evenly matched, stars\nwouldn’t burn long enough for life to develop on an orbiting\nplanet. Scientists refer to this as an anthropic coincidence, or a\ncoincidence related to mankind’s very existence.\nHere’s another example that Stenger reminds us of: A vacuum\nin the universe is a lot less dense than we previously thought\n(139 times less dense, in fact). That’s significant because if the\noriginal higher estimates had been correct, the universe would\nhave blown apart eons ago.”\n– How Stuff Works (http://science.howstuffworks.com/\nscience-vs-myth/everyday-myths/anthropic-principle.htm)\n\n43\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":44,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\n- Rare Earth Principle (read http://science.\nhowstuffworks.com/life/evolution/earthjust-right-for-life.htm)\n- Ecosystems (Aquatic, Terrestrial)\n- Food Chains and Webs\nDo note: We cannot recreate the creation of the\nuniverse. We have to look at the proofs and see\nwhich is more plausible.\nWhen we take on the theist worldview to see\nthe origin of the universe, we can find out in the\nBible the probable cause of the universe. We can\nsee an Intelligent Designer behind the creation\nof the universe.\n\nGenesis 1:1 (KJV)\nIn the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.\nPsalm 19:1 (KJV)\nThe heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth\nhis handiwork.\n\nHow did the origin of life take place?\nd. Natural Selection\nEvolutionists say…\n\nCreationists say…\n\nNatural Selection\n\nGod created all\n\nEvolutionists perspective on the origin of life\nis that it involved a process called “Natural\nSelection”.\nAccording to evolutionary theory, the earth in\nthe initial stages had an atmosphere completely\ndifferent from ours today. Scientists at first\nthought it contained methane, ammonia,\nhydrogen and water vapor. (However, most\nhave since revised their theories to suggest that\nthe atmosphere primarily consisted of carbon\ndioxide, water vapor and nitrogen.)\n44\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":45,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nThen by the action of ultraviolet rays, electrical\ndischarges, and a continuous bombardment of\nhighly charged particles, molecules were formed\nspontaneously and randomly. The molecules\nincluded sugars, amino acids, and pieces of\nDNA. More and more pieces clustered together\nand formed increasingly larger molecules and\nmolecular chains. These giant molecules then\nreacted until a primitive cell stage was reached,\nagain through a random process.\nFinally, these clusters of proto-cells absorbed\nother molecules and at some point began to\nreproduce. Thus developed the first living cells.\nThose first living cells fed on the molecules still\nleft in the “primeval soup.”\nThis evolutionary theory is basing its assumption\non chance and “trial and error”.\nEvolutionist are not able to answer the origin\nto the first cell. The make-up of a single cell is\nextremely specified and complex. It did not just\nrandomly fall into place.\nFor example, take a single bacteria cell:\n• One bacterium contains some 1500\ndifferent enzymes\n• Each of which consist of several\nhundred amino acids\n• Those various amino acids must\nbe arranged in precisely the RIGHT\nSEQUENCE\n• The chance that a given enzyme –\nconsisting of 200 amino acids (of which\nthere are 20 different kinds) could develop\nby chance is 1 in 20^200\n• The chance is practically nil\n• And that is only ONE of the necessary 1500\nenzymes for ONE bacterium\n\n45\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":46,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nWhat more the origin of a single living cell?\nWhich would require billions of kilos of each of\nthe many different enzymes and DNA molecules,\ncombining and recombining randomly, until,\nagainst all probability, the right random\ncombination occurred.\nWhen we look at how cells form and develop,\nscientists have discovered that there is\ninformation in the cells that give instructions,\nto tell where each should go or do. The three\nsequences of letters below illustrate a random\narrangement, a highly ordered buy redundant\narrangement, and a highly ordered, information\nintensive arrangement:\n(a) random:\nACDBGEF ADGEBFC CBFGEAD\n(b) ordered but redundant (like a crystal):\nABCDEFG ABCDEFG ABCDEFG\n(c) ordered and information intensive (like\nDNA or protein):\nTHIS SEQUENCE OF LETTERS CONTAINS A\nMESSAGE!\nIn order for a system to be specified and\ncomplex, there has to be someone that specified\nthose information.\nModern scientific research has discovered that\nthe DNA molecule within a living organism is\nwhat is responsible for carrying the instructions\nof the cells. Human DNA consists of about 3\nbillion bases, and more than 99 percent of\nthose bases are the same in all people. The\norder, or sequence, of these bases determines\nthe information available for building and\nmaintaining an organism, similar to the way in\nwhich letters of the alphabet appear in a certain\norder to form words and sentences.\n\n46\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":47,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nAn important property of DNA is that it can\nreplicate, or make copies of itself. Each strand of\nDNA in the double helix can serve as a pattern\nfor duplicating the sequence of bases. This is\ncritical when cells divide because each new cell\nneeds to have an exact copy of the DNA present\nin the old cell.\nThe DNA is what tells the amino acids how to\nbe arranged, which therefore determines what\nkind of protein is developed. Within a protein,\nmultiple amino acids are linked together by\npeptide bonds, thereby forming a long chain.\nThese protein chains have to be arranged in\na specified order or else it would not form its\nstructure. Any ONE wrong or misarranged point\nin the chain can render the entire chain useless.\nThe sequence is to be specific.\nSo this therefore begs the question: “Who put\nthe information there?”\nThere has to be an Intelligent mind behind\nthe information. Someone put it in there, it\ncould not have been random.\nWhen do we infer design?\n- A highly improbable event\n- A pattern or functional outcome\nWhen you have a finely tuned system that\nalso produces a function, then you know that\nintelligence is involved.\n\n47\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":48,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nNeither observation nor controlled experiment\nhas shown natural selection manipulating\nmutations so as to produce a new gene,\nhormone, enzyme system, or organ. Michael\nPitman, Adam and Evolution (London: Rider,\n1984), p. 67-68\nDarwin himself: “There are two or three million\nspecies on earth. A sufficient field one might\nthink for observation; but it must be said today\nthat in spite of all the evidence of trained\nobservers, not one change of the species to\nanother is on record.” Life and Letters, Vol. 3, p.\n25.\nThe birth of a new species has not been ever\nwitnessed by any man, natural selection in this\nsense has not been proven to exist.\nInstead, the Bible tells us:\n\nThe earth brought forth vegetation, plants yielding seed\naccording to their own kinds, and trees bearing fruit in which is\ntheir seed, each according to its kind. And God saw that it was\ngood.\n12\n\nSo God created the great sea creatures and every living creature\nthat moves, with which the waters swarm, according to their kinds,\nand every winged bird according to its kind.\n21\n\nThe word “kind” (occurs ten times in Genesis\n1) refers to species, or families. Each created\nfamily was to produce only its own kind. This\nforever precludes the drifting, changing process\nrequired by organic evolution where one species\nturns into another. This is exactly what the fossil\nrecords reveal.\n\n48\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":49,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nThere is a difference between micro-evolution\nand macro-evolution.\n- Micro-evolution are adaptations and\nmutations that do effect minor changes\nwithin certain species and animals, but\nthese never produce a new family or type.\nCreationists believe in micro-evolution.\n- But evolution theory demands a belief in\nmacro-evolution: that mutations occur\nover enough time to create whole new\nkinds of animals. This does not exist.\nEvery living kind was created by God in the\nCreation week. It was good. There is no macroevolution to evolve new species. All that is to\nexist on this Earth as living beings was created\nthen and has not been changed since.\nWe possess adaptive genes and we have the\nability to make species extinct. But no new kind\nof evolution has been ever seen.\nTake note that God did not say there could be\nno changes within the family. He did not create\nall the varieties of dogs, cats, horses, fish, etc. in\nthe very beginning. There was only a male and\nfemale of each species, and many changes have\nsince occurred to produce a wide assortment of\nvarieties within the family. But the reality is that\ncats have always remained cats, dogs are still\ndogs, and men are still men.\n\n49\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":50,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\ne. Old Earth Theory\nAge of the Earth\nEvolutionists say…\n\nCreationists say…\n\nBillions of Years Old\n\nApproximately 6,000\n\nEvolution say that fossils and geologic\ntestings showed that the Earth is billions\nof years old through use of Carbon Dating.\n\nHow do we verify if carbon dating is accurate?\nThe carbon 14 dating method was developed\nduring the late 1940s and early 1950s by Dr.\nWillard F. Libby, who won a Nobel Peace Prize for\nhis excellent work. He cautioned, however, that\ncarbon 14 dating is only accurate to about 4,000\nyears. After that amount of time, the accuracy\nbecomes untrustworthy.\nToday, carbon dating can typically measure up\nto 50,000 years old. Most scientists have openly\nprofessed that any age older than 50,000 years\ncannot be 100% verified since the technology\ndoes not allow for it and the C14 atoms will have\nvanished by then.\n\n“The oldest dates that can be reliably measured by radiocarbon\ndating are around 50,000 years ago”\n– Wikipedia\n\n50\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":51,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nTo have accurate carbon dating:\n1) The quantity of radioactive elements\npresent when the item was first formed\nmust be known.\n2) The rate of radioactive decay must be\nconstant over time.\n3) The item must have been insulated from\noutside factors.\nExcerpt From: Nicholas Comninellis. “Creative Defense.”\n\nNot possible, because:\n1) Elements can decay and change into other\nelements. There is no way to know this.\n2) Radioactive decay rates are not as\nconstant as supposed.\n3) An item is not able to be insulated from\noutside factors. A rock embedded among\nother rocks will be affected, especially with\nporous factors.\n4) Additionally, the ratio of carbon\nbeing absorbed is rapidly changing\ndue to climate changes and change\nin atmospheric levels. This affects the\nabsorption of carbon in bodies and affects\nthe carbon dating process.\nThe Bible timeline tells us that we have a young\nEarth, approximately 6,000 years old or so.\n\nSome Evidences of a Young Earth:\n• Human Population Growth Rate\nTaking into account wars, plagues, famine and other\ndisasters, growth of human population is estimated at 1.5\npercent per year. If human beings are estimated to have\nlived one million years starting from zero people, we would\nhave three trillion people today. However, if you work\nbetween one single couple and the population size today,\nit takes around 4,000 years to get to our numbers today.\n(Henry M. Morris and John D. Morris, Modern Creation\nTrilogy, vol. 2 (Green Forest, AR: Master Books, 1996), p. 317320.)\n51\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":52,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\n• Historical Evidences of World Empires\nThe first known world empire arose in only 3100 B.C. There\nis no recorded history before that of existent world empires.\nCould there have been none?\n“Colin Renfrew, the premier living archaeological and\nlinguistic scholar in England, sums up the conclusions\nof enormous research by declaring that 3100 B.C. is\napproximately the date of the founding of the world’s oldest\nempire, located in Egypt. There are even some Egyptologists\nwho argue that Egypt’s first dynasty did not start until\naround 2000 B.C. ” Colin Renfrew, Before Civilization (New\nYork, NY: Alfred A. Knopf, 1975), p. 21, 25, 28, 74.\nSir Isaac Newton, in his book “The Chronology of Ancient\nKingdoms Amended”, was upset with the Egyptian records\nthat stated that their empire started before 5000BC.\n• Magnetic Field Force\nThe Earth’s magnetic field is falling (weakening) over time, at\naround 5% per century.\nIn a recent article (May 2016) by Sciencealert.com, it\nsays:\n“New research has shown in the most detail yet how rapidly\nEarth’s magnetic field - which acts like a shield to protect us\nfrom harsh solar winds and cosmic radiation - is changing,\ngetting weaker over some parts of the world, and strengthening\nover others.\n…over the past few years it’s become clear that the invisible\nbubble that protects our planet from the harsh conditions of\nouter space has been getting weaker and weaker.\nAccording to scientists’ best estimates, the field is now\nweakening around 10 times faster than initially thought, losing\napproximately 5 percent of its strength every decade. But they\ndon’t really know why, or what that means for our planet.”\n\n“If we assume this current rate of decrease has been\nand will be constant, then two startling conclusions are\ninevitable. First, within about 1,400 years our magnetic\nfield will disappear entirely. Secondly, if we look backward\nabout 10,000 years, the earth’s magnetic field would have\nbeen as strong as that of a magnetic star and incapable of\nsupporting life. These conclusions would clearly limit the\npotential age of the earth today to less than 10,000 years.”\nExcerpt From: Nicholas Comninellis. “Creative Defense.”\n52\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":53,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nNoah’s Flood\nEvolution: Flood is false.\nCreation: The flood is real, not symbolic. Evidences of the\nflood can be found in nature.\nEvolutionists like to question the authenticity or mathematical\nprobability of Noah and the ark. They claim it is falsified\nbecause it is not possible to fit two of every animal onto that\nArk.\n#1. Two of every kind. Not two of every animal. Labradors,\nGolden Retrievers, Dalmatian are types of… dogs! Same\nspecies. Kind = species.\n#2. Who said Noah brought full grown animals onto the Ark?\nWhy can’t he have brought babies?\nNoah’s flood has changed the world we live in, it is vastly\ndifferent from the pre-flood world. This affects geology\ncolumns, and the mapping of the world now compared to preflood.\n- Grand Canyon, exits a higher elevation than entrance. Is\nit really evolution or is it a work of God?\n- “Altitude is another challenge to the formation of the\nGrand Canyon by the proposed “slowly flowing river”\ntheory. The top of the Grand Canyon is over 6,000 feet\nabove sea level. But the river that supposedly “carved”\nthese walls “billions of years ago” enters the canyon\nat only 2,800 feet above sea level. To “carve” those\nwalls, the river would have had to flow uphill over\n3,200 feet vertically. Clearly, the river did not form the\nGrand Canyon, for rivers do not flow uphill!” Nicholas\nComninellis. “Creative Defense”.\n\n53\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":54,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nIII. Evil and Suffering\nIf God is all-loving and all-powerful why\nis there so much evil and suffering in this\nworld?\nMany of us have at one point or another thought\nthis, “Why? It’s just not fair! God, why would You\nallow…?”\nAt times life is simply not fair. In fact, most\npeople have muttered, “Why? Why would God\nallow something so cruel… so evil?” Where\nwas He? Doesn’t He care? Left unanswered or\nincorrectly answered, these questions often\nbecome the basis for denying the existence of\nGod or rejecting the goodness of God or both. It\ncan erode our faith.\nTo properly unpack this question and find an\nanswer to the question of evil and suffering, we\nhave to first look at the definitions to set the\nparameters to this subject.\nWhat is Evil?\n• Evil is the corruption of good\n• The absence of good, when good\nshould exist\n• The departure from the way life ought\nto be\n• Evil is the moral choice of bad over\ngood, arising from the badness of\ncharacter. In Greek, the word kakia, which\nemanates from “badness in character,”\nmeans “wicked, depraved” and “morally\nreprehensible”\n• A violation of the will of God\n• A perversion of the Word of God\n• Evil is that which causes evil\no An evil person causes evil\no An evil spirit causes evil that leads to an\nevil generation\n\n54\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":55,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nIf God made all things, doesn’t that mean He created evil?\n• Evil is not a thing, but rather is a\ncondition resulting from the improper\nuse or perversion of a good thing\n• Evil exists in something else, something\nit corrupts – corrupted goodness. A\ngood knife can be used by an evil man\nto commit murder.\n• Evil is the absence of good. It is an\nintruder brought in by human beings.\nEvil was not created by God. Adam and\nEve chose to disobey God. Evil is not\nthe opposite of good but the absence\nof good.\n• Everything God created as good, but\nthe intentional wrong choices of Adam\nand Eve resulted in an aberration of the\ngood things God created.\n\nGenesis 13:1\nGod saw all that he made, and it was very good.\n\nDoes God cause evil?\nGod cannot ever cause evil. God cannot do\nanything that is contradictory to His character.\nOtherwise, He ceases to be God. The Bible clearly\nteaches that God is good.\n“You are not a God who takes pleasure in evil;\nwith you the wicked cannot dwell.… Dear friend,\ndo not imitate what is evil but what is good.\nAnyone who does what is good is from God.\nAnyone who does what is evil has not seen God.”\n(Psalm 5:4; 3 John 11)\n\n55\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":56,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nThe Problem of Evil?\nThe very existence of evil in our world presents\na major problem to many people who know the\nclaims about God—that He is morally perfect,\nall-powerful, and all-knowing. The premise\nis that evil cannot coexist alongside a good,\nall-powerful, and all-knowing God because\nthey are mutually exclusive of one another.\nTherefore, skeptics conclude that the presence\nof evil in the world negates the presence of a\ngood, all-powerful, and all-knowing God. The\nproblem involves three components and three\nassumptions:\nIf God is all-good and all-powerful, why does He\nallow evil?\n• There are 3 components contained in\nanswering this classic question\no #1 God is all-good\no #2 God is all-powerful\no #3 Evil is present in the world\n• The 3 assumptions are\no #1 If God is all-good – He would want\nto prevent evil\no #2 If God is all-powerful – He could\nprevent evil\no #3 If God is all-knowing – He could\nanticipate evil and therefore stop it\n• If any 1 component is missing, then you\ndon’t have a problem.\no #1 If God is not all-good, the problem\nvanishes. God is a “cosmic demon” who\ncauses evil.\no #2 If God is not all-powerful, the\nproblem disappears. God is too weak\nand powerless to stop evil.\no #3 If no evil is present in the world,\nthe problem evaporates. Evil (sin and\nsuffering) is mere illusion.\n\n56\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":57,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\n• All 3 components are true, based on the\nBible\no #1 God is good, and He gave people\nfree will, which is good.\n• Psa 92:15\no #2 God is all-powerful, and He can do\nanything that is logical, but it is illogical\nfor Him to both grant free will and\nconstrain it.\n• Isa 46:10-11\no #3 Evil and its effects (sin and suffering)\nare present in the world because\npeople chose to exert their God-given\nfree will and disobey God.\n• Romans 3:23\nWhy would a good, all-powerful God allow suffering?\n• God sometimes allows suffering in order\nto bring about a greater good.\n• God sometimes allows evil and sufferings\nthrough:\no The free will of human beings\no Natural order (earthquakes, death, etc.)\no Evil spirit beings\n• God always has a good purpose for our\nsuffering\no He allows suffering to expose our sin\no He allows suffering to produce much\ngood\no He allows suffering to change our\nperspective\no He allows suffering to bless our future\nJames 5:11 (AMP)\n  You know how we call those blessed (happy) who were steadfast\n[who endured]. You have heard of the endurance of Job, and you\nhave seen the Lord’s [purpose and how He richly blessed him in\nthe] end, inasmuch as the Lord is full of pity and compassion and\ntenderness and mercy.\n11\n\n57\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":58,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nWhat are the causes for evil and suffering in the world?\nThere is no single clear cause for the evil and\nsuffering in the world, for many variable can be\ninvolved.\n• The result of our choices\n• The result of the choices of others\n• The result of some evil spirit beings\n• The result of natural order\n\nIf God did not create evil, how did He create Satan, who is\nthe embodiment of evil?\nGod did not create “Satan.” He created “Lucifer,\nson of the morning” (Isa 14:12) – an angelic\nbeing who, because of rebellion against God,\nwas cast out of heaven. Only after he sinned did\nhe become Satan, a name that literally means\n“adversary.” Only then did he become the\nadversary of God and of all that is good.\nAngelic beings are created with a will, however\nunlike human beings, they do not have a right to\nexercise that will. When Satan, exercised his will\nto want to be like God, he was cast out. Angelic\nbeings cannot get a second chance, they are not\ngiven the privilege of repentance.\nWhat is the difference between angels and\nhumans? We humans have a body of flesh. In\nour fleshly bodes, we are able to feel pain – we\ncan experience suffering – that leads us to godly\nsorrow that produces repentance.\n\n58\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":59,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\nHow can a God of love be the God of wrath at the same\ntime? These 2 attributes are incompatible.\nLove and wrath are not incompatible and can\ncertainly exist at the same time within the same\nperson.\n• A mother who intensely loves her baby\nwill, at the same time, have wrath against\na child molester who intends to harm\nher baby. She might even have wrath\nagainst her own beloved child for being\ndisobedient and for being disrespectful to\nher.\n• When you read that “God is love,” the\nGreek word for “love” used here is agape,\nwhich means a commitment to seek\nanother’s highest good. God is never\nwithout His love for you.\n• His wrath is in response to sin and is\nexpressed against anything that seeks\nto harm you or any other object of His\nlove. This truth was illustrated in the\nLord’s defeat of the Egyptian army as they\npursued the Israelites in order to destroy\nthem.\nThis subject can boil down to the FREEDOM OF\nCHOICE that God has bestowed upon us human\nbeings. Love presents a choice.\nThe freedom of choice is like a coin:\n• On one side, we have the right to choose\n• However, on the flip side, we also have to\nbe responsible for the exercised right of\nmaking our choices.\n\n59\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":60,"text":"See: creation.com/evoquest for supporting references.\n\nDr Marc Kirschner, chair of the Department of Systems\nBiology, Harvard Medical School, stated: “In fact, over\nthe last 100 years, almost all of biology has proceeded\nindependent of evolution, except evolutionary biology\nitself. Molecular biology, biochemistry, physiology, have\nnot taken evolution into account at all.” Dr Skell wrote, “It\nis our knowledge of how these organisms actually operate,\nnot speculations about how they may have arisen millions\nof years ago, that is essential to doctors, veterinarians,\nfarmers ….” Evolution actually hinders medical discovery.\nThen why do schools and universities teach evolution so\ndogmatically, stealing time from experimental biology that\nso benefits humankind? creation.com/science#relevance\n\nBREAKTHROUGHS DUE TO EVOLUTION?\n\n13. WHERE ARE THE SCIENTIFIC\n\nEvolutionists often use flexible story-telling to ‘explain’\nobservations contrary to evolutionary theory. NAS (USA)\nmember Dr Philip Skell wrote, “Darwinian explanations\nfor such things are often too supple: Natural selection\nmakes humans self-centered and aggressive—except\nwhen it makes them altruistic and peaceable. Or natural\nselection produces virile men who eagerly spread their\nseed—except when it prefers men who are faithful\nprotectors and providers. When an explanation is so\nsupple that it can explain any behavior, it is difficult to\ntest it experimentally, much less use it as a catalyst\nfor\nscientific\ndiscovery.”\ncreation.com/sexstories\n\nTELLING TOLERATED?\n\n12. WHY IS EVOLUTIONARY ‘JUST-SO’ STORY-\n\nIf everything evolved, and we invented God, as per\nevolutionary teaching, what purpose or meaning is there\nto human life? Should students be learning nihilism (life is\nmeaningless) in science classes? creation.com/chesterton\n\nDISTRIBUTED BY:\n\nCMI has offices in:\nAustralia Canada New Zealand Singapore\nSouth Africa USA UK/Europe\n\nLog on to\nContact us for a free information pack or to make ministry\nenquiries, visit: creation.com/contactus\n\nhoW can i get more information?\n\nMore copies of this and similar creation pamphlets are\navailable through Creation Ministries International. Write\nfor a sample pack with price list.\n\nThis pamphlet and others like it have been produced by\nCreation Ministries International (CMI) and made available\nto concerned individuals and churches who wish to help\nspread awareness of this greatly censored information.\nThe distributor(s) may have put their name in the white\nspace below.\n\nWho is responsible for this pamphlet?\n\nKarl Popper, famous philosopher of science, said\n“Darwinism is not a testable scientific theory, but a\nmetaphysical [religious] research programme ....” Michael\nRuse, evolutionist science philosopher admitted, “Evolution\nis a religion. This was true of evolution in the beginning,\nand it is true of evolution still today.” If “you can’t teach\nreligion in science classes”, why is evolution taught?\ncreation.com/evo-religious, creation.com/notscience\n\nWHY IS A FUNDAMENTALLY RELIGIOUS\nIDEA, A DOGMATIC BELIEF SYSTEM THAT FAILS\nTO EXPLAIN THE EVIDENCE, TAUGHT IN SCIENCE\nCLASSES?\n\n15.\n\n10 14\n11 15\n12\n13\n\nMIND/ INTELLIGENCE, MEANING, ALTRUISM AND\nMORALITY?\n\n11. HOW DID BLIND CHEMISTRY CREATE\n\nYou cannot do experiments, or even observe what\nhappened, in the past. Asked if evolution has been observed,\nRichard Dawkins said, “Evolution has been observed. It’s\njust that it hasn’t been observed while it’s happening.”\ncreation.com/notscience#distinction\n\n14.\n\nSCIENCE INVOLVES EXPERIMENTING TO\nFIGURE OUT HOW THINGS WORK; HOW THEY\nOPERATE. WHY IS EVOLUTION, A THEORY ABOUT\nHISTORY, TAUGHT AS IF IT IS THE SAME AS THIS\nOPERATIONAL SCIENCE?\n\nProfessor Gould wrote, “the maintenance of stability within species must be considered as a major\nevolutionary problem.” creation.com/living_fossils\n\nUNCHANGED OVER SUPPOSED HUNDREDS\nOF MILLIONS OF YEARS, IF EVOLUTION HAS\nCHANGED WORMS INTO HUMANS IN THE SAME\nTIME FRAME?\n\nQUESTIONS FOR\n\n15 EVOLUTIONISTS\n\nevolution!\n\nQuestion\n\nSTSINOITULOVE\n\n10. HOW DO ‘LIVING FOSSILS’ REMAIN\n\nMODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 2\n\n60\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"3":{"lesson":3,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":23,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 3\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will be able to explain the concept\nof grace, faith and obedience\n\n•\n\nThe student will find the correlation between\nNoah’s day and our present day\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will examine the story of how\nCain, Abel and Noah concluded that grace,\nfaith and obedience is necessary for their\nsalvation\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience Age of Human Government\nRefer to Chart L3.1-3\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 3\n\nCast (Characters)\nGod ,Cain and Abel, Seth, Enoch and Noah\n\nAdam\n\nCain\n\nAbel\n\nSeth\n\nEnosh\n\nKenan\n\nMahalalel\n\nJered\n\nEve\n\nOther Sons\n& Daughters\n\nOther children\n\nEnoch\n\nMethuselah\nOther children\n\nLamech\nOther children\n\nNoah\n\nOther children\n\nOther children\n\nOther children\n\nOther children\n\nOther children\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"Lesson 3\n\nLesson Summary\nIn this lesson, we will explore life outside of the Garden\nand the lives of Adam’s children, Cain and Abel. We will\nsee how the problem of sin continued in humanity,\nleading to God’s judgment. In the midst of judgment,\nGod introduces a plan of salvation to a man called\nNoah. Noah’s demonstration of faith and obedience to\nGod led to the saving of his household.\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Cain and Abel\n\n4\n\nB. God’s Mercy and Cain’s Response\n\n6\n\nC. Seth and Enoch\n\n9\n\nD. Noah\n-\n\nPlan of Salvation\n\n-\n\nNoah’s response\n\n-\n\nResult\n\n10\n\nE. Grace, Faith and Obedience\n\n12\n\nF. God establishes a covenant\n\n14\n\nG. Comparing Noah’s Day and Our Day\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"A\nLesson 3\n\nCAIN AND ABEL\nRefer to Chart L3.1-3\nThe following chart will illustrate the contrast\nbetween the previous lesson and the story of\nCain and Abel.\nGenesis 3\n\nGenesis 4\n\nThe beginning of sin\n\nThe progress and fruit\nof sin\n\nSin in the first family\n\nSin spreads to the\nfamily of Man\n\nSin against God\n\nSin against fellowman\n\nEnmity prophesied\n\nEnmity evidenced\n\nTwo Offerings\nGenesis 4:1-5\nNow Adam knew Eve his wife, and she conceived and bore Cain, and\nsaid, “I have acquired a man from the LORD.” 2 Then she bore again,\nthis time his brother Abel. Now Abel was a keeper of sheep, but Cain\nwas a tiller of the ground. 3 And in the process of time it came to pass\nthat Cain brought an offering of the fruit of the ground to the LORD. 4\nAbel also brought of the firstborn of his flock and of their fat. And the\nLORD respected Abel and his offering, 5 but He did not respect Cain\nand his offering. And Cain was very angry, and his countenance fell.\n\n4\n\nCain\n\nAbel\n\nThe name Cain means\n“acquired” or “possessed”.\nIt could be that Eve\nbelieved she had acquired\nthe child who would fulfill\nthe promise of Genesis\n3:15.\n\nThe name Abel means\n“breath” or “vapour”.\nPerhaps he was\nnamed as such due\nto an awareness of\nthe fleeting nature of\nman’s life.\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"Cain\nLesson 3\n\nCain was a tiller of the\nsoil.\n\nAbel\nAbel was the first\nshepherd. The word\n“keeper” literally\nmeans “feeder”.\n\nCain and Abel brought God two different kinds\nof offerings representing two different types of\nworship: God-directed and man-created.\n\nAbel’s offering: God-Directed\nHebrews 11:4\nBy faith Abel offered to God a more excellent sacrifice than Cain,\nthrough which he obtained witness that he was righteous, God\ntestifying of his gifts; and through it he being dead still speaks.\n\n• Abel approached God in His prescribed way\n• Firstborn and fat of his flock suggest that\nAbel offered the best parts to God\n• Abel’s offering was more excellent (greater\nin quantity and quality) than Cain’s\n• Abel’s offering revealed that he also came\nwith the right attitude in worshiping God\nCain’s offering: Man-Created\nJude 1:11\nWoe to them! For they have gone in the way of Cain..\n1 John 3:12\nnot as Cain who was of the wicked one and murdered his brother.\nAnd why did he murder him? Because his works were evil and his\nbrother’s righteous.\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"• Cain did not come in God’s prescribed way,\nhence his offering was rejected\n• He brought an offering to God based on his\nown terms (the way of Cain)\n• Man-created ways of worshiping God is\nconsidered evil and not righteous in the\nBible\n\nLesson 3\n\nProverbs 14:12\nThere is a way that seems right to a man, But its end is the way of\ndeath.\n12\n\nKey #1: We must approach God on His\nterms and not ours.\n\nB\n\nGOD’S MERCY AND CAIN’S RESPONSE\nGenesis 4:6-8\nSo the LORD said to Cain, “Why are you angry? And why has your\ncountenance fallen? 7 If you do well, will you not be accepted? And if\nyou do not do well, sin lies at the door. And its desire is for you, but\nyou should rule over it.”\n\nWhen God confronted Cain, He gave Cain an\nopportunity to recover. God’s response to Cain\ngives us an understanding of God’s character.\nKey #2: Before God passes judgment,\nHe will always extend mercy.\n\n6\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Question: How did God extend mercy to Cain in\nGenesis 4:6-8?\nLesson 3\n\nGod extended mercy to Cain by giving him an\nopportunity to change his offering.\n“If you do well, will you not be accepted?”\n\nHebrews 12:5-6 (ICB)\nYou have forgotten his encouraging words for his sons: “My son,\ndon’t think the Lord’s discipline of you is worth nothing. And don’t\nstop trying when the Lord corrects you. 6 The Lord corrects those he\nloves. And he punishes everyone he accepts as his child.”\n\nCain’s Response – The First Murder\nGenesis 4:8-9\nNow Cain talked with Abel his brother; and it came to pass, when\nthey were in the field, that Cain rose up against Abel his brother\nand killed him. 9 Then the LORD said to Cain, “Where is Abel your\nbrother?” He said, “I do not know. Am I my brother’s keeper?”\n\nQuestion: How did Cain respond to God’s correction?\nCain rejected God’s mercy and committed the first\nmurder\nCain chose not to repent but rather gave a sarcastic\nresponse to God\nRather than owning up, Cain chose to lie to God\nCain revealed a disrespectful and arrogant attitude\nbefore God\n\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"Judgment on Cain\nLesson 3\n\nGenesis 4:10-16\nAnd He said, “What have you done? The voice of your brother’s blood\ncries out to Me from the ground. 11 So now you are cursed from the\nearth, which has opened its mouth to receive your brother’s blood\nfrom your hand. 12 When you till the ground, it shall no longer yield\nits strength to you. A fugitive and a vagabond you shall be on the\nearth.” 13 And Cain said to the LORD, “My punishment is greater than\nI can bear! 14 Surely You have driven me out this day from the face of\nthe ground; I shall be hidden from Your face; I shall be a fugitive and\na vagabond on the earth, and it will happen that anyone who finds\nme will kill me.” 15 And the LORD said to him, “Therefore, whoever\nkills Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold.” And the LORD\nset a mark on Cain, lest anyone finding him should kill him. 16 Then\nCain went out from the presence of the LORD…\n\n• Cain and his works were cursed (v11-12)\n• Cain would end up a fugitive and vagabond\non the earth (v12)\n• Cain did not respond to his judgment with\nremorse but rather complaint (v13-14)\n• Cain received a mark to protect him from\nany person who would try to kill him (v15)\n• Cain went out of the presence of God (V16)\n• Instead of being the first link to the “Seed of\nthe Woman” (Genesis 3:15), he became the\nfirst link to the “Seed of the Serpent” who\nwould oppose God and His people.\nThe principles of God will never change. He will\nalways teach us the correct way while extending\nmercy, but if we reject mercy we will one day live\nwithout God’s presence forever, like Cain.\n\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"C\nLesson 3\n\nSETH AND ENOCH\nSeth\nBecause of Abel’s death and Cain’s departure,\nGod gave Adam and Eve another son to continue\nthe line that will bring forth the child of promise\n(“seed of the woman”).\nGenesis 4:25\nAnd Adam knew his wife again, and she bore a son and named him\nSeth, “For God has appointed another seed for me instead of Abel,\nwhom Cain killed.”\n\nSeth – “substitute”\nEnoch\nIn the genealogy of the seed of the woman,\nEnoch stands out because it was said that he did\nnot see death. He was the seventh descendant\nfrom Adam.\nGenesis 5:24\nAnd Enoch walked with God; and he was not, for God took him.\n\nThis is what the New Testament says about Enoch.\nHebrews 11:5\nBy faith Enoch was taken away so that he did not see death, “and\nwas not found, because God had taken him”; for before he was taken\nhe had this testimony, that he pleased God.\n\nEnoch was known to be righteous in the midst of\na wicked generation (Jude 14-16)\nEnoch is an example of what will happen to those\nwho please God and walk with Him in the future\n(see 1 Thessalonians 4:13-18).\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"D\nLesson 3\n\nNOAH\nRefer to Chart L3.2-3\nNoah, a descendant of Enoch, was also a righteous man\nin the midst of a wicked generation.\nJudgment\n\nGenesis 6:5-7\nThen the LORD saw that the wickedness of man was great in the\nearth, and that every intent of the thoughts of his heart was only\nevil continually. 6 And the LORD was sorry that He had made man on\nthe earth, and He was grieved in His heart. 7 So the LORD said, “I will\ndestroy man whom I have created from the face of the earth, both\nman and beast, creeping thing and birds of the air, for I am sorry that\nI have made them.”\n\nGod was going to send judgment upon the evil\nupon the earth, but Noah found grace in the eyes\nof God.\n\nGenesis 6:8-9\nBut Noah found grace in the eyes of the LORD. 9 This is the\ngenealogy of Noah. Noah was a just man, perfect in his generations.\nNoah walked with God.\n\nPlan of salvation\nGod told Noah His plans to destroy the earth\nand also a plan to be saved from the coming\ndestruction.\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"Genesis 6:13-16, 19-20\n\nLesson 3\n\nAnd God said to Noah, “The end of all flesh has come before Me,\nfor the earth is filled with violence through them; and behold, I will\ndestroy them with the earth. 14 “Make yourself an ark of gopherwood;\nmake rooms in the ark, and cover it inside and outside with pitch. 15\nAnd this is how you shall make it: The length of the ark shall be three\nhundred cubits, its width fifty cubits, and its height thirty cubits. 16 You\nshall make a window for the ark, and you shall finish it to a cubit from\nabove; and set the door of the ark in its side. You shall make it with\nlower, second, and third decks…19 And of every living thing of all flesh\nyou shall bring two of every sort into the ark, to keep them alive with\nyou; they shall be male and female. 20 Of the birds after their kind, of\nanimals after their kind, and of every creeping thing of the earth after\nits kind, two of every kind will come to you to keep them alive.\n\nNoah’s plan of salvation involves building an ark\naccording to God’s commandment. He was also\ntold to gather the animals into the ark. Every\ndetail of God’s instructions was crucial for them to\nbe saved.\nNoah’s Response\n\nGenesis 6:22\nThus Noah did; according to all that God commanded him, so he did.\nHebrews 11:7\nBy faith Noah, being divinely warned of things not yet seen, moved\nwith godly fear, prepared an ark for the saving of his household,\nby which he condemned the world and became heir of the\nrighteousness which is according to faith.\n\nResult\n\nGenesis 7:21-23\nAnd all flesh died that moved on the earth: birds and cattle and\nbeasts and every creeping thing that creeps on the earth, and every\nman. 22 All in whose nostrils was the breath of the spirit of life, all that\nwas on the dry land, died. 23 So He destroyed all living things which\nwere on the face of the ground: both man and cattle, creeping thing\nand bird of the air. They were destroyed from the earth. Only Noah\nand those who were with him in the ark remained alive.\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"2 Peter 2:5\nand did not spare the ancient world, but saved Noah, one of eight\npeople, a preacher of righteousness, bringing in the flood on the\nworld of the ungodly;\n\nLesson 3\n\n1 Peter 3:20\nwho formerly were disobedient, when once the Divine longsuffering\nwaited in the days of Noah, while the ark was being prepared, in\nwhich a few, that is, eight souls, were saved through water.\n\nE\n\nGRACE, FAITH AND OBEDIENCE\nThe story of Noah teaches us that God’s way of\nsalvation involves 3 important elements: Grace,\nFaith and Obedience.\nGrace\n• God’s favor\n• A gift\n• His favour towards us causes Him to initiate\nsomething to help us\n• No human effort can earn salvation or be\nmade right with God unless He initiates it\n• Grace is God’s part\n\nEphesians 2:8-9\nFor by grace you have been saved through faith, and that not\nof yourselves; it is the gift of God, 9 not of works, lest anyone\nshould boast.\n\nNote to Teacher: Grace does not eliminate our choice.\nGod has given us the freedom either to surrender\nto Him or reject Him, but we can contribute nothing\npositive to earn our own salvation.\n\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"Hebrews 12:15 (NLT)\n\nLesson 3\n\nLook after each other so that none of you fails to receive the\ngrace of God. Watch out that no poisonous root of bitterness\ngrows up to trouble you, corrupting many.\n\nFaith\n• When we believe the word of God in what it\ntells us to be true and instructs us regarding\nGod’s ways\n• The root word for “faith” in Greek is peithō,\nwhich means to be persuaded, to trust, to\nhave confidence in\n• Faith is our part (in response to God’s grace)\n\nHebrews 11:1\nNow faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of\nthings not seen.\n\nThe attitude of faith however is something that\ncannot be seen with the human eye. How then\ncan we tell if someone truly possesses faith?\nObedience\n• True faith isn’t merely mental assent, but it has a\ncorresponding action called obedience\n• Obedience is proof of our faith\n• Obedience is our part (in response to God’s grace)\n\nHebrews 11:7\nBy faith Noah…prepared an ark…\nJames 2:18 (NLT)\nNow someone may argue, “Some people have faith; others have good\ndeeds.” But I say, “How can you show me your faith if you don’t have\ngood deeds? I will show you my faith by my good deeds.”\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"(Note to Teacher: You can also refer to examples of\nfaith in Hebrews 11 and see how men of God will\ndemonstrate their faith by their obedience to God\n\nLesson 3\n\nQuestion: Can you identify how grace, faith and\nobedience comes into play in the story of Noah?\nGrace: God initiates a salvation plan for Noah\nFaith: Noah believed what God said will come to pass\nObedience: Noah built the ark for the saving of his household\n\nKey #3: We receive God’s gift of salvation by\nresponding in faith and obedience.\n\nF\n\nGOD ESTABLISHES A COVENANT\nAfter the waters subsided, Noah built an altar\nbefore God and sacrificed clean animals to\nHim. God then gave Noah and his family the\ncommandment He gave to Adam initially,\n\nGenesis 9:1\nSo God blessed Noah and his sons, and said to them: “Be fruitful and\nmultiply, and fill the earth.\n\nGod made a covenant with Noah and his family.\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"Genesis 9:12-17\n\nLesson 3\n\nAnd God said: “This is the sign of the covenant which I make between\nMe and you, and every living creature that is with you, for perpetual\ngenerations: 13 I set My rainbow in the cloud, and it shall be for the\nsign of the covenant between Me and the earth. 14 It shall be, when\nI bring a cloud over the earth, that the rainbow shall be seen in the\ncloud; 15 and I will remember My covenant which is between Me\nand you and every living creature of all flesh; the waters shall never\nagain become a flood to destroy all flesh. 16 The rainbow shall be in\nthe cloud, and I will look on it to remember the everlasting covenant\nbetween God and every living creature of all flesh that is on the earth.”\n17\nAnd God said to Noah, “This is the sign of the covenant which I have\nestablished between Me and all flesh that is on the earth.”\n\nDifference between a contract and a covenant\nContract\nObligation: “I have to”\nImpersonal: “Involves\nsomething I have to do”\nConditional: “If you do\nyour part, I’ll do mine”\nLeverage: “I look out for\nmy own best interest”\nSuspicion: “I want\nassurance that you will do\nyour part”\nCompromise: “I’ll meet\nyou halfway”\nTemporary: “Once all\nstipulations have been\nmet, the contract is over”\n\nCovenant\n\nOpportunity: “I want\nto”\nPersonal: “Involves all\nthat I am”\nUnconditional: “I’ll do\nmy part whether you\ndo yours or not”\nLoyalty: “I am looking\nout for your best\ninterest”\nTrust: “I will certainly\ndo my part”\nSacrifice: “I’ll give\n100%”\nPermanent: “I will\ncontinue to do this as\nlong as I draw breath”\n\nCovenants best describe God’s relationship toward us.\nCovenants always include a token or “sign” between\nGod and man. These signs seal the agreement and\ncovenant.\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"Question: What is the physical sign of God’s covenant with Noah?\nLesson 3\n\nThe rainbow\n\nKey #4: God saved Man to establish a\ncovenant with them.\n\nG\n\nCOMPARING NOAH’S DAY AND OUR DAY\nDays of Noah\n\nComing of Christ\n\nGreat wickedness\n(Genesis 6:5)\n\nEvil men and seducers\n(2 Timothy 3:13)\n\nEarth full of violence\n(Genesis 6:11)\nNoah, a preacher of\nrighteousness (2 Peter\n2:5)\nUngodly punished by\nflood (2 Peter 3:5-7)\n\nPerilous times (2\nTimothy 3:1)\nGospel will be\npreached in all the\nworld (Matthew 24:14)\nUngodly punished by\nfire (2 Peter 3:5-7)\n\n2 Peter 3:3-10\nknowing this first: that scoffers will come in the last days, walking according to\ntheir own lusts, 4 and saying, “Where is the promise of His coming? For since\nthe fathers fell asleep, all things continue as they were from the beginning\nof creation.” 5 For this they willfully forget: that by the word of God the\nheavens were of old, and the earth standing out of water and in the water,\n6\nby which the world that then existed perished, being flooded with water. 7\nBut the heavens and the earth which are now preserved by the same word,\nare reserved for fire until the day of judgment and perdition of ungodly men.\n8\nBut, beloved, do not forget this one thing, that with the Lord one day is as\na thousand years, and a thousand years as one day. 9 The Lord is not slack\nconcerning His promise, as some count slackness, but is longsuffering toward\nus, not willing that any should perish but that all should come to repentance. 10\nBut the day of the Lord will come as a thief in the night, in which the heavens\nwill pass away with a great noise, and the elements will melt with fervent heat;\nboth the earth and the works that are in it will be burned up.\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Matthew 24:37-39\n\nLesson 3\n\nBut as the days of Noah were, so also will the coming of the Son of Man be. 38\nFor as in the days before the flood, they were eating and drinking, marrying\nand giving in marriage, until the day that Noah entered the ark, 39 and did not\nknow until the flood came and took them all away, so also will the coming of\nthe Son of Man be.\n\nThe account of Noah is in the Bible to give us a warning\nthat God will do exactly what He said He will do, even if\npeople scoff and live in sin. There is coming judgment\nto our world today and we need to prepare ourselves\nlike Noah, by responding in faith and obedience to\nGod’s plan of salvation.\nKey #5: We need to prepare ourselves for\ncoming judgment.\n\n17\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 3\n\nRefer to Chart L3.3-3\n1. We must approach God on His terms and\nnot ours.\n2. Before God passes judgment, He will always\nextend mercy.\n3. We receive God’s gift of salvation by\nresponding in faith and obedience.\n4. God saved Man to establish a covenant\nwith them.\n5. We need to prepare ourselves for coming\njudgment.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"Charts\nLesson 3\n\n19\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"Charts\nLesson 3\n\n20\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"Lesson 3\n\nModular Section\n1. Global flood traditions\n2. Scientific study endorses Seaworthiness of\nArk\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 3\n\nI. Global Flood Traditions\nDr. Duane Gish, in Dinosaurs by Design,\nsays there are more than 270 stories from\ndifferent cultures around the world about\na devastating flood. This chart shows the\nsimilarities that several myths have with the\nGenesis account of Noah’s Flood. Although\nthere are varying degrees of accuracy, these\nlegends and stories all contain similarities to\naspects of the same historical event—Noah’s\nFlood.\n\nChart adapted from B.C. Nelson, The Deluge Story in Stone, Appendix 11, Flood Traditions, Figure\n38, Augsburg, Minneapolis, 1931\n\n22\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 3\n\nII. Scientific Study Endorses Seaworthiness of\nArk\nThe proportions of the Ark were found to\ncarefully balance the conflicting demands of\nstability, comfort, and strength.\n\nNoah’s Ark was the focus of a major 1993\nscientific study headed by Dr. Seon Hong at\nthe world-class ship research center KRISO,\nbased in Daejeon, South Korea. Dr. Hong’s\nteam compared twelve hulls of different\nproportions to discover which design was\nmost practical. No hull shape was found\nto significantly outperform the 4,300-yearold biblical design. In fact, the Ark’s careful\nbalance is easily lost if the proportions\nare modified, rendering the vessel either\nunstable, prone to fracture, or dangerously\nuncomfortable.\nThe research team found that the proportions\nof Noah’s Ark carefully balanced the\nconflicting demands of stability (resistance\nto capsizing), comfort (“seakeeping”), and\nstrength. In fact, the Ark has the same\nproportions as a modern cargo ship.\nThe study also confirmed that the Ark could\nhandle waves as high as 100 ft (30 m).\nSource: worldwideflood.com/ark/hull_form/hull_optimization.htm\n\n23\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"4":{"lesson":4,"sourceType":"Student Notes","pageCount":26,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 4\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience\n\nAge of Human Government\n\nAge of Promise\n\nRefer to Chart L4.1-3\n\nCast (Characters)\nGod, Shem, Abraham, Sarah, Isaac, Jacob, Joseph\n\nLesson Summary\nAfter the flood, humanity began to populate the earth\nonly to end up rebelling against God again by building\nthe tower of Babel. It was in the midst of this climate\nof ungodliness that Abraham was called by God to\nfollow Him. In this lesson, we will see how Abraham\nand his descendants Isaac, Jacob and Joseph grew and\ndemonstrated their faith in God. This lesson will also\nillustrate the struggle between God’s rule and Man’s rule.\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 4\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Babel/Babylon\n\n3\n\nB. Abraham\n•\n\nAbram’s Background\n\n•\n\nGod’s Calling\n\n•\n\nAbram’s Flaws\n\n•\n\nGod’s Promise\n\n•\n\nAbram’s Impatience\n\n•\n\nGod’s Covenant\n\n•\n\nJudgment on Sodom and Gomorrah\n\n•\n\nIsaac’s Birth and Abraham’s Test\n\n5\n\nC. Jacob/Israel\n\n8\n\nD. Joseph\n\n9\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"A\nLesson 4\n\nBABEL\nNoah had three sons: Shem, Japheth and Ham.\nShem and Japheth were blessed by Noah, but\nHam was not because he exposed his father’s\nnakedness (see Genesis 9:20-27). Ham’s wife gave\nbirth to Cush, who was the father of Nimrod, the\nfounder of Babel (see Genesis 10:8-10).\n\nGenesis 11:1-4\nNow the whole earth had one language and one speech. 2 And it\ncame to pass, as they journeyed from the east, that they found a\nplain in the land of Shinar, and they dwelt there. 3 Then they said to\none another, “Come, let us make bricks and bake them thoroughly.”\nThey had brick for stone, and they had asphalt for mortar. 4 And they\nsaid, “Come, let us build ourselves a city, and a tower whose top is in\nthe heavens; let us make a name for ourselves, lest we be scattered\nabroad over the face of the whole earth.”\n\nThe tower of Babel became humanity’s symbol\nof ruling their lives without God. This was also an\nact of rebellion against God because He had told\nthem to “be fruitful, multiply, and replenish the\nearth” (Genesis 9:1).\nGod broke the people apart by confounding their\nlanguages, leading to their scatter.\n\nGenesis 11:7-9\nCome, let Us go down and there confuse their language, that they\nmay not understand one another’s speech.” 8 So the Lord scattered\nthem abroad from there over the face of all the earth, and they\nceased building the city. 9 Therefore its name is called Babel, because\nthere the Lord confused the language of all the earth; and from there\nthe Lord scattered them abroad over the face of all the earth.\n\n3\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"B\nLesson 4\n\nAbram\nThrough Noah’s son Shem, in the ninth generation,\nGod chose a man named Abram to be in the\nlineage of the “righteous seed”. God’s plan was\nto call Abram and make a great nation of people\nfrom him. Through Abram and his descendants,\nGod revealed Himself to the world and provided\nan example of how people who are in a covenant\nrelationship with God would be blessed.\nAbram’s Background\n• Abram came from Ur of the Chaldees\n(Genesis 11:31)\n• Abram’s father was Terah whose family\nserved other gods (Joshua 24:2)\n• Abram’s wife is Sarai while his nephew\nwas Lot\nGod’s Calling\n\nGenesis 12:1-3\nNow the LORD had said to Abram: “Get out of your country, From\nyour family And from your father’s house, To a land that I will show\nyou. 2 I will make you a great nation; I will bless you And make your\nname great; And you shall be a blessing. 3 I will bless those who bless\nyou, And I will curse him who curses you; And in you all the families\nof the earth shall be blessed.”\nGenesis 12:4-5\nSo Abram departed as the LORD had spoken to him, and Lot went\nwith him. And Abram was seventy-five years old when he departed\nfrom Haran. 5 Then Abram took Sarai his wife and Lot his brother’s\nson, and all their possessions that they had gathered, and the people\nwhom they had acquired in Haran, and they departed to go to the\nland of Canaan. So they came to the land of Canaan.\nHebrews 11:8-10\nBy faith Abraham obeyed when he was called to go out to the\nplace which he would receive as an inheritance. And he went out,\nnot knowing where he was going. 9 By faith he dwelt in the land of\npromise as in a foreign country, dwelling in tents with Isaac and\nJacob, the heirs with him of the same promise; 10 for he waited for\nthe city which has foundations, whose builder and maker is God.\n\n4\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"Lesson 4\n\nKey #1: God is still calling individuals\nto\nand\nHim\n\nAbram’s Flaws\nAbram did not begin his journey of faith\nperfect. He struggled initially just like every\none of us does.\n\nGenesis 12:11-13\nAnd it came to pass, when he was close to entering Egypt, that he said\nto Sarai his wife, “Indeed I know that you are a woman of beautiful\ncountenance. 12 Therefore it will happen, when the Egyptians see you,\nthat they will say, ‘This is his wife’; and they will kill me, but they will let\nyou live. 13 Please say you are my sister, that it may be well with me for\nyour sake, and that I may live because of you.”\n\nIn Egypt, Abram lied to protect himself instead of\ntrusting in God’s protection while he was in the\nface of danger (he did it again in Genesis 20).\n\nGod’s Promise\nNevertheless, God gave Abram a promise that\nHe would make a great nation from Him with\nmany descendants.\n\nGenesis 15:5\nThen He brought him outside and said, “Look now toward heaven, and\ncount the stars if you are able to number them.” And He said to him,\n“So shall your descendants be.”\n\n5\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"Abram’s Impatience\nLesson 4\n\nAbram and Sarah did not have any children\nand decided to take matters into their own\nhands. Instead of trusting God’s promise,\nSarah gave Hagar, her maid, to Abram so that\nshe could bear a child.\n\nGenesis 16:1-4\nNow Sarai, Abram’s wife, had borne him no children. And she had\nan Egyptian maidservant whose name was Hagar. 2 So Sarai said to\nAbram, “See now, the Lord has restrained me from bearing children.\nPlease, go in to my maid; perhaps I shall obtain children by her.” And\nAbram heeded the voice of Sarai. 3 Then Sarai, Abram’s wife, took\nHagar her maid, the Egyptian, and gave her to her husband Abram to\nbe his wife, after Abram had dwelt ten years in the land of Canaan. 4\nSo he went in to Hagar, and she conceived. And when she saw that she\nhad conceived, her mistress became despised in her eyes.\nGenesis 16:15-16\nSo Hagar bore Abram a son; and Abram named his son, whom Hagar\nbore, Ishmael. 16 Abram was eighty-six years old when Hagar bore\nIshmael to Abram.\n\nThe result of Abram and Sarai’s impatience\nwas the birth of Ishmael. Ishmael’s\ndescendants later on became the oppressors\nof Abram’s promised descendants.\n\nGod’s Covenant\nAlthough Abram made a mistake, God was\nfaithful and continued to work in Abram’s life.\nGod told Abram that He wanted to establish a\ncovenant with him and his descendants. It was\nhere that God changed his name from Abram to\nAbraham which means “father of a multitude”.\n\n6\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Genesis 17:4-5\n\nLesson 4\n\n“As for Me, behold, My covenant is with you, and you shall be a father\nof many nations. 5 No longer shall your name be called Abram, but\nyour name shall be Abraham; for I have made you a father of many\nnations.\nGenesis 17:7-8\nAnd I will establish My covenant between Me and you and your\ndescendants after you in their generations, for an everlasting\ncovenant, to be God to you and your descendants after you. 8 Also I\ngive to you and your descendants after you the land in which you are\na stranger, all the land of Canaan, as an everlasting possession; and I\nwill be their God.”\n\nHere are the conditions of the covenant:\n\nGenesis 17:10-14\nThis is My covenant which you shall keep, between Me and you\nand your descendants after you: Every male child among you shall\nbe circumcised; 11 and you shall be circumcised in the flesh of your\nforeskins, and it shall be a sign of the covenant between Me and you.\n12\nHe who is eight days old among you shall be circumcised, every male\nchild in your generations, he who is born in your house or bought with\nmoney from any foreigner who is not your descendant. 13 He who is\nborn in your house and he who is bought with your money must be\ncircumcised, and My covenant shall be in your flesh for an everlasting\ncovenant. 14 And the uncircumcised male child, who is not circumcised\nin the flesh of his foreskin, that person shall be cut off from his people;\nhe has broken My covenant.”\n\nKey #2:\nis Man’s\npart in accepting God’s covenant.\n\nWhile physical circumcision is the sign of the\ncovenant for Abraham, God has another sign of\ncovenant for us today (more in Lesson 8 and 9).\n\n7\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"Judgment on Sodom and Gomorrah\nLesson 4\n\nLike Noah, God appeared to Abraham to warn\nhim of the impending judgment of the city of\nSodom and Gomorrah. Although Abraham was\nnot living in those cities, his nephew Lot and\nfamily were living there.\n\nGenesis 18:20-21\nAnd the LORD said, “Because the outcry against Sodom and Gomorrah\nis great, and because their sin is very grave, 21 I will go down now and\nsee whether they have done altogether according to the outcry against\nit that has come to Me; and if not, I will know.”\n\nAbraham pleaded with God by negotiating a\ncondition to spare Sodom and Gomorrah.\n\nGenesis 18:32-33\nThen he said, “Let not the Lord be angry, and I will speak but once\nmore: Suppose ten should be found there?” And He said, “I will not\ndestroy it for the sake of ten.” 33 So the LORD went His way as soon\nas He had finished speaking with Abraham; and Abraham returned\nto his place.\n\nHere is a summarized sequence of events that happened\nin Sodom in Genesis 19 hereafter:\n• Two angels arrived into the city and were received by Lot\ninto His home (v1-3)\n• All the men of the city demanded Lot to hand over the\nangels to rape them (v4-5)\n• Lot offered his daughters instead as the men pressed to\nenter his home (v8-9)\n• The angels smite the men with blindness (v11)\n• The angels warned Lot to depart from Sodom (v12-15)\n• The angels took Lot and his family out and warned them\nnot to look back (v16)\n• Brimstone and fire rained upon Sodom and Gomorrah as\nthe entire cities were destroyed (v24-25)\n• Lot’s wife looked back and she became a pillar of salt (v26)\n\n8\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"Jude 1:7 (NLT)\n\nLesson 4\n\nAnd don’t forget Sodom and Gomorrah and their neighboring\ntowns, which were filled with immorality and every kind of sexual\nperversion. Those cities were destroyed by fire and serve as a\nwarning of the eternal fire of God’s judgment.\nLuke 17:28-30, 32\nLikewise as it was also in the days of Lot: They ate, they drank, they\nbought, they sold, they planted, they built; 29 but on the day that Lot\nwent out of Sodom it rained fire and brimstone from heaven and\ndestroyed them all. 30 Even so will it be in the day when the Son of\nMan is revealed…32 Remember Lot’s wife.\n\nSodom and Gomorrah were so wicked that God couldn’t\neven find ten righteous men to spare in the city.\n\nIsaac’s Birth and Abraham’s Test\nIsaac was born when Abraham was 100 and\nSarah was 90 years old. God showed Himself\nonce again to be faithful.\n\nHebrews 11:11\nBy faith Sarah herself also received strength to conceive seed, and\nshe bore a child when she was past the age, because she judged Him\nfaithful who had promised.\nGenesis 21:5\nNow Abraham was one hundred years old when his son Isaac was\nborn to him.\n\nKey #3: God\n\n9\n\nfulfills His promises.\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"After many years, God told Abraham to sacrifice\nIsaac (Genesis 22:1-2). This was Abraham’s test of\nhis love, faith and trust in God.\nLesson 4\nGenesis 22:3-8\nSo Abraham rose early in the morning and saddled his donkey, and\ntook two of his young men with him, and Isaac his son; and he split\nthe wood for the burnt offering, and arose and went to the place of\nwhich God had told him. 4 Then on the third day Abraham lifted his\neyes and saw the place afar off. 5 And Abraham said to his young\nmen, “Stay here with the donkey; the lad and I will go yonder and\nworship, and we will come back to you.” 6 So Abraham took the wood\nof the burnt offering and laid it on Isaac his son; and he took the fire\nin his hand, and a knife, and the two of them went together. 7 But\nIsaac spoke to Abraham his father and said, “My father!” And he said,\n“Here I am, my son.” Then he said, “Look, the fire and the wood, but\nwhere is the lamb for a burnt offering?” 8 And Abraham said, “My son,\nGod will provide for Himself the lamb for a burnt offering.” So the two\nof them went together.\n\nAbraham demonstrated his faith by declaring\nIsaac’s return from the sacrifice and stated that\nGod will provide for Himself a lamb offering.\n\nHebrews 11:17-19\nBy faith Abraham, when he was tested, offered up Isaac, and he who\nhad received the promises offered up his only begotten son, 18 of\nwhom it was said, “In Isaac your seed shall be called,” 19 concluding\nthat God was able to raise him up, even from the dead, from which\nhe also received him in a figurative sense.\n\n10\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"Genesis 22:9-14\n\nLesson 4\n\nThen they came to the place of which God had told him. And\nAbraham built an altar there and placed the wood in order; and he\nbound Isaac his son and laid him on the altar, upon the wood. 10 And\nAbraham stretched out his hand and took the knife to slay his son.\n11\nBut the Angel of the LORD called to him from heaven and said,\n“Abraham, Abraham!” So he said, “Here I am.” 12 And He said, “Do\nnot lay your hand on the lad, or do anything to him; for now I know\nthat you fear God, since you have not withheld your son, your only\nson, from Me.” 13 Then Abraham lifted his eyes and looked, and there\nbehind him was a ram caught in a thicket by its horns. So Abraham\nwent and took the ram, and offered it up for a burnt offering instead\nof his son. 14 And Abraham called the name of the place, The-LORDWill-Provide; as it is said to this day, “In the Mount of The LORD it\nshall be provided.”\nGenesis 22:15-18\nThen the Angel of the LORD called to Abraham a second time out of\nheaven, 16 and said: “By Myself I have sworn, says the LORD, because\nyou have done this thing, and have not withheld your son, your only\nson-- 17 blessing I will bless you, and multiplying I will multiply your\ndescendants as the stars of the heaven and as the sand which is on\nthe seashore; and your descendants shall possess the gate of their\nenemies. 18 In your seed all the nations of the earth shall be blessed,\nbecause you have obeyed My voice.”\n\nKey #4: God\nwe choose to\n\n11\n\nHimself to us when\nourselves to Him.\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"C\n\nJACOB/ISRAEL\n\nLesson 4\n\nRefer to Chart L4.2-3\nWe see the same transformation of Abraham’s\nfaith in the lives of his descendants. His son, Isaac,\nhad two sons, Jacob and Esau.\n\nGenesis 25:21-34\nNow Isaac pleaded with the LORD for his wife, because she was\nbarren; and the LORD granted his plea, and Rebekah his wife\nconceived. 22 But the children struggled together within her; and she\nsaid, “If all is well, why am I like this?” So she went to inquire of the\nLORD. 23 And the LORD said to her: “Two nations are in your womb,\nTwo peoples shall be separated from your body; One people shall\nbe stronger than the other, And the older shall serve the younger.”\n24\nSo when her days were fulfilled for her to give birth, indeed there\nwere twins in her womb. 25 And the first came out red. He was like a\nhairy garment all over; so they called his name Esau. 26 Afterward his\nbrother came out, and his hand took hold of Esau’s heel; so his name\nwas called Jacob. Isaac was sixty years old when she bore them. 27\nSo the boys grew. And Esau was a skillful hunter, a man of the field;\nbut Jacob was a mild man, dwelling in tents. 28 And Isaac loved Esau\nbecause he ate of his game, but Rebekah loved Jacob. 29 Now Jacob\ncooked a stew; and Esau came in from the field, and he was weary.\n30\nAnd Esau said to Jacob, “Please feed me with that same red stew,\nfor I am weary.” Therefore his name was called Edom. 31 But Jacob\nsaid, “Sell me your birthright as of this day.” 32 And Esau said, “Look,\nI am about to die; so what is this birthright to me?” 33 Then Jacob\nsaid, “Swear to me as of this day.” So he swore to him, and sold his\nbirthright to Jacob. 34 And Jacob gave Esau bread and stew of lentils;\nthen he ate and drank, arose, and went his way. Thus Esau despised\nhis birthright.\n\nEsau\n• Esau sold his birthright to Jacob for bread and a\nstew of lentils\n• A birthright entitles the firstborn of both a\ndouble portion of his father’s inheritance and\nthe responsibility of being the spiritual leader of\nthe family (Deuteronomy 21:15-17, Exodus 13:2,\nGenesis 27:29)\n• Esau represented someone who forsook\nspiritual things for personal desires\n\n12\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"Jacob\nLesson 4\n\n• Jacob means “supplanter”\n• His life demonstrated a person who obtained\nhis goals through cunning and deception\n• He desired the right things, but did it the wrong\nway\n• Jacob and Rebekah deceived Isaac in order to\nreceive a blessing (Genesis 27:1-29)\n• Jacob was forced to run from Esau to Laban, his\nuncle (Genesis 27:41-28:5)\n• Jacob had an encounter with God at Bethel\n(Genesis 28:10-22)\n• Jacob was tricked into marrying Laban’s older\ndaughter Leah instead of Rachel after working\nfor him for 7 years.\n• Jacob worked another 7 years and ended up\nmarrying Rachel (Genesis 29:20-30)\n• After being deceived by Laban, Jacob and Rachel\ntricked Laban as they fled his home\n• As he was escaping, Jacob hears news that Esau\nwas coming for him with 400 men. (Genesis\n32:1-8)\n• All this while, Jacob had never turned to God for\nanything in his life. This incident was the turning\npoint in Jacob’s life\n\nGenesis 32:9-12 (NLT)\nThen Jacob prayed, “O God of my grandfather Abraham, and God\nof my father, Isaac—O LORD, you told me, ‘Return to your own land\nand to your relatives.’ And you promised me, ‘I will treat you kindly.’\n10 I am not worthy of all the unfailing love and faithfulness you have\nshown to me, your servant. When I left home and crossed the Jordan\nRiver, I owned nothing except a walking stick. Now my household fills\ntwo large camps! 11 O LORD, please rescue me from the hand of my\nbrother, Esau. I am afraid that he is coming to attack me, along with\nmy wives and children. 12 But you promised me, ‘I will surely treat\nyou kindly, and I will multiply your descendants until they become as\nnumerous as the sands along the seashore—too many to count.’”\n\n• Jacob then had a personal encounter with God\nwhere he wrestled with a manifestation of God\nand ended up walking with a limp. God changed\nhis name from Jacob to Israel.\n\n13\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"Genesis 32:27-28\nSo He said to him, “What is your name?” He said, “Jacob.” 28 And He\nsaid, “Your name shall no longer be called Jacob, but Israel; for you\nhave struggled with God and with men, and have prevailed.”\n\nLesson 4\n\nJacob’s new walk with a limp was evidence that\nJacob was no longer able to rely on his own natural\nstrength, but needed to lean on God.\n\nKey #5: God wants us to rely on His\nrather than our own\n\nD\n\nJOSEPH\nJacob/Israel had 12 sons born from 2 wives and 2\nmaidservants.\n\n14\n\nBirth\nOrder\n\nName of Son\n\nBirth\nMother\n\nKey Verses\n\n1\n\nReuben\n\nLeah\n\nGen. 29:32; 35:22; 37:21-22, 29;\n49:3-4\n\n2\n\nSimeon\n\nLeah\n\nGen. 29:33; 34:25-31; 49:5-7\n\n3\n\nLevi\n\nLeah\n\nGen. 29:34; 34:25-31; 49:5-7\n\n4\n\nJudah\n\nLeah\n\nGen. 29: 35; 37:26; 38:1-30; 49:8-12\n\n5\n\nDan\n\nBilhah\n\nGen. 30:5-6; 49:16-18\n\n6\n\nNaphtali\n\nBilhah\n\nGen. 30:7-8; 49:20\n\n7\n\nGad\n\nZilpah\n\nGen. 30:10-11; 49:19\n\n8\n\nAsher\n\nZilpah\n\nGen. 30:12-13; 49:20\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"Lesson 4\n\n9\n\nIssachar\n\nLeah\n\nGen. 30:17-18; 49:14-15\n\n10\n\nZebulun\n\nLeah\n\nGen. 30:19-20; 49:13\n\n11\n\nJoseph\n\nRachael\n\nGen. 30:22-24; 49:22-26\n\n12\n\nBenjamin\n\nRachael\n\nGen. 35:16-18; 49:27\n\nJoseph was favored amongst his brothers. God gave\nJoseph dreams of greatness.\n\nGenesis 37:5-11\nNow Joseph had a dream, and he told it to his brothers; and they\nhated him even more. 6 So he said to them, “Please hear this dream\nwhich I have dreamed: 7 There we were, binding sheaves in the field.\nThen behold, my sheaf arose and also stood upright; and indeed your\nsheaves stood all around and bowed down to my sheaf.” 8 And his\nbrothers said to him, “Shall you indeed reign over us? Or shall you\nindeed have dominion over us?” So they hated him even more for\nhis dreams and for his words. 9 Then he dreamed still another dream\nand told it to his brothers, and said, “Look, I have dreamed another\ndream. And this time, the sun, the moon, and the eleven stars bowed\ndown to me.” 10 So he told it to his father and his brothers; and his\nfather rebuked him and said to him, “What is this dream that you\nhave dreamed? Shall your mother and I and your brothers indeed\ncome to bow down to the earth before you?” 11 And his brothers\nenvied him, but his father kept the matter in mind.\n\nPIT\nThe dreams and Jacob’s favoritism created jealousy in\nhis brothers and conflict for the family. The brothers\nplotted to murder Jospeph, but instead of killing him,\nthey sold him as a slave.\n\n15\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"Genesis 37:3-4\n\nLesson 4\n\nNow Israel loved Joseph more than all his children, because he was\nthe son of his old age. Also he made him a tunic of many colors. 4 But\nwhen his brothers saw that their father loved him more than all his\nbrothers, they hated him and could not speak peaceably to him.\nGenesis 37:28\nThen Midianite traders passed by; so the brothers pulled Joseph up\nand lifted him out of the pit, and sold him to the Ishmaelites for\ntwenty shekels of silver. And they took Joseph to Egypt.\n\nPOTIPHAR\n\nGenesis 39:1\nNow Joseph had been taken down to Egypt. And Potiphar, an officer\nof Pharaoh, captain of the guard, an Egyptian, bought him from the\nIshmaelites who had taken him down there.\n\nWhile working for Potiphar, Joseph gained favour\nwith Potiphar and the attention of his wife. She tried\nseducing him but Joseph resisted. He was then falsely\naccused by Potiphar’s wife and thrown in prison.\n\nPRISON\n\nGenesis 39:20\nThen Joseph’s master took him and put him into the prison, a place\nwhere the king’s prisoners were confined. And he was there in the\nprison.\n\n16\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Lesson 4\n\nWhile in prison, Joseph gained favour with the jailor\nand became the leader of the prison. He interpreted\nthe dreams of two prisoners (a baker and a butler).\nUpon being reinstated, the butler forgot about\nJoseph for two years. Later, Pharaoh had a dream\nthat needed interpretation. It was then that the\nbutler remembered Joseph and recommended him\nto Pharaoh. Joseph interpreted the dream and was\npromoted to the second ruler of Egypt after Pharaoh.\nHe was tasked to administer the gathering of food to\nprepare for the upcoming famine.\n\nPALACE\n\nGenesis 41:39-40\nThen Pharaoh said to Joseph, “Inasmuch as God has shown you all\nthis, there is no one as discerning and wise as you. 40 You shall be over\nmy house, and all my people shall be ruled according to your word;\nonly in regard to the throne will I be greater than you.”\n\nAfter seven years of harvest, the world experienced a\nseven-year famine which forced Joseph’s family to go\nto Egypt to buy food. It was then that Joseph’s dream\nwas fulfilled as they bowed to him without knowing\nwho he was.\nBefore Joseph revealed himself to his family, he\ntested his brothers regarding their treatment of their\nyoungest brother Benjamin. He then saw that they\nhad changed from the last experience he had with\nthem.\n\nISRAEL MOVED INTO EGYPT\nGenesis 47:11\nAnd Joseph situated his father and his brothers, and gave them a\npossession in the land of Egypt, in the best of the land, in the land of\nRameses, as Pharaoh had commanded.\n\n17\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"After the death of Jacob, Joseph could have taken\nrevenge on his brothers, but chose to forgive them.\n\nLesson 4\nGenesis 50:19-20\nJoseph said to them, “Do not be afraid, for am I in the place of God? 20\nBut as for you, you meant evil against me; but God meant it for good,\nin order to bring it about as it is this day, to save many people alive.\n\nHad Joseph killed his brothers, he would have\nmurdered the “seed” whom the promised future\nMessiah would come from.\nJoseph also believed that Israel and his descendants\nwould one day leave Egypt to go to the land God\npromised Abraham, Isaac and Jacob.\n\nGenesis 50:24-25\nAnd Joseph said to his brethren, “I am dying; but God will surely visit\nyou, and bring you out of this land to the land of which He swore to\nAbraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.” 25 Then Joseph took an oath from the\nchildren of Israel, saying, “God will surely visit you, and you shall carry\nup my bones from here.”\nHebrews 11:22 (ESV)\nBy faith Joseph, at the end of his life, made mention of the exodus of\nthe Israelites and gave directions concerning his bones.\n\nAfter Joseph’s death, Israel continued to multiply and\nprosper in the land of Egypt until a new Pharaoh arose\nand knew not Joseph (Exodus 1:8).\n\n18\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 4\n\nRefer to Chart L4.3-3\n1. God is still calling individuals to trust and\nfollow Him.\n2. Obedience is Man’s part in accepting God’s\ncovenant.\n3. God always fulfills His promises.\n4. God reveals Himself to us when we choose\nto surrender ourselves to Him.\n5. God wants us to rely on His strength rather\nthan our own.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n19\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"Charts\nLesson 4\n\n20\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"Charts\nLesson 4\n\n21\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"Lesson 4\n\nModular Section\n1. Evolutionary Language Search Lands at\nBabel\n2. Was the Dispersion at Babel a Real Event?\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 4\n\nI. Evolutionary Language Search Lands at Babel\n\nApes around the world can understand\neach other, so why do intellectually superior\nhumans have around 7,000 distinct\nlanguages? queries evolutionary biologist\nMark Pagel. Pagel, a professor at the\nUniversity of Reading in the UK, heads a team\nsearching for an evolutionary explanation for\nour many languages. “Why,” he asks, “would\nhumans evolve a system of communication\nthat prevents them with communicating with\nother members of the same species?\nSo, in a New Scientist editorial called “War\nof words: The language paradox explained,”\nPagel writes:\nYou could take a gorilla or chimpanzee from its troop and plop it\ndown anywhere these species are found, and it would know how\nto communicate. You could repeat this with donkeys, crickets or\ngoldfish and get the same outcome.\nThis highlights an intriguing paradox at the heart of human\ncommunication. If language evolved to allow us to exchange\ninformation, how come most people cannot understand what most\nother people are saying?\n\nIn other words, if humans evolved language in\norder to communicate with each other, then\nwhy did language continue to evolve in a way\nthat interfered with such communication?\nPagel finds the biblical explanation best. Of\ncourse, he does not consider the Bible to be\na reliable historical source and therefore tries\nto apply its principles to his model of social\nevolution.\nby Dr. Elizabeth Mitchell on January 5, 2013\nSource: Excerpts from https://answersingenesis.org/tower-of-babel/\nevolutionary-language-search-lands-at-babel/\n\n23\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":24,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 4\n\nII. Was the Dispersion at Babel a Real Event?\nZiggurats throughout the World\nThe Tower of Babel has traditionally been\ndepicted as a type of ziggurat, although the\nBible doesn’t give specific dimensions. The\nHebrew word for tower used in Genesis 11,\nreferring to the Tower of Babel, is migdal: a\ntower; by analogy, a rostrum; figuratively, a\n(pyramidal) bed of flowers.\nInterestingly, this word means tower but\nfiguratively reflects a flowerbed that yields a\npyramidal shape. This gives a little support\nto the idea that the Tower of Babel may have\nbeen pyramidal or ziggurat shaped. In what\nis now Iraq, Robert Koldewey excavated a\nstructure some think to be the foundation\nof the original Tower of Babel. It underlays a\nlater ziggurat that was thought to be built by\nHammurabi in the 19th century B.C.7\n\u0007When people were scattered from the Tower\nof Babel in the time of Peleg, they likely took\nthis building concept with them to places all\nover the world. It makes sense that many of\nthe families that were scattered from Babel\ntook varying ideas of the tower to their new\nlands and began building projects of their\nown.\nZiggurats, pyramids, mounds, and the\nlike have been found in many parts of the\nworld—from Mesopotamia to Egypt to South\nAmerica. The ancient Chinese built pyramids\nand the Mississippian culture built mounds.\nPyramids are classed slightly differently from\nziggurats, as are mounds, but the similarities\nare striking.\nby Bodie Hodge on August 19, 2010\n\n24\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":25,"text":"25\n\nMODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 4\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":26,"text":"26\n\nMODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 4\n\nCharts\n\nStudent’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"5":{"lesson":5,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":23,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 5\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will identify Man’s need for a\nDeliverer to save us from the bondage of sin\n\n•\n\nThe student will recognize that the shedding\nand application of innocent blood is necessary\nfor salvation\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will relate their current condition\nto the story of the Exodus\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience\n\nAge of Human Government\n\nAge of Promise\n\nAge of Law\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 5\n\nCast (Characters)\nPharaoh, Moses, Israelites\n\nLesson Summary\nOur last lesson ended with Joseph being reunited with his\nfamily and his family moving to Egypt. It was great while\nJoseph and the Pharaoh that knew him were living. However,\nafter they died things changed drastically for the children of\nIsrael. Remember that God had given a promise to Abraham!\nEgypt was not the Promised Land for the Israelites. Exodus\ntells the story of how God raised up a deliverer to save His\npeople from bondage. It is a testimony of God keeping His\npromises and moves us one step further along in the story of\nGod’s plan of salvation for mankind.\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"Lesson 5\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Israel in Bondage\n\n4\n\nB. Moses – God’s chosen deliverer\n\n5\n\nC. Judgement on Egypt\n\n10\n\nD. Passover: Israel’s Plan of Salvation in Egypt\n\n11\n\nE. Exodus\n\n13\n\nF. Birth of the Nation of Israel\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"A\nLesson 5\n\nISRAEL IN BONDAGE\nAs prophesied by God to Abraham, Israel was\nforced into slavery in Egypt by a new Pharaoh.\n\nExodus 1:8\nNow there arose a new king over Egypt, who did not know Joseph.\nGenesis 15:13 NKJV\n“Then He said to Abram: “Know certainly that your descendants will be\nstrangers in a land that is not theirs, and will serve them, and they will\nafflict them four hundred years.”\nExodus 1:10-14\ncome, let us deal shrewdly with them, lest they multiply, and it happen,\nin the event of war, that they also join our enemies and fight against\nus, and so go up out of the land.” 11 Therefore they set taskmasters\nover them to afflict them with their burdens. And they built for\nPharaoh supply cities, Pithom and Raamses. 12 But the more they\nafflicted them, the more they multiplied and grew. And they were in\ndread of the children of Israel. 13 So the Egyptians made the children\nof Israel serve with rigor. 14 And they made their lives bitter with hard\nbondage--in mortar, in brick, and in all manner of service in the field.\nAll their service in which they made them serve was with rigor.\n\nPharaoh tried to kill the Hebrew male babies\nSatan is always trying to kill the “promise\nseed” (Genesis 3:15) that would destroy his\nwork and bring salvation to the world.\n\nExodus 1:16\n“And he said, “When you do the duties of a midwife for the Hebrew\nwomen, and see them on the birthstools, if it is a son, then you shall\nkill him; but if it is a daughter, then she shall live.””\nExodus 1:22\n“So Pharaoh commanded all his people, saying, “Every son who is born\nyou shall cast into the river, and every daughter you shall save alive.”\n\nIn like manner, what Israel went through in\nEgypt is what happens when we are in sin.\n4\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"John 8:34\nJesus answered them, “Most assuredly, I say to you, whoever commits\nsin is a slave of sin.\n\nLesson 5\n\nKey #1: Sin puts us in bondage and death\n\nNote to Teacher: God never intended for Israel to stay\nin Egypt. They were there because of the sin of Joseph’s\nbrothers. Israel was His chosen nation but they were\nenjoying the wealth, food and comfort in Egypt. When\nthings took a turn for them and they became slaves in\nEgypt, Israel began to cry out to God for a deliverer to\ntake them out of bondage.\n\nExodus 2:23-25\nNow it happened in the process of time that the king of Egypt died.\nThen the children of Israel groaned because of the bondage, and they\ncried out; and their cry came up to God because of the bondage. 24\nSo God heard their groaning, and God remembered His covenant\nwith Abraham, with Isaac, and with Jacob. 25 And God looked upon the\nchildren of Israel, and God acknowledged them.\n\nB\n\nMOSES – GOD’S CHOSEN DELIVERER\nRefer to Chart L5.1-5\n\nKey #2: God’s plan of salvation involves\na Deliverer\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"Exodus 1:17\n\nLesson 5\n\nBut the midwives feared God, and did not do as the king of Egypt\ncommanded them, but saved the male children alive.\n\nOne of the babies saved and hidden from\nPharaoh’s armies was Moses. Moses was the\nchild of Jochebed.\n\nExodus 2:1-3\nAnd a man of the house of Levi went and took as wife a daughter of\nLevi. 2 So the woman conceived and bore a son. And when she saw\nthat he was a beautiful child, she hid him three months. 3 But when\nshe could no longer hide him, she took an ark of bulrushes for him,\ndaubed it with asphalt and pitch, put the child in it, and laid it in the\nreeds by the river’s bank.\n\nMoses was found by Pharaoh’s daughter who\nadopted him as her own. She then gave him to\nbe cared for by his own mother Jochebed until he\nwas grown (Exodus 2:4-10).\nAlthough Moses was raised by Pharaoh’s\ndaughter, his faith was in God and the promises\nHe had given to Israel.\n\nHebrews 11:24-27\nBy faith Moses, when he became of age, refused to be called the son\nof Pharaoh’s daughter, 25 choosing rather to suffer affliction with the\npeople of God than to enjoy the passing pleasures of sin, 26 esteeming\nthe reproach of Christ greater riches than the treasures in Egypt; for\nhe looked to the reward. 27 By faith he forsook Egypt, not fearing the\nwrath of the king; for he endured as seeing Him who is invisible.\n\n6\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Moses tried to save Israel using his own strength\nLesson 5\n\nExodus 2:11-15\nNow it came to pass in those days, when Moses was grown, that he\nwent out to his brethren and looked at their burdens. And he saw an\nEgyptian beating a Hebrew, one of his brethren. 12 So he looked this\nway and that way, and when he saw no one, he killed the Egyptian and\nhid him in the sand. 13 And when he went out the second day, behold,\ntwo Hebrew men were fighting, and he said to the one who did the\nwrong, “Why are you striking your companion?” 14 Then he said, “Who\nmade you a prince and a judge over us? Do you intend to kill me as\nyou killed the Egyptian?” So Moses feared and said, “Surely this thing is\nknown!” 15 When Pharaoh heard of this matter, he sought to kill Moses.\nBut Moses fled from the face of Pharaoh and dwelt in the land of\nMidian; and he sat down by a well.\n\nMoses fled to the desert of Midian where he\ndwelt for 40 years.\n\nGod called Moses from a burning bush\n\nExodus 3:1-10\nNow Moses was tending the flock of Jethro his father-in-law, the\npriest of Midian. And he led the flock to the back of the desert, and\ncame to Horeb, the mountain of God. 2 And the Angel of the LORD\nappeared to him in a flame of fire from the midst of a bush. So he\nlooked, and behold, the bush was burning with fire, but the bush was\nnot consumed. 3 Then Moses said, “I will now turn aside and see this\ngreat sight, why the bush does not burn.” 4 So when the LORD saw\nthat he turned aside to look, God called to him from the midst of the\nbush and said, “Moses, Moses!” And he said, “Here I am.” 5 Then He\nsaid, “Do not draw near this place. Take your sandals off your feet, for\nthe place where you stand is holy ground.” 6 Moreover He said, “I am\nthe God of your father--the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and\nthe God of Jacob.” And Moses hid his face, for he was afraid to look\nupon God. 7 And the LORD said: “I have surely seen the oppression of\nMy people who are in Egypt, and have heard their cry because of their\ntaskmasters, for I know their sorrows. 8 So I have come down to deliver\nthem out of the hand of the Egyptians, and to bring them up from that\nland to a good and large land, to a land flowing with milk and honey,\nto the place of the Canaanites and the Hittites and the Amorites and\nthe Perizzites and the Hivites and the Jebusites. 9 Now therefore,\nbehold, the cry of the children of Israel has come to Me, and I have\nalso seen the oppression with which the Egyptians oppress them. 10\nCome now, therefore, and I will send you to Pharaoh that you may\nbring My people, the children of Israel, out of Egypt.”\n\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"Moses gave 4 excuses to God on why he could\nnot do what God called him to do:\nLesson 5\n\n• Who am I that I should go? (Exodus 3:10-11)\n• But suppose they will not believe me or\nlisten to my voice? (Exodus 4:1)\n• I am not eloquent (Exodus 4:10)\n• Lord, You made the wrong choice (Exodus\n4:13)\n\nGod reminded Moses his natural abilities and\ntalents were not sufficient for the task. But\nrather it was God working through him to\nbring salvation to Israel.\n\nExodus 4:11-12\nSo the LORD said to him, “Who has made man’s mouth? Or who\nmakes the mute, the deaf, the seeing, or the blind? Have not I, the\nLORD? 12 Now therefore, go, and I will be with your mouth and teach\nyou what you shall say.”\n\nHowever, Moses’ unbelief kindled God’s anger\nand Aaron his brother was sent to go with him.\n\nExodus 4:14\nSo the anger of the LORD was kindled against Moses, and He said: “Is\nnot Aaron the Levite your brother? I know that he can speak well. And\nlook, he is also coming out to meet you. When he sees you, he will be\nglad in his heart.\n\nGod reveals His name\nThe name of God carries: His identity, authority,\npower and character. God revealed His name to\nMoses to let Israel know who He is.\n\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"Exodus 3:13-15\n\nLesson 5\n\nThen Moses said to God, “Indeed, when I come to the children of Israel\nand say to them, ‘The God of your fathers has sent me to you,’ and\nthey say to me, ‘What is His name?’ what shall I say to them?” 14 And\nGod said to Moses, “I AM WHO I AM.” And He said, “Thus you shall say\nto the children of Israel, ‘I AM has sent me to you.’ “ 15 Moreover God\nsaid to Moses, “Thus you shall say to the children of Israel: ‘The LORD\nGod of your fathers, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the\nGod of Jacob, has sent me to you. This is My name forever, and this is\nMy memorial to all generations.’\n\nNote to Teacher: Watch Bible Project Video Word Study\nYHWH “LORD”\n\n“I Am who I Am” carries the meaning of God\nbeing the Eternal and Self-Existent One, a\nbeing who is Omnipotent, Omnipresent, and\nOmniscient. Another form of this name is\nYahweh (Jehovah), which is the redemptive\nname of God in the Old Testament (Exodus 6:38). Translators of the King James Version would\nreplace Yahweh with LORD (all capital letters).\n\nMoses asks Pharaoh to release God’s people\n\nExodus 5:1-2\nAfterward Moses and Aaron went in and told Pharaoh, “Thus says the\nLORD God of Israel: ‘Let My people go, that they may hold a feast to\nMe in the wilderness.’ “ 2 And Pharaoh said, “Who is the LORD, that I\nshould obey His voice to let Israel go? I do not know the LORD, nor will\nI let Israel go.”\n\nBecause of Pharaoh’s refusal to release Israel,\nGod sent judgments to Egypt and the gods\nthey worship.\n\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"C\n\nJUDGEMENT ON EGYPT\n\nLesson 5\n\nRefer to Chart L5.2-5\n\nNote to Teacher: Note to Teacher Video link for the first\nnine plagues (Prince of Egypt):\nhttps://youtu.be/-tVTEyuCKn4\n\nThese are the ten plagues:\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\nBlood\nFrogs\nLice\nFlies\nMurrain (Cattle disease)\nBoils\nHail\nLocusts\nDarkness\nDeath of the firstborn\n\nExodus 11:4-6\nThen Moses said, “Thus says the LORD: ‘About midnight I will go out\ninto the midst of Egypt; 5 and all the firstborn in the land of Egypt\nshall die, from the firstborn of Pharaoh who sits on his throne, even\nto the firstborn of the female servant who is behind the handmill,\nand all the firstborn of the animals. 6 Then there shall be a great cry\nthroughout all the land of Egypt, such as was not like it before, nor\nshall be like it again.\n\nIn previous lessons we learn that before God passes\nJudgement, He will always extend mercy.\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"D\n\nPASSOVER: ISRAEL’S PLAN OF\nSALVATION IN EGYPT\n\nLesson 5\n\nRefer to Chart L5.3-5\n\nExodus 12:3-7\nSpeak to all the congregation of Israel, saying: ‘On the tenth day of\nthis month every man shall take for himself a lamb, according to the\nhouse of his father, a lamb for a household. 4 And if the household\nis too small for the lamb, let him and his neighbor next to his house\ntake it according to the number of the persons; according to each\nman’s need you shall make your count for the lamb. 5 Your lamb\nshall be without blemish, a male of the first year. You may take it\nfrom the sheep or from the goats. 6 Now you shall keep it until the\nfourteenth day of the same month. Then the whole assembly of the\ncongregation of Israel shall kill it at twilight. 7 And they shall take\nsome of the blood and put it on the two doorposts and on the lintel\nof the houses where they eat it.\nExodus 12:12-13\nFor I will pass through the land of Egypt on that night, and will strike\nall the firstborn in the land of Egypt, both man and beast; and against\nall the gods of Egypt I will execute judgment: I am the LORD. 13 Now\nthe blood shall be a sign for you on the houses where you are. And\nwhen I see the blood, I will pass over you; and the plague shall not be\non you to destroy you when I strike the land of Egypt.\nExodus 12:22-23\nAnd you shall take a bunch of hyssop, dip it in the blood that is in\nthe basin, and strike the lintel and the two doorposts with the blood\nthat is in the basin. And none of you shall go out of the door of his\nhouse until morning. 23 For the LORD will pass through to strike\nthe Egyptians; and when He sees the blood on the lintel and on the\ntwo doorposts, the LORD will pass over the door and not allow the\ndestroyer to come into your houses to strike you.\n\nKey #3: God’s plan of salvation requires\nthe shedding and application of the\ninnocent blood.\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"Hebrews 9:22 (AMP)\n\nLesson 5\n\n[In fact] under the Law almost everything is purified by means of\nblood, and without the shedding of blood there is neither release\nfrom sin and its guilt nor the remission of the due and merited\npunishment for sins.\n\nGod’s people obeyed His commandment\n\nExodus 12:28\n“Then the children of Israel went away and did so; just as the Lord had\ncommanded Moses and Aaron, so they did.”\n\nPharaoh releases Israel\n\nExodus 12:29-31\nAnd it came to pass at midnight that the LORD struck all the firstborn\nin the land of Egypt, from the firstborn of Pharaoh who sat on his\nthrone to the firstborn of the captive who was in the dungeon, and\nall the firstborn of livestock. 30 So Pharaoh rose in the night, he, all\nhis servants, and all the Egyptians; and there was a great cry in Egypt,\nfor there was not a house where there was not one dead. 31 Then\nhe called for Moses and Aaron by night, and said, “Rise, go out from\namong my people, both you and the children of Israel. And go, serve\nthe LORD as you have said.\n\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"E\nLesson 5\n\nEXODUS\nRefer to Chart L5.4-5\nPharaoh finally agreed to let the Israelites go,\nand God led them out of Egypt. Exodus means\n“coming out”.\nExodus 13:17-18\nThen it came to pass, when Pharaoh had let the people go, that God\ndid not lead them by way of the land of the Philistines, although that\nwas near; for God said, “Lest perhaps the people change their minds\nwhen they see war, and return to Egypt.” 18 So God led the people\naround by way of the wilderness of the Red Sea. And the children of\nIsrael went up in orderly ranks out of the land of Egypt.\n\nGod’s Presence in the Cloud\n\nExodus 13:21-22\nAnd the LORD went before them by day in a pillar of cloud to lead the\nway, and by night in a pillar of fire to give them light, so as to go by\nday and night. 22 He did not take away the pillar of cloud by day or the\npillar of fire by night from before the people.\n\nThe cloud overshadowed them as they\njourneyed out of Egypt. While journeying, they\nreceived news that Pharaoh changed his mind\nand decided to hunt down the Israelites.\n\nExodus 14:5-6\nNow it was told the king of Egypt that the people had fled, and the\nheart of Pharaoh and his servants was turned against the people;\nand they said, “Why have we done this, that we have let Israel go\nfrom serving us?” 6 So he made ready his chariot and took his\npeople with him.\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"Crossing the Red Sea\nLesson 5\n\nExodus 14:19-26\nAnd the Angel of God, who went before the camp of Israel, moved and\nwent behind them; and the pillar of cloud went from before them and\nstood behind them. 20 So it came between the camp of the Egyptians\nand the camp of Israel. Thus it was a cloud and darkness to the one,\nand it gave light by night to the other, so that the one did not come\nnear the other all that night. 21 Then Moses stretched out his hand\nover the sea; and the LORD caused the sea to go back by a strong east\nwind all that night, and made the sea into dry land, and the waters\nwere divided. 22 So the children of Israel went into the midst of the sea\non the dry ground, and the waters were a wall to them on their right\nhand and on their left. 23 And the Egyptians pursued and went after\nthem into the midst of the sea, all Pharaoh’s horses, his chariots, and\nhis horsemen. 24 Now it came to pass, in the morning watch, that the\nLORD looked down upon the army of the Egyptians through the pillar\nof fire and cloud, and He troubled the army of the Egyptians. 25 And He\ntook off their chariot wheels, so that they drove them with difficulty;\nand the Egyptians said, “Let us flee from the face of Israel, for the\nLORD fights for them against the Egyptians.” 26 Then the LORD said to\nMoses, “Stretch out your hand over the sea, that the waters may come\nback upon the Egyptians, on their chariots, and on their horsemen.”\nExodus 14:28\nThen the waters returned and covered the chariots, the horsemen,\nand all the army of Pharaoh that came into the sea after them. Not so\nmuch as one of them remained.\n\nThe crossing of the Red Sea was the turning\npoint for Israel’s deliverance from the bondage\nof Egypt. The story of how God brought Israel\nout of Egypt and journey through the wilderness\nbecame examples for us today.\n\n1 Corinthians 10:1-6\nMoreover, brethren, I do not want you to be unaware that all our\nfathers were under the cloud, all passed through the sea, 2 all were\nbaptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea, 3 all ate the same\nspiritual food, 4 and all drank the same spiritual drink. For they drank\nof that spiritual Rock that followed them, and that Rock was Christ.\n5\nBut with most of them God was not well pleased, for their bodies\nwere scattered in the wilderness. 6 Now these things became our\nexamples, to the intent that we should not lust after evil things as\nthey also lusted.\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"Key #4: The Exodus of Israel is an example\nof our salvation today.\n\nLesson 5\n\nNote to Teacher: You will see that the cloud and\nthe sea represent a type and shadow of our New\nTestament salvation. Just like how the Israelites were\nbaptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea, we\nalso are baptized into the presence of God and in\nwater. We will learn more about these concepts in\nLessons 8 and 9.\n\nF\n\nBIRTH OF THE NATION OF ISRAEL\nGod leads the Israelites through the wilderness\nto Mount Sinai. Moses was called by God to go\nto the top of the mountain where he meets with\nGod. It was there that God laid down the laws\nwhich would govern the people and thus the\nnation of Israel was formed. Remember that\nthe Israelites had been in bondage in Egypt for\nthe last 430 years! They had no civil structure or\nsocietal identity. It was here at Mount Sinai that\nGod gave them the blueprints of His plans to\ncreate a nation of people who belonged to Him.\nThe laws would govern their daily living, including\nmoral, ceremonial and civil laws as well as the\nplan to build the Tabernacle.\n\nExodus 19:5-6\nNow therefore, if you will indeed obey My voice and keep My\ncovenant, then you shall be a special treasure to Me above all people;\nfor all the earth is Mine. 6 And you shall be to Me a kingdom of priests\nand a holy nation.’ These are the words which you shall speak to the\nchildren of Israel.”\n\nGod made it clear at Mount Sinai His plan to\ncreate a holy nation, set apart and different from\nthe other cultures around them.\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"Lesson 5\n\nKey #5: God wants to save a group of people\nto be set apart for Him.\nIn the next lesson, we will learn how God made a way\nfor His people to come before Him as a holy nation.\n\nSummary of Lesson\nRefer to Chart L5.5-5\n\n1. Sin puts us in bondage and death.\n2. God’s plan of salvation involves a Deliverer.\n3. God’s plan of salvation requires the shedding and\napplication of innocent blood.\n4. The Exodus of Israel is an example of our salvation\ntoday.\n5. God wants to save a group of people to be set\napart for Him.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Charts\nLesson 5\n\n17\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"Charts\nLesson 5\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"Charts\nLesson 5\n\n19\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"Lesson 5\n\nModular Section\n1. Why did God harden Pharaoh’s heart?\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 5\n\nI. Why did God harden Pharaoh’s\nheart?\nMany wise and reputable commentators\npropose that when the Bible says that God\nhardened Pharaoh’s heart, what it really means\nis that God simply facilitated a process that\nPharaoh himself initiated. After all, the Bible\nrepeatedly also states that Pharaoh hardened\nhis own heart, i.e. Exodus 8:15 and 32.\nDr. Norman Geisler, for instance, a scholar\nwhose work we regard highly and frequently\ncite in this publication, holds that God did not\ndirectly harden Pharaoh’s heart (or anyone\nelse’s heart for that matter) contrary to their\nown free choice, but only indirectly, through\ntheir own choice. In their excellent book When\nCritics Ask (©1992 Victor Books), Geisler and\nHowe say,\n\n“God in His omniscience foreknew exactly how Pharaoh would\nrespond, and He used it to accomplish His purposes. God\nordained the means of Pharaoh’s free but stubborn action…”\n\nAnd that’s the position of many other respected\ncommentators. But not all. There are those\nwho believe that the simplest and most\naccurate reading of Exodus chapters 4-9, and\nthe corresponding text in Romans 9:17, rather\nindicates that it was God Himself, and none\nother, who was the primary, initiating, direct,\nand driving force behind Pharaoh’s choice to\nharden his heart.\nSource: ChristianAnswers.net\n\n21\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 5\n\nCharts\n\nPlagues and gods of Egypt Comparison\nThe 10 Plagues - Jehovah Versus the Gods of Egypt\nPLAGUE\n\nGODS OF EGYPT\n\n1\n\nWATER TURNED TO\nBLOOD\nExodus 7:14-25\n\n• Khnum: Guardian of river’s\nsource.\n• Hapi: Spirit of the Nile.\n• Osiris: Nile was his\nbloodstream\n\n2\n\nFROGS\nExodus 8:1-15\n\n3\n\nLICE\nExodus 8:16-19\n\n• Hapi\n• Heqt\n\nINTERESTING NOTES\n• Duplicated by the Egyptians\n• Occurs in Goshen where\nIsraelites lived.\n• Dead fish - putrid smell\n\nFrog goddess to Egypt. • Duplicated by the Egyptians\nBoth related to fertility. • Occurs in Goshen where\nIsraelites lived.\n\n• Seb: The earth god of Egypt\n\n• Not duplicated by the Egyptians\n• Occurs in Goshen where\nIsraelites lived.\n• Attributed to the “finger or God.”\n\n• Uatchit: The fly god of Egypt\n\n• God now makes a separation\nbetween the Egyptians and the\nIsraelites.\n• No more plagues will come\nupon the Israelites.\n\n• Ptah\n• Hathor\n• Mnevis\n• Amon\n\n• Affects property.\n• Death of livestock.\n\n4\n\nFLIES\nExodus 8:20-32\n\n5\n\nDISEASE ON CATTLE\nExodus 9:1-7\n\n6\n\nBOILS\nExodus 9:8-12\n\n• Sekhmet: Egyptian goddess\nof Epidemics\nEgyptian gods of\n• Serapis\n• Imhotep healing.\n\n• Affects physical bodies\n• Pharaoh’s magicians cannot\neven appear in court.\n\n7\n\nHAIL\nExodus 9:13-35\n\n• Nut: Egyptian sky goddess.\n• Isis & Seth: Egyptian\nagriculture deities.\n• Shu: Egyptian god of the\natmosphere\n\n• Historical uniqueness for such a\nstorm in Egypt.\n• Pharaoh confesses his sin but\nlater changes his mind.\n\n8\n\nLOCUSTS\nExodus 10:1-20\n\n• Serapia: Egyptian deity\nprotector from Locusts\n\n• Pharaoh offers a compromise.\n• The compromise is rejected.\n• Pharaoh again confesses his sin.\n\n• Re\nEgyptian\n• Amon-re\nsun\n• Aten\ngods.\n• Atum\n• Horus\n• Thoth: Egyptian moon god.\n\n• Dark in Egypt at midday.\n• Apparently light was still\nprovided for the Israelites in\nGoshen.\n\n9\n\n10\n\nDARKNESS\nExodus 10:21-29\n\nDEATH OF FIRST BORN\nExodus 12:29-36\n\nEgyptian gods\nassociated\nbulls and\ncows.\n\nThis plague was a Judgement on all of Egypt’s gods, including\nPharaoh himself. In Exodus 1, Pharaoh had killed the sons of Israel.\nNow the Lord kills the firstborn sons of the Egyptians (Exodus 11-12).\nPharaoh will let Israel go. He will later loose his army to death in the\nRed Sea (Exodus 14:4-31).\n\nSource: Barnes’ Bible Charts\n\n22\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 5\n\nComparison of Moses and Jesus\nMoses\n\nJesus\n\nPharaoh tried to kill him as a baby\n(Exodus 1:22)\n\nHerod tried to kill him as a baby\n(Matthew 2:16)\n\nHe was hidden from Pharaoh\n(Exodus 2:2)\n\nHe was hidden from Herod by his parents taking\nhim to Egypt at the instructions of an angel\n(Matthew 2:13)\n\nMoses saw the burdens of his brethren and had\ncompassion\n(Exodus 2:11)\n\nJesus saw His people as sheep without a\nshepherd and had compassion on them\n(Mark 6:34)\n\nMoses was the law-giver for the nation of Israel\n(John 1:17)\n\nJesus came to fulfill the law and taught it\n(Matthew 5:17)\n\nMoses was a mediator between God and the\npeople; a priest from the tribe of Levi\n(Exodus 19)\n\nJesus is the Mediator of the New Covenant, our\nHigh Priest who obtained eternal redemption\nfor us\n(Hebrews 9:11-15)\n\nMoses’ mission was to redeem Israel from\nslavery in Egypt\n\nJesus’ mission was to redeem mankind from\nslavery to sin\n\nSources:\nhttp://www.agapebiblestudy.com/charts/Typology%20of%20Moses%20and%20Jesus.htm\nhttp://www.confidentfaith.net/moses-and-jesus-devine-similarities\nhttp://www.desiringgod.org/articles/how-christ-fulfilled-and-ended-the-old-testament-regime\n\n23\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"6":{"lesson":6,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":27,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 6\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will be able to list the different ways God\nintroduces His holiness to the children of Israel.\n\n•\n\nThe student will be able to list the different articles of\nthe Tabernacle and its purposes.\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will be able to state the correlation between\nthe Tabernacle and Jesus Christ.\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience\n\nAge of Human Government\n\nAge of Promise\n\nAge of Law\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 6\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Israel, The Beginning of A Holy Nation\n\n3\n\nB. God’s Desire For A Holy People\n\n5\n\nC. God’s Holy Presence and Power\n\n6\n\nD. God’s Holy Law\n\n7\n\nE. God’s Holy Place - The Tabernacle\n\n9\n\nF. Furnishings of the Tabernacle\n\n12\n\nG. God’s Holy Land\n\n21\n\nH. The Tabernacle and A Holy Saviour\n\n22\n\nLesson Summary\nThe Israelites had been delivered from Egypt and were\nwalking through the wilderness on the way to Mount Sinai\nand the Promised Land. Moses led them to their first\ndestination, Mount Sinai, where God gave Moses and Israel\nthe Law.\nRefer to Chart L6.1-7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"A\nLesson 6\n\nISRAEL, THE BEGINNING OF A HOLY NATION\nExodus 19:5-6\n“Now therefore, if you will indeed obey My voice and keep My\ncovenant, then you shall be a special treasure to Me above all people;\nfor all the earth is Mine. 6 And you shall be to Me a kingdom of priests\nand a holy nation.’ These are the words which you shall speak to the\nchildren of Israel.”\n\nGod wanted to reveal His holiness to the world\nthrough His chosen covenant nation - Israel.\nThe religions of the nations they were passing\nthrough (Canaan) were notoriously immoral and\ninvolved worshiping idols and consorting with\ntemple prostitutes, both male and female.\n\nLeviticus 18:3\n“According to the doings of the land of Egypt, where you dwelt, you\nshall not do; and according to the doings of the land of Canaan,\nwhere I am bringing you, you shall not do; nor shall you walk in their\nordinances.”\n\nSimilarly, God’s desire for His people today in the\nNew Testament is for us to be a holy people set\napart for Him.\n\n1 Peter 2:9\n“But you are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, a holy nation,\nHis own special people, that you may proclaim the praises of Him who\ncalled you out of darkness into His marvelous light.”\n\n3\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"B\nLesson 6\n\nGOD’S DESIRE FOR A HOLY PEOPLE\nGod is Holy\n\nLeviticus 11:44\n“For I am the Lord your God. You shall therefore consecrate\nyourselves, and you shall be holy; for I am holy...”\n\nContrary to what you may hear today in some\nsermons and popular Christian songs, the\nemphasis in the Bible is on the holiness of God\nand not on the love of God.\nGod’s love is a holy love, for the Bible states that\n“God is light” (1 John 1:5) as well as “God is love”\n(4:8,16).\nLove without holiness portrays the wrong\nperspective of God.\nFor the children of Israel, the presence of the\ncloud of glory and the pillar of fire reminded\nIsrael that Jehovah was a holy God and “a\nconsuming fire” (Deut. 4:24; Heb. 12:29). To face\nGod’s holiness is to encounter His power.\nNote to teachers: To further illustrate this point,\nyou may wish to show The Animated Explanation of\nGod’s Holiness by the Bible Project (https://youtu.be/\nl9vn5UvsHvM), stopping at 2:53 min.\n\nGod desires His people to be holy.  This is\nbecause He wants to dwell among them and for\nthem to draw near to Him.\nExodus 29:46\n“And they shall know that I am the Lord their God, who brought them\nup out of the land of Egypt, that I may dwell among them. I am the\nLord their God.”\n\nKey #1: We need to be holy to be in a\nrelationship with a holy God.\n4\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"What does it mean to be holy?\nLesson 6\n\nWe typically understand holiness to be moral purity\nor righteous behaviour. However, the Hebrew word\nfor “holy” that Moses used in Leviticus means: “That\nwhich is set apart and marked off, that which is\ndifferent.”\nIn other words, holiness is to be set apart to God\nor to belong to God. Just as a bride is set apart for\nher bridegroom, God desires for His people to be\nwholly dedicated to Him.\nIn fact, the camp where the children of Israel dwelt\nwas considered holy because God was there with\nHis people.\n\nDeuteronomy 23:14\n“For the LORD your God walks in the midst of your camp, to deliver\nyou and give your enemies over to you; therefore your camp shall be\nholy, that He may see no unclean thing among you, and turn away\nfrom you. “\n\nHow does God make Israel different from\nthe nations of the world?\n• God revealed to them His holy presence and\npower.\n• God gave them a holy law to govern them.\n• God gave them plans to build a holy place.\n• God appointed a holy priesthood to serve Him.\n• God is leading them to a holy land.\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"C\nLesson 6\n\nGOD’S HOLY PRESENCE AND POWER\nUnlike Egypt and the nations around them, God\nrevealed Himself as the one true and exclusive God.\n\nDeuteronomy 6:4-6\n“Hear, O Israel: The LORD our God, the LORD is one! 5 You shall love\nthe LORD your God with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all\nyour strength. 6 “And these words which I command you today shall\nbe in your heart.“\nIsaiah 44:6\n“Thus says the LORD, the King of Israel, and his Redeemer, the LORD\nof hosts: ‘I am the First and I am the Last; Besides Me there is no God.”\n\nKey #2: God reveals His holiness to\nIsrael by revealing Himself to be the\none and only God.\n\nJehovah demonstrated His power as the one\ntrue God by judging the gods of Egypt and\ndestroying the Egyptian army at the Red Sea.\n\nExodus 12:12\n“For I will pass through the land of Egypt on that night, and will strike\nall the firstborn in the land of Egypt, both man and beast; and against\nall the gods of Egypt I will execute judgment: I am the LORD.”\n\n6\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"On Mount Sinai, God gave Israel a glimpse of\nHis Holy Presence.\nLesson 6\nExodus 20:18\n“Now all the people witnessed the thunderings, the lightning flashes,\nthe sound of the trumpet, and the mountain smoking; and when the\npeople saw it, they trembled and stood afar off.”\n\nD\n\nGOD’S HOLY LAW\nGod’s Law reflected His desire for Israel.\n\nDeuteronomy 7:6-8\n“For you are a holy people to the Lord your God; the Lord your God\nhas chosen you to be a people for Himself, a special treasure above\nall the peoples on the face of the earth. 7 The Lord did not set His love\non you nor choose you because you were more in number than any\nother people, for you were the least of all peoples; 8 but because the\nLord loves you, and because He would keep the oath which He swore\nto your fathers, the Lord has brought you out with a mighty hand, and\nredeemed you from the house of bondage, from the hand of Pharaoh\nking of Egypt.”\n\nGod’s statutes and ordinances governed the\ndaily life of the people and told them what was\nright and wrong, what was clean and unclean,\nand shows how God blesses obedience and\npunishes disobedience. The laws of God govern\nthe country (like a constitution).\n\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"An example of God’s commandments would be\nthe Ten Commandments found in Exodus 20:117.\nLesson 6\nNote to teachers: Please take time to go through each\ncommandment with the students and explain it to\nthem.\n\n1. “You shall have no other gods before Me.”\n(Ex 20:3)\n2. “You shall not make for yourself a carved\nimage…” (Ex 20:4)\n3. “You shall not take the name of the Lord your\nGod in vain…” (Ex 20:7)\n4. “Remember the Sabbath day, to keep it holy.”\n(Ex 20:8)\n5. “Honor your father and your mother, that\nyour days may be long upon the\nland…” (Ex 20:12)\n6. “You shall not murder.” (Ex 20:13)\n7. “You shall not commit adultery.” (Ex 20:14)\n8. “You shall not steal.” (Ex 20:15)\n9. “You shall not bear false witness against your\nneighbor.” (Ex 20:16)\n10. “You shall not covet…” (Ex 20:17)\nThe Law reveals sin and brings us to Christ.\n\nGalatians 3:19 (NLT)\n“Why, then, was the law given? It was given alongside the promise to\nshow people their sins. But the law was designed to last only until the\ncoming of the child who was promised...”\nGalatians 3:24\n“Therefore the law was our tutor to bring us to Christ, that we might\nbe justified by faith.”\n\nKey #3: The law reveals sin and\npoints us to our need for a Saviour.\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"E\nLesson 6\n\nGOD’S HOLY PLACE – THE TABERNACLE\nThe Tabernacle was a moveable “tent of meeting”\nthat God commanded Moses to build. The Hebrew\nword for Tabernacle means “to dwell with”. God\nwanted to dwell among his people, the Israelites.\nHe wanted to fellowship with them and be able to\ncommunicate with them.\nRefer to Chart L6.2-7\n\nWe study the tabernacle to understand the steps\nthe Lord laid out for sinful people to approach a\nholy God.\nGod gave Moses the plans to build the Tabernacle.\n\nExodus 25:9\n“According to all that I show you, that is, the pattern of the tabernacle\nand the pattern of all its furnishings, just so you shall make it.”\nHebrews 8:5\nwho serve the copy and shadow of the heavenly things, as Moses was\ndivinely instructed when he was about to make the tabernacle. For He\nsaid, “See that you make all things according to the pattern shown you\non the mountain.”\n\nThe importance of the Tabernacle plan is revealed\nby the detailed instructions found in 50 chapters\nof the Bible: Exodus, 13 chapters; Numbers, 13\nchapters; Leviticus, 18 chapters; Deuteronomy, 2\nchapters; and Hebrews, 4 chapters.\n\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"1. In the second year after they left Egypt,\nthe Tabernacle was fully constructed and\ncompleted.\nLesson 6\nNumbers 1:50-51\n“but you shall appoint the Levites over the tabernacle of the\nTestimony, over all its furnishings, and over all things that belong to it;\nthey shall carry the tabernacle and all its furnishings; they shall attend\nto it and camp around the tabernacle. 51 And when the tabernacle is\nto go forward, the Levites shall take it down; and when the tabernacle\nis to be set up, the Levites shall set it up. The outsider who comes near\nshall be put to death.”\n\nThe Tabernacle was fully portable so that Israel\ncould always journey with the presence of God in\nthe Wilderness.\n2. The Tabernacle was tended to by a holy\npriesthood.\nThe Jewish priesthood belonged only to the tribe of\nLevi.\nPriests were holy men, set apart for service to God.\nThey oversaw the care of the furnishings in the\nTabernacle. They were also responsible to guard\nGod’s sanctuary and approaching God’s altar.\nIn the Old Testament, only selected individuals were\nable to approach God as priests.\nIn the New Testament, every true believer in\nJesus Christ is a priest of God with the privilege of\napproaching God and offering spiritual sacrifices to\nHim.\n1 Peter 2:5\n“you also, as living stones, are being built up a spiritual house, a holy\npriesthood, to offer up spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through\nJesus Christ.”\n1 Peter 2:9\nBut you are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, a holy nation,\nHis own special people, that you may proclaim the praises of Him who\ncalled you out of darkness into His marvelous light\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"3. The children of Israel set up a camp\naround the Tabernacle facing it.\nLesson 6\nNumbers 2:2 (MSG)\n“The People of Israel are to set up camp circling the Tent of Meeting\nand facing it…”\n\nQuestion: Why do you think God wanted the\nTabernacle to be in the center of camp with the\ntents facing it?\n\n4. God’s presence abides in the Tabernacle.\n\nExodus 40:36-38\n“Whenever the cloud was taken up from above the tabernacle, the\nchildren of Israel would go onward in all their journeys. 37 But if the\ncloud was not taken up, then they did not journey till the day that it\nwas taken up. 38 For the cloud of the LORD was above the tabernacle\nby day, and fire was over it by night, in the sight of all the house of\nIsrael, throughout all their journeys.”\n\nThe Israelites always knew when God wanted them\nto move by watching the pillars of fire by night and\ncloud by day.\n\nNumbers 9:21-23\n“So it was, when the cloud remained only from evening until morning:\nwhen the cloud was taken up in the morning, then they would journey;\nwhether by day or by night, whenever the cloud was taken up, they\nwould journey. 22 Whether it was two days, a month, or a year that\nthe cloud remained above the tabernacle, the children of Israel\nwould remain encamped and not journey; but when it was taken up,\nthey would journey. 23 At the command of the LORD they remained\nencamped, and at the command of the LORD they journeyed; they\nkept the charge of the LORD, at the command of the LORD by the\nhand of Moses.”\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"The significance of being led by God was\nestablished by the Israelites following the cloud and\npillar of fire through the wilderness.\nLesson 6\n\nThe New Testament reveals the necessity of\nfollowing the Spirit of God with this statement: “For\nas many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are\nsons of God. “ - Romans 8:14 (for further reading\nsee Romans 8:1-5)\n\nIf we are going to be the children of God, we\nmust be led by Him.\n\nF\n\nFURNISHINGS OF THE TABERNACLE\nOverview of the Tabernacle\nRefer to Chart L6.3-7\nHebrews 9:1-9\n“Then indeed, even the first covenant had ordinances of divine service\nand the earthly sanctuary. 2 For a tabernacle was prepared: the first\npart, in which was the lampstand, the table, and the showbread,\nwhich is called the sanctuary; 3 and behind the second veil, the part\nof the tabernacle which is called the Holiest of All, 4 which had the\ngolden censer and the ark of the covenant overlaid on all sides with\ngold, in which were the golden pot that had the manna, Aaron’s rod\nthat budded, and the tablets of the covenant; 5 and above it were the\ncherubim of glory overshadowing the mercy seat. Of these things we\ncannot now speak in detail. 6 Now when these things had been thus\nprepared, the priests always went into the first part of the tabernacle,\nperforming the services. 7 But into the second part the high priest\nwent alone once a year, not without blood, which he offered for\nhimself and for the people’s sins committed in ignorance; 8 the Holy\nSpirit indicating this, that the way into the Holiest of All was not yet\nmade manifest while the first tabernacle was still standing. 9 It was\nsymbolic for the present time…”\n\nKey #4: The Tabernacle contains\nthe blueprint of how we can\napproach a holy God.\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"I. The Tabernacle was built God’s way\nLesson 6\nExodus 26:30\n“And you shall raise up the tabernacle according to its pattern which\nyou were shown on the mountain.”\n\nGod’s plan had to be followed exactly. From the\nbeginning of creation, God has always placed\nsignificance on details.\nQuestion: Can you think of another object of\nsalvation for which God gave specific instructions to\nbuild which was built properly and saved an entire\nfamily?\n(Noah’s Ark)\n\nII. Gate of the Court\nSee Exodus 27:16-17 for reference to the gate.\nFirst, a person would enter the gate of the court to\noffer a sacrifice for sin or thanksgiving.\nIt is significant that there was only one way to enter\nthe Tabernacle. This is to reveal that there was and\nis only one specific way to enter salvation and a\nrelationship with God.\n\nJohn 10:9\n“I am the door. If anyone enters by Me, he will be saved, and will go in\nand out and find pasture.”\nJohn 10:1\n“Most assuredly, I say to you, he who does not enter the sheepfold\nby the door, but climbs up some other way, the same is a thief and a\nrobber.“\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"III. The Brazen Altar\nLesson 6\n\nRefer to Chart L6.4-7\n\nExodus 27:1-2\n“You shall make an altar of acacia wood, five cubits long and five cubits\nwide--the altar shall be square--and its height shall be three cubits. 2\nYou shall make its horns on its four corners; its horns shall be of one\npiece with it. And you shall overlay it with bronze.”\n\nFor God to dwell amongst Israel, there needed to\nbe a solution for their sin. God required a sacrifice\nfor their sins. God told Adam and Eve that the result\nof their sin was death. However, God had mercy on\nthem and provided them with a temporary covering\nfor their sin. Instead of immediately requiring\ntheir own blood (death), God allowed the blood of\nan animal to atone for sin, making it possible for\nworshippers to enter into God’s presence.\n\nLeviticus 17:11\n“For the life of the flesh is in the blood, and I have given it to you upon\nthe altar to make atonement for your souls; for it is the blood that\nmakes atonement for the soul.”\n\nAnimals would be sacrificed and burnt upon the\nAltar. Once a year on the Day of Atonement, the\nHigh Priest would take this blood into the Most Holy\nPlace and sprinkle it upon the Mercy Seat of the Ark\nof the Covenant. This would push forward the sins\nof Israel until the next year.\nIn the New Testament, Jesus came to become the\nsacrifice for our sins (we will explore more about\nwho Jesus is in the following lesson).\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"John 1:29\n\nLesson 6\n\n“The next day John saw Jesus coming toward him, and said, “Behold!\nThe Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world!”\n1 Peter 1:18-19\n“knowing that you were not redeemed with corruptible things, like\nsilver or gold, from your aimless conduct received by tradition from\nyour fathers, 19 but with the precious blood of Christ, as of a lamb\nwithout blemish and without spot.”\n\nIV. The Brazen Laver\nThis is a place of washing and cleansing.\nExodus 30:17-19\n“Then the LORD spoke to Moses, saying: 18 “You shall also make a\nlaver of bronze, with its base also of bronze, for washing. You shall put\nit between the tabernacle of meeting and the altar. And you shall put\nwater in it, 19 for Aaron and his sons shall wash their hands and their\nfeet in water from it.”\nExodus 30:20-21\n“When they go into the tabernacle of meeting, or when they come\nnear the altar to minister, to burn an offering made by fire to the\nLORD, they shall wash with water, lest they die. 21 So they shall wash\ntheir hands and their feet, lest they die. And it shall be a statute\nforever to them--to him and his descendants throughout their\ngenerations.”\n\nQuestion: What would happen if the priests\nby-passed washing at the Laver?\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"V. The Holy Place\nLesson 6\n\nRefer to Chart L6.5-7\nGolden Candlestick (Exodus 25:31-37)\nThe Candlestick was the only light in the Holy Place,\nand it was never extinguished. It signified (a type\nof) Jesus who is the only true light of the world. His\nlight will never disappear!\n\nJohn 8:;12\n“Then Jesus spoke to them again, saying, “I am the light of the world.\nHe who follows Me shall not walk in darkness, but have the light of\nlife.”\n\nTable of Shewbread (Exodus 25:23-30)\nTwelve loaves of Shewbread were placed upon\na table in the Holy Place; one for each tribe. The\nShewbread was replenished every Sabbath and was\ngiven for food to the High Priest and his sons. The\nbread was a type of Jesus who is the bread of life\nand food for the hungry soul!\n\nJohn 6:35\n“And Jesus said to them, “I am the bread of life. He who comes to Me\nshall never hunger, and he who believes in Me shall never thirst.”\nLuke 4:4\n“But Jesus answered him, saying, “It is written, ‘Man shall not live by\nbread alone, but by every word of God.’ “\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Lesson 6\n\nThe Altar of Incense (Exodus 30:1-10)\nThe Altar of Incense represents the place of daily\ncommunication with God. Incense was burned\ndaily. The incense was a type of our daily prayers to\nGod.\n\nRevelation 5:8\n“Now when He had taken the scroll, the four living creatures and the\ntwenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb, each having a harp, and\ngolden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints.”\n\nThe continual burning shows the necessity for our\ncontinuous prayer and praise.\n\n1 Thessalonians 5:17-18\n“pray without ceasing, 18 in everything give thanks; for this is the will\nof God in Christ Jesus for you.”\n\nThe Altar of Incense was placed right before the\nveil, which separated the Holy Place from the Holy\nof Holies, and thus was nearest to the Ark of the\nCovenant. Prayer gives us direct access with God!\n\nExodus 30:6\n“And you shall put it before the veil that is before the ark of the\nTestimony, before the mercy seat that is over the Testimony, where I\nwill meet with you.”\n\n17\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"VI. The Holy of Holies\nLesson 6\n\nRefer to Chart L6.6-7\nThere is a veil (thick curtain) that separated the holy\nplace from the holy of holies.\n\nExodus 26:33\n“And you shall hang the veil from the clasps. Then you shall bring\nthe ark of the Testimony in there, behind the veil. The veil shall be a\ndivider for you between the holy place and the Most Holy.”\n\nWhat did the veil symbolize?\nHebrews 10:19-20\n“Therefore, brethren, having boldness to enter the Holiest by the\nblood of Jesus, 20 by a new and living way which He consecrated for\nus, through the veil, that is, His flesh,”\n\nQuestion: Who was on the other side of the veil?\n\nMark 15:37-38\n“And Jesus cried out with a loud voice, and breathed His last. 38 Then\nthe veil of the temple was torn in two from top to bottom.”\n\nInside the body of Christ (beyond the veil), the\nSpirit of God lived! When He died, the way into\nthe presence of God became open to anyone who\ndesires to enter!\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"The Ark of the Covenant (Contained three\nimportant items)\nLesson 6\n\n1. Pot of Manna – reminded Israel of their\nmurmuring and unbelief\n\nExodus 16:2-4\n“Then the whole congregation of the children of Israel complained\nagainst Moses and Aaron in the wilderness. 3 And the children of\nIsrael said to them, “Oh, that we had died by the hand of the LORD in\nthe land of Egypt, when we sat by the pots of meat and when we ate\nbread to the full! For you have brought us out into this wilderness to\nkill this whole assembly with hunger.” 4 Then the LORD said to Moses,\n“Behold, I will rain bread from heaven for you. And the people shall\ngo out and gather a certain quota every day, that I may test them,\nwhether they will walk in My law or not.”\n\n2. Aaron’s rod that budded – reminded them of\ntheir rebellion and pride of Korah against the priest\nof God\nNumbers 17:1-10\n“And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying: 2 “Speak to the children of\nIsrael, and get from them a rod from each father’s house, all their\nleaders according to their fathers’ houses--twelve rods. Write each\nman’s name on his rod. 3 And you shall write Aaron’s name on the rod\nof Levi. For there shall be one rod for the head of each father’s house.\n4 Then you shall place them in the tabernacle of meeting before the\nTestimony, where I meet with you. 5 And it shall be that the rod of\nthe man whom I choose will blossom; thus I will rid Myself of the\ncomplaints of the children of Israel, which they make against you.”\n6 So Moses spoke to the children of Israel, and each of their leaders\ngave him a rod apiece, for each leader according to their fathers’\nhouses, twelve rods; and the rod of Aaron was among their rods.\n7 And Moses placed the rods before the LORD in the tabernacle of\nwitness. 8 Now it came to pass on the next day that Moses went into\nthe tabernacle of witness, and behold, the rod of Aaron, of the house\nof Levi, had sprouted and put forth buds, had produced blossoms\nand yielded ripe almonds. 9 Then Moses brought out all the rods from\nbefore the LORD to all the children of Israel; and they looked, and each\nman took his rod. 10 And the LORD said to Moses, “Bring Aaron’s rod\nback before the Testimony, to be kept as a sign against the rebels, that\nyou may put their complaints away from Me, lest they die.”\n\n19\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"3. The Tablets of Stone of the Ten Commandments\n– reminded them of their worship of the golden calf\nin rebellion to God\nLesson 6\nExodus 16:2-4\n“Now when the people saw that Moses delayed coming down from\nthe mountain, the people gathered together to Aaron, and said to him,\n“Come, make us gods that shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the\nman who brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we do not know what\nhas become of him…4 And he received…gold … and made a molded\ncalf. Then they said, “This is your god, O Israel, that brought you out\nof the land of Egypt!” …7 And the Lord said to Moses, “Go, get down!\nFor your people whom you brought out of the land of Egypt have\ncorrupted themselves. …19 So it was, as soon as he came near the\ncamp, that he saw the calf and the dancing. So Moses’ anger became\nhot, and he cast the tablets out of his hands and broke them at the\nfoot of the mountain.”\n\nThe Mercy Seat\nThe Mercy Seat was the cover for the Ark of the\nCovenant. It was covered by the wings of two\ngolden cherubim. The Mercy Seat represents the\nmercy of God that saves us. This seat had innocent\nblood poured upon it (Leviticus 16:15), pointing to\nthe redemptive work of Christ.\n\nExodus 25:22\n“And there I will meet with you, and I will speak with you from above\nthe mercy seat, from between the two cherubim which are on\nthe ark of the Testimony, about everything which I will give you in\ncommandment to the children of Israel.”\n\n20\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"G\nLesson 6\n\nGOD’S HOLY LAND\nThe holy presence of God, the holy law, the holy\npriesthood and the holy place (Tabernacle) was with\nIsrael the whole time as they journeyed through the\nwilderness to God’s holy land.\nIsrael belonged to God because He redeemed them\nfrom Egypt to be His very own. The land belonged\nto the Lord, and He gave it to Israel with a condition\nthat they do nothing to defile it.\n\nNumbers 35:34\n“Therefore do not defile the land which you inhabit, in the midst of\nwhich I dwell; for I the LORD dwell among the children of Israel.’ ”\n\nA holy God wants His holy people to live in a holy\nland.\nThis holy land is what is commonly known as the\npromise land which God promised Moses when He\ncalled him from the burning bush.\nExodus 3:17\n“and I have said I will bring you up out of the affliction of Egypt to\nthe land of the Canaanites and the Hittites and the Amorites and the\nPerizzites and the Hivites and the Jebusites, to a land flowing with milk\nand honey.”\n\nJust like the children of Israel, life on earth is not\nour final destination. The Bible calls us “pilgrims”\npassing through this life.  God has prepared a final\nresting place for those who choose to follow Him\nand ultimately spend eternity with Him.\nHebrews 11:13, 16\n“These all died in faith, not having received the promises, but having\nseen them afar off were assured of them, embraced them and\nconfessed that they were strangers and pilgrims on the earth… 16 But\nnow they desire a better, that is, a heavenly country. Therefore God\nis not ashamed to be called their God, for He has prepared a city for\nthem.\n\n21\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"H\nLesson 6\n\nTHE TABERNACLE AND A HOLY SAVIOUR\nEvery year, there is a special day called the Day\nof Atonement. The high priest in Israel would go\nthrough the furnishings of the Tabernacle and\nmake an atonement for the sins of the nation at\nthe mercy seat. He would take the blood of the\nsacrificial animal to atone for the sins of Israel.\nThis act is a prelude to an actual day where Jesus\nwould come and become both the High Priest and\nsacrifice for the atonement of our sins.\n\nHebrews 9:11-12\n“But Christ came as High Priest of the good things to come, with the\ngreater and more perfect tabernacle not made with hands, that is, not\nof this creation. 12 Not with the blood of goats and calves, but with\nHis own blood He entered the Most Holy Place once for all, having\nobtained eternal redemption.”\n\nThere are two paths when we look at the Tabernacle.\n1. Man to God – Path of Faith\nCourt Gate --> Brazen Altar --> Brazen Laver --> Ark of\nCovenant --> Holy of Holies\nThis is talking about Man approaching God by faith.\nBut before man can draw near to God, God initiated a\nrelationship with us.\n2. God to Man – Path of Grace\nHoly of Holies --> Ark of Covenant --> Brazen Laver -->\nBrazen Altar --> Court Gate\nThis is called the Path of Grace. It represents the path\nfrom God to Man. God in His grace came out of the Holy of\nholies, robed Himself in flesh, and made a way for man to\nenter into the Holy of holies through grace.\nKey #5: God came in flesh so that\nwe can approach Him in faith.\n22\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 6\n\nRefer to Chart L6.7-7\n\n1. We need to be holy to be in a relationship\nwith a holy God.\n2. God reveals His holiness to Israel by\nrevealing Himself to be the one and only\nGod.\n3. The law reveals sin and points us to our\nneed for a Saviour.\n4. The Tabernacle contains the blueprint of\nhow we can approach a holy God.\n5. God came in flesh so that we can approach\nHim in faith.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n23\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":24,"text":"Charts\nLesson 6\n\n24\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":25,"text":"Charts\nLesson 6\n\n25\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":26,"text":"Charts\nLesson 6\n\n26\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":27,"text":"Charts\nLesson 6\n\n27\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"7":{"lesson":7,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":42,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 7\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will be able to describe the\npurpose of why Jesus came\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will compare Jesus with the God\nof the Old Testament and conclude that they\nare One\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience\n\nAge of Human Government\n\nAge of Law\n\nAge of Promise\n\nChurch Age\n\nCharacters\nJesus, Mary, John the Baptist, Jews\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 7\n\nLesson Summary\n•\n\nIsrael enters the Promise Land under the leadership\nof Joshua\n\n•\n\nIsrael fell into idolatry after the death of Joshua\n\n•\n\nIsrael was led by judges and eventually kings\n\n•\n\nThe first 3 kings were Saul, David and Solomon\n\n•\n\nIsrael was then divided into the North (Israel) and\nSouth (Judah)\n\n•\n\nEvery time Israel/Judah was led by a good king, they\nwould prosper\n\n•\n\nHowever, when a bad king would lead Israel/Judah\ninto idolatry, God would judge them by allowing a\nforeign army to take them captive\n\n•\n\nDuring this time, prophets would be sent by God to\nforetell Israel of a future Messiah who would deliver\nthem from captivity and establish the kingdom of\nGod through Israel\n\n•\n\nThe New Testament begins with Israel being under\nthe Roman Empire’s rule\n\nRefer to Chart L7.1-5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"Lesson 7\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Introduction to the New Testament\n\n4\n\nB. Birth of Jesus\n\n5\n\nC. John the Baptist\n\n6\n\nD. The Life Ministry of Jesus\n\n7\n\nE.  Who Does the Bible say Jesus Is?\n\n14\n\nF. Jesus forgave sins\n\n17\n\nG.  The Death, Burial and Resurrection of Jesus\nChrist\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"A\nLesson 7\n\nINTRODUCTION TO THE NEW TESTAMENT\nRefer to Chart L7.2-5\n\nThe New Testament can be divided into 4 main parts.\n1. The Gospels (Matthew to John) – contains the\nbiography of Jesus Christ: His earthly ministry and His\ndeath, burial and resurrection. The Gospels introduce\nChrist to us.\n2. The Acts of the Apostles (Acts) – contains the birth and\nlife of the original Church. It tells us what the disciples\n(apostles) of Jesus Christ did and taught in continuation\nof what He started on earth. Acts also contains the first\nconversion of Jews, Gentiles and Samaritans- which led\nto their salvation. Acts shows us how to be in Christ.\n3. The Epistles (Romans to Jude) – contains letters\nwritten by apostles (leaders of the Church) to both\nchurches and individuals. The epistles are instructions\nto believers on how to live out the teachings of Jesus\nChrist and the Church. The Epistles teach us how to\nstay in Christ.\n4. The Revelation of Jesus Christ (Revelation) – contains\nletters written to the churches regarding future events\non the earth and eternity. This letter also contains the\nfinal revealing of who Jesus is. Revelation tells us how\neverything will end for those who choose to stay in\nChrist and those who don’t.\nIn this lesson, we will mostly be covering the books of\nthe Gospels. Do note that even though these books are\ncategorized under the New Testament, those living in\nthe time of the Gospels were still governed by the Old\nTestament Law. The New Testament only came into effect\nafter the death of Jesus Christ (see Hebrews 9:16-17).\n\n4\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"Hebrews 9:16-17\nFor where there is a testament, there must also of necessity be the\ndeath of the testator. 17 For a testament is in force after men are\ndead, since it has no power at all while the testator lives.\n\nLesson 7\n\nB\n\nBIRTH OF JESUS\nRefer to Chart L7.3-5\nHaving found favour with God, a young virgin girl, Mary,\nwas chosen to be the mother of the baby Jesus.\n\nLuke 1:31-35\nAnd behold, you will conceive in your womb and bring forth a Son, and\nshall call His name JESUS. 32 He will be great, and will be called the Son\nof the Highest; and the Lord God will give Him the throne of His father\nDavid. 33 And He will reign over the house of Jacob forever, and of His\nkingdom there will be no end.” 34 Then Mary said to the angel, “How\ncan this be, since I do not know a man?” 35 And the angel answered\nand said to her, “The Holy Spirit will come upon you, and the power of\nthe Highest will overshadow you; therefore, also, that Holy One who is\nto be born will be called the Son of God.\nMatthew 1:20-23\nBut while he thought about these things, behold, an angel of the Lord\nappeared to him in a dream, saying, “Joseph, son of David, do not be\nafraid to take to you Mary your wife, for that which is conceived in her\nis of the Holy Spirit. 21 And she will bring forth a Son, and you shall call\nHis name JESUS, for He will save His people from their sins.” 22 So all\nthis was done that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the Lord\nthrough the prophet, saying: 23 “Behold, the virgin shall be with child, and\nbear a Son, and they shall call His name Immanuel,” which is translated,\n“God with us.”\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"In Hebrew, the name Jesus means - “Jehovah salvation” or\n“Jehovah is salvation”.\nLesson 7\n\nJesus is also referred to as “God with us” or the “Son of\nGod”.\nThe term Son of God does not mean that there is “another\nGod”. This would contradict what Jehovah has been telling\nIsrael in the Old Testament about one God (Deuteronomy\n6:4, Isaiah 44:6).\nThe term Son of God refers to the physical body of God\nin flesh. The Bible never uses the term “God the Son”, but\nrather Son of God. This is because the essence of God has\nnever been human flesh, but rather Spirit (John 4:24).\nIn the New Testament, God manifested Himself in flesh\nthrough the person of Jesus Christ.\nIsaiah 9:6\nFor unto us a Child is born, unto us a Son is given; And the government\nwill be upon His shoulder. And His name will be called Wonderful,\nCounselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.\n1 Timothy 3:16\nAnd without controversy great is the mystery of godliness: God was\nmanifested in the flesh, justified in the Spirit, seen by angels, preached\namong the Gentiles, believed on in the world, Received up in glory.\n\nThe birth of Jesus also fulfills the prophecy given in\nGenesis 3:15 (in Lesson 2) where a child born of a woman\nwould destroy Satan and His kingdom.\n\nGenesis 3:15\nAnd I will put enmity Between you and the woman, and between your\nseed and her Seed; He shall bruise your head, and you shall bruise His\nheel.”\n\nKey #1: Jesus came to reverse the curse of\nsin and destroy the work of Satan.\n6\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"C\n\nJOHN THE BAPTIST\n\nLesson 7\n\nThe introduction of Jesus to Israel was preceded by\na man named John who was God’s messenger to\nprepare the way for Him.\nMalachi 3:1\n“Behold, I send My messenger, And he will prepare the way before Me.\nAnd the Lord, whom you seek, Will suddenly come to His temple, Even\nthe Messenger of the covenant, In whom you delight. Behold, He is\ncoming,” Says the LORD of hosts.\nLuke 3:3-6 (NLT)\nThen John went from place to place on both sides of the Jordan\nRiver, preaching that people should be baptized to show that they\nhad turned to God to receive forgiveness for their sins. 4 Isaiah had\nspoken of John when he said, “He is a voice shouting in the wilderness,\n‘Prepare the way for the LORD’s coming! Clear the road for him! 5\nThe valleys will be filled, and the mountains and hills made level. The\ncurves will be straightened, and the rough places made smooth. 6 And\nthen all people will see the salvation sent from God.’”\n\n(See Isaiah 40:3-4 for the prophecy of Isaiah\nregarding John)\nJohn the Baptist also teaches us that repentance is\nthe prerequisite for God coming into our lives.\nJohn introduces Jesus\nWhen Jesus was approximately thirty years old,\nJohn saw Jesus coming to the river where he\nwas baptizing people. It was there where He\nannounced Jesus is as the sacrificial Lamb who will\ndie for the atonement of human sin.\n\nJohn 1:29\nThe next day John saw Jesus coming toward him, and said, “Behold!\nThe Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world!\n\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"Note to Teacher: Make reference to the animal\nsacrificed for Adam and Eve, the Passover, the ram\nthat God gave Abraham, and the animal sacrifice on\nthe Day of Atonement in the Tabernacle.\n\nLesson 7\n\nJohn also said that Jesus is the one who will baptize\nthe people with the Spirit of God.\n\nLuke 3:15-16\nNow as the people were in expectation, and all reasoned in their\nhearts about John, whether he was the Christ or not, 16 John answered,\nsaying to all, “I indeed baptize you with water; but One mightier than I\nis coming, whose sandal strap I am not worthy to loose. He will baptize\nyou with the Holy Spirit and fire.\n\nD\n\nTHE LIFE MINISTRY OF JESUS\nAfter being baptized by John the Baptist (see\nMatthew 3:13-17), Jesus began His ministry on\nearth by demonstrating miracles, ministering to the\npeople, preaching and teaching.\nMiracles\nJesus performed numerous miracles while He was\non the earth. While some of Jesus’ miracles were\ndone out of compassion for the people, others\nrevealed His true identity.\nHealing\n\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"Matthew 9:27-31\n\nLesson 7\n\nWhen Jesus departed from there, two blind men followed Him, crying\nout and saying, “Son of David, have mercy on us!” 28 And when He had\ncome into the house, the blind men came to Him. And Jesus said to\nthem, “Do you believe that I am able to do this?” They said to Him,\n“Yes, Lord.” 29 Then He touched their eyes, saying, “According to your\nfaith let it be to you.” 30 And their eyes were opened. And Jesus sternly\nwarned them, saying, “See that no one knows it.” 31 But when they had\ndeparted, they spread the news about Him in all that country.\n\nRaising the dead\n\nJohn 11:43-45\nNow when He had said these things, He cried with a loud voice,\n“Lazarus, come forth!” 44 And he who had died came out bound hand\nand foot with graveclothes, and his face was wrapped with a cloth.\nJesus said to them, “Loose him, and let him go.” 45 Then many of\nthe Jews who had come to Mary, and had seen the things Jesus did,\nbelieved in Him.\n\nCalming the storm\n\nMark 4:35-41\nOn the same day, when evening had come, He said to them, “Let us\ncross over to the other side.” 36 Now when they had left the multitude,\nthey took Him along in the boat as He was. And other little boats were\nalso with Him. 37 And a great windstorm arose, and the waves beat\ninto the boat, so that it was already filling. 38 But He was in the stern,\nasleep on a pillow. And they awoke Him and said to Him, “Teacher, do\nYou not care that we are perishing?” 39 Then He arose and rebuked\nthe wind, and said to the sea, “Peace, be still!” And the wind ceased\nand there was a great calm. 40 But He said to them, “Why are you\nso fearful? How is it that you have no faith?” 41 And they feared\nexceedingly, and said to one another, “Who can this be, that even the\nwind and the sea obey Him!”\n\n(See Job 9:8 on how Jehovah declares that He alone\ntreads on the waves of the sea)\n\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"Casting out evil spirits\nLesson 7\n\nLuke 4:33-37\nNow in the synagogue there was a man who had a spirit of an unclean\ndemon. And he cried out with a loud voice, 34 saying, “Let us alone!\nWhat have we to do with You, Jesus of Nazareth? Did You come to\ndestroy us? I know who You are--the Holy One of God!” 35 But Jesus\nrebuked him, saying, “Be quiet, and come out of him!” And when the\ndemon had thrown him in their midst, it came out of him and did not\nhurt him. 36 Then they were all amazed and spoke among themselves,\nsaying, “What a word this is! For with authority and power He\ncommands the unclean spirits, and they come out.” 37 And the report\nabout Him went out into every place in the surrounding region.\n\nThis portion of Jesus’ ministry is unique because\nnone of the Old Testament men of God ever\npossessed authority over demons. Jesus cast them\nout with only His words.\nMultiplying food to feed thousands\n\nMatthew 14:15-21\nWhen it was evening, His disciples came to Him, saying, “This is a\ndeserted place, and the hour is already late. Send the multitudes away,\nthat they may go into the villages and buy themselves food.” 16 But Jesus\nsaid to them, “They do not need to go away. You give them something\nto eat.” 17 And they said to Him, “We have here only five loaves and two\nfish.” 18 He said, “Bring them here to Me.” 19 Then He commanded the\nmultitudes to sit down on the grass. And He took the five loaves and\nthe two fish, and looking up to heaven, He blessed and broke and gave\nthe loaves to the disciples; and the disciples gave to the multitudes. 20\nSo they all ate and were filled, and they took up twelve baskets full of\nthe fragments that remained. 21 Now those who had eaten were about\nfive thousand men, besides women and children.\n\nKey #2: Jesus still demonstrates His power\nthrough miracles today!\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"Preaching and Teaching\nLesson 7\n\nMatthew 4:17\nFrom that time Jesus began to preach and to say, “Repent, for the\nkingdom of heaven is at hand.”\nMatthew 7:28-29\nAnd so it was, when Jesus had ended these sayings, that the people\nwere astonished at His teaching, 29 for He taught them as one having\nauthority, and not as the scribes.\nMatthew 13:10-11\nAnd the disciples came and said to Him, “Why do You speak to them\nin parables?” 11 He answered and said to them, “Because it has been\ngiven to you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to\nthem it has not been given.\n\nWhat are parables and why did Jesus teach in\nparables?\nA parable is a short story with a hidden or secret\nmeaning.\nJesus constantly used parables to illustrate abstract\nideas and concepts. He used everyday objects such\nas fish, seeds, and soil and connected these objects\nto unfamiliar, spiritual concepts. Jesus wanted the\nvery complicated things about the kingdom of\nGod to be understood. So, He simplified spiritual\nconcepts into familiar illustrations to make it easy\nfor the people who wanted to learn.\nJesus taught in parables to reveal the treasures of\ntruth to hungry people while hiding it from those\nwho were not interested.\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"Matthew 13:12-16 (NLT)\n\nLesson 7\n\nTo those who listen to my teaching, more understanding will be given,\nand they will have an abundance of knowledge. But for those who are\nnot listening, even what little understanding they have will be taken\naway from them. 13 That is why I use these parables, For they look,\nbut they don’t really see. They hear, but they don’t really listen or\nunderstand. 14 This fulfills the prophecy of Isaiah that says, ‘When you\nhear what I say, you will not understand. When you see what I do, you\nwill not comprehend. 15 For the hearts of these people are hardened,\nand their ears cannot hear, and they have closed their eyes— so their\neyes cannot see, and their ears cannot hear, and their hearts cannot\nunderstand, and they cannot turn to me and let me heal them.’ 16 “But\nblessed are your eyes, because they see; and your ears, because they\nhear.\n\nMaking Disciples\nAlthough a crowd followed Jesus for his miracles\nand provision, Jesus did not commit Himself to them\n(John 2:24-25). He chose to dedicate most of his\nministry on earth to investing in disciples.\n\nMatthew 4:19\nThen He said to them, “Follow Me, and I will make you fishers of men.”\n\nWho are disciples?\nDisciples are those who actively demonstrate a\ncommitment to follow Jesus, learning of Him. A true\ndisciple is one who actively hears and obeys the\nteachings of Jesus. Making disciples later became\nthe commission Jesus gave to the Church (Matthew\n28:19-20)\n\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"Matthew 16:24\n\nLesson 7\n\nThen Jesus said to His disciples, “If anyone desires to come after Me,\nlet him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow Me.\nJohn 8:31-32\nThen Jesus said to those Jews who believed Him, “If you abide in My\nword, you are My disciples indeed. 32 And you shall know the truth,\nand the truth shall make you free.”\n\nThese disciples later continued His ministry. Jesus\nsent them to do the same works that He did.\n\nMatthew 10:1, 5-8\nAnd when He had called His twelve disciples to Him, He gave them\npower over unclean spirits, to cast them out, and to heal all kinds of\nsickness and all kinds of disease….5 These twelve Jesus sent out and\ncommanded them, saying: “Do not go into the way of the Gentiles, and\ndo not enter a city of the Samaritans. 6 But go rather to the lost sheep\nof the house of Israel. 7 And as you go, preach, saying, ‘The kingdom of\nheaven is at hand.’ 8 Heal the sick, cleanse the lepers, raise the dead,\ncast out demons. Freely you have received, freely give.\n\nKey #3: Jesus is still looking for disciples today.\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"E\nLesson 7\n\nWHO DOES THE BIBLE SAY JESUS IS?\nThe Messiah, the Son of God\n\nMatthew 11:1-5\nNow it came to pass, when Jesus finished commanding His twelve\ndisciples, that He departed from there to teach and to preach in their\ncities. 2 And when John had heard in prison about the works of Christ,\nhe sent two of his disciples 3 and said to Him, “Are You the Coming\nOne, or do we look for another?” 4 Jesus answered and said to them,\n“Go and tell John the things which you hear and see: 5 The blind see\nand the lame walk; the lepers are cleansed and the deaf hear; the\ndead are raised up and the poor have the gospel preached to them.\n\nNote to Teacher: Watch Bible Project “Messiah” for\nfurther explanation\n\nJohn 20:30-31\nAnd truly Jesus did many other signs in the presence of His disciples,\nwhich are not written in this book; 31 but these are written that you\nmay believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God, and that believing\nyou may have life in His name.\n\nWord becoming flesh\n\nJohn 1:1, 14\nIn the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the\nWord was God…14  And the Word became flesh and dwelt among\nus, and we beheld His glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the\nFather, full of grace and truth.\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"God manifested in the flesh\nLesson 7\n\n1 Timothy 3:16\nAnd without controversy great is the mystery of godliness: God was\nmanifested in the flesh, Justified in the Spirit, Seen by angels, Preached\namong the Gentiles, Believed on in the world, Received up in glory.\n\nImage of the invisible God\n\nColossians 1:15\nHe is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn over all creation.\nJohn 14:6-9\nJesus said to him, “I am the way, the truth, and the life. No one comes\nto the Father except through Me. 7 “If you had known Me, you would\nhave known My Father also; and from now on you know Him and have\nseen Him.” 8 Philip said to Him, “Lord, show us the Father, and it is\nsufficient for us.” 9 Jesus said to him, “Have I been with you so long,\nand yet you have not known Me, Philip? He who has seen Me has seen\nthe Father; so how can you say, ‘Show us the Father’?\n\nJesus and the Father are One\n\nJohn 10:30-33\nI and My Father are one. 31 Then the Jews took up stones again\nto stone Him. 32 Jesus answered them, “Many good works I have\nshown you from My Father. For which of those works do you stone\nMe?” 33 The Jews answered Him, saying, “For a good work we do not\nstone You, but for blasphemy, and because You, being a Man, make\nYourself God.”\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"The “I Am” of the Old Testament\nLesson 7\n\nJohn 8:56-59\nYour father Abraham rejoiced to see My day, and he saw it and was\nglad.” 57 Then the Jews said to Him, “You are not yet fifty years old, and\nhave You seen Abraham?” 58 Jesus said to them, “Most assuredly, I say\nto you, before Abraham was, I AM.” 59 Then they took up stones to\nthrow at Him; but Jesus hid Himself and went out of the temple, going\nthrough the midst of them, and so passed by.\n\nKey #4: Jesus is the God of the Old\nTestament revealing Himself in flesh.\n\nWhy did God come in flesh?\nGod, being essentially a Spirit, cannot shed blood or\ndie. Therefore, He created a body for Himself, and\noffered it for the redemption of humanity.\nIsaiah 59:15-20 (TLB)\n…the Lord saw all the evil and was displeased to find no steps taken\nagainst sin.16He saw no one was helping you and wondered that no\none intervened. Therefore he himself stepped in to save you through\nhis mighty power and justice.20…a Redeemer to those in Zion who\nhave turned away from sin.”\n2 Corinthians 5:18-19\nNow all things are of God, who has reconciled us to Himself through\nJesus Christ, and has given us the ministry of reconciliation, 19 that is,\nthat God was in Christ reconciling the world to Himself, not imputing\ntheir trespasses to them, and has committed to us the word of\nreconciliation.\nTitus 2:13-14\nlooking for the blessed hope and glorious appearing of our great God\nand Savior Jesus Christ, 14who gave Himself for us, that He might\nredeem us from every lawless deed and purify for Himself His own\nspecial people, zealous for good works.”\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Key #5: God came in flesh to save us from\nour sins.\n\nLesson 7\n\nF\n\nJESUS FORGAVE SINS\nAmong all that Jesus did while walking on this earth, there\nwasn’t anything more controversial than when He went\naround forgiving people’s sins.\n\nMatthew 9:2-7\nThen behold, they brought to Him a paralytic lying on a bed. When\nJesus saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Son, be of good cheer;\nyour sins are forgiven you.” 3 And at once some of the scribes said\nwithin themselves, “This Man blasphemes!” 4 But Jesus, knowing their\nthoughts, said, “Why do you think evil in your hearts? 5 For which is\neasier, to say, ‘Your sins are forgiven you,’ or to say, ‘Arise and walk’?\n6\nBut that you may know that the Son of Man has power on earth to\nforgive sins”--then He said to the paralytic, “Arise, take up your bed,\nand go to your house.” 7 And he arose and departed to his house.\nMark 2:5-7\nWhen Jesus saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Son, your sins\nare forgiven you.” 6 And some of the scribes were sitting there and\nreasoning in their hearts, 7 “Why does this Man speak blasphemies\nlike this? Who can forgive sins but God alone?”\n\nBy forgiving sin, Jesus was claiming to be God Himself.\nThis created an uproar amongst the Jewish religious\nleaders who then later sought to murder Him. Jesus did\nmore than forgive sin, He died to pay the penalty of sin.\n\n17\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"G\nLesson 7\n\nTHE DEATH, BURIAL AND\nRESURRECTION OF JESUS CHRIST\nRefer to Chart L7.4-5\nAfter a betrayal by one of his disciples and an unlawful\ntrial set up by the Jewish religious leaders, Jesus was\nbrought to Pontius Pilate for judgement.\n\nMatthew 27:1-2\nWhen morning came, all the chief priests and elders of the people\nplotted against Jesus to put Him to death. 2 And when they had\nbound Him, they led Him away and delivered Him to Pontius Pilate the\ngovernor.\n\nThe people of Israel then persuaded Pontius Pilate to\nsentence Jesus to die on the cross.\n\nMatthew 27:22-23\nPilate said to them, “What then shall I do with Jesus who is called\nChrist?” They all said to him, “Let Him be crucified!” 23 Then the\ngovernor said, “Why, what evil has He done?” But they cried out all the\nmore, saying, “Let Him be crucified!”\n\nJesus was tortured on the way to the cross\nMatthew 27:26-31\nThen he released Barabbas to them; and when he had scourged Jesus,\nhe delivered Him to be crucified. 27 Then the soldiers of the governor\ntook Jesus into the Praetorium and gathered the whole garrison\naround Him. 28 And they stripped Him and put a scarlet robe on Him.\n29 When they had twisted a crown of thorns, they put it on His head,\nand a reed in His right hand. And they bowed the knee before Him and\nmocked Him, saying, “Hail, King of the Jews!”30 Then they spat on Him,\nand took the reed and struck Him on the head. 31 And when they had\nmocked Him, they took the robe off Him, put His own clothes on Him,\nand led Him away to be crucified.\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"The Whipping\nLesson 7\n\nDr. C. Truman Davis, who studied crucifixion from a\nmedical perspective, describes the Roman torture: “The\nheavy whip is brought down with the full force again\nand again across the shoulders, back and legs. At first,\nthe heavy thongs cut through the skin only. As the\nblows continue, they cut deeper into the subcutaneous\ntissues, producing first an oozing of blood from the\ncapillaries and veins of the skin, and finally spurting\narterial bleeding from vessels in the underlying\nmuscles. The small balls of lead first produce large,\ndeep bruises which are broken open by subsequent\nblows. Finally the skin of the back is hanging in long\nribbons and the entire area is an unrecognizable mass\nof torn, bleeding tissue. When it is determined by the\ncenturion in charge that the prisoner is near death, the\nbeating is finally stopped.”\n\nIsaiah 53:3-7\nHe is despised and rejected by men, A Man of sorrows and acquainted\nwith grief. And we hid, as it were, our faces from Him; He was\ndespised, and we did not esteem Him. 4 Surely He has borne our griefs\nAnd carried our sorrows; Yet we esteemed Him stricken, Smitten by\nGod, and afflicted. 5 But He was wounded for our transgressions, He\nwas bruised for our iniquities; The chastisement for our peace was\nupon Him, And by His stripes we are healed. 6 All we like sheep have\ngone astray; We have turned, every one, to his own way; And the LORD\nhas laid on Him the iniquity of us all. 7 He was oppressed and He was\nafflicted, Yet He opened not His mouth; He was led as a lamb to the\nslaughter, And as a sheep before its shearers is silent, So He opened\nnot His mouth.\n\nJesus was crucified\nNote to Teacher: Watch the Hope on the trial and\ncrucifixion of Jesus\n\nJesus experienced hours of limitless pain, cycles of twisting,\njoint-rending cramps, intermittent partial asphyxiation,\nsearing pain where tissue is torn from His lacerated back\nas He moves up and down against the rough timber. Then\nanother agony begins -- a terrible crushing pain deep in the\n19\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"Lesson 7\n\nchest as the pericardium slowly fills with serum and begins to\ncompress the heart. One remembers again the 22nd Psalm, the\n14th verse: “I am poured out like water, and all my bones are\nout of joint; my heart is like wax; it is melted in the midst of my\nbowels.”\nIt is now almost over. The loss of tissue fluids has reached\na critical level; the compressed heart is struggling to pump\nheavy, thick, sluggish blood into the tissue; the tortured lungs\nare making a frantic effort to gasp in small gulps of air. The\nmarkedly dehydrated tissues send their flood of stimuli to\nthe brain. Jesus gasps His fifth cry, “I thirst.” One remembers\nanother verse from the prophetic 22nd Psalm: “My strength is\ndried up like a potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth to my jaws;\nand thou has brought me into the dust of death.” A sponge\nsoaked in posca, the cheap, sour wine which is the staple drink\nof the Roman legionaries, is lifted to His lips. He apparently\ndoesn’t take any of the liquid.\nThe body of Jesus is now in extremes, and He can feel the chill of\ndeath creeping through His tissues. “It is finished.” His mission\nof atonement has completed. Finally He can allow his body to\ndie…\nApparently, to make doubly sure of death, the legionnaire drove\nhis lance through the fifth interspace between the ribs, upward\nthrough the pericardium and into the heart. The 34th verse of\nthe 19th chapter of the Gospel according to St. John reports:\n“And immediately there came out blood and water.” That is,\nthere was an escape of water fluid from the sac surrounding\nthe heart, giving postmortem evidence that Our Lord died not\nthe usual crucifixion death by suffocation, but of heart failure (a\nbroken heart) due to shock and constriction of the heart by fluid\nin the pericardium.\nSource: Dr. C. Truman Davis, “A Physician’s View of the Crucifixion of Jesus Christ”, <http://\nwww1.cbn.com/medical-view-of-the-crucifixion-of-jesus-christ>\n\n20\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"1 Peter 2:21-24\n\nLesson 7\n\nFor to this you were called, because Christ also suffered for us, leaving\nus an example, that you should follow His steps: 22 “Who committed no\nsin, Nor was deceit found in His mouth”; 23 who, when He was reviled,\ndid not revile in return; when He suffered, He did not threaten, but\ncommitted Himself to Him who judges righteously; 24 who Himself\nbore our sins in His own body on the tree, that we, having died to sins,\nmight live for righteousness--by whose stripes you were healed.\n\nWhat was the attitude of Jesus while He was suffering on the\ncross?\nHebrews 12:2\nlooking unto Jesus, the author and finisher of our faith, who for the joy\nthat was set before Him endured the cross, despising the shame, and\nhas sat down at the right hand of the throne of God.\n\nThe Jews and Romans did not take the life of Jesus. Jesus\nwillingly offered Himself to them to fulfill His plan to save\nhumanity and restore a relationship with them.\n\nMatthew 26:53-54\nOr do you think that I cannot now pray to My Father, and He will\nprovide Me with more than twelve legions of angels? 54 How then\ncould the Scriptures be fulfilled, that it must happen thus?”\n\nThis was the hidden plan that God had prepared before time\neven began.\n\n1 Corinthians 2:7-8 (NLT)\nNo, the wisdom we speak of is the mystery of God—his plan that\nwas previously hidden, even though he made it for our ultimate\nglory before the world began. 8 But the rulers of this world have not\nunderstood it; if they had, they would not have crucified our glorious\nLord.\n\n21\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"When Jesus died, the veil of the temple was torn\nLesson 7\n\nWhen Jesus died, the veil of the Temple, which served as the\nbarrier between the dwelling place of God’s Spirit in the Most\nHoly Place and the world, ripped from top to bottom.\n\nMatthew 27:50-51\nAnd Jesus cried out again with a loud voice, and yielded up His spirit.\n51 Then, behold, the veil of the temple was torn in two from top to\nbottom; and the earth quaked, and the rocks were split\n\nThis was the sign that the sin no longer stands in the way of\nus discovering our relationship with God, through the blood\nof Jesus Christ.\n\nBurial and Resurrection\nJesus was buried in a tomb by one of his disciples.\n\nMatthew 27:57-60 (NLT)\nAs evening approached, Joseph, a rich man from Arimathea who had\nbecome a follower of Jesus, 58 went to Pilate and asked for Jesus’\nbody. And Pilate issued an order to release it to him. 59 Joseph took\nthe body and wrapped it in a long sheet of clean linen cloth. 60 He\nplaced it in his own new tomb, which had been carved out of the rock.\nThen he rolled a great stone across the entrance and left.\n\nAfter three days in the grave, Jesus came back to life and\nrevealed himself to the disciples with many infallible proofs.\n\n22\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"John 20:24-29\n\nLesson 7\n\nNow Thomas, called the Twin, one of the twelve, was not with them\nwhen Jesus came. 25 The other disciples therefore said to him, “We\nhave seen the Lord.” So he said to them, “Unless I see in His hands\nthe print of the nails, and put my finger into the print of the nails, and\nput my hand into His side, I will not believe.” 26 And after eight days\nHis disciples were again inside, and Thomas with them. Jesus came,\nthe doors being shut, and stood in the midst, and said, “Peace to you!”\n27 Then He said to Thomas, “Reach your finger here, and look at My\nhands; and reach your hand here, and put it into My side. Do not be\nunbelieving, but believing.” 28 And Thomas answered and said to Him,\n“My Lord and my God!” 29 Jesus said to him, “Thomas, because you\nhave seen Me, you have believed. Blessed are those who have not\nseen and yet have believed.”\n\nJesus’ resurrection declares God’s victory over sin and death\nand let us know that we too can experience the same victory\nthrough Jesus Christ.\n\n1 Corinthians 15:53-57 (NLT)\nFor our dying bodies must be transformed into bodies that will never\ndie; our mortal bodies must be transformed into immortal bodies. 54\nThen, when our dying bodies have been transformed into bodies that\nwill never die, this Scripture will be fulfilled: “Death is swallowed up\nin victory. 55 O death, where is your victory? O death, where is your\nsting?” 56 For sin is the sting that results in death, and the law gives\nsin its power. 57 But thank God! He gives us victory over sin and death\nthrough our Lord Jesus Christ.\n\nKey #6: The death, burial and resurrection\nof Jesus Christ is the gospel that saves Man.\n\n23\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":24,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 7\n\nRefer to Chart L7.5-5\n1. Jesus came to reverse the curse of sin and\ndestroy the work of Satan.\n2. Jesus still demonstrates His power through\nmiracles today!\n3. Jesus is still looking for disciples today.\n4. Jesus is the God of the Old Testament\nrevealed in flesh.\n5. God came in flesh to save us from our sins.\n6. The death, burial and resurrection of Jesus\nChrist is the gospel that saves Man.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n24\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":25,"text":"Charts\nLesson 7\n\n25\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":26,"text":"Charts\nLesson 7\n\n26\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":27,"text":"Charts\nLesson 7\n\n27\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":28,"text":"Lesson 7\n\nModular Section\n1. Why the Identity of Jesus Matters\n2.  What does the Scripture say about Jesus?\n3.  God is One\n4. God is Holy and He is the Spirit\n5. God is Everywhere, All Knowing, All\nPowerful\n6. God is the Father and Creator\n7. God became Flesh (The Son)\n8.  Who is Jesus?\n9. The Name of God\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":29,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nI. Why the Identity of Jesus Matters\na. The identity of Jesus Christ is the\nfoundation by which the Church is built\nupon\nMatthew 16:13-18\nWhen Jesus came into the region of Caesarea Philippi, He asked His\ndisciples, saying, “Who do men say that I, the Son of Man, am?” 14 So\nthey said, “Some say John the Baptist, some Elijah, and others Jeremiah\nor one of the prophets.” 15 He said to them, “But who do you say that\nI am?” 16 Simon Peter answered and said, “You are the Christ, the Son\nof the living God.” 17 Jesus answered and said to him, “Blessed are\nyou, Simon Bar-Jonah, for flesh and blood has not revealed this to you,\nbut My Father who is in heaven. 18 And I also say to you that you are\nPeter, and on this rock I will build My church, and the gates of Hades\nshall not prevail against it.\n\nb. It determines what true worship of God is\n\nJohn 4:22-24\nYou worship what you do not know; we know what we worship, for\nsalvation is of the Jews. 23 But the hour is coming, and now is, when\nthe true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit and truth; for the\nFather is seeking such to worship Him. 24 God is Spirit, and those who\nworship Him must worship in spirit and truth.”\n\nc. It is essential for our salvation\n\nJohn 8:24\nTherefore I said to you that you will die in your sins; for if you do not\nbelieve that I am He, you will die in your sins.”\nActs 4:12\nNor is there salvation in any other, for there is no other name under\nheaven given among men by which we must be saved.”\n\n29\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":30,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nd. It releases God’s power to work\n\nMark 6:1-6\nThen He went out from there and came to His own country, and His\ndisciples followed Him. 2 And when the Sabbath had come, He began\nto teach in the synagogue. And many hearing Him were astonished,\nsaying, “Where did this Man get these things? And what wisdom is\nthis which is given to Him, that such mighty works are performed by\nHis hands! 3 Is this not the carpenter, the Son of Mary, and brother of\nJames, Joses, Judas, and Simon? And are not His sisters here with us?”\nAnd they were offended at Him. 4 But Jesus said to them, “A prophet is\nnot without honor except in his own country, among his own relatives,\nand in his own house.” 5 Now He could do no mighty work there,\nexcept that He laid His hands on a few sick people and healed them.\n6And He marveled because of their unbelief. Then He went about the\nvillages in a circuit, teaching.\n\n“A lot of people will never get the full force, because they got Jesus in\nsecond place”\n– T.W. Barnes\n\nFaith in Jesus name released healing to a\ncrippled man.\n\nActs 3:16 (NLT)\n“Through faith in the name of Jesus, this man was healed—and you\nknow how crippled he was before. Faith in Jesus’ name has healed him\nbefore your very eyes.\nJohn 7:38\nHe who believes in Me, as the Scripture has said, out of his heart will\nflow rivers of living water.”\n\n30\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":31,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nII. What does the Scripture say\nabout Jesus?\nOur belief in who Jesus is must come from what\nthe Scriptures say about Him.\n\nJohn 5:39\nYou search the Scriptures, for in them you think you have eternal life;\nand these are they which testify of Me.\n\nLuke 24:27\nAnd beginning at Moses and all the Prophets, He expounded to them\nin all the Scriptures the things concerning Himself.\n\nJohn 1:1,14\nIn the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the\nWord was God…14 And the Word became flesh and dwelt among\nus, and we beheld His glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the\nFather, full of grace and truth.\n\nWe begin our discovery of the identity of Jesus\nby first knowing the attributes of God.\nIII. God is One\nDeuteronomy 6:4-8\n“Hear, O Israel: The LORD our God, the LORD is one! 5 You shall love\nthe LORD your God with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all\nyour strength. 6 “And these words which I command you today shall\nbe in your heart. 7 You shall teach them diligently to your children, and\nshall talk of them when you sit in your house, when you walk by the\nway, when you lie down, and when you rise up. 8 You shall bind them\nas a sign on your hand, and they shall be as frontlets between your\neyes.\n\n31\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":32,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nLORD – “I Am” or Jehovah, referencing the God\nof Israel in the Old Testament.\nThis scripture is the daily confession of faith\nfor the Jewish people, called the shema, and\nit is the fundamental truth of God. The shema\nwas given to them after their exodus from the\npolytheistic culture of Egypt and prior to their\nentry into the promise land.\nJesus quotes the shema when asked about the\ngreatest commandment.\n\nMark 12:29-31\nJesus answered him, “The first of all the commandments is: ‘Hear, O\nIsrael, the LORD our God, the LORD is one. 30 And you shall love the\nLORD your God with all your heart, with all your soul, with all your\nmind, and with all your strength.’ This is the first commandment.\n31 And the second, like it, is this: ‘You shall love your neighbor as\nyourself.’ There is no other commandment greater than these.”\n\nBoth the Old and New Testament teaches\nus that Jehovah God is one.\n\nIsaiah 43:10-11\n“You are My witnesses,” says the LORD, “And My servant whom I have\nchosen, that you may know and believe Me, and understand that I am\nHe. Before Me there was no God formed, nor shall there be after Me.\n11 I, even I, am the LORD, and besides Me there is no savior.\n\n1 Chronicles 17:20\nO LORD, there is none like You, nor is there any God besides You,\naccording to all that we have heard with our ears.\n\n32\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":33,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nIsaiah 44:8\nDo not fear, nor be afraid; Have I not told you from that time, and\ndeclared it? You are My witnesses. Is there a God besides Me? Indeed\nthere is no other Rock; I know not one.’ “\n\nJames 2:19\nYou believe that there is one God. You do well. Even the demons\nbelieve--and tremble!\n\nKey #1: There is only one God\nIV. GOD IS HOLY AND HE IS THE SPIRIT\n\nJohn 4:24\nGod is Spirit, and those who worship Him must worship in spirit and\ntruth.”\n\nSo just what is a Spirit? The Webster’s Dictionary\ndefines spirit as: “A supernatural, rational being\nusually invisible to human beings but having the\npower to become visible at will.”\n\nIsaiah 57:15\nFor thus says the High and Lofty One Who inhabits eternity, whose\nname is Holy: “I dwell in the high and holy place, With him who has a\ncontrite and humble spirit, To revive the spirit of the humble, And to\nrevive the heart of the contrite ones.\n\nHoly means that God is separate and apart\nfrom anything in this world. He is perfect and\npure and there is none like Him.\nThat is why the Bible also calls God the Holy\nSpirit.\n33\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":34,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nPsalm 51:11\nDo not cast me away from Your presence, and do not take Your Holy\nSpirit from me.\n\nKey #2: God is the Holy Spirit\n\nV. GOD IS EVERYWHERE, ALL\nKNOWING, ALL POWERFUL\na. Everywhere - Omnipresent\nBecause God is a Spirit He can be everywhere\nat the same time. And, He is the only Spirit that\nis truly omnipresent. All other spirits, such as\ndemons, angels, and Satan, are confined to only\none specific location at one time. And although\nGod is everywhere present, He is not nature\nor found and worshiped in the things we see\nbecause He isn’t many things (trees, water,\nstars, universe) in one being. He created what\nwe see, but He isn’t what we see.\n\nPsalm 139:7-10\nWhere can I go from Your Spirit? Or where can I flee from Your\npresence? 8 If I ascend into heaven, You are there; If I make my bed\nin hell, behold, You are there. 9 If I take the wings of the morning, and\ndwell in the uttermost parts of the sea, 10 Even there Your hand shall\nlead me, And Your right hand shall hold me.\n\nNote to Teacher: Describe how God can operate in\ndifferent places in different ways all by Himself. This\nis to help answer the question about Jesus’ baptism in\nthe future.\n\n34\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":35,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nb. All Knowing - Omniscient\n\nPsalm 139:1-6\nO LORD, You have searched me and known me. 2 You know my sitting\ndown and my rising up; You understand my thought afar off. 3 You\ncomprehend my path and my lying down, And are acquainted with all\nmy ways. 4 For there is not a word on my tongue, But behold, O LORD,\nYou know it altogether. 5 You have hedged me behind and before, And\nlaid Your hand upon me. 6 Such knowledge is too wonderful for me; It\nis high, I cannot attain it.\n\nThe only limitations God has are those he\nwillingly places upon Himself, resulting from\nhis moral nature. For example: He is holy and\nsinless, and He abides by His moral nature. It is\ntherefore impossible for God to lie or contradict\nHis Word\n\nc. All Powerful - Omnipotent\nGenesis 35:11\nAlso God said to him: “I am God Almighty. Be fruitful and multiply; a\nnation and a company of nations shall proceed from you, and kings\nshall come from your body.\n\nJob 42:2\n“I know that You can do everything, and that no purpose of Yours can\nbe withheld from You.\n\n35\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":36,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nVI. GOD IS THE FATHER AND\nCREATOR\nMalachi 2:10\nHave we not all one Father? Has not one God created us?\n\nIsaiah 44:24\nThus says the LORD, your Redeemer, And He who formed you from\nthe womb: “I am the LORD, who makes all things, Who stretches out\nthe heavens all alone, Who spreads abroad the earth by Myself;\n\nIsaiah 45:18\nFor thus says the LORD, Who created the heavens, Who is God, Who\nformed the earth and made it, Who has established it, Who did not\ncreate it in vain, Who formed it to be inhabited: “I am the LORD, and\nthere is no other.\n\nRomans 8:14-16\nor as many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are sons of God. 15\nFor you did not receive the spirit of bondage again to fear, but you\nreceived the Spirit of adoption by whom we cry out, “Abba, Father.” 16\nThe Spirit Himself bears witness with our spirit that we are children of\nGod\n\nGod is called Father because He is the creator\nof humanity. He is also the Father of those who\nhave been born again into His kingdom. He\nis the Father of the baby that was born from\nMary’s womb because it is the Holy Spirit who\ncaused the conception.\n\n36\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":37,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nKey #3: God is the Father\nVII. GOD BECAME FLESH (THE SON)\nGod became flesh to save Man from their\nsins and to reconcile them to Him (without\nthe shedding of innocent blood, there is no\nremission of sins)\n\nIsaiah 59:15-16\nSo truth fails, and he who departs from evil makes himself a prey.\nThen the LORD saw it, and it displeased Him That there was no justice.\n16 He saw that there was no man, and wondered that there was no\nintercessor; Therefore His own arm brought salvation for Him; And His\nown righteousness, it sustained Him.\n\n2 Corinthians 5:18-19\nNow all things are of God, who has reconciled us to Himself through\nJesus Christ, and has given us the ministry of reconciliation, 19 that is,\nthat God was in Christ reconciling the world to Himself, not imputing\ntheir trespasses to them, and has committed to us the word of\nreconciliation.\n\nMatthew 1:21-23\nAnd she will bring forth a Son, and you shall call His name JESUS, for\nHe will save His people from their sins.” 22 So all this was done that it\nmight be fulfilled which was spoken by the Lord through the prophet,\nsaying: 23 “Behold, the virgin shall be with child, and bear a Son, and\nthey shall call His name Immanuel,” which is translated, “God with us.”\n\nNote to Teacher: Matthew 1:21-23 fulfills an Old\nTestament prophecy in Isaiah 7:14 of Messiah being\nborn of a virgin and called Immanuel.\n\n37\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":38,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nKey #4: God became flesh to save us from\nour sins. This flesh is called the Son of God.\n\nIsaiah 9:6\nFor unto us a Child is born, unto us a Son is given; And the government\nwill be upon His shoulder. And His name will be called Wonderful,\nCounsellor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.\n\nVIII. WHO IS JESUS\n\n2 Corinthians 4:4\nwhose minds the god of this age has blinded, who do not believe, lest\nthe light of the gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God,\nshould shine on them.\n\nColossians 1:15\nHe is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn over all creation.\n\nJohn 14:7-9\n“If you had known Me, you would have known My Father also; and\nfrom now on you know Him and have seen Him.” 8 Philip said to Him,\n“Lord, show us the Father, and it is sufficient for us.” 9 Jesus said to\nhim, “Have I been with you so long, and yet you have not known Me,\nPhilip? He who has seen Me has seen the Father; so how can you say,\n‘Show us the Father’?\n\nKey #5: Jesus is the image of the invisible\nGod\n\n38\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":39,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\na. Jesus is called Lord and God\n\nJohn 20:28\nAnd Thomas answered and said to Him, “My Lord and my God!”\n\nColossians 2:9-10\nFor in Him dwells all the fullness of the Godhead bodily; 10 and you\nare complete in Him, who is the head of all principality and power.\n\n1 Timothy 3:16\nAnd without controversy great is the mystery of godliness: God was\nmanifested in the flesh, Justified in the Spirit, Seen by angels, Preached\namong the Gentiles, Believed on in the world, Received up in glory.\n\nb. Jesus is the Saviour of the world\n\n2 Peter 1:1\nSimon Peter, a bondservant and apostle of Jesus Christ, to those who\nhave obtained like precious faith with us by the righteousness of our\nGod and Savior Jesus Christ\n\nJehovah in the Old Testament said that besides\nHimself, there is no Savior.\n\n39\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":40,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nIsaiah 43:10-11\n“You are My witnesses,” says the LORD, “And My servant whom I have\nchosen, that you may know and believe Me, And understand that I am\nHe. Before Me there was no God formed, nor shall there be after Me.\n11 I, even I, am the LORD, and besides Me there is no savior.\n\nc. Jesus is both God and Man\n\nHebrews 2:17-18\nTherefore, in all things He had to be made like His brethren, that He\nmight be a merciful and faithful High Priest in things pertaining to\nGod, to make propitiation for the sins of the people. 18 For in that He\nHimself has suffered, being tempted, He is able to aid those who are\ntempted.\n\n40\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":41,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nBy correctly understanding that Jesus was\nboth fully God and fully man will answer most\nquestions about the Godhead. We can read\nScripture about Jesus and determine whether\nit describes his Deity or humanity or both; we\ncan read when Jesus speaks and determine\nwhether He speaks as a man or as God, or both.\nSince there is only one God, we cannot think of\ntwo persons in the Godhead or two Gods, but\nwe must think of the divine Spirit and authentic\nhuman flesh.\nIX. THE NAME OF GOD\n\nZechariah 14:9\nAnd the LORD shall be King over all the earth. In that day it shall be-“The LORD is one,” And His name one.\n\nBy reading the Bible from Genesis to Revelation,\nwe discover that God used names and titles\nto reveal new things about Himself (Jehovah,\nthe I AM, etc.). Each new name and title helped\ndefine the new way they would know Him and\nhow He would relate to them.\n\n41\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":42,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 7\n\nAfter God became flesh and revealed Himself\nas Jesus, the Bible never again reveals a new\nname! Jesus (meaning Jehovah is become my\nSalvation) is the complete and final name given\nto redeem mankind and reveal the One God.\n\nActs 4:12\nNor is there salvation in any other, for there is no other name under\nheaven given among men by which we must be saved.”\n\nColossians 3:17\nAnd whatever you do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord\nJesus, giving thanks to God the Father through Him.\n\nKey #6: Jesus is the revealed name of the\none God\n\n42\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"8":{"lesson":8,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":38,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 8\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will be able to explain what the\ngospel is and how to obey the gospel\n\n•\n\nThe student will be able to tell us how baptism\nis administered in the original Church\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will demonstrate a desire to\nrepent and be water baptised in Jesus name.\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience\n\nAge of Human Government\n\nAge of Law\n\nAge of Promise\n\nChurch Age\n\nCast (Characters)\nJesus, 120 at the Upper Room (this includes 11 apostles,\nMary, Brothers of Jesus, and women), Jews in Jerusalem\nvisiting on the Day of Pentecost, Paul, Philip, converts\nin Samaria, converts from Cornelius’ household, former\ndisciples of John the Baptist\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 8\n\nLesson Background\nJesus had just resurrected from the tomb and had given his\napostles his final words by commissioning them to preach\nthe gospel, repentance and remission of sins in His name.\nThey were then told to wait in Jerusalem for the promise of\nthe Holy Spirit.\n\nLuke 24:46-49\nThen He said to them, “Thus it is written, and thus it was necessary\nfor the Christ to suffer and to rise from the dead the third day, 47\nand that repentance and remission of sins should be preached in\nHis name to all nations, beginning at Jerusalem. 48 And you are\nwitnesses of these things. 49 Behold, I send the Promise of My Father\nupon you; but tarry in the city of Jerusalem until you are endued with\npower from on high.”\nActs 1:1-5 (NLT)\nIn my first book I told you, Theophilus, about everything Jesus began\nto do and teach 2 until the day he was taken up to heaven after\ngiving his chosen apostles further instructions through the Holy\nSpirit. 3 During the forty days after his crucifixion, he appeared to\nthe apostles from time to time, and he proved to them in many ways\nthat he was actually alive. And he talked to them about the Kingdom\nof God. 4 Once when he was eating with them, he commanded\nthem, “Do not leave Jerusalem until the Father sends you the gift he\npromised, as I told you before. 5 John baptized with water, but in just\na few days you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.”\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"Lesson 8\n\nLesson Outline\nA. New Testament Plan of Salvation\n\n4\n\nB. True Biblical Faith Consist of Knowledge,\nAgreement and Obedience\n\n8\n\nC. Repentance\n\n11\n\nD. Water Baptism\n\n12\n\nE. Purpose of Baptism\n\n14\n\nF. Baptisms by the Early Church\n\n18\n\nG. The Name of Jesus in Baptism\n\n20\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"A\n\nNEW TESTAMENT PLAN OF\nSALVATION\n\nLesson 8\n\nRefer to Chart L8 . 1-4\nIn each time period, God has given men and\nwomen a very specific pathway of Salvation.\nWith Noah, it was the ark. With Abraham, it\nwas circumcision. With the Israelites, it was the\nTabernacle. And with us, it is the New Testament\npathway of Salvation, the New Birth, as taught by\nJesus and His Apostles.\n\nKey #1: God has a specific\nplan for salvation today!\nJust like with Noah, Abraham, and the Tabernacle,\nthe common principles of salvation include Grace,\nFaith and Obedience.\nFor example, in the story of Noah, what saved\nNoah and his family? Was it grace, faith and\nobedience?\n\nHebrews 11:7\nBy faith Noah, being divinely warned of things not yet seen, moved\nwith godly fear, prepared an ark for the saving of his household,\nby which he condemned the world and became heir of the\nrighteousness which is according to faith.\n\n4\n\n•\n\nIt was God’s grace that divinely warned Noah\nand gave Him a plan.\n\n•\n\nHowever, it was Noah’s faith that responded to\nGod’s word.\n\n•\n\nNoah and his family had to prepare an ark upon\nbelieving God’s warning. He had to obey God.\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"What is Grace?\nLesson 8\n\nEphesians 2:8\nFor by grace you have been saved through faith, and that not of\nyourselves; it is the gift of God,\n\nAlthough there are a few definitions of grace, in the\ncontext of salvation, grace is:\n•\n\nThe unmerited favor of God towards man\n\n•\n\nIt’s God’s free gift to many\n\nGrace and Salvation\n•\n\nSalvation is an undeserved, unearned blessing\nthat God bestows freely\n\n•\n\nGod does all the work involved in saving a soul\nfrom start to finish\n\n•\n\nNobody can say that “I deserved salvation”\n\n•\n\nMan’s salvation is a product of God’s grace from\nstart to finish.\n\n•\n\nGrace provided the plan and sacrifice for us to\nbe saved\n\n•\n\nGrace came in the person of Jesus Christ who\nbecame our sacrifice for sin.\n\nJohn 1:17\nFor the law was given through Moses, [but] grace and truth came\nthrough Jesus Christ.\nRomans 3:24-25\nbeing justified freely by His grace through the redemption that is\nin Christ Jesus, 25 whom God set forth [as] a propitiation by His\nblood, through faith, to demonstrate His righteousness, because in\nHis forbearance God had passed over the sins that were previously\ncommitted,\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"Even though Jesus Christ died for the whole\nworld, not everyone is automatically saved.\nLesson 8\n\nWe need to have faith in Jesus Christ to be saved\nJust as grace alone does not save us, we need to\nhave faith in Jesus Christ to be saved.\nJohn 3:16\nFor God so loved the world that He gave His only begotten Son, that\nwhoever believes in Him should not perish but have everlasting life.\n\nWhat does it mean to believe in Christ?\n•\n\nIt means believing that He is our Lord and Savior\n\n•\n\nIt also means believing that His words contain\nthe words of eternal life. Jesus taught us how we\nare to enter the kingdom of God.\n\nJohn 3:3-5\nJesus answered and said to him, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless\none is born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God.” 4 Nicodemus\nsaid to Him, “How can a man be born when he is old? Can he\nenter a second time into his mother’s womb and be born?” 5 Jesus\nanswered, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless one is born of water\nand the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God.\n\nThere are two components of the New Birth: Born\nof Water and Born of Spirit. In the following two\nlessons, we will unpack what these two terms\nmean.\n•\n\n6\n\nBelieving in Christ means we believe in His\ndeath, burial and resurrection which we call\n“Gospel”.\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Romans 1:16\n\nLesson 8\n\nFor I am not ashamed of the gospel of Christ, for it is the power of\nGod to salvation for everyone who believes, for the Jew first and also\nfor the Greek.\n1 Corinthians 15:1-4\nMoreover, brethren, I declare to you the gospel which I preached\nto you, which also you received and in which you stand, 2 by which\nalso you are saved, if you hold fast that word which I preached to\nyou--unless you believed in vain. 3 For I delivered to you first of all\nthat which I also received: that Christ died for our sins according\nto the Scriptures, 4 and that He was buried, and that He rose again\nthe third day according to the Scriptures, The Gospel is good news\nbecause it is the message of salvation to those who are bound in\nthe prison of sin. The Gospel announces to us that the God of the\nuniverse, robed Himself in flesh – Jesus Christ, and died on a cross to\nredeem lost mankind through Death, Burial and Resurrection.\n\nThe Gospel is good news because it is the message\nof salvation to those who are bound in the prison of\nsin. The Gospel announces to us that the God of the\nuniverse, robed Himself in flesh – Jesus Christ, and\ndied on a cross to redeem lost mankind through\nDeath, Burial and Resurrection.\n\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"B\nLesson 8\n\nTRUE BIBLICAL FAITH CONSIST OF\nKNOWLEDGE, AGREEMENT AND\nOBEDIENCE.\nKnowledge\nRomans 10:14, 17\nHow then shall they call on Him in whom they have not believed?\nAnd how shall they believe in Him of whom they have not heard?\nAnd how shall they hear without a preacher? 17 So then faith comes\nby hearing, and hearing by the word of God.\n\nAt the birth of the Church on the Day of\nPentecost (Acts 2:1-4), Peter addressed the Jewish\ncrowd who witnessed this miracle by telling\nthem about the message of Jesus’ death and\nresurrection. He ended up declaring that Jesus is\nboth Lord and Christ.\n\nActs 2:22-24, 36\n“Men of Israel, hear these words: Jesus of Nazareth, a Man attested\nby God to you by miracles, wonders, and signs which God did\nthrough Him in your midst, as you yourselves also know-- 23 Him,\nbeing delivered by the determined purpose and foreknowledge\nof God, you have taken by lawless hands, have crucified, and put\nto death; 24 whom God raised up, having loosed the pains of\ndeath, because it was not possible that He should be held by it… 36\n“Therefore let all the house of Israel know assuredly that God has\nmade this Jesus, whom you crucified, both Lord and Christ.”\n\nWhen we choose to believe the Word that is\npreached to us, we need to agree with the Word of\nGod. Faith alone is not enough to save us.\n\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"James 2:17-20\n\nLesson 8\n\nThus also faith by itself, if it does not have works, is dead. 18 But\nsomeone will say, “You have faith, and I have works.” Show me your\nfaith without your works, and I will show you my faith by my works.\n19 You believe that there is one God. You do well. Even the demons\nbelieve--and tremble! 20 But do you want to know, O foolish man,\nthat faith without works is dead?\n\nAgreement\nActs 2:37\nNow when they heard this, they were cut to the heart, and said to\nPeter and the rest of the apostles, “Men and brethren, what shall we\ndo?”\n\nThis is the most important question for all those\nwho hear the gospel. Their conviction and response\nlet us know that they are in agreement with the\nmessage of the gospel.\nBut true agreement with God require us to obey His\nWord.\n\nMatthew 7:21\n“Not everyone who says to Me, ‘Lord, Lord,’ shall enter the kingdom\nof heaven, but he who does the will of My Father in heaven.\nHebrews 5:9\nAnd having been perfected, He became the author of eternal\nsalvation to all who obey Him\n\nKey #2: We need to believe and\nobey the gospel to be saved.\n\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"Lesson 8\n\nJust like Noah’s day, it requires God’s grace\nworking with our faith and obedience to bring\nabout our New Testament salvation. Jesus came\nto die for humanity on the cross. It was through\nHis grace that salvation was offered to the world.\nBut because God gave Man the freedom of\nchoice, they still have to believe God’s message\nand obey His commandments to receive this free\ngift of salvation.\n\nObedience\nPaul then gave them instruction on how they can\nobey the gospel.\n\nActs 2:38\nThen Peter said to them, “Repent, and let every one of you be\nbaptized in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins; and\nyou shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.\n\nJust as there are 3 parts to the Gospel, there are\nalso 3 parts to obeying the gospel”\n\nRefer to Chart L8 . 2-4\n\nKey #3: We obey the Gospel through\nRepentance, Water Baptism in Jesus name\nand being filled with the Holy Spirit.\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"C\nLesson 8\n\nREPENTANCE\nWe obey the death portion of the Gospel through\nrepentance. In repentance, I die to my old life; my\nold faith. I die to my own will and say yes to God.\nRepentance comes from the Greek word\nmetanoeo which means “a change of mind”.\nRepentance is turning to God so that we can turn\nfrom sin.\nRepentance is the will of God\n\n2 Peter 3:9\nThe Lord is not slack concerning His promise, as some count\nslackness, but is longsuffering toward us, not willing that any should\nperish but that all should come to repentance.\nLuke 13:3\nI tell you, no; but unless you repent you will all likewise perish.\n\nRepentance will lead us to God’s truth\n\n2 Timothy 2:25\n… if God perhaps will grant them repentance, so that they may know\nthe truth\n2 Corinthians 7:10\nFor godly sorrow produces repentance leading to salvation, not to be\nregretted; but the sorrow of the world produces death\n\nRepentance is humbling oneself and\nacknowledging that you need God\n\nMatthew 5:3\n“Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"Repentance activates God’s mercy\nLesson 8\nProverbs 28:13\nHe who covers his sins will not prosper, but whoever confesses and\nforsakes them will have mercy.\n\nThe fruit of true repentance is a change in action\n\nActs 2:37\nNow when they heard this, they were cut to the heart, and said to Peter\nand the rest of the apostles, “Men and brethren, what shall we do?”\n\nKey #4: We experience the death of our old\nlife of sin through our choice of repentance.\n\nD\n\nWATER BAPTISM\nWe obey the burial portion of the Gospel through\nwater baptism.\n\nRomans 6:3-5\nOr do you not know that as many of us as were baptized into Christ\nJesus were baptized into His death? 4 Therefore we were buried with\nHim through baptism into death, that just as Christ was raised from\nthe dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in\nnewness of life. 5 For if we have been united together in the likeness of\nHis death, certainly we also shall be in the likeness of His resurrection.\n\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"Lesson 8\n\nKey #5: We experience burial to our old life/\nnature in water baptism.\n\nWhat does it mean to be baptised?\nThe word baptism comes from the Greek word\n“baptizo” which means to immerse, submerge, to\nmake overwhelmed (fully wet).\n\nNote to teachers: See modular lesson “Immersed or\nSprinkled”\n\nExample of Baptism:\n\nActs 8:26-38\nNow an angel of the Lord spoke to Philip, saying, “Arise and go\ntoward the south along the road which goes down from Jerusalem\nto Gaza.” This is desert. 27 So he arose and went. And behold, a man\nof Ethiopia, a eunuch of great authority under Candace the queen of\nthe Ethiopians, who had charge of all her treasury, and had come to\nJerusalem to worship, 28 was returning. And sitting in his chariot, he\nwas reading Isaiah the prophet. 29 Then the Spirit said to Philip, “Go\nnear and overtake this chariot.” 30 So Philip ran to him, and heard\nhim reading the prophet Isaiah, and said, “Do you understand what\nyou are reading?” 31 And he said, “How can I, unless someone guides\nme?” And he asked Philip to come up and sit with him. 32 The place in\nthe Scripture which he read was this: “He was led as a sheep to the\nslaughter; And as a lamb before its shearer is silent, So He opened\nnot His mouth. 33 In His humiliation His justice was taken away, and\nwho will declare His generation? For His life is taken from the earth.”\n34\nSo the eunuch answered Philip and said, “I ask you, of whom does\nthe prophet say this, of himself or of some other man?” 35 Then Philip\nopened his mouth, and beginning at this Scripture, preached Jesus to\nhim. 36 Now as they went down the road, they came to some water.\nAnd the eunuch said, “See, here is water. What hinders me from\nbeing baptized?” 37 Then Philip said, “If you believe with all your heart,\nyou may.” And he answered and said, “I believe that Jesus Christ\nis the Son of God.” 38 So he commanded the chariot to stand still.\nAnd both Philip and the eunuch went down into the water, and he\nbaptized him.\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"Lesson 8\n\n•\n\nThey were in a desert, a place that lacks water\n\n•\n\nThey obeyed God despite the inconvenience of\nfinding water\n\n•\n\nThe criteria for Ethiopian being baptize is His\nfaith in who Jesus is\n\n•\n\nFaith is necessary in baptism\n\n•\n\nBaptism is the obedience that proves true faith\n\nMark 16:16\nHe who believes and is baptized will be saved; but he who does not\nbelieve will be condemned.\n\nE\n\nPURPOSE OF BAPTISM\nWashes away our sins\n\nActs 22:16\nAnd now why are you waiting? Arise and be baptized, and wash away\nyour sins, calling on the name of the Lord.’\n\nRemission of sins\nRemission means my sins are forgiven,\npardon and removed. I receive deliverance\nfrom God.\n\nActs 2:38\nThen Peter said to them, “Repent, and let every one of you be\nbaptized in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins; and\nyou shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"Puts us in Christ\nLesson 8\n\nThe Word of God tells us that eternal life and\nsalvation is found in Christ.\n\n1 John 5:11\nAnd this is the testimony: that God has given us eternal life, and this\nlife is in His Son.\n2 Timothy 2:10\n…that they also may obtain the salvation which is in Christ Jesus with\neternal glory.\n\nSo how do I get into Christ?\n\nGalatians 3:27\nFor as many of you as were baptized into Christ have put on Christ.\n\nBeing in Christ also means I am also in the\nBody of Christ.\n\nActs 2:41\nThen those who gladly received his word were baptized; and that day\nabout three thousand souls were added to them.\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"This is where we contact the blood of Jesus\nLesson 8\n\nMatthew 26:28\nFor this is My blood of the new covenant, which is shed for many for\nthe remission of sins.\nActs 2:38 (KJV)\nThen Peter said unto them, Repent, and be baptized every one of\nyou in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins, and ye shall\nreceive the gift of the Holy Ghost.\nRevelation 1:5\nTo Him who loved us and washed us from our sins in His own blood\n\nWhen we look at Matthew 26:28, it says our\nsins are remitted by the blood of Jesus. While\nin Acts 2:38, Peter says that water baptism in\nJesus name remits sin. There seems to be a\ncontraction.\nSo what washes our sin? Blood or Water\nbaptism?\nThe answer is both. The blood of Jesus is\napplied to us when we are baptised in jesus\nname.\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Saves us\nLesson 8\n\n1 Peter 3:21\nThere is also an antitype which now saves us--baptism (not the\nremoval of the filth of the flesh, but the answer of a good conscience\ntoward God)…\nMark 16:16\nHe who believes and is baptized will be saved; but he who does not\nbelieve will be condemned.\n\nIf I truly believe in God and His Word, my\nbelief would lead to my obedience. It is not\njust the water or the act alone that saves us,\nbut my faith and surrender to God that does.\n\nBurial of our old life of sin\n\nRomans 6:4-6\nTherefore we were buried with Him through baptism into death, that\njust as Christ was raised from the dead by the glory of the Father,\neven so we also should walk in newness of life.\n\nWater baptism is one of the two parts of the\nnew birth in Christ (John 3:5).\n\nPuts us in covenant with God\n\nColossians 2:11-12\nIn Him you were also circumcised with the circumcision made\nwithout hands, by putting off the body of the sins of the flesh, by the\ncircumcision of Christ, 12 buried with Him in baptism, in which you\nalso were raised with Him through faith in the working of God, who\nraised Him from the dead.\n\n17\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"F\nLesson 8\n\nBAPTISMS BY THE EARLY CHURCH\nJews\nActs 2:37-41\nNow when they heard this, they were cut to the heart, and said to\nPeter and the rest of the apostles, “Men and brethren, what shall we\ndo?” 38 Then Peter said to them, “Repent, and let every one of you be\nbaptized in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins; and\nyou shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit. 39 For the promise is to\nyou and to your children, and to all who are afar off, as many as the\nLord our God will call.” 40 And with many other words he testified and\nexhorted them, saying, “Be saved from this perverse generation.” 41\nThen those who gladly received his word were baptized; and that day\nabout three thousand souls were added to them.\n\nSamaritans (Half Jews, Half Gentiles)\n\nActs 8:5, 12, 16\nThen Philip went down to the city of Samaria and preached Christ to\nthem….12But when they believed Philip as he preached the things\nconcerning the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, both men\nand women were baptized… 16 For as yet He had fallen upon none of\nthem. They had only been baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus.\n\nGentiles\n\nActs 10:44-48\nWhile Peter was still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell upon\nall those who heard the word. 45 And those of the circumcision who\nbelieved were astonished, as many as came with Peter, because\nthe gift of the Holy Spirit had been poured out on the Gentiles also.\n46\nFor they heard them speak with tongues and magnify God. Then\nPeter answered, 47 “Can anyone forbid water, that these should not\nbe baptized who have received the Holy Spirit just as we have?” 48\nAnd he commanded them to be baptized in the name of the Lord.\nThen they asked him to stay a few days.\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"Disciples of John the Baptist (Re-baptized)\nLesson 8\nActs 19:1-5\nAnd it happened, while Apollos was at Corinth, that Paul, having\npassed through the upper regions, came to Ephesus. And finding\nsome disciples 2 he said to them, “Did you receive the Holy Spirit\nwhen you believed?” So they said to him, “We have not so much as\nheard whether there is a Holy Spirit.” 3 And he said to them, “Into\nwhat then were you baptized?” So they said, “Into John’s baptism.” 4\nThen Paul said, “John indeed baptized with a baptism of repentance,\nsaying to the people that they should believe on Him who would\ncome after him, that is, on Christ Jesus.” 5 When they heard this, they\nwere baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus.\n\nQuestion: In what name was baptism administered in\nall these instances?\n\n19\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"G\nLesson 8\n\nTHE NAME OF JESUS IN BAPTISM\nIn Bible days, a name was usually chosen for its\nmeaning. It bears the identity, nature and authority\nof the individual. God also uses His name to reveal\nHimself and to bring salvation to humanity.\n\nPsalm 54:1\n…Save me, O God, by Your name, and vindicate me by Your strength.\nActs 4:12\nNor is there salvation in any other, for there is no other name under\nheaven given among men by which we must be saved.”\nLuke 24:46-47\nThen He said to them, “Thus it is written, and thus it was necessary\nfor the Christ to suffer and to rise from the dead the third day, 47 and\nthat repentance and remission of sins should be preached in His\nname to all nations, beginning at Jerusalem.\n\nKey #6: The only Biblical way to\nbe baptized is in Jesus name.\n\nNote to teachers: See modular lesson “Baptism in\nJesus name”\n\nPhilippians 2:10-11\nthat at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of those in heaven,\nand of those on earth, and of those under the earth, 11 and that\nevery tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of\nGod the Father.\nColossians 3:17\nAnd whatever you do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord\nJesus, giving thanks to God the Father through Him.\n\n20\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"What about Matthew 28:19?\nMatthew 28:19 NKJV\n\nLesson 8\n\nGo therefore and make disciples of all the nations, baptizing them in\nthe name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit\n\nSome have stated that baptism should be done\nby invoking the titles “Father, Son and Holy Spirit”.\nIs this verse in contradiction to the commands of\nJesus in Luke 24, Mark 16 and how the apostles\nbaptized in the Book of Acts?\nContext\n\nMatthew 28:18-20\nAnd Jesus came and spoke to them, saying, “All authority has\nbeen given to Me in heaven and on earth. Go therefore and make\ndisciples of all the nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father\nand of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, teaching them to observe all\nthings that I have commanded you; and lo, I am with you always,\neven to the end of the age.” Amen.\n\n21\n\n•\n\nJesus declared that He has all authority.\nTherefore, it is natural to conclude that baptism\nshould be done in His authority and name.\n\n•\n\nMatthew mentions a singular name that we are\nto be baptized in\n\n•\n\nFather, Son and Holy Spirit are not names but\nrather titles\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"The name of the Father, Son and Holy Spirit\n1. The name of the Father\nLesson 8\n\nJesus came to reveal the name of the Father.\n\nJohn 5:43\nI have come in My Father’s name\nJohn 17:6\n“I have manifested Your name to the men whom You have given Me\nout of the world.\n\n2. The name of the Son\n\nMatthew 1:21\nAnd she will bring forth a Son, and you shall call His name JESUS, for\nHe will save His people from their sins.”\n\n3. The name of the Holy Spirit\n\nJohn 14:26\nBut the Helper, the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in My\nname, He will teach you all things, and bring to your remembrance\nall things that I said to you.\n\nWhen we are baptized in the name of Jesus, we\nare obeying Matthew’s command to baptize in the\nname of the Father, Son and Holy Spirit. There is no\ncontradiction to his command!\n\nActs 22:16\nAnd now why are you waiting? Arise and be baptized, and wash away\nyour sins, calling on the name of the Lord.’\n\n22\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"Lesson 8\n\nNote to teachers: You can end the lesson by sharing\nyour repentance and baptism experience. You can also\nshare about your life before and after conversion.\n\nSummary of Lesson\nRefer to Chart L8 . 4-4\n\n1. God has a specific plan for salvation today.\n2. We need to believe and obey the gospel to\nbe saved.\n3. We obey the Gospel through Repentance,\nWater Baptism in Jesus name and being\nfilled with the Holy Spirit.\n4. We experience the death of our old life of\nsin through our choice of repentance.\n5. We experience burial to our old life/nature\nin water baptism.\n6. The only Biblical way to be baptized is in\nJesus name.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n23\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":24,"text":"Charts\nLesson 8\n\n24\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":25,"text":"Charts\nLesson 8\n\n25\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":26,"text":"Lesson 8\n\nModular Section\n1. Immerse or Sprinkle\n2. Baptism in the name of Jesus Christ\n3. The Sinner’s Prayer\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":27,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nI. Immerse or Sprinkle\n\nBAPTIZO – GREEK\n\nRHANTIZO – GREEK\n\nImmersion (Greek “baptizo”)\n\nSprinkling (Greek “Rhantizo”)\n\nMuch water – John 3:23\n\nNONE\n\nInto the water – Acts 8:38\nOut of the water – Acts 8:39\nBuried in water – Romans 6:4\nPlanted in water – Romans 6:5\n\nThese are writings from imminent Bible scholars\nand authorities on this subject. Most of these\nreferences can be found in your local library.\nGREEK\n\n27\n\nGREEK-ENGLISH LEXICON by\nLIDDEL, SCOTT & THAYER\n\nRHANTIZO – GREEK\n\nImmersion (Greek “baptizo”)\n\nBaptism taken from Greek word\nBaptizo – to Dip, Immerse\n\nCLASSIC GREEK-ENGLISH DIC. By\nPOLLET\n\nGreek word baptizo means to dip\nunder.\n\nGREEK-ENGLISH DIC. by DIVRY’S\n\nGreek word baptizo – to immerse\n\nEMPHATIC DIAGLOTT CONTAINS\nORIGINAL GREEK TEXT\n\nIn every instance, the Greek word\nbaptizo is translated\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":28,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nAUTHORITIES\nSCHAFF-HERZOG\n\nBaptism was always a burial.\nThe command to baptize was a\ncommand to immerse.\nVol.1, Pg. 451.\n\nRELIGIOUS ENCY. RELIGIOUS\nENCY. OF BIBLE\n\nImmersion was oldest method\nemployed.\nBuried in Baptism Romans 6:4\nPg. 61. Paragraph 2.\n\nENCYCLOPEDIA DIC\n\nIt is evident that the action\nperformed in baptizing was\nimmersion. Pg. 202.\n\nWORLD BOOK ENCYCLOPEDIA\n\nThe early church practiced\nimmersion or submerging under\nthe water.\nVolume 2, Pg. 70\n\nENCYCLOPEDIA OF LUTHERAN\nCHURCH\n\nMartin Luther preferred\nimmersion as more true to original\npractice.\nVolume 1, Pg 188.\n\nPULPIT COMMENTARY\n\nRomans 6:4 “Buried in Baptism.”\nThe reference is to baptism by\nimmersion.\nVolume 18, Pg 156.\n\nLOGIC\nAn important factor is overlooked by the\nexponents of sprinkling. The original New\nTestament text and the spoken language of\nthat day was Greek. The authors of the New\nTestament knew the Greek word “Baptizo”\nmeant to immerse. They also knew the Greek\nword “Rhantizo” meant to sprinkle. These oftenused words were never interchangeable, having\nseparate meanings. If GOD had intended for HIS\nministers to sprinkle, the Greek word “Rhantizo”\nwould have been employed, not “Baptizo.\n\n28\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":29,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nACCORDING TO ENCYCLOPAEDIA &\nTHESAURUS\nAccording to Roget’s International Thesaurus,\n4th edition, the word Baptism means the same\nas immersion 320. 2. The meanings in that\ncategory are as follows:\nPlunge, submergence, submersion, immersion,\nimmergence, engulfment, inundation, burial,\ndipping, ducking, dousing, sousing, sinking,\ndunking, duck, souse.\n320.7 category as follows:\nSubmerge, submerse, immerse, immerge,\nmerge, sink, bury, engulf, inundate, deluge,\ndrown, overwhelm, dip, duck, dunk, souse,\nplunge in water, baptize.\nReader’ Digest Great Encyclopaedia Dictionary:\nBaptism = 1. > The act of baptizing or being\nbaptized; especially the Christian sacrament\nof initiation, symbolizing rebirth and\npurification, commitment to CHRIST 2. > Any\ninitiatory or purifying experience. 3. > Any\nreligious ablution, signifying a purification or\nconsecration. Of baptesme<<LL\nbaptismus<<\nGreek Baptismos Immersion.\nBaptise = To immerse in water or pour or\nsprinkle water in Christian baptism.\nTo administer baptism of baptizer <LL baptizer\ninto Immerse, wash.\nEven though meanings in the dictionary explain\ndifferent modes of what later developed\nin baptismal history, it plainly shows it still\noriginally came from the root meaning of\nimmersion.\n\n29\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":30,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nA clear picture is illustrated of the early Church’s\nbaptismal practice. In at least nine instances in\nthe Book of Acts, people were baptized as soon\nas they heard and responded to the Gospel\nmessage. Let’s check the record.\nScripture\n\nAgent\n\nBelievers\n\nPlace\n\nHow soon\n\nActs 2:37-41\n\nPeter and the\nApostles\n\n3,000 Believer\n\nJerusalem\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 8:12\n\nPhilip\n\nAll Believers\n\nSamaria\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 8:36-39\n\nPhilip\n\nEthiopian Church\n\nDesert of\nGaza\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 9:18\n\nAnanias\n\nSaul of Tarsus\n\nDamascus\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 10:44-48\n\nPeter\n\nCornelius Family\n\nCaesarea\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 16:14-15\n\nPaul\n\nLydia and woman\n\nThyatira\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 16:32-34\n\nPaul and Silas Philippian jailer\n\nPhilippi\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 18:8\n\nPaul\n\nCrispus and others\n\nEphesus\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nActs 19:1-6\n\nPaul\n\nTwelve disciples of\nJohn the Baptist\n\nEphesus\n\nImmediate after\nrepentance\n\nBAPTISM IS IMPORTANT AND SHOULD BE\nADMINISTERED ACCORDING TO SCRIPTURE\n[Matthew 3:1-2; Matthew 3:5-6] = The ministry\nof John the Baptist included baptism.\n[Matthew 29:19 and Luke 24:47] = The LAST\nmessage preached by JESUS was a command\nto baptize all nations in HIS NAME for the\nRemission of sins.\n[Acts 2:38] = The First message preached by the\nApostles resulted in a command for everyone to\nbaptize in JESUS Name\n[Mark 16:16] = Baptism is for all Believers.\n\n30\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":31,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nII. BAPTISM IN THE NAME OF JESUS\nCHRIST\nRefer to Chart L8 . 3-4\nBelow Are Two Columns Listing the Scripture\nWhere The Apostles Either Taught or Practiced\nWater Baptism\nIN JESUS NAME\n\nIN FATHER SON AND\nHOLY SPIRIT\n\nActs 2:38\n“Then Peter said unto them, Repent and be\nbaptized everyone of you in the Name of\nJESUS CHRIST for the remission of sins.”\nActs 8:16\n“For as yet he was fallen upon none of\nthem: only they were baptized in the Name\nof the LORD JESUS.”\nActs 10:48\n“And he commanded them to be baptized\nin the Name of the LORD JESUS.”\nRomans 6:3\n“Know ye not that so many of us as we were\nbaptized into JESUS CHRIST were baptized\ninto HIS death?”\nActs 19:5\n“When they heard this they were baptized\nin the Name of the LORD JESUS.”\n1Corinthians 6:11\n“But ye are washed, but ye are sanctified,\nbut ye are justified in the Name of the\nLORD JESUS…….”\nActs 4:12\n“Neither is there salvation in any other: for\nthere is none other NAME under heaven\ngiven among men whereby we must be\nsaved.”\nColossians 3:17\n“And whatsoever ye do in word deed, do all\nin the NAME of the LORD JESUS.”\nMatthew 28:19\n“Go therefore, and teach all nations,\nbaptizing them in the NAME of the Father,\nand of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost:”\nEphesians 4:5\nONE LORD ONE Faith, ONE Baptism\n\n31\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":32,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nIN THE NAME OF THE LORD JESUS CHRIST\nHOW DID THE EARLY CHURCH INTERPRET CHRIST’S\nCOMMAND IN MATTHEW 28:19? ACTS 2:38, 8:16 , 10:48 AND\n19:5 are four Biblical references that answer this question. If\nthe Biblical record is not enough, please examine the findings\nof the educated, scholars, and historians.\n\nBritannica Encyclopedia, 11th Edition, Volume\n3, pages 365 – Baptism was changed from the\nname of JESUS to words Father, Son & Holy\nGhost in 2nd Century.\nCanney Encyclopedia of Religion, page 53\nThe early church baptized in the name of the\nLord Jesus until the second century.\nHastings Encyclopedia of Religion, Volume 2\nChristian baptism was Administered using the\nwords “in the name of Jesus” page 377. Baptism\nwas always in the name of Jesus until the time\nof Justin Martyr, page 389.\nSchaff – Herzog Religious Encyclopedia,\nVolume 1, page 435 – The New Testament\nknows only the baptism in the name of Jesus.\nHastings Dictionary of Bible, page 88\nIt must be acknowledged that three-fold name\nof Matthew 28:19 does not appear to have been\nused by the primitive church, but rather the\nname of Jesus Christ or Lord Jesus.\nFirst Century Christians INVOKED OR CALLED the Name of\nJesus over believers in water baptism. If, as some say, “the\nName of Jesus means the authority of Jesus,” then so much\nmore should the NAME, rather than titles, be called an\nindividual in baptism. Read Matthew 28:18, Acts 4:12 and\nColossians 2:9\n\n32\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":33,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nORAL INVOCATION OF THE NAME\nSome people contend that “baptism in the\nname of Jesus” means only the authority and\npower of Jesus name and does not mean the\nname should be uttered orally. However, the\nBible tells us that we are to orally invoke the\nname of Jesus.\n\nActs 22:16\nAnd now why are you waiting? Arise and be baptized, and wash away\nyour sins, calling on the name of the Lord.’\n\nCalling (epikaleō) - to entitle; by implication to\ninvoke (for aid, worship, testimony, decision,\netc.):- appeal (unto), call (on, upon), surname\nSee also Acts 7:59, 15:17 and James 2:7\nIt is interesting to note as well that in other\nsituations in the Bible, “in the name of Jesus”\nmeans really uttering the name of Jesus. We see\nthat in Mark 16:17-18 we are to pray for the sick\nin His name.\n\nJames 5:14\nIs anyone among you sick? Let him call for the elders of the church,\nand let them pray over him, anointing him with oil in the name of the\nLord.\nActs 3:6\nThen Peter said, “Silver and gold I do not have, but what I do have I\ngive you: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, rise up and walk.”\n\n33\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":34,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nIII. THE SINNER’S PRAYER\n“Ministers frequently tell lost people that\nthey need to ‘pray the sinner’s prayer.’\nExactly what is this ’sinner’s prayer’? Is this\nprayer biblically based? If not, what is its\norigin?”\nThe so-called “sinner’s prayer” is a popular\nphenomenon in Protestant circles. It is\nemployed at the conclusion of various\ndenominational “revival” services in appeals\nto convince sincere people to “get saved.” It\nfrequently is found as the ending in “gospel”\ntracts, urging people to “repeat these words\nfrom the bottom of your heart.”\nThe “Sinner’s Prayer” takes various forms, all\nof which have the same general thrust. Here is\none form of it:\n“Heavenly Father, I know that I am a sinner and\nthat I deserve to go to hell. I believe that Jesus\nChrist died on the cross for my sins. I do now\nreceive him as my Lord and personal Savior. I\npromise to serve you to the best of my ability.\nPlease save me. In Jesus’ name, Amen.”\nThe following observations concerning this\n“prayer” should be carefully considered.\n\nIs the “Sinner’s Prayer” in the New\nTestament?\nThe sentiments of this prayer are found\nnowhere in the literature of the New Testament\nthat pertains to the sinner’s responsibility under\nthe law of Christ. A careful study of the cases of\nconversion in the book of Acts will reveal that in\nnot a single instance is the sinner instructed\nor encouraged to “pray” for his or her salvation.\n\n34\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":35,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nRather, those honest souls who longed for\nredemption were admonished to “believe” on\nthe Lord (Acts 16:31), “repent and be immersed\n… for the forgiveness of [their] sins” (Acts 2:38;\ncf. 22:16), in order to enjoy a relationship with\nChrist (Gal. 3:27), and enter his spiritual body (1\nCor. 12:13).\nWHAT ABOUT ACTS 2:21?\nSome claim that Acts 2:21 is a proof-text for\nthe so-called sinner’s prayer. Let’s compare this\nverse with several others from the same book,\nthe same author.\n\nActs 2:21 (ASV)\nAnd it shall be, that whosoever shall call on the name of the Lord shall\nbe saved.\nActs 2:38 (ASV)\nAnd Peter said unto them, Repent ye, and be baptized every one of\nyou in the name of Jesus Christ unto the remission of your sins; and\nye shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.\nActs 22:16 (KJV)\nAnd now why tarriest thou? arise, and be baptized, and wash away\nthy sins, calling on the name of the Lord.\n\nThe claim that Acts 2:21 provides authority\nfor the “sinner’s prayer” is baseless. The “call”\ncontemplated in this passage was fulfilled when\npenitent sinners surrendered to the terms\nof the gospel plan of redemption, explicitly\nannounced later on the same occasion.\nThe “remission of sins” (38) is the equivalent\nof “saved” (21). Accordingly, the “call” of verse\n21 is obviously a generic term which embraces\nthe “repent … and be immersed” which was\ncommanded of believers in verse 38.\n\n35\n\nMoreover, this calling-obedience connection is\nfurther established in Acts 22:16. Note that the\nvery act of submitting to the Lord’s command to\nbe immersed is the manifestation of “calling” on\nhis name.\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":36,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nSAYING “LORD, LORD IS NOT ENOUGH\nScripture elsewhere makes it very clear that the\nmere act of “calling” out the Lord’s name, in an\nattempt to access divine mercy, in the absence\nof obedience, is an exercise in futility.\n“Not everyone who says unto me, Lord, Lord,\nshall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he\nwho does [present tense—persistently does]\nthe will of my Father who is in heaven” (Mt.\n7:21).\nAgain, the Savior pointedly inquired:\nLuke 6:46\nAnd why do you call me, Lord, Lord, and do not the things that I say?”\n\nPRAYER IS FOR THE CHILD OF GOD\nPrayer is an avenue of communication between\na “child of God” and his heavenly Father. The\nmodel prayer begins: “Our Father in heaven …”\n(Mt. 6:9). One becomes a child of the Father by\nmeans of the “born-again” process (Jn. 3:3-5),\nnot by praying.\nSAUL’S PRAYERS DID NOT SAVE HIM\nSaul of Tarsus prayed for three days after\narriving in the city of Damascus, yet his sins\nwere not “washed away” until he was immersed\nin water in obedience to the divine command\n(Acts 9:11; 22:16). If there ever was a case of\nthe “sinner’s prayer” being exercised, surely this\nwas it; yet it was for naught.\n\n36\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":37,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nWHERE DID THE “SINNER’S PRAYER”\nORIGINATE?\nThe “sinner’s prayer” probably evolved, in\nsome form or another, in the early days of\nthe Protestant Reformation movement, as a\nmisguided reaction against the Roman Catholic\ndogma of justification by means of meritorious\nworks.\nFor example, Jacobus Faber (c. 1450-1536),\nwho has been called “the father of the French\nreformation” (though he never formally left the\nCatholic Church), wrote a commentary on the\nepistles of Paul in 1512. (This was five years\nbefore Luther’s break with the Roman Church\nin Germany.) In this volume Faber argued that\njustification is obtained through faith without\nworks (see McClintock & Strong 1969, p. 441).\nLater, rebelling against the “merit works”\nsystem of Romanism, Luther would contend\nthat salvation is on the basis of “faith alone.”\nAccording to one biographer, Luther exclaimed:\n\n“I, Doctor Martin Luther, unworthy herald of the gospel of our Lord Jesus\nChrist, confess this article, that faith alone without works justifies before\nGod”\n(D’Aubigne 1955, p. 56)\n\n37\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":38,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 8\n\nSo convinced was Luther of this proposition\nthat, when producing his own translation of the\nNew Testament, he altered the text of Romans\n3:28 to read: “a man is justified by faith only.”\nThe word “only” is not in any Greek manuscript\navailable. Luther even rejected the divine origin\nof the book of James because of its emphasis\non “works,” in addition to faith.\nTo believe, therefore, that one may be justified\nfrom sin, by simply praying the “sinner’s prayer”\nas a substitute for obedience to the plan of\nsalvation, is to labor under a delusion that is\nvoid of biblical support. Undoubtedly, many\nwho offer the “sinner’s prayer” are exceedingly\nsincere. Sincerity alone, however, is unavailing\n(Prov. 14:12; Acts 23:1; 26:9).\n\n38\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"9":{"lesson":9,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":31,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 9\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will recognize that God desires to fill\nevery person with His Spirit\n\n•\n\nThe student will identify that speaking in\ntongues is the only initial biblical evidence that\naccompanies the receiving of the Holy Spirit\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will respond by indicating his/her\ndesire to receive the Holy Spirit\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience\n\nAge of Human Government\n\nAge of Law\n\nAge of Promise\n\nChurch Age\n\nCast (Characters)\nJesus, Nicodemus, Peter, Cornelius and family, Paul, John,\nJohn the Baptist’s disciples, Philip, Samaritans and Ananias\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 9\n\nLesson Background\nJesus gave specific instructions to His disciples before His\nascension to the clouds, which was to wait for the Promise\nof the Father. The disciples obeyed the instructions of Jesus,\nand when the Spirit of God was poured out for the first\ntime, this started a revival in establishing the first Church\nof God. This revival continued all throughout the book of\nActs and the Epistles, illustrating the outpouring of salvation\nto all of Asia in the first-century. As the first-century world\nexperienced this spiritual awakening, epistles to churches\ncontinued to establish the Word of Truth among believers,\nstrengthening the faith.\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Recap on the Plan of Salvation\n\n3\n\nB. Who is the Holy Spirit\n\n4\n\nC. Old Testament Promise of God’s Spirit\n\n5\n\nD. Jesus reaffirms the Promise of the Spirit\n\n5\n\nE. Being Born of the Spirit\n\n6\n\nF. First Outpouring of God’s Spirit\n\n7\n\nG. Why do we need the Holy Spirit in us?\n\n11\n\nH. Receiving the Spirit by Faith\n\n14\n\nI. Parallels Between Physical Birth and\nSpiritual Birth\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"A\n\nRECAP ON THE PLAN OF\nSALVATION\n\nLesson 9\n\nRefer to Chart L9 . 1-2\n\nActs 2:38\nThen Peter said to them, “Repent, and let every one of you be\nbaptized in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins; and\nyou shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.\n\nJesus described our response to the Gospel\nmessage as the born-again experience. Obedience\nto being born again is the plan of salvation for\neveryone today.\n\nJohn 3:5-7\nJesus answered, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless one is born\nof water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God. 6 That\nwhich is born of the flesh is flesh, and that which is born of the Spirit\nis spirit. 7 Do not marvel that I said to you, ‘You must be born again.’\n\nIn the previous lesson, we studied about the\nnecessity of repentance, what is repentance, and how\nwe repent. We have also covered what it means to be\nborn again of water - through water baptism in Jesus’\nname. In this lesson, we would be studying what it\nmeans to be born again of the Spirit (also known as\nthe infilling of the Spirit of God).\n\n3\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"B\nLesson 9\n\nWHO IS THE HOLY SPIRIT\nKey #1: The Holy Spirit is the\neternal Spirit of God.\n\nGenesis 1:2\nThe earth was without form, and void; and darkness was on the\nface of the deep. And the Spirit of God was hovering over the face\nof the waters.\n1 Peter 1:16\nbecause it is written, “Be holy, for I am holy.”\nJohn 4:24\nGod is Spirit, and those who worship Him must worship in spirit\nand truth.\n\nThis same Spirit was manifested in the flesh as\nJesus Christ and continues to live in believers today.\n\n1 Timothy 3:16\nAnd without controversy great is the mystery of godliness: God was\nmanifested in the flesh, justified in the Spirit, Seen by angels, Preached\namong the Gentiles, Believed on in the world, Received up in glory.\nRomans 8:9\nBut you are not in the flesh but in the Spirit, if indeed the Spirit of God\ndwells in you. Now if anyone does not have the Spirit of Christ, he is\nnot His.\n\n4\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"C\n\nOLD TESTAMENT PROMISE OF\nGOD’S SPIRIT\n\nLesson 9\nJoel 2:28-29\n“And it shall come to pass afterward That I will pour out My Spirit on\nall flesh; Your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, Your old men\nshall dream dreams, Your young men shall see visions. 29 And also\non My menservants and on My maidservants I will pour out My Spirit\nin those days.\nIsaiah 44:3\nFor I will pour water on him who is thirsty, and floods on the dry\nground; I will pour My Spirit on your descendants, And My blessing\non your offspring;\nEzekiel 37:14\nI will put My Spirit in you, and you shall live, and I will place you in\nyour own land. Then you shall know that I, the LORD, have spoken it\nand performed it,” says the LORD.’ “\n\nD\n\nJESUS REAFFIRMS THE PROMISE\nOF THE SPIRIT\nJohn 7:37-39\nOn the last day, that great day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried\nout, saying, “If anyone thirsts, let him come to Me and drink. 38 He\nwho believes in Me, as the Scripture has said, out of his heart will\nflow rivers of living water.” 39 But this He spoke concerning the Spirit,\nwhom those believing in Him would receive; for the Holy Spirit was\nnot yet given, because Jesus was not yet glorified.\nJohn 14:15-18\n“If you love Me, keep My commandments. 16 And I will pray the\nFather, and He will give you another Helper, that He may abide with\nyou forever-- 17 the Spirit of truth, whom the world cannot receive,\nbecause it neither sees Him nor knows Him; but you know Him, for\nHe dwells with you and will be in you. 18 I will not leave you orphans; I\nwill come to you.\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"Acts 1:4-5\nAnd being assembled together with them, He commanded them not\nto depart from Jerusalem, but to wait for the Promise of the Father,\n“which,” He said, “you have heard from Me; 5 for John truly baptized\nwith water, but you shall be baptized with the Holy Spirit not many\ndays from now.”\n\nLesson 9\n\nKey #2: Both the Old Testament and Jesus\npromises the gift of the Holy Spirit.\n\nE\n\nBEING BORN OF SPIRIT\nThe outpouring of God’s Spirit is described by Jesus\nas being born of the Spirit.\n\nJohn 3:5-8\nJesus answered, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless one is born\nof water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God. 6 That\nwhich is born of the flesh is flesh, and that which is born of the Spirit\nis spirit. 7 Do not marvel that I said to you, ‘You must be born again.’\n8\nThe wind blows where it wishes, and you hear the sound of it, but\ncannot tell where it comes from and where it goes. So is everyone\nwho is born of the Spirit.”\n\nNote to teachers: “Everyone” means that this is a\ncommon experience\n\n6\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Discussion Questions\nWhat element did Jesus use to describe someone\nbeing born of the Spirit?\n\nLesson 9\n\nCan you list some characteristics of wind?\n\nHow did Jesus describe the effects of wind?\n\nF\n\nFIRST OUTPOURING OF GOD’S SPIRIT\nThe first instance of the Holy Spirit being poured\nout was on the Day of Pentecost. There were 120\ndisciples who obeyed Jesus to wait in the upper room\n\nActs 2:1-4\nWhen the Day of Pentecost had fully come, they were all with one\naccord in one place. 2 And suddenly there came a sound from\nheaven, as of a rushing mighty wind, and it filled the whole house\nwhere they were sitting. 3 Then there appeared to them divided\ntongues, as of fire, and one sat upon each of them. 4 And they were\nall filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak with other tongues,\nas the Spirit gave them utterance.\n\nQuestion\nWhat happened to the disciples when they were\nfilled with the Holy Spirit?\n\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"Other Accounts of Believers\nReceiving the Spirit of God\nLesson 9\n\nAll throughout the book of Acts, the Bible records\nthat there were other instances of people being\nfilled with the Spirit of God.\nThe Gentiles at Cornelius’ House\n\nActs 10:44-48\nWhile Peter was still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell upon\nall those who heard the word. 45 And those of the circumcision who\nbelieved were astonished, as many as came with Peter, because the\ngift of the Holy Spirit had been poured out on the Gentiles also. 46 For\nthey heard them speak with tongues and magnify God. Then Peter\nanswered, 47 “Can anyone forbid water, that these should not be\nbaptized who have received the Holy Spirit just as we have?” 48 And\nhe commanded them to be baptized in the name of the Lord. Then\nthey asked him to stay a few days.\n\nThe reason Peter and the Jews knew that\nCornelius’ household had received the Baptism of\nthe Holy Ghost is because they heard them speak\nwith tongues.\nWhen Peter returned to Jerusalem from\nCornelius’ house, he explained to the Jewish\nChristians about why he went to a Gentile’s house\nwith the gospel of salvation.\n\nActs 11:11-17\nAt that very moment, three men stood before the house where I\nwas, having been sent to me from Caesarea. 12 Then the Spirit told\nme to go with them, doubting nothing. Moreover these six brethren\naccompanied me, and we entered the man’s house. 13 And he told\nus how he had seen an angel standing in his house, who said to him,\n‘Send men to Joppa, and call for Simon whose surname is Peter, 14 who\nwill tell you words by which you and all your household will be saved.’\nAnd as I began to speak, the Holy Spirit fell upon them, as upon us\nat the beginning. 16 Then I remembered the word of the Lord, how He\nsaid, ‘John indeed baptized with water, but you shall be baptized with\nthe Holy Spirit.’ 17 If therefore God gave them the same gift as He gave\nus when we believed on the Lord Jesus Christ, who was I that I could\nwithstand God?”\n15\n\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"Note to teachers: See Acts 15:7-9 for Peter’s account to\nthe Jerusalem Church council regarding this incident\n\nLesson 9\n\nJohn’s Disciples in Ephesus\n\nActs 19:1-6\nAnd it happened, while Apollos was at Corinth, that Paul, having\npassed through the upper regions, came to Ephesus. And finding\nsome disciples 2 he said to them, “Did you receive the Holy Spirit\nwhen you believed?” So they said to him, “We have not so much as\nheard whether there is a Holy Spirit.” 3 And he said to them, “Into\nwhat then were you baptized?” So they said, “Into John’s baptism.” 4\nThen Paul said, “John indeed baptized with a baptism of repentance,\nsaying to the people that they should believe on Him who would\ncome after him, that is, on Christ Jesus.” 5 When they heard this, they\nwere baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus. 6 And when Paul had\nlaid hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they spoke\nwith tongues and prophesied.\n\nNote to teachers: Point out to students that these\ndisciples, although possess belief in God, still needed\nto receive the Holy Spirit in a separate experience.\n\nSamaritans receiving the Holy Spirit\n\nActs 8:14-20\nNow when the apostles who were at Jerusalem heard that Samaria had\nreceived the word of God, they sent Peter and John to them, 15 who,\nwhen they had come down, prayed for them that they might receive\nthe Holy Spirit. 16 For as yet He had fallen upon none of them. They\nhad only been baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus. 17 Then they laid\nhands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit. 18 And when Simon\nsaw that through the laying on of the apostles’ hands the Holy Spirit\nwas given, he offered them money, 19 saying, “Give me this power also,\nthat anyone on whom I lay hands may receive the Holy Spirit.” 20 But\nPeter said to him, “Your money perish with you, because you thought\nthat the gift of God could be purchased with money!\n\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"Lesson 9\n\nAlthough the Scripture does not mention speaking\nin tongues when they receive the Holy Spirit in\nthis instance, this account shows that there is an\noutward evidence that can be seen or heard.\n\nNote to teachers: Those in Samaria were repented\nand baptized yet it does not mean they automatically\nreceive the Holy Spirit.\n\nThe Apostle Paul received the Holy Spirit\n\nActs 9:17-18\nAnd Ananias went his way and entered the house; and laying his\nhands on him he said, “Brother Saul, the Lord Jesus, who appeared\nto you on the road as you came, has sent me that you may receive\nyour sight and be filled with the Holy Spirit.” 18 Immediately there\nfell from his eyes something like scales, and he received his sight at\nonce; and he arose and was baptized.\n\nAlthough the Bible does not mention Paul speaking\nin tongues in this account, we know later that he\nwas able to do so.\n\n1 Corinthians 14:18\nI thank my God I speak with tongues more than you all\n\nSpeaking in tongues is a visible and audible\nexperience when a person receives the Holy\nSpirit. This was also what Isaiah prophesied would\nhappen: “For with stammering lips and another\ntongue will he speak to this people” (Isaiah 28:11).\nKey #3: Speaking in tongues is the initial\nevidence of someone receiving the Holy Spirit.\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"Our Tongue Reveals our Heart\nJesus tells us that our tongues reveal the\ncontent of our hearts.\n\nLesson 9\n\nMatthew 12:34\nBrood of vipers! How can you, being evil, speak good things? For out of\nthe abundance of the heart the mouth speaks.\nJames 3:2-5 (NLT)\nIndeed, we all make many mistakes. For if we could control our\ntongues, we would be perfect and could also control ourselves in\nevery other way. 3 We can make a large horse go wherever we want\nby means of a small bit in its mouth. 4 And a small rudder makes a\nhuge ship turn wherever the pilot chooses to go, even though the\nwinds are strong. 5 In the same way, the tongue is a small thing that\nmakes grand speeches. But a tiny spark can set a great forest on fire.\nJames 3:8\nbut no man can tame the tongue. It is an unruly evil, full of\ndeadly poison\n\nG\n\nWHY DO WE NEED THE HOLY SPIRIT IN US?\nThe Spirit of God identifies us as belonging to Christ\n\nRomans 8:9\nBut you are not in the flesh but in the Spirit, if indeed the Spirit of\nGod dwells in you. Now if anyone does not have the Spirit of Christ,\nhe is not His.\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"The Holy Spirit is the seal of someone who believes the\ngospel of salvation\nLesson 9\nEphesians 1:13-14\nIn Him you also trusted, after you heard the word of truth, the\ngospel of your salvation; in whom also, having believed, you were\nsealed with the Holy Spirit of promise, 14 who is the guarantee of our\ninheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, to the\npraise of His glory.\n\nThe Holy Spirit brings us back to God’s love\n\nRomans 5:5\nNow hope does not disappoint, because the love of God has been\npoured out in our hearts by the Holy Spirit who was given to us.\n\nThe Holy Spirit writes God’s laws in our hearts and\nempowers us to walk in His ways\n\nJeremiah 31:33\nBut this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel\nafter those days, says the LORD: I will put My law in their minds, and\nwrite it on their hearts; and I will be their God, and they shall be My\npeople.\nEzekiel 36:26-27\nI will give you a new heart and put a new spirit within you; I will take\nthe heart of stone out of your flesh and give you a heart of flesh. 27\nI will put My Spirit within you and cause you to walk in My statutes,\nand you will keep My judgments and do them.\n\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"The Holy Spirit is our internal Teacher and Comforter\nLesson 9\n\nJohn 14:26\nBut the Comforter, which is the Holy Ghost, whom the Father will\nsend in my name, he shall teach you all things, and bring all things to\nyour remembrance, whatsoever I have said unto you.\nJohn 16:13\nHowever, when He, the Spirit of truth, has come, He will guide\nyou into all truth; for He will not speak on His own authority, but\nwhatever He hears He will speak; and He will tell you things to come.\n\nThe Holy Spirit brings joy, peace and hope\n\nRomans 15:13\nNow may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing,\nthat you may abound in hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.\nColossians 1:27\nTo them God willed to make known what are the riches of the glory\nof this mystery among the Gentiles: which is Christ in you, the hope\nof glory.\n\nThe Holy Spirit produces the character the of Christ\nin us\n\nGalatians 5:22-23\nBut the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, kindness,\ngoodness, faithfulness, 23 gentleness, self-control. Against such there\nis no law.\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"The Holy Spirit empowers us to bless the body of\nChrist with special gifts\nLesson 9\n1 Corinthians 12:7-11\nBut the manifestation of the Spirit is given to each one for the profit\nof all: 8 for to one is given the word of wisdom through the Spirit, to\nanother the word of knowledge through the same Spirit, 9 to another\nfaith by the same Spirit, to another gifts of healings by the same\nSpirit, 10 to another the working of miracles, to another prophecy, to\nanother discerning of spirits, to another different kinds of tongues,\nto another the interpretation of tongues. 11 But one and the same\nSpirit works all these things, distributing to each one individually as\nHe wills.\n\nThe Holy Spirit gives us power to be witnesses\n\nActs 1:8\nBut you shall receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon you;\nand you shall be witnesses to Me in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and\nSamaria, and to the end of the earth.”\n\nH\n\nRECEIVING THE SPIRIT BY FAITH\nThe Holy Spirit is God’s gift to Man and is received by faith.\n\nEphesians 2:8-9\nFor by grace you have been saved through faith, and that not of\nyourselves; it is the gift of God, 9 not of works, lest anyone should\nboast.\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"Lesson 9\n\nKey #4: Having faith in Jesus is the key\nto receiving the gift of the Holy Spirit.\n\nIf we have placed our faith in Jesus Christ, we can receive\nthe Holy Spirit anytime and anywhere.\n\nActs 2:39\nFor the promise is to you and to your children, and to all who are\nafar off, as many as the Lord our God will call.”\nLuke 11:9-13\n“So I say to you, ask, and it will be given to you; seek, and you will\nfind; knock, and it will be opened to you. 10 For everyone who asks\nreceives, and he who seeks finds, and to him who knocks it will\nbe opened. 11 If a son asks for bread from any father among you,\nwill he give him a stone? Or if he asks for a fish, will he give him a\nserpent instead of a fish? 12 Or if he asks for an egg, will he offer him\na scorpion? 13 If you then, being evil, know how to give good gifts\nto your children, how much more will your heavenly Father give the\nHoly Spirit to those who ask Him!”\n\nKey #5: Anyone can receive the gift of\nthe Holy Spirit anytime and anywhere.\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"I\nLesson 9\n\nPARALLELS BETWEEN PHYSICAL BIRTH\nAND SPIRITUAL BIRTH\nPhysical Birth\n\nSpiritual Birth\n\nIn conception, there must be a\nseed. The man holds the seed,\nwhich fertilises an egg in the woman’s body\n\nGod’s grace revealed to someone\nthe plan of salvation in the Word of\nGod. The Word of God is likened to\nthe seed\n1 Peter 1:23 having been born\nagain, not of corruptible seed but\nincorruptible, through the word of\nGod which lives and abides forever\n\nThe baby fetus starts to grow and\ndevelop. At this stage, the baby is\nstill considered unborn.\n\nThe person grows in faith\n• After someone hears the\nGospel, they receive the seed\nand their faith grows (Romans\n10:17)\n• At this stage, the person is not\nborn again yet\nThere are 3 aspects to believing:\n• Must have knowledge first\n• Agree with the message\n(believe)\n• Develop into application\n(action)\nIllustration:\nIf someone shouts “fire, fire, fire”\n(knowledge), if you really believe\nthat person (agree with the\nmessage), you will run out of the\nbuilding (application, action).\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Lesson 9\n\nPhysical Birth\n\nSpiritual Birth\n\nAt around 26 weeks onward (6-7\nmonths), the baby starts to turn\naround. This indicates they are\nready for birth.\n\nRepentance\n• After the preaching of God’s\nWord, the person changes his\nmind which includes his actions\n• Repentance is saying sorry\nand changing direction to walk\ntowards God\n• Every step is a step of faith\nAt this stage, there is faith and\nrepentance, but the person is\nnot born again yet. He or she still\nneeds to be born of water and of\nspirit to enter the kingdom of God\n(John 3:3-5).\n\nThe water bag breaks. The baby is\nborn and the doctors verifies life in\nthe baby through their first cry. We\nknow the baby is breathing when\nthe baby lets out a cry.\n\n17\n\nThe born again experience has two\nparts – being born of water and of\nSpirit.\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 9\n\nRefer to Chart L9 . 2-2\n\n1. The Holy Spirit is the eternal Spirit of God.\n2. Both the Old Testament and Jesus promises\nthe gift of the Holy Spirit.\n3. Speaking in tongues is the initial evidence of\nsomeone receiving the Holy Spirit.\n4. Having faith in Jesus is the key to receiving\nthe gift of the Holy Spirit.\n5. Anyone can receive the gift of the Holy Spirit\nanytime and anywhere.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"Charts\nLesson 9\n\n19\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"Lesson 9\n\nModular Section\n6 SIMPLE STEPS TO EXPLAIN HOW TO\nRECEIVE THE HOLY SPIRIT\n1) First, all seekers must Repent: It is impossible to\nreceive Holy Ghost without Repentance.\n\n1 John 1:8-9\n“8 If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is\nnot in us. 9 If we confess our sins, He is faithful and just to forgive us\nour sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.”\nActs 3:19\n“Repent therefore and be converted, that your sins may be blotted out,\nso that times of refreshing may come from the presence of the Lord,”\n\nAction step for Teachers: You can pray with the\nstudent if he/she is ready to receive the Holy Spirit.\nRepentance is needed to prepare the student’s heart\nto receive the Holy Spirit. Help the student to remove\nall barriers. Sin, unforgiveness, pride, or any unclean\nthing that may block them from receiving. You may\nwant to ask them what they would like to repent\nabout.\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\n2) Desire: Seeker must desire the Holy Ghost. God will\nnot force His Spirit on anyone.\n\nRevelation 3:20\n“Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears My voice\nand opens the door, I will come in to him and dine with him, and\nhe with Me.”\nMatthew 7:7-8\n“7 “Ask, and it will be given to you; seek, and you will find; knock,\nand it will be opened to you. 8 For everyone who asks receives,\nand he who seeks finds, and to him who knocks it will be opened.”\n\n3) Faith: Seeker must believe they will receive the Holy\nSpirit\n\nHebrews 11:1\n“Now faith is the assurance of things hoped for, the conviction of\nthings not seen.” ESV\nHebrews 11:6\n“But without faith it is impossible to please Him, for he who comes\nto God must believe that He is, and that He is a rewarder of those\nwho diligently seek Him.”\n\n21\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\n4) Praise: God inhabits praise. Draw near to God\n(through praise) and He will draw near to you\n\nJames 4:8\n“Draw near to God, and he will draw near to you.” ESV\nPsalms 22:3\n“But You are holy, Enthroned in the praises of Israel”\nPsalms 100:4\n“Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and into his courts with\npraise: be thankful unto him, and bless his name”\n\nAction step for Teacher: Help the student reach out\nby leading the student through thanksgiving, praise &\nworship. Let the student know that he/she should not\nanalyze with his/her mind, but allow himself/herself to\nreceive this gift. Encourage the student to verbalize his\nor her praise with words such as Hallelujah, Thank You\nJesus, I Love You Jesus.\n5) Focus: Seeker must keep their mind on Jesus. Do not\nallow mind to wander.\n6) Yield: When the Holy Ghost comes upon the seeker\n–stop speaking in known tongue, allow the Spirit to\nspeak.\n\nActs 2:4\nAnd they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak\nwith other tongues, as the Spirit gave them utterance.\nRomans 8:26\n“Likewise the Spirit helps us in our weakness. For we do not know\nwhat to pray for as we ought, but the Spirit himself intercedes for\nus with groanings too deep for words.”\n\n22\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\nAction step for Teachers: If the student is praying,\nask the student to reach out by faith. Observe the\nstudent’s progress in reaching out and then ask\nthe student to stop praying in English (or native\nlanguage) and begin speaking in tongues. He/She\nmay only have a few words but ask him/her to go\nahead and speak those in faith, and other words will\nfollow. Encourage the student and let him/her know\nthat as he/she yields his/her tongue to the Spirit,\nhe/she will begin to feel a wonderful release of the\nSpirit.\nIf the student attempts but eventually fails to receive the\nHoly Spirit, please make sure you do the following:\n\n23\n\n-\n\nExplain to him/her that he/she has not failed or been\nrejected. God wants to give him/her the Holy Spirit\nbut he/she may not be ready\n\n-\n\nTry to find out if there are any barriers or fears\nthat is hindering him/her to release his/her faith\ncompletely\n\n-\n\nGive him/her advice on how he/she can prepare his/\nher heart to be ready for God’s Spirit and that it is a\nprocess\n\n-\n\nEncourage him/her to continue reading the Word of\nGod, revise this lesson, seek to overcome fears and\nget to know God better\n\n-\n\nIf the student has questions, please try to address\nthose questions to lead him/her to a place where\nhim/her is ready for God’s infilling\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":24,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\nFrequently Asked Questions\n1) Men in the Old Testament had\nthe Holy Spirit move on them,\nbut they were never filled with\nthe Spirit\nA: The student might wonder why “If the Holy\nSpirit was not yet poured out, how come\nGod’s Spirit moved on men in the OT?”\nThe Bible says the Spirit of the Lord came\nupon those men.\nDavid the Anointed King\n\n1 Samuel 16:13\n“13 Then Samuel took the horn of oil and anointed him in the midst of\nhis brothers; and the Spirit of the Lord came upon David from that day\nforward. So Samuel arose and went to Ramah”\n\nGideon Mighty Man of Valour\n\nJudges 6:34\n“34 But the Spirit of the Lord came upon Gideon; then he blew the\ntrumpet, and the Abiezrites gathered behind him”.\n\nThe Spirit of the Lord came upon these few\nother men: Othniel, the first Judge (Judges\n3:10), Samson (Judges 13:25), Ezekiel\n(Ezekiel 11:5).\nIn Strong’s Concordance, “came upon”\nmeans to wrap around, as if putting on a\ngarment, to clothe, to array, to wear. Only\ncertain men in the Old Testament had the\nSpirit of God come upon them, usually for\na season to accomplish a part of God’s will.\n24\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":25,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\nThe Bible also mentioned that the Spirit\nof God could depart from these men (for\nexample Saul in 1 Samuel 16:4). This was\nnot an infilling of the Holy Spirit, as God\ndesired to pour out His spirit on all men\nand it was not something that could depart\nfrom them.\n2) The things of God can only\nbe received spiritually, never\ncarnally\nA:\n\n1 Corinthians 2:10-14\n“But God has revealed them to us through His Spirit. For the Spirit\nsearches all things, yes, the deep things of God. 11 For what man knows\nthe things of a man except the spirit of the man which is in him? Even\nso no one knows the things of God except the Spirit of God. 12 Now we\nhave received, not the spirit of the world, but the Spirit who is from\nGod, that we might know the things that have been freely given to\nus by God. 13 These things we also speak, not in words which man’s\nwisdom teaches but which the Holy Spirit teaches, comparing spiritual\nthings with spiritual. 14 But the natural man does not receive the things\nof the Spirit of God, for they are foolishness to him; nor can he know\nthem, because they are spiritually discerned.”\n\nHaving the Spirit of God is essential to\nour walk with God because it enables our\nunderstanding and discerning of the things\nof God. Just as a blind man cannot judge\nan art contest, a deaf man cannot judge a\nsinging contest, we are unable to process and\nunderstand the things of God fully unless we\nhave His Spirit in us. If we really want to grow\nin our grace and knowledge of Christ, we can\nonly do so with His Spirit in us.\n\n25\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":26,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\n3) Did Jesus need to be filled with\nthe Holy Spirit?\nA: No, He did not. Jesus was the Spirit of God\nrobed in flesh. He was conceived of the\nSpirit (Matthew 1:18, Luke1:35). The reason\nwhy the Spirit descended on Jesus, was\na confirmation for John the Baptist, with\nregards to what God has promised to tell\nJohn in his role as a forerunner for Christ:\n\nJohn 1: 32-34\nAnd John bare record, saying, I saw the Spirit descending from heaven\nlike a dove, and it abode upon him. 33 And I knew him not: but he that\nsent me to baptize with water, the same said unto me, Upon whom\nthou shalt see the Spirit descending, and remaining on him, the same\nis he which baptizeth with the Holy Ghost. 34 And I saw, and bare record\nthat this is the Son of God.\n\n4) How the first outpouring of His Spirit\nfulfilled the prophecies from OT and John\nthe Baptist\nA:\nActs 2:1-4, NKJV\nWhen the Day of Pentecost had fully come, they were all with one\naccord in one place (“they were all together in one place” ESV). 2 And\nsuddenly there came a sound from heaven, as of a rushing mighty\nwind, and it filled the whole house where they were sitting. 3 Then there\nappeared to them divided tongues, as of fire, and one sat upon each of\nthem. 4 And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak\nwith other tongues, as the Spirit gave them utterance.\n\nThe mighty wind relates to Jesus’ words in\nJohn 3:7-8, fire was what John referenced\nthe Holy Spirit to, tongues was what Isaiah\nprophesied about and witnessing was what\nthe disciples did immediately once they\nwere filled with God’s Spirit (Acts 2:14-38).\n26\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":27,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\nIsaiah 28:11\n“For with stammering lips and another tongue will he speak to this\npeople”\nJohn 3:7-8\n“Do not marvel that I said to you, ‘You must be born again.’ 8 The wind\nblows where it wishes, and you hear the sound of it, but cannot tell\nwhere it comes from and where it goes. So is everyone who is born of\nthe Spirit.”\nMatthew 3:11\n“As for me, I baptize you with water for repentance, but He who is\ncoming after me is mightier than I, and I am not fit to remove His\nsandals; He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and fire.”\n\n5) Significance of the Day of Pentecost (Type\n& Shadow fulfillment)\nA: There was a specific reason why God\npoured out His spirit on the day of\nPentecost (Acts 2:1-4)\nWhy the day of Pentecost?\nThe day of Pentecost (feast of weeks) was\na feast/festival institutionalized by God to\ncelebrate 50 days after the wave offering\nof the Passover. This was given under\nthe Law (Leviticus 23:15, Deuteronomy\n16:9). This was commanded by God after\nthe deliverance of the children of Israel\nfrom Egypt through the Passover. It was\nexactly 50 days later after the Passover\nand Exodus that the law was given on the\nday of Pentecost (see Exodus 19:3-6). The\nlaw included the Tabernacle Plan, the OT\nSalvation Plan.\nJesus was crucified on the day of the\nPassover (John 13:1, Matthew 26:2) and the\nHoly Spirit was first poured out on man\n27\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":28,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\non the day of Pentecost, paralleling the 50\nday timeline of the Old Testament events.\nJust as a lamb had to be slain for men to\nbe free (Passover), Christ was the perfect\nlamb who was slain for the sin of the world\n- and the Holy Spirit was given so that the\nlaw could be written in the hearts of men\n(exactly as prophesied in Jeremiah 31:31-33\nand as fulfillment of the law given to Moses\non Mount Sinai)! On the same day the Holy\nSpirit was poured out, 3000 were born\nagain into the Church. This fulfilled the\n“type” of the Tabernacle Plan, the OT plan\nof salvation.\nThe old way of salvation through the law\nand the tabernacle plan was the type\nand shadow of the new way of salvation\nestablished on the day of Pentecost. God’s\ntiming is exact, as both of these events\noccurred on the same calendar date!\n\n6) Tongues has not ceased yet\nA: Some confuse the passage of scripture\nin 1 Corinthians 13 as an indication that\ntongues has ceased today.\n\n1 Corinthians 13:8-12\n“Love never fails. But whether there are prophecies, they will\nfail; whether there are tongues, they will cease; whether there is\nknowledge, it will vanish away. 9 For we know in part and we prophesy\nin part. 10 But when that which is perfect has come, then that which\nis in part will be done away. 11 When I was a child, I spoke as a child, I\nunderstood as a child, I thought as a child; but when I became a man,\nI put away childish things. 12 For now we see in a mirror, dimly, but\nthen face to face. Now I know in part, but then I shall know just as I\nalso am known.”\n\n28\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":29,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\nWhat the section of Scriptures is denoting\nis the fact that love may fail in the presence\nof tongues, and not the ceasing of tongues.\n1 Corinthians 13 is the popular passage on\nlove, with the emphasis on the way of how\nwe are to love one another. However, it is\nalso cautioned that under some situations,\nlove will fail. These things are what we\nknow only in part now, but one day we will\nfully understand.\nSome further insist that the perfect has\ncome with the completion of the New\nTestament. What this passage is speaking\nabout when it says “when that which is\nperfect has come, then that which is in\npart will be done away” is the teaching\nconcerning the return of Jesus Christ (the\nOne that is perfect) to the earth. The New\nTestament could not have ended with the\nfinal book of the Bible - because we are\nstill living under the period of Grace! It\ncannot be that when John wrote “Amen” in\nthe book of Revelation that everyone then\nimmediately stopped speaking in tongues.\nThe plan of salvation still applies for us\ntoday - Acts 2:38 is still valid, Acts 2:4 is still\nvalid!\nPerfection refers to only when Christ\ncomes again. The world we live in today is\nnot perfect, neither are we perfect. But the\nBible promises that one day the world will\nbe perfect again -  after Christ returns.\nMoreover, the passage of scripture will\nbe taken out of context if we read it\nas “tongues has ceased, all we need is\nlove”. Preceding chapter 13 is the writer’s\nemphasis on earnestly seeking out the\nbest gifts within spiritual giftings - including\nthe gift of tongues. Without His spirit,\nwe will not be able to unlock giftings.\nMoreover, the next chapter (chapter 14)\nhas more exhortation to forbid not to\nspeak in tongues (14:39) and the writer’s\nown gratitude towards God for speaking in\n\n29\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":30,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\ntongues more than others (14:18). It would\nbe extremely odd and inconsistent to find\nthe same writer indicating that tongues\nhas ceased in the chapter before. The\nonly explanation will be that it has never\nbeen about the ceasing of tongues. The\nharmony of the Scriptures also point to\nthis explanation.\n\n1 Corinthians 14:18\n“I thank my God I speak with tongues more than you all”\n\nSpeaking in tongues is not a\nman-made experience\nAn article by The New York Times on Nov 7, 2006 “A\nNeuroscientific Look at Speaking In Tongues” made these\ndiscoveries through research:\nResearchers at the University of Pennsylvania took brain\nimages of five women while they spoke in tongues and\nfound that their frontal lobes — the thinking, willful part\nof the brain through which people control what they do\n— were relatively quiet, as were the language centers.\nContrary to what may be a common perception, studies\nsuggest that people who speak in tongues rarely suffer\nfrom mental problems. A recent study of nearly 1,000\nevangelical Christians in England found that those who\nengaged in the practice were more emotionally stable\nthan those who did not.\nThe new findings contrasted sharply with images taken\nof other spiritually inspired mental states like meditation,\nwhich is often a highly focused mental exercise,\nactivating the frontal lobes.\nSource: http://www.nytimes.com/2006/11/07/health/07brain.html\n\n30\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":31,"text":"31\n\nMODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 9\n\nDifference between the Gift of the Holy\nSpirit (Acts 2:38) and Gifts of the Spirit\n(1 Corinthians 12 and 14)\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"10":{"lesson":10,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":37,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 10\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will state the importance of the\napostles’ doctrine to a believer’s faith\n\n•\n\nThe student will be able to explain who the\napostles were\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will be able to compare their current\nbeliefs with the apostles’ doctrine and express the\nsimilarities/differences\n\nTimeline\nAge of Innocence Age of Conscience\n\nAge of Human Government\n\nAge of Law\n\nAge of Promise\n\nChurch Age\n\nCharacters\nJesus, Apostles, The Church\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 10\n\nLesson Summary\nIn this lesson, we will be examining what happened\nafter the Day of Pentecost where three thousand souls\nwere converted. We will also discover who the apostles\nwere, their authority, and why their doctrine matters to\nthe faith of the early Church.\n\nLesson Outline\nA. What Happened After the Day of Pentecost\n\n3\n\nB. What is the Apostles Doctrine\n\n4\n\nC. Where Did the Apostles Get Their Doctrine\nFrom?\n\n6\n\nD. What were the Apostles Commanded to Do\nWith the Doctrine?\n\n9\n\nE. The Foundation of the Church is the\nApostles’ Doctrine\n\n12\n\nF. Persecution of the Church for the Doctrine\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"A\n\nWhat Happened After the Day\nof Pentecost\n\nLesson 10\nActs 2:41-43\nThen those who gladly received his word were baptized; and that\nday about three thousand souls were added to them. 42 And they\ncontinued steadfastly in the apostles’ doctrine and fellowship, in the\nbreaking of bread, and in prayers. 43 Then fear came upon every soul,\nand many wonders and signs were done through the apostles.\n\nWhat did the 3000 new converts do after they were\nborn again? How did they come together in devoted\nfellowship? How did they live out their new found\nChristian faith?\nLuke writes that these new converts, “continued\nsteadfastly in the apostles’ doctrine.”\n\nWhat does that mean, “to continue steadfastly?”\nThe term “to continue steadfastly,” means to live\nin. To continue steadfastly means to seek the Truth,\ndiscuss the Truth, find the Truth, and practice/walk\nthe Truth.\nThese believers adjusted their lives in accordance\nwith their new life in Jesus Christ.\nThey were not doing this on their own. They had the\nHoly Spirit, who was seeking to guide them into all\nTruth. They also had the apostlesʼ instructing them\nalong those lines.\nToday, we have the apostlesʼ doctrine. It is the\nBible. The entire New Testament was written by an\napostle, or a close associate. All the writers of the\nNew Testament were either personal witnesses to\nthe resurrection of Jesus Christ or have encountered\nthese witnesses before.\n3\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"Key #1: We need to continue steadfastly in the\napostles’ doctrine after we are born again.\n\nLesson 10\n\nB\n\nWhat is the Apostles’ Doctrine\nRefer to Chart L10.1-6\nWho are the Apostles\nAs mentioned in Lesson 8, the apostles were the\ndisciples handpicked by Jesus Christ to continue His\nwork on the earth through the Church.\n\nLuke 6:13\nAnd when it was day, He called His disciples to [Himself]; and from\nthem He chose twelve whom He also named apostles.\n\nThe apostles were so important that Jesus even said\nthat our faith must come from their words. Their\nteachings became the distinction between truth and\ndeception.\n\n1 John 4:6 (NLT)\nBut we belong to God, and those who know God listen to us. If they\ndo not belong to God, they do not listen to us. That is how we know if\nsomeone has the Spirit of truth or the spirit of deception.\n\nKey #2: The apostles were chosen and\nauthorised by Jesus to build upon what He\nstarted on this earth.\n\n4\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"Doctrine\nDoctrine (Greek: Didache) – “instruction”\nLesson 10\n\nThe apostles’ doctrine is the instruction delivered to\nthe New Testament Church by the apostles. These\napostles were close to Jesus personally and were\nentrusted with the responsibility of teaching His\ndoctrine to the Church and spreading it to all nations.\n\nMatthew 28:19-20\nGo therefore and make disciples of all the nations, baptizing them\nin the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, 20\nteaching them to observe all things that I have commanded you; and\nlo, I am with you always, even to the end of the age.” Amen.\n\nWithin these verses, we observe Church continuance,\na continual cycle of teaching and baptizing. This\ncommandment lives on until the world ends or until\nall nations are taught.\nThe apostles’ doctrine is not only taught and believed\nin the days of the original apostles, but it is still to be\ntaught today until Jesus Christ returns.\n\nMatthew 16:18\nAnd I also say to you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build\nMy church, and the gates of Hades shall not prevail against it.\n\nJesus told Peter, one of the apostles, that the gates\nof hell will not prevail against the Church that He\nbuilds. If we look for a New Testament Church today,\nthe first and most prominent birthmark to look for is:\n“the apostles’ doctrine”.\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"C\nLesson 10\n\nWhere did the Apostles get their Doctrine\nfrom\nKey #3: The apostles received the doctrine\nfrom Jesus Himself.\nAmongst all the religious professors living in that day,\nthese men were the ones that were most qualified to\ntestify the resurrection of Jesus.\nThink about it:\n• They were Jesus’ most ardent followers during His\nearthly ministry\n• They walked with Jesus, talked with Him, listened to\nHis sermons and teachings, as well as explanations\nto His parables.\n• They personally witnessed His way of life as well as\ndeath\n• They have eyes to see and ears to hear many other\nthings that Jesus taught and preached\nFurthermore, Jesus called them into office and gave\nthem power and authority to do His bidding.\n\nMatthew 16:19\nAnd I will give you the keys of the kingdom of heaven, and whatever\nyou bind on earth will be bound in heaven, and whatever you loose\non earth will be loosed in heaven.”\nMatthew 18:18\nAssuredly, I say to you, whatever you bind on earth will be bound in\nheaven, and whatever you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven.\n\n6\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Therefore, the apostles’ doctrine is not something\nthey invented themselves. It is in complete\nagreement with the will of God.\nLesson 10\n\nThrough divine guidance the apostles established\ndoctrines and practices for the church, nothing other\nthan what God had established in heaven.\nThe apostles were the ambassadors of Christ\nled by God’s Spirit\n\nJohn 16:12-13\nI still have many things to say to you, but you cannot bear them now.\nHowever, when He, the Spirit of truth, has come, He will guide you into\nall truth; for He will not speak 13on His own authority, but whatever He\nhears He will speak; and He will tell you things to come.\nJohn 14:26\nBut the Helper, the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in My name,\nHe will\n\nTo say we must listen to the words of Jesus in the\nGospels, but not obey the teaching of the apostles in\nthe later books is false. Jesus Himself said that if we\nreject the apostles, we also reject Him.\n\nLuke 10:16\nHe who hears you hears Me, he who rejects you rejects Me, and he\nwho rejects Me rejects Him who sent Me.”\n\nThe apostles together with Christ and prophets\nformed the foundation of the Church\n\nRevelation 21:14\nNow the wall of the city had twelve foundations, and on them were\nthe names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb.\n\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"Lesson 10\n\nEphesians 2:19-20\nNow, therefore, you are no longer strangers and foreigners, but\nfellow citizens with the saints and members of the household of\nGod, 20 having been built on the foundation of the apostles and\nprophets, Jesus Christ Himself being the chief corner stone,\n\nJesus is the chief cornerstone; He was the first piece\nof foundation that was laid\nThe apostles added on to that first piece and formed\nthe foundation of the Church\nRejecting the authority of the apostles make\nyou a false teacher\n\n1 Corinthians 14:37\nIf anyone thinks himself to be a prophet or spiritual, let him\nacknowledge that the things which I write to you are the commandments of the Lord.\nRomans 16:17-18\nNow I urge you, brethren, note those who cause divisions and offenses, contrary to the doctrine which you learned, and avoid them.\n18 For those who are such do not serve our Lord Jesus Christ, but\ntheir own belly, and by smooth words and flattering speech deceive\nthe hearts of the simple.\n\nPeople who deviate from the doctrine of the apostles,\ncause division and apostasy. We must note them and\navoid them, keep away from them.\nOur fellowship is determined by the apostles’\ndoctrine\nIt is only through the apostles and their teaching’s\nthat we can have fellowship with our Lord Jesus\nChrist.\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"1 John 1:3\nthat which we have seen and heard we declare to you, that you also\nmay have fellowship with us; and truly our fellowship is with the\nFather and with His Son Jesus Christ.\n\nLesson 10\n\n(See also Acts 19:8-9)\nThe apostles’ doctrine will lead us to one Lord,\none faith, one baptism\n\n2 Corinthians 11:3-4\nBut I fear, lest somehow, as the serpent deceived Eve by his craftiness, so your minds may be corrupted from the simplicity that is\nin Christ. 4 For if he who comes preaches another Jesus whom we\nhave not preached, or if you receive a different spirit which you\nhave not received, or a different gospel which you have not accepted--you may well put up with it!\nEphesians 4:4-6\nThere is one body and one Spirit, just as you were called in one\nhope of your calling;5 one Lord, one faith, one baptism; 6 one God\nand Father of all, who is above all, and through all, and in you all.\n\nD\n\nWhat Were the Apostles Commanded to\nDo With the Doctrine?\nPropagate it by means of teaching and preaching\n\nMatthew 28:19-20\nGo therefore and make disciples of all the nations, baptizing them\nin the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, 20\nteaching them to observe all things that I have commanded you; and\nlo, I am with you always, even to the end of the age.” Amen.\n\n(Refer to Mark 16:15-20, Luke 24:44-53 for more\nexamples)\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"Acts 5:28 saying,\n\nLesson 10\n\n“Did we not strictly command you not to teach in this name? And look,\nyou have filled Jerusalem with your doctrine, and intend to bring this\nMan’s blood on us!”\n1 Timothy 1:3\nAs I urged you when I went into Macedonia--remain in Ephesus that\nyou may charge some that they teach no other doctrine\n\nProtect it\n2 Thessalonians 3:4\nAnd we have confidence in the Lord concerning you, both that you\ndo and will do the things we command you.\nColossians 2:8\nBeware lest anyone cheat you through philosophy and empty deceit,\naccording to the tradition of men, according to the basic principles of\nthe world, and not according to Christ.\n2 Timothy 4:3-4\nFor the time will come when they will not endure sound doctrine, but\naccording to their own desires, because they have itching ears, they\nwill heap up for themselves teachers; 4 and they will turn their ears\naway from the truth, and be turned aside to fables.\nRomans 16:17-18\nNow I urge you, brethren, note those who cause divisions and offenses, contrary to the doctrine which you learned, and avoid them. 18\nFor those who are such do not serve our Lord Jesus Christ, but their\nown belly, and by smooth words and flattering speech deceive the\nhearts of the simple.\nPhilippians 3:17\nBrethren, join in following my example, and note those who so walk,\nas you have us for a pattern.\n2 Thessalonians 3:14-15\nAnd if anyone does not obey our word in this epistle, note that person and do not keep company with him, that he may be ashamed. 15\nYet do not count him as an enemy, but admonish him as a brother.\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"Preserve it\nLesson 10\n1 Timothy 4:13\nTill I come, give attention to reading, to exhortation, to doctrine.\n1 Timothy 4:16\nTake heed to yourself and to the doctrine. Continue in them, for in\ndoing this you will save both yourself and those who hear you.\nLuke 1:3\nit seemed good to me also, having had perfect understanding of all\nthings from the very first, to write to you an orderly account, most\nexcellent Theophilus,\n1 Corinthians 14:37\nIf anyone thinks himself to be a prophet or spiritual, let him\nacknowledge that the things which I write to you are the\ncommandments of the Lord.\n1 Timothy 3:14\nThese things I write to you, though I hope to come to you shortly;\n2 Peter 3:1\nBeloved, I now write to you this second epistle (in both of which I stir\nup your pure minds by way of reminder),\n1 John 2:7\nBrethren, I write no new commandment to you, but an old\ncommandment which you have had from the beginning. The old\ncommandment is the word which you heard from the beginning.\n\nKey #4: We need to propagate, protect and\npreserve the apostles’ doctrine\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"E\nLesson 10\n\nThe Foundation of the Church is the\nApostles’ Doctrine\n1 Timothy 3:15\nbut if I am delayed, I write so that you may know how you ought to\nconduct yourself in the house of God, which is the church of the living\nGod, the pillar and ground of the truth.\n\nThe Church is not a physical building. The word\nChurch comes from the Greek word “ekklesia” which\nmeans “an assembly of called out ones”. God wants to\nseparate a group of people who would then unite to\nlove and commit themselves to Him.\n\n1 Peter 2:9\nBut you are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, a holy nation,\nHis own special people, that you may proclaim the praises of Him who\ncalled you out of darkness into His marvelous light;\n\n(Refer to Lesson 2 on creation. God is a separating\nGod. Just as He separated light from darkness and\nNight from Day, God separates good from evil, right\nfrom wrong, truth from error).\n\nLuke 12:51\nDo you suppose that I came to give peace on earth? I tell you, not at\nall, but rather division.\n\nIt is not surprising that Jesus’ teachings and the\napostles’ doctrine bring a division.\n\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"Lesson 10\n\nJohn 17:17\nSanctify them by Your truth. Your word is truth.\nJohn 17:17 (AMP)\nSanctify them [purify, consecrate, separate them for Yourself, make\nthem holy] by the Truth; Your Word is Truth.\n\nIt is doctrine which separates the denominations of the\nworld.\nIt is doctrine which clearly identifies the church from\nworldly organizations.\nEven though there are many groups and organizations\nthat are developed and maintained for charitable\ncauses, the purpose of the church is to witness the\nresurrection of Jesus Christ and spread His doctrine.\nIt is the apostles’ doctrine which gives the church her\nidentity and that identity is found in Jesus Christ.\n\nKey #5: The apostles’ doctrine separates us\nfrom the world so that we can be joined to\nChrist\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"F\nLesson 10\n\nPersecution of the Church for the Doctrine\nRefer to Chart L10.2-6\n\nMatthew 16:18\nAnd I also say to you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build My\nchurch, and the gates of Hades shall not prevail against it.\n\nThe three things to be noted in the above passage are\nthese: 1) Christ will have a Church in the world, 2) the\nChurch will face resistance by the strength and powers\nof hell, and 3) the Church, despite the attack of Satan,\nwill continue to grow and prosper\n\n1. Jesus prophesied false teachers and persecution\nin the last days\n\nMatthew 24:9-11\nThen they will deliver you up to tribulation and kill you, and you will\nbe hated by all nations for My name’s sake. 10 And then many will be\noffended, will betray one another, and will hate one another. 11 Then\nmany false prophets will rise up and deceive many.\n\n2. Stephen was the Church’s first martyr\n\nActs 7:59-60\nAnd they stoned Stephen as he was calling on God and saying, “Lord\nJesus, receive my spirit.” 60 Then he knelt down and cried out with a\nloud voice, “Lord, do not charge them with this sin.” And when he had\nsaid this, he fell asleep.\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"3. The Church suffered persecution for the truth\nLesson 10\n\nActs 4:18\nAnd they called them and commanded them not to speak at all nor\nteach in the name of Jesus.\nActs 8:1, 4\nNow Saul was consenting to his death. At that time a great\npersecution arose against the church which was at Jerusalem; and\nthey were all scattered throughout the regions of Judea and Samaria,\nexcept the apostles… Therefore those who were scattered went\neverywhere preaching the word.\n\nThe early Church suffered and endured persecution,\nbut they never stopped preaching and teaching\nthe Gospel message. In fact, history records that\npersecution only caused the Church to grow\nexponentially. Entire villages and many religious leaders\nbecame Christians; even entire nations were swept into\nChristianity.\nSo, if there is only one Gospel that the Apostles taught\nand that the early Church was willing to die for, why are\nthere so many different types of churches with different\nteachings regarding salvation?\nTo understand the answer to this question, we must\nlook at what happened to the church after the book of\nActs ends (See Modular Section on Church History)\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 10\n\nRefer to Chart L10.6-6\n\n1. We need to continue steadfastly in the\napostles’ doctrine after we are born again\n2. The apostles were chosen and authorised\nby Jesus to build upon what He started on\nthis earth.\n3. The apostles received the doctrine from\nJesus Himself\n4. We need to propagate, protect and preserve\nthe apostles’ doctrine\n5. The apostles’ doctrine separates us from\nthe world so that we can be joined to Christ\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Charts\nLesson 10\n\n17\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":18,"text":"Charts\nLesson 10\n\n18\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":19,"text":"Charts\nLesson 10\n\n19\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":20,"text":"Lesson 10\n\nModular Section\n1. Church History\na. Apostolic Christianity: The Church\nPersecuted\nb. The Dark Ages\nc. Reformation Christianity\nd. The Church Restored\n2. The Apostles’ Doctrine is the Word of God\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":21,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nI. Church History\nRefer to Chart L10.3-6\n\nIn this part of the lesson, we will be doing a\nmini history lesson on the evolution of the\nChurch. In the lesson, we talked about the\ndanger of false teachers who would preach\nfalse doctrines. Sadly, the Church that once\nwas steadfast in the Apostolic Doctrine gave\nin to compromise and the pure doctrine\nbegan to be corrupted.\na. Apostolic Christianity: The Church\nPersecuted\n\nJohn 15:19-20 (NKJV)\n19 “If you were of the world, the world would love its own. Yet\nbecause you are not of the world, but I chose you out of the world,\ntherefore the world hates you. 20 “Remember the word that I said\nto you, ‘A servant is not greater than his master.’ If they persecuted\nMe, they will also persecute you. If they kept My word, they will keep\nyours also.\nActs 13:50 (NKJV)\nBut the Jews stirred up the devout and prominent women and the\nchief men of the city, raised up persecution against Paul and Barnabas, and expelled them from their region.\nRevelations 12:11 (NKJV)\n11 “And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb and by the\nword of their testimony, and they did not love their lives to the\ndeath.\n\n1. Many people began being put to death for\nTruth. History records many terrible things\nthat happened during the reign of the Roman\nEmperor Nero 64 A.D. Until the reign of Nero,\nChristianity was opposed, but tolerated.\nWhen Nero came to power, he blamed\nChristians for setting the city of Rome on fire.\n21\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":22,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nHistory records that Nero was personally\nresponsible for this tragic fire, and he used\nthis false story to regain popularity in Rome.\nThe result was that great persecution came\nagainst Christians. Many were beheaded,\nburned alive, and history even records that\nChristians were wrapped and smeared with\ntar, fastened to poles in Nero’s garden, and\nthen set on fire.\nIt was during this time Apostle Peter and Paul\nwere martyred. All the apostles except John\nwho was exiled to the island of Patmos (the\nApostle who wrote the book of Revelation)\ndied horrible deaths as martyrs. Many books\nvary as to the location and details of the\ndeaths of the Apostles and the leaders of\nthe Church; however, most historical records\nshow the same basic details regarding\ntheir deaths: Philip, Andrew and Jude were\ncrucified, Matthew was slain in Ethiopia,\nMatthias and James were beheaded,\nBartholomew was skinned alive, Thomas\nwas killed with a spear, Mark was dragged\nto death, Luke was hung, Peter was crucified\nupside down, Paul was beheaded with the\nsword, and James was stoned and finally\nbeaten to death with a club.\nNote: To say that you were a Christian\nduring the days of the early Church was\nalmost a synonym to the word martyr (Acts\n1:8). People who became Christians knew\nthat they had to be willing to lose their lives\nbecause the possibility of death was so\ngreat. It is sad, but today some Christians\nare embarrassed to pray a blessing over\ntheir food in public!\nVespasian succeeded Nero as the Emperor of\nRome, and in 70 A.D. right after the Passover,\nTitus his son, a Roman general, destroyed\nJerusalem and dispersed the Jewish people\nall around the world. This actually fulfilled\n\n22\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":23,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nJesus’ prophecy about the destruction of the\nTemple and Jerusalem (see Luke 19:41-44\nand Luke 23:28-31).\nVespasian was responsible for the Coliseum\nin Rome where Christians were tortured as\ncheap entertainment.\n2. During the last generation of the first century\nfrom 68-100 A.D., the Church suffered severe\npersecution, but their doctrines did not\nchange. Satan persecuted the church using\nworld leaders, yet persecution spread the\nGospel and the believers multiplied.\n3. This period of Christianity is known as\nApostolic Christianity. It began with the\ndirect leadership of the Apostles from 33-100\nA.D. There was either revival or riot in every\ncity where the gospel was preached!\n4. Many Churches today have lost their\npower and witness simply because of their\ndeparture from the original truths taught\nby the Church - “The Gospel, or the faith\nonce delivered to the church”—of which, the\nApostles had so fervently warned the Church\nnot to do (See Acts 20:28-32, Galatians 1:6-12,\nJude 1:3-4 and 2 Peter 3:1-18). There is only\nONE true gospel!\nb. The Dark Ages\n1. After John’s death about 100 A.D., a new\nstrategy of the enemy began. Heresies\n(opinions contrary to the doctrines taught\nby the Apostles) began to arise within\nChristianity. About 120 A.D. with the writings\nof earliest Church Fathers, Christianity in\nmany aspects became quite different from\nthe days of Peter and Paul.\n2. One such departure from Truth was\nGnosticism derived from the word Gnosis,\n\n23\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":24,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nmeaning knowledge. Gnostics claimed to\nhave a unique mysterious knowledge. They\ntaught that the visible world of matter was\nevil and that only the unseen, spiritual\nrealm was good. This teaching is false since\nScripture states that our bodies which can\nbe seen are the Temple of the Holy Ghost\n(1Corinthians 6:19). Also, demons are\nunseen, and they are not good.\n3. Another false teaching of the second century\nwas that of the Montanists in 155 A.D. Its\nfounder declared himself to be a mouthpiece\nof the Holy Ghost. Elevating himself above\nthe authority of scripture, he proclaimed the\nimmediate coming of Christ, strict self-denial,\nabstinence from meat and encouraged his\nfollowers not to marry. Paul warned against\nsuch departure from the faith (see 1 Timothy\n4:1-3).\n4. This time-period was known as the Church\nFathers Christianity and is best described\nin one word - CHANGE. Change from Truth\nto heresy. Now, let’s look at some of the\nhistorical changes that took place.\n\n24\n\n5. It was approximately 200 A.D. that the term\nTrinity, a term not found in the Bible,\nbegan to be taught. It was made popular\nby a man named Tertullian, a lawyer from\nnorthern Africa. This was a new theology\nabout the Godhead which later became\nthe central foundation of the Roman\nCatholic church. The basic teaching is that\nin the Godhead are three separate, distinct\npersons: God the Father, God the Son and\nGod the Holy Spirit. This teaching says that\nthe three persons are distinct from one\nanother (different minds and wills), but\nthat they are co-equal, co-eternal and cosubstantial. This concept is foreign to Jewish\nChristianity and to the Oneness of God as\ntaught to Abraham, Moses and the tribes of\nIsrael, and found in the Old Testament’s First\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":25,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nCommandment. Many scholars believe that\nTertullian’s doctrine can be traced back to\nthe influence of Egyptian theologies of triple\ndivinities or godheads. Tertullian became\nknown as the father of Latin and Western\nTrinity, and so a horizontal view of the Trinity\nwas developed.\n6. Other philosophers during this time period,\nsuch as, Origen declared that everyone will\neventually be saved, and that sinners will be\npunished in a way that will actually result\nin their restoration. This actually removed\nthe incentive to live a godly life and to reach\nthe lost world; a direct contradiction to the\ncommandment of Jesus to go and teach\nall nations! Such humanistic philosophy\nalso clearly disregards Christ’s command in\nJohn 3 which states that we must be Born\nAgain. Origen also taught that God was\ntranscendent (a pure spirit without a body\nor parts) in a manner which contradicted\nTertullian. For Origen, the Father constantly\nbegets the Son by eternal regeneration.\nThe Son is God, but only because God is His\nsource, not intrinsic and self-sufficient like\nthe Father. The Son is less than the Father.\nThe Father is superior to everything existing\n(including the Son) and the source of all other\nbeings. The Son is superior to all rational\ncreatures (including the Holy Spirit). The\nHoly Spirit is superior to the saints (that is\nsuperior to all holy beings, including angels\nand sanctified humans). Thus, a vertical\nconcept of the Trinity was developed.\n\n25\n\n7. In 312 A.D., the new Roman Emperor\nConstantine became both head of the\nRoman Church and the head of the Roman\nEmpire. Soon after uniting Christianity\nand the Roman Empire together by his\nposition, Constantine formed the Catholic,\nor Universal Church, of Rome. Soon\nafterwards, Constantine’s Edict of Toleration\nwas published in 313 A.D., which officially\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":26,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nended Christian persecution. Thousands of\nheathens joined the Roman Catholic Church\nbecause it soon became a political honour\nin Rome to be considered a Christian. The\nmere association with Christianity secured\na passport to political, military and social\npromotion. No longer was Christianity\ntransforming the world. Rather the world\nwas transforming Christianity!\n8. On May 20th, 325 A.D., a meeting, called by\nthe Catholic Church, was attended by 300\nbishops who ruled churches throughout the\nknown world. This is considered the first\nchurch counsel of the Catholic Church and\nis called The Council of Nicea. This Council\nwas used to formulate new Church rules\nand doctrines especially concerning the\nquestions “What is God, and how does Jesus\nfit into God?” The Council, after much debate,\nconcluded that God is composed of separate\nbeings. This is where Trinity became the\nofficial doctrine of the Catholic Church\n9. In 381 A.D. at the Council of Constantinople\n(today’s Istanbul, Turkey), the Creed of Nicea\nwas declared to be the sole, legal religion in\nthe empire. The doctrine of the Trinity was\nnow fully established by Roman law. And, all\nwho opposed this creed were branded as\ntraitors and heretics, were ex-communicated,\nsuffered great punishment, and even lost\ntheir lives. Instantly, anyone who believed\nthat God was One and not a Trinity became\nshut off from society and the religious ruling\npowers.\n\n26\n\n10. As the Apostolic era faded so did many\nscriptural practices. Greek philosophers\nintroduced strange doctrines and heathen\npractices when Constantine’s Edict invited\ninfluential heathens to assume leadership\nroles. Thus, corruption, pagan ideas,\nsuperstitions and ceremonies crept in.\nFormer heathen feasts became church\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":27,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nfestivals and were given new names and\nobservances. The world fell into a time\nperiod known as the dark ages.\na. The Lord’s Supper became a sacrifice\ninstead of a memorial. The Catholic\nChurch taught transubstantiation (idea\nthat the wine became the actual blood\nof Jesus and that the bread became the\nactual flesh of Jesus).\nb. In 431 A.D., a Catholic Council convened\nin Ephesus which established that Mary\nwas the mother of God. It is important to\nnote that in this same city the goddess\nDiana, the supposed mother of the gods,\nhad been worshiped (Acts 19:28-35). Acts\n19:35 “Men of Ephesus, what man is there\nwho does not know that the city of the\nEphesians is temple guardian of the great\ngoddess Diana.” To provide a Christian\nflavor, the name was simply changed\nfrom Diana to Mary.\nc. Bishops ruled over the priests, called the\nclergy, and the Pope ruled over everyone\nelse (461 A.D.).\nd. The doctrine of Purgatory, or “the\nintermediate place between heaven and\nhell,” was declared true in 593 A.D. Prayer\nto the dead was now taught as helpful for\npeople’s salvation.\ne. Holy Water started to be used (850 A.D.).\nf. Celibacy was imposed upon all clergy\nby Pope Gregory the 7th of Hildabrand\n(ruled in 1073 and 1085 A.D.). Priests\n\n27\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":28,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nwere required to renounce their wives\nand children or to give up their offices.\nThis was the end of marriage among the\nCatholic clergy. The Bible says that men\nshould be married (see I Timothy 3:15 and 1 Timothy 3:12). He also claimed\nthat the Roman Catholic Pope alone was\nthe rock of the Church, and that he was\nabove all earthly sovereigns.\ng. The beginning of praying a set of\nrepetitious prayers known as the rosary\nstarted (1090 A.D.). This was instituted\neven though Jesus, Himself, told us not to\npray in a vain, repetitious way in Matthew\n6:7.\nh. The sale of indulgences began which was\na system of payment for the release of\nsins. Wealthy men could pay for their\nsins in advance to avoid risk of eternal\ndamnation (1190 A.D.).\ni. The Inquisition started in 1209 A.D. (read\nabout this online). The ruling church put\nanyone to death who didn’t agree with its\nteachings. The method of sprinkling for\nbaptism became doctrine, and the only\nprocedure used to baptize (1240 A.D.).\n11. In 1054 A.D., the Catholic Church split into\ntwo organizations because of the debate\nover the different doctrines of the Trinity [the\nWestern Trinity (Tertullian) and the Eastern\nTrinity view (Origen)]. Also, the Western\nChurch spoke Latin and believed in icons (or\nstatues and relics that could be prayed to),\nbut the Eastern Church spoke Greek and did\nnot believe in icons. The Pope in Rome ex-\n\n28\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":29,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\ncommunicated the Bishop in Constantinople.\nThe Churches were then called “The Roman\nCatholic Church” (Latin Western) and “The\nGreek Orthodox Church” (Greek Eastern\nChurch). The men who led the Reformation\naway from icons were not seeking to\nwithdraw themselves from the Roman\nCatholic Church. Rather, they were sincerely\nseeking to improve it. That is why the\nchurches of the east stayed the same in basic\ndoctrines. We find that many of the greatest\nreformers throughout history stayed within\nthe Roman Catholic Church until they were\nliterally thrown out or excommunicated.\n12. In 1540 A.D. at The Council of Trent, it was\ndeclared that the traditions of the Roman\nCatholic Church become equal in authority\nto anything the Bible said! This is in complete\ncontradiction to the Scripture which states\nnot to add or take away from the Word of\nGod (see Revelation 22:19).\nc. Reformation Christianity\nRefer to Chart L10.4-6\nBrave reformers started the Reformation.\nMany of them founded Protest or Protestant\nchurches. This was the beginning of\nReformation Christianity — “Saved by\nfaith alone!” Yet, they also continued to\ncarry some of the doctrines of the Greek\nphilosophers — their attitude was that the\nApostles were ignorant and so God left it\nto them to interpret scripture correctly. In\n1382, John Wycliffe of England led a Protest\nmovement for freedom from the Catholic\nChurch. He insisted that Christ was the head\nof the Church, not the Pope; and that the\nBible, not the Catholic Church, was the sole\nauthority for the believer. He translated the\nfirst English New Testament.\n\n29\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":30,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\na) 1400-1500A.D.\n• John Huss (1455 A.D.) invented the\nprinting press which made the Bible\navailable to the public.\nb) 1500-1600A.D.\n• Martin Luther, a Catholic monk, on\nOctober 31st, 1517, nailed his theses to\nthe door of a church. His theses gave 95\nreasons why the sale of indulgences was\nwrong. This started the Reformation and\nthe Lutheran Church which believed in\nJustification by Faith.\n• The Anabaptists of Switzerland in 1525\nsaw that infant baptism was incorrect.\n• John Calvin founded Calvinism (1531 A.D.)\n• Anglican/Episcopalian/Church of England\n(1534 A.D.) formed when the Pope would\nnot grant a divorce to King Henry VIII.\n• John Knox led the reformation in Scotland\nand formed the Presbyterians (1536 A.D.)\nand instituted communion as a memorial.\n• Thomas Cartwright led a group in\nEngland that desired to purify the Church\nof England. This group became known as\nthe Puritans/Separatists and formed the\nCongregational Church (1580 A.D.) They\nbelieved in the separation of Church and\nState.\nc) 1600-1700A.D.\n• The first Baptist Church (1609-1612\nA.D.) was formed. They separated from\nthe Church of England because of their\nbaptismal practices (by immersion only).\nThey were against baptism by sprinkling.\n• The first American colonists were\n\n30\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":31,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nSeparatists called Pilgrims (1620 A.D.).\n• George Fox in 1647 led a revival\nmovement in which many spoke with\ntongues. The people of this movement\nwere called the Quakers, or Friends.\nd) 1700-1800A.D.\n• The Moravians were started. They\nwere a group which took the Great\nCommission very seriously and sent\nmany missionaries around the world. It\nis stated that they conducted the longest\ncontinuous prayer chain in history.\n• Jonathan Edwards is linked with the Great\nAwakening in New England in North\nAmerica where many repented and were\nmoved by the power of God.\n• George Whitefield and the Wesley\nBrothers (Charles & John) began to\npreach the methods of living a holy\nlife for God and became known as the\nMethodists (1739 A.D.). Also, through the\nMethodists, Sunday school was started\nfor children.\n\n31\n\ne) 1800-1900 A.D.\n• The Christian Church (1820) preached\nthat baptism was for the remission of\nsins.\n• Charles Finney (1821-1842) was a great\nrevivalist in America, and he started the\nanxious seat or altar area where people\ncould come to pray after a preached\nmessage.\n• Thomas Campbell, a former Presbyterian,\nformed the Disciples of Christ (1846).\n• Charles Spurgeon grew large crowds\nwhen he preached.\n• Dwight L. Moody (1865) formed the\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":32,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nYoung Men’s Christian Association (YMCA)\nin America which was formed to keep\nyouth off the streets.\nf) Pentecostalism (1900)\nRefer to Chart L10.5-6\n\n32\n\n• People began to receive the Baptism\nof the Holy Ghost with the evidence of\nspeaking with tongues in large numbers\nfrom every Christian organization in the\nworld.\n• On January 1, 1901 in Topeka, Kansas,\nAgnes Ozman a Bible school student\nreceived the Holy Spirit speaking in other\ntongues after 3 days of intense fasting\nand prayer—the school had sought the\nLord to know the sign of receiving the\nHoly Spirit. Soon, many others received\nthe experience. Pockets of people had\nalways throughout the ages received the\nHoly Spirit with evidence of speaking in\ntongues, but this single event sparked a\nrevival where many sought and received\nthe Holy Spirit baptism.\n• As the news spread, Holy Spirit\noutpourings started to spread across\nKansas, Missouri, Texas and California\nand to the rest of the world. In Los\nAngeles, California, on Azusa Street\n(1906), a congregation began to pray\nfor the outpouring of the Spirit. This\ncongregation was unique for many in\nthat time were chained by the idea of\nracism—black men and women could\nnot mix with white men and women. But\nthe Spirit broke prejudice and thousands\nfrom around the world, missionaries,\naccomplished ministers, and people from\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":33,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nall walks of life came and received the\nHoly Spirit speaking with tongues. Soon,\nthe entire nation of America was swept\ninto the revival fires of Pentecostalism.\nProgressively more light, truth and\nrevelation started to occur. Filled with\nthe fresh experience of the Holy Spirit\nbaptism, men began searching the Word\nof God with new fervor (John 16:13\n“Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is\ncome, he will guide you into all truth”).\nThroughout history, whenever sincere\nhearts sought for God, more scriptural\ntruths were always revealed.\nd. The Church Restored\n\n33\n\nAlthough throughout history, groups who\nbelieved in the Oneness of God can be\nfound, there was never a strongly visible,\nworld-wide movement of this great scriptural\nTruth until 1913 (see The Way Called Heresy,\nan excellent book on Oneness movements\nthroughout history). During a camp-meeting\nin California of Pentecostals from around\nthe world (including China, Canada, and\nother countries) the message of Jesus name\nbaptism was revealed to the attendees. Soon,\nmany Christian people began to see the\nnecessity of rebaptism. Many left everything\nthey had to preach this wonderful truth.\nAlmost instantly, in just one year, entire\ncongregations were being rebaptized across\nthe United States, Mexico, and Canada.\nAs the message circled the globe, Russia,\nIndia, China and many other countries were\npenetrated with the Gospel message of\nOneness and Jesus name baptism in just a\nfew years. In one location in China, 4 people\nwere born again of the water and Spirit every\nday for 4 years (see Profiles of Pentecostal\nMissionaries, Mary Wallace, pg. 328). At\none specific point in this particular area,\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":34,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\n600 Chinese were baptized in Jesus name\nin 6 weeks (see Phenomenon of Pentecost,\nFrank Ewart, pg. 140). Today, the Oneness\nmovement now stands at 617 Oneness\norganizations worldwide with at least 27\nmillion known believers worldwide (Our God\nis One: The Story of Oneness Pentecostals,\nTalmadge French).\nII. The Apostles’ Doctrine is the Word of God\n\nJohn 17:17-20\nSanctify them by Your truth. Your word is truth. 18 As You sent Me\ninto the world, I also have sent them into the world. 19 And for their\nsakes I sanctify Myself, that they also may be sanctified by the truth.\n20 “I do not pray for these alone, but also for those who will\nbelieve in Me through their word;\n\nThere were 400 silent years between the Old\nTestament and the New Testament. After\nthat, God chose to reveal His Words through\nthe apostles’ doctrine. This was the doctrine\nthat He handed to the apostles for them to\nimpact the world.\n2 Timothy 3:16\nAll Scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for\ndoctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness\n\nQuestions to consider:\nIf the apostles’ doctrine was not the Word\nof God, then why would the early Church be\nsteadfast in it?\n\n34\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":35,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nActs 2:42\nAnd they continued steadfastly in the apostles’ doctrine and\nfellowship, in the breaking of bread, and in prayers.\n\nWhy would Paul instruct Timothy to teach no\nother doctrine?\n\n1 Timothy 1:3\nAs I urged you when I went into Macedonia--remain in Ephesus that\nyou may charge some that they teach no other doctrine,\n\nWhy did Paul refer to his writings as the\ncommandments of the Lord?\n\n1 Corinthians 14:37\nIf anyone thinks himself to be a prophet or spiritual, let him\nacknowledge that the things which I write to you are the\ncommandments of the Lord.\n\nIf doctrine is not powerful, then why did Paul\ntell Timothy that it has the power to save?\n\n1 Timothy 4:16\nTake heed to yourself and to the doctrine. Continue in them, for in\ndoing this you will save both yourself and those who hear you.\n\n35\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":36,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nIf the apostles’ doctrine were mere\ninstructions, why did Paul write in his epistles\nto note any person who did not obey the\nwords of the epistles and have no company\nwith him?\n\n2 Thessalonians 3:14\nAnd if anyone does not obey our word in this epistle, note that person\nand do not keep company with him, that he may be ashamed.\n\nIf they were mere instructions, why would\nPeter refer them as the commandments of\nJesus Christ?\n\n2 Peter 3:2\nthat you may be mindful of the words which were spoken before by\nthe holy prophets, and of the commandment of us, the apostles of the\nLord and Savior\n\nWhy were believers told to remember the\nwords of the apostles?\n\nJude 1:17\nBut you, beloved, remember the words which were spoken before by\nthe apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ:\n\nNotice how the apostles’ doctrine and the\nWord of God is used interchangeably in the\nbook of Acts.\n\n36\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":37,"text":"MODULAR SECTIONS\n\nLesson 10\n\nActs 2:42\nAnd they continued steadfastly in the apostles’ doctrine and\nfellowship, and in breaking of bread, and in prayers.\nActs 4:2\nBeing grieved that they taught the people, and preached through\nJesus the resurrection from the dead.\nActs 4:29-31\nAnd now, Lord, behold their threatenings: and grant unto thy\nservants, that with all boldness they may speak thy word, By\nstretching forth thine hand to heal; and that signs and wonders may\nbe done by the name of thy holy child Jesus. And when they had\nprayed, the place was shaken where they were assembled together;\nand they were all filled with the Holy Ghost, and they spake the word\nof God with boldness.\nActs 4:33\nAnd with great power gave the apostles witness of the resurrection\nof the Lord Jesus: and great grace was upon them all.\nActs 5:25\nThen came one and told them, saying, Behold, the men whom ye put\nin prison are standing in the temple, and teaching the people.\nActs 5:28-29\nSaying, did not we straitly command you that ye should not teach in\nthis name? and, behold, ye have filled Jerusalem with your doctrine,\nand intend to bring this man’s blood upon us. Then Peter and the\nother apostles answered and said, we ought to obey God rather than\nmen.\nActs 5:42\nAnd daily in the temple, and in every house, they ceased not to teach\nand preach Jesus Christ.\nActs 6:2\nThen the twelve called the multitude of the disciples unto them, and\nsaid, It is not reason that we should leave the word of God, and serve\ntables.\nActs 6:4\nBut we will give ourselves continually to prayer, and to the ministry\nof the word.\nActs 6:7\nAnd the word of God increased; and the number of the disciples\nmultiplied in Jerusalem greatly; and a great company of the priests\nwere obedient to the faith.\n\n37\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]},"11":{"lesson":11,"sourceType":"Student Notes","pageCount":20,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 11\n\nTimeline\nRefer to Chart L11 . 1-5\n\nCast (Characters)\nJesus, disciples, the Church, Anti-Christ, False prophet"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 11\n\nLesson Background\nBefore Jesus ascended, He pinpointed a generation who\nwould be living on earth immediately before His return.\nSeveral of the signs mentioned will affect every nation in\nthe earth. Some will affect the nation of Israel while others\ndescribe the condition of the church. The signs precede two\nmajor events in human history called the Rapture and the\nGreat Tribulation.\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Jesus spoke of His return in the future\n\n3\n\nB. Signs of the end (Global)\n\n3\n\nC. Signs of the end (Israel)\n\n5\n\nD. Signs within the Church\n\n6\n\nE. The Rapture\n\n7\n\nF. The Great Tribulation\n\n12\n\n•\n\nSeal\n\n•\n\nTrumpets\n\n•\n\nAntichrist and False Prophet\n\n•\n\nVials"},{"page":3,"text":"A\n\nJESUS SPOKE OF HIS RETURN IN\nTHE FUTURE\n\nLesson 11\nJohn 14:2-3\n“In My Father’s house are many mansions; if it were not so, I would\nhave told you. I go to prepare a place for you. 3 “And if I go and\nprepare a place for you, I will come again and receive you to Myself;\nthat where I am, there you may be also.\nActs 1:11\nwho also said, “Men of Galilee, why do you stand gazing up into\nheaven? This same Jesus, who was taken up from you into heaven,\nwill so come in like manner as you saw Him go into heaven.”\n\nJesus Christ is coming back again to receive His\ndisciples (the Church). Until then, the world will\nexperience signs that lets us know that we are near\nthe end time.\n\nB\n\nSIGNS OF THE END (GLOBAL)\nJesus on signs of the end times\nRefer to Chart L11 . 2-5\nMatthew 24:3-13\nNow as He sat on the Mount of Olives, the disciples came to Him\nprivately, saying, “Tell us, when will these things be? And what will\nbe the sign of Your coming, and of the end of the age?”4 And Jesus\nanswered and said to them: “Take heed that no one deceives you.5\n“For many will come in My name, saying, ‘I am the Christ,’ and will\ndeceive many.6 “And you will hear of wars and rumors of wars. See\nthat you are not troubled; for all these things must come to pass,\nbut the end is not yet.7 “For nation will rise against nation, and\nkingdom against kingdom. And there will be famines, pestilences,\nand earthquakes in various places.8 “All these are the beginning of\nsorrows.9 “Then they will deliver you up to tribulation and kill you,\nand you will be hated by all nations for My name’s sake.10 “And\nthen many will be offended, will betray one another, and will hate\none another.11 “Then many false prophets will rise up and deceive\nmany.12 “And because lawlessness will abound, the love of many will\ngrow cold.13 “But he who endures to the end shall be saved.\n\n3"},{"page":4,"text":"Lesson 11\n\n1. False Christ – deception\n2. Wars and rumors of wars\n3. Nation against nation, kingdom against kingdom\n4. Famines, pestilence, earthquakes in various\nplaces\n5. Church persecuted for the name of Jesus\n6. Offenses, betrayal and hatred\n7. False prophets and deception\n8. Lawlessness\n9. Diminishing love\n\nCharacteristics of people\n\n2 Timothy 3:1-7\nBut know this, that in the last days perilous times will come: 2 For\nmen will be lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boasters, proud,\nblasphemers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy,3 unloving,\nunforgiving, slanderers, without self-control, brutal, despisers of\ngood, 4 traitors, headstrong, haughty, lovers of pleasure rather than\nlovers of God, 5 having a form of godliness but denying its power.\nAnd from such people turn away! 6 For of this sort are those who\ncreep into households and make captives of gullible women loaded\ndown with sins, led away by various lusts,7 always learning and never\nable to come to the knowledge of the truth.\n1 Thessalonians 5:1-4\nBut concerning the times and the seasons, brethren, you have no\nneed that I should write to you. 2 For you yourselves know perfectly\nthat the day of the Lord so comes as a thief in the night. 3 For when\nthey say, “Peace and safety!” then sudden destruction comes upon\nthem, as labor pains upon a pregnant woman. And they shall not\nescape.\nLuke 17:28-30\n“Likewise as it was also in the days of Lot: They ate, they drank, they\nbought, they sold, they planted, they built; 29 “but on the day that Lot\nwent out of Sodom it rained fire and brimstone from heaven and\ndestroyed them all. 30 “Even so will it be in the day when the Son of\nMan is revealed.\n\n4"},{"page":5,"text":"Knowledge and travel\nLesson 11\n\nDaniel 12:4\n“But you, Daniel, shut up the words, and seal the book until the time\nof the end; many shall run to and fro, and knowledge shall increase.”\n\nC\n\nSIGNS OF THE END (ISRAEL)\nAnother sign of being in the end times is the\nregathering of Israel to their land. Israel has always\nbeen an indicator of God’s prophetic time clock.\n\nJeremiah 30:3\n‘For behold, the days are coming,’ says the LORD, ‘that I will bring\nback from captivity My people Israel and Judah,’ says the LORD. ‘And\nI will cause them to return to the land that I gave to their fathers, and\nthey shall possess it.’ “\n3\n\nAmos 9:14-15\nI will bring back the captives of My people Israel; They shall build the\nwaste cities and inhabit them; They shall plant vineyards and drink\nwine from them; They shall also make gardens and eat fruit from\nthem. 15 I will plant them in their land, And no longer shall they be\npulled up From the land I have given them,” Says the LORD your God.\n\n5"},{"page":6,"text":"This prophecy was fulfilled in 14 May 1948 when\nthe United Nations gave a resolution to reinstate\nIsrael back into their land after the world war. Israel\nbecame the only nation in the world ever to be\n“born again”. God promises that they will never be\ntaken again!\n\nLesson 11\n\nKey #1: The signs in the world lets us know\nthat we are\nliving in the end times\n\nD\n\nSIGNS WITHIN THE CHURCH\nThe Church of God will experience both a falling away\n(apostasy) and great expansion and revival\nFall away from the truth\n\nMatthew 24:24\n“For false christs and false prophets will rise and show great signs\nand wonders to deceive, if possible, even the elect.\n2 Thessalonians 2:3\nLet no one deceive you by any means; for that Day will not come\nunless the falling away comes first, and the man of sin is revealed,\nthe son of perdition\n\nFalling away (Greek: apostasia)- defection from\nthe truth\n\n6"},{"page":7,"text":"Revival and expansion of the Church\nLesson 11\n\nJoel 2:1, 12-13, 27-29\nBlow the trumpet in Zion, and sound an alarm in My holy mountain!\nLet all the inhabitants of the land tremble; For the day of the LORD is\ncoming, for it is at hand...\n“Now, therefore,” says the LORD, “Turn to Me with all your heart,\nwith fasting, with weeping, and with mourning.” 13 So rend your\nheart, and not your garments; Return to the LORD your God, For He\nis gracious and merciful, Slow to anger, and of great kindness; And\nHe relents from doing harm.\n12\n\nThen you shall know that I am in the midst of Israel: I am the LORD\nyour God And there is no other. My people shall never be put to\nshame. 28 “And it shall come to pass afterward That I will pour out My\nSpirit on all flesh; Your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, Your\nold men shall dream dreams, Your young men shall see vision. 29 And\nalso on My menservants and on My maidservants I will pour out My\nSpirit in those days.\n27\n\nMatthew 24:14\n“And this gospel of the kingdom will be preached in all the world as a\nwitness to all the nations, and then the end will come.\n\nIt is not hard to name the two most evangelistic\nperiod in Church history: the early Church, and\nthe Church in the end times. Both of these eras\nshare a common belief that Jesus Christ is coming\nback soon. This event is commonly known as the\nRapture.\n\nE\n\nTHE RAPTURE\nRefer to Chart L11 . 3-5\n\n1 Thessalonians 4:15-18\nFor this we say to you by the word of the Lord, that we who are alive\nand remain until the coming of the Lord will by no means precede\nthose who are asleep.16 For the Lord Himself will descend from\nheaven with a shout, with the voice of an archangel, and with the\ntrumpet of God. And the dead in Christ will rise first. 17 Then we who\nare alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the\nclouds to meet the Lord in the air. And thus we shall always be with\nthe Lord. 18 Therefore comfort one another with these words.\n\n7"},{"page":8,"text":"Lesson 11\n\nThe word “Rapture” comes from the Latin word\nmeaning “Caught up”.\nThe Rapture is the appearing of Jesus to gather His\nChurch to be with Him.\nThe Rapture is not to be confused with the second\ncoming of Jesus. The Rapture is Jesus coming FOR\nHis Church while the second coming is Jesus coming\nWITH His Church.\n\nMatthew 24:30-31\n“Then the sign of the Son of Man will appear in heaven, and then all\nthe tribes of the earth will mourn, and they will see the Son of Man\ncoming on the clouds of heaven with power and great glory. 31 “And\nHe will send His angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they will\ngather together His elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven\nto the other.\n\nFacts about the rapture\nThe Rapture will come suddenly\n\nMatthew 24:36-39\n“But of that day and hour no one knows, not even the angels of\nheaven, but My Father only. 37 But as the days of Noah were, so also\nwill the coming of the Son of Man be. 38 For as in the days before\nthe flood, they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in\nmarriage, until the day that Noah entered the ark, 39 and did not\nknow until the flood came and took them all away, so also will the\ncoming of the Son of Man be.\n1 Corinthians 15:51-52\nBehold, I tell you a mystery: We shall not all sleep, but we shall all\nbe changed--52 in a moment, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last\ntrumpet. For the trumpet will sound, and the dead will be raised\nincorruptible, and we shall be changed.\n\n8"},{"page":9,"text":"We will put on immortality at the Rapture\n\nLesson 11\n\n1 Corinthians 15:53- 54\nFor this corruptible must put on incorruption, and this mortal must put\non immortality. 54 So when this corruptible has put on incorruption,\nand this mortal has put on immortality, then shall be brought to pass\nthe saying that is written: “Death is swallowed up in victory.”\n\nThe Rapture will deliver us from the judgment\nof God to come upon the earth\n\n1 Thessalonians 5:9-10\nFor God did not appoint us to wrath, but to obtain salvation through\nour Lord Jesus Christ, 10 who died for us, that whether we wake or\nsleep, we should live together with Him\n\nThe Rapture will be selective\n\nLuke 17:34-36\n“I tell you, in that night there will be two men in one bed: the one will\nbe taken and the other will be left. 35 “Two women will be grinding\ntogether: the one will be taken and the other left. 36 “Two men will be in\nthe field: the one will be taken and the other left.”\n\n9"},{"page":10,"text":"Who will make it to the Rapture?\nLesson 11\n\nThe promise of the Rapture was given to the\nChurch. We need to be part of the Church, the\nkingdom of God to be saved!\n\nActs 2:38-41\nThen Peter said to them, “Repent, and let every one of you be\nbaptized in the name of Jesus Christ for the remission of sins; and\nyou shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit. 39 “For the promise is to\nyou and to your children, and to all who are afar off, as many as the\nLord our God will call.” 40 And with many other words he testified and\nexhorted them, saying, “Be saved from this perverse generation.” 41\nThen those who gladly received his word were baptized; and that day\nabout three thousand souls were added to them.\nJohn 3:5\nJesus answered, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless one is born of\nwater and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God.\nColossians 1:27\nTo them God willed to make known what are the riches of the glory\nof this mystery among the Gentiles: which is Christ in you, the hope\nof glory.\n\nKey #2: Only those who are\ninto the kingdom of God will make it to\nthe Rapture\n\n10"},{"page":11,"text":"How does the Rapture affect us today?\n1. It causes us to consider our salvation\n\nLesson 11\n\n2 Corinthians 6:2\nFor He says: “In an acceptable time I have heard you, And in the day\nof salvation I have helped you.” Behold, now is the accepted time;\nbehold, now is the day of salvation.\n\n2. It produces a desire in us to be holy to be\nready for the Rapture\nTitus 2:11-13\nFor the grace of God that brings salvation has appeared to all men,\n12\nteaching us that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should\nlive soberly, righteously, and godly in the present age,13 looking for\nthe blessed hope and glorious appearing of our great God and Savior\nJesus Christ\n1 John 3:3\nAnd everyone who has this hope in Him purifies himself, just as He\nis pure.\n\n3. It causes us to reprioritise our lives (time,\nmoney, goal) to God and His kingdom\nActs 1:6-8\nTherefore, when they had come together, they asked Him, saying,\n“Lord, will You at this time restore the kingdom to Israel? 7 And He\nsaid to them, “It is not for you to know times or seasons which the\nFather has put in His own authority. 8 “But you shall receive power\nwhen the Holy Spirit has come upon you; and you shall be witnesses\nto Me in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the end of\nthe earth.”\nMatthew 6:33\nBut seek first the kingdom of God and His righteousness, and all\nthese things shall be added to you.\n\nGod is not asking us to guess when the Rapture is going to\ntake place, but rather focus on what He commanded us to\ndo… be a witness!\nThose who do not make it to the Rapture will be left behind\non earth to face a series of judgments in a period known as\nthe Great Tribulation.\n\n11"},{"page":12,"text":"Key #3: Those who do not make it to the Rapture\nwill have to face the\n\nLesson 11\n\nF\n\nTHE GREAT TRIBULATION\nRefer to Chart L11 . 4-5\nBible scholars have different views of when the Great\nTribulation will start. Some say it will happen before the\nrapture and resume only after the Church is gone while\nothers say that it only starts after the rapture.\nRegardless of their views, they all agree that the earth\nwill experience a great tribulation never seen before in\nhuman history.\n\nMatthew 24:21\nFor then there will be great tribulation, such as has not been since\nthe beginning of the world until this time, no, nor ever shall be.\n\nThe great tribulation is a combination of God’s vindication\nfor wickedness and injustice, satan’s attempt to destroy\nman, and Israel’s opportunity to cry out for their Messiah\nonce again.\n\nThe Book of Revelation summarizes the great tribulation\ninto four sets of seven judgments: Seven Seals, Seven\nTrumpets, Seven Vials and Seven Thunders (Note:\nThunder judgments are not revealed to us in Scripture,\nRevelation 10:4)\n\n12"},{"page":13,"text":"Seal Judgment (Revelation 6)\nLesson 11\n\nSeal 1 – White Horse (Conquering Leader)\nSeal 2 – Red Horse (War)\nSeal 3 – Black Horse (Inflation of Food)\nSeal 4 – Pale Horse (Death)\nSeal 5 – Martyrs crying for justice\nSeal 6 – Earthquake and signs from the sky\nSeal 7 – Silence in heaven (Seven Trumpets released)\n\nTrumpet Judgment (Revelation 8)\nTrumpet 1 – Judgment on Land (1/3 of trees burned,\nand all green grass)\nTrumpet 2 – Judgment on Salt Water (1/3 of oceans\nblood, 1/3 of ships & fish)\nTrumpet 3 – Judgment on Fresh Water (1/3 of drinking\nwater poisoned)\nTrumpet 4 – Judgment on Heavens (1/3 of sun, moon\nand stars darkened)\nTrumpet 5 – Army of Demonic Locusts from\nBottomless Pit (five months)\n\nRevelation 9:6\nIn those days men will seek death and will not find it; they will desire\nto die, and death will flee from them.\n\nTrumpet 6 – Army of (Demonic?) Horsemen – by now,\nhalf of mankind is dead\n\nRevelation 9:20-21\nBut the rest of mankind, who were not killed by these plagues, did\nnot repent of the works of their hands, that they should not worship\ndemons, and idols of gold, silver, brass, stone, and wood, which can\nneither see nor hear nor walk. 21 And they did not repent of their\nmurders or their sorceries or their sexual immorality or their thefts.\n\nTrumpet 7 – Great Voices in Heaven\n\n13"},{"page":14,"text":"Vial Judgment (Revelation 16)\nLesson 11\n\nVial 1 – Grievous Sores\nVial 2 – Sea Turned to Blood (all salt water)\nVial 3 – Rivers Turned to Blood (all fresh water)\nVial 4 – Scorching Heat from the Sun\nVial 5 – Darkness and Pain\n\nRevelation 16:8-11\nAnd the fourth angel poured out his vial upon the sun; and power\nwas given unto him to scorch men with fire. 9 And men were\nscorched with great heat, and blasphemed the name of God, which\nhath power over these plagues: and they repented not to give him\nglory. 10 And the fifth angel poured out his vial upon the seat of the\nbeast; and his kingdom was full of darkness; and they gnawed their\ntongues for pain, 11 And blasphemed the God of heaven because of\ntheir pains and their sores, and repented not of their deeds.\n\nVial 6 – Armies Cross Euphrates River (gathering to\nBattle of Armageddon)\nVial 7 – Great Earthquake and Hail\n\nAppearance of the Antichrist and False Prophet\nThe Great Tribulation will see two characters (symbolized\nas “beasts” in Revelation) rise to prominence in the world\nstage.\n(You can read 13:1-18 for description of these two\nindividuals)\n1. First Beast – Antichrist\nAntichrist – pseudo Christ\nA forceful political leader who will dominate world\nleadership in a one world system of government.\nThis government will envelop all political, religious\nand economic areas of life.\n\n2. Second Beast – False Prophet\nA religious leader who will show forth false signs\nand wonders to deceive the world into worshiping\nthe Antichrist.\n\n14"},{"page":15,"text":"2 Thessalonians 2:3-4, 9-10\nLet no one deceive you by any means; for that Day will not come\nunless the falling away comes first, and the man of sin is revealed,\nthe son of perdition, 4 who opposes and exalts himself above all\nthat is called God or that is worshiped, so that he sits as God in the\ntemple of God, showing himself that he is God. ...9 The coming of\nthe lawless one is according to the working of Satan, with all power,\nsigns, and lying wonders, 10 and with all unrighteous deception\namong those who perish, because they did not receive the love of\nthe truth, that they might be saved.\n\nLesson 11\n\nSummary of actions by the two beasts\n•\n\n•\n•\n•\n•\n\nAntichrist will appear to be favourable to the Jews\nand negotiate a peace treaty that allows them to\nrebuild their Third Temple (See Daniel 9:27)\nThis peace agreement will be broken midway and He\nwill turn against Israel\nAntichrist will blaspheme God, His name, tabernacle\nand heavenly dwellers\nGod’s people will be persecuted and warred against\nThe Antichrist will cause all to be marked in the right\nhand or forehead to buy or sell\n\nJudgment on those who take Mark of the Beast\n\nRevelation 14:11\nAnd the smoke of their torment ascends forever and ever; and they\nhave no rest day or night, who worship the beast and his image, and\nwhoever receives the mark of his name.”\n\n15"},{"page":16,"text":"Judgment on the religious and economic system\nof the Antichrist and False prophet\nLesson 11\n\nSee Revelation 17-18\nThe Anti-Christ and False prophet will afterward lead a\nworld army against the nation of Israel. This war is named\n“the battle of Armageddon” and will pave the way for the\nsecond coming of Jesus Christ.\n\nLessons from the Great Tribulation\n•\n•\n•\n\nThere is no mention of the Church in this period\nbecause of the Rapture\nWe do not hear of conversion in this period except\nfor the Jewish people\nEven if there was a slim possibility of someone\nturning to God in this era, it would be near\nimpossible to live for God in such a condition\n\nKey #4: We must make it to the Rapture because\nof the\nto come\n\n16"},{"page":17,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 11\n\nRefer to Chart L11 . 5-5\n1. The signs in the world lets us know that we\nare currently living in the end times.\n2. Only those who are born again into the\nkingdom of God will make it to the Rapture.\n3. Those who do not make it to the Rapture\nwill have to face the Great Tribulation.\n4. We must make it to the Rapture because of\nthe judgments to come.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n17"},{"page":18,"text":"Charts\nLesson 11\n\n18"},{"page":19,"text":"Charts\nLesson 11\n\n19"},{"page":20,"text":"Charts\nLesson 11\n\n20"}]},"12":{"lesson":12,"sourceType":"Teacher Notes","pageCount":17,"pages":[{"page":1,"text":"Lesson 12\n\nLesson Objectives\nPrimary Objective\n•\n\nThe student will be able to recall the sequence of\nevents after the tribulation leading up to eternity\n\n•\n\nThe student will be able to describe both heaven\nand the lake of fire\n\nSecondary Objectives\n•\n\nThe student will reassess their life and\npriorities in light of eternity\n\nTimeline\n\nCast (Characters)\nJesus, Saints, Sinners, Angels, Anti-Christ, False prophet,\nSatan\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":2,"text":"Lesson 12\n\nLesson Background\nJust before Jesus and His saints intervene to save Israel at the\nBattle of Armageddon, we see a prophecy of the Marriage\nSupper of the Lamb. The Battle of Armageddon will usher\nin the kingdom of God where Jesus will rule the earth for a\nmillennium (a thousand years). Satan will then be released\nto deceive the nations and attempt to lead a final rebellion\nagainst Jesus and His saints. Afterward, there will be a Great\nWhite Throne Judgment where every human being from\nevery age will stand before God, the Righteous Judge, and be\nallocated their final place for eternity.\n\nLesson Outline\nA. Marriage Supper of the Lamb\nB. The Second coming of Jesus\n•\n\nThe Battle of Armageddon\n\nC. Millennium Kingdom of God\n\n3\n3\n6\n\nD. Judgments of God\n•\n\nJudgment Seat of Christ\n\n8\n\n• White Throne Judgment\nE. Eternity\n\n11\n\n•\n\nLake of Fire\n\n•\n\nA New Heaven and Earth\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":3,"text":"A\n\nMARRIAGE SUPPER OF THE LAMB\nRefer to Chart L12.1-3\n\nLesson 12\n\nPrior to the second coming of Jesus, the raptured\nChurch, who is the Bride of Christ, will gather at the\nMarriage Supper of the Lamb.\n\nRevelation 19:7-9\nLet us be glad and rejoice and give Him glory, for the marriage of the\nLamb has come, and His wife has made herself ready.” 8 And to her it\nwas granted to be arrayed in fine linen, clean and bright, for the fine\nlinen is the righteous acts of the saints. 9 Then he said to me, “Write:\n‘Blessed are those who are called to the marriage supper of the\nLamb!’ “ And he said to me, “These are the true sayings of God.”\n\nJesus will now return to earth with His saints to\ndefeat the Antichrist and the combine armies of\nthe world.\n\nB\n\nTHE SECOND COMING OF JESUS\nThe second coming of Jesus to establish the\nphysical kingdom of God on earth was prophesied\nnumerous times in the Old Testament.\nNebuchadnezzar’s dream\nKing Nebuchadnezzar had a dream of empires\nthat would arise on earth starting from\nBabylon. Through Daniel’s interpretation, we\nknow that the final kingdom that would arise\nwould be God’s kingdom who will rule the\nworld and stand forever.\n\n3\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":4,"text":"Daniel 2:44\n\nLesson 12\n\nAnd in the days of these kings the God of heaven will set up a\nkingdom which shall never be destroyed; and the kingdom shall not\nbe left to other people; it shall break in pieces and consume all these\nkingdoms, and it shall stand forever.\n\nDaniel’s dream\nDaniel also had a dream about the\ncharacteristics of empires that arise on the\nearth. The conclusion of his dream was also\nabout the coming kingdom of God.\n\nDaniel 7:21-22, 27\nI was watching; and the same horn was making war against the\nsaints, and prevailing against them, 22 until the Ancient of Days came,\nand a judgment was made in favor of the saints of the Most High,\nand the time came for the saints to possess the kingdom… 27 Then\nthe kingdom and dominion, And the greatness of the kingdoms\nunder the whole heaven, Shall be given to the people, the saints\nof the Most High. His kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all\ndominions shall serve and obey Him.’\n\nBattle of Armageddon\nAll nations will gather together against\nJerusalem.\n\nZechariah 14:1-5\nBehold, the day of the LORD is coming, and your spoil will be divided\nin your midst. 2 For I will gather all the nations to battle against\nJerusalem; The city shall be taken, the houses rifled, And the women\nravished. Half of the city shall go into captivity, But the remnant of\nthe people shall not be cut off from the city. 3 Then the LORD will\ngo forth and fight against those nations, As He fights in the day of\nbattle. 4 And in that day His feet will stand on the Mount of Olives,\nwhich faces Jerusalem on the east. And the Mount of Olives shall\nbe split in two, from east to west, making a very large valley; Half\nof the mountain shall move toward the north and half of it toward\nthe south. 5 Then you shall flee through My mountain valley, For the\nmountain valley shall reach to Azal. Yes, you shall flee as you fled\nfrom the earthquake In the days of Uzziah king of Judah. Thus the\nLORD my God will come, And all the saints with You.\n\n4\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":5,"text":"Lesson 12\n\nIsrael will not be able to stand against the\ncombined armies of the world, but Jesus will\nrescue them. Also, Jesus brings with Him the\nChurch that has previously gone to the Marriage\nSupper of the Lamb. The Church enters as the\nArmies in Heaven, clothed in linen and riding on\nwhite horses.\n\nRevelation 19:11-16\nNow I saw heaven opened, and behold, a white horse. And He who\nsat on him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness He\njudges and makes war. 12 His eyes were like a flame of fire, and on\nHis head were many crowns. He had a name written that no one\nknew except Himself. 13 He was clothed with a robe dipped in blood,\nand His name is called The Word of God. 14 And the armies in heaven,\nclothed in fine linen, white and clean, followed Him on white horses.\nNow out of His mouth goes a sharp sword, that with it He should\nstrike the nations. And He Himself will rule them with a rod of iron.\nHe Himself treads the winepress of the fierceness and wrath of\nAlmighty God. 16 And He has on His robe and on His thigh a name\nwritten: KING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS.\n15\n\nOutcome of the battle\nBoth the Antichrist and False prophet will be\nthrown into the Lake of Fire while satan will be\nbound in prison of the bottomless pit for one\nthousand years.\n\nRevelation 19:19-21\nAnd I saw the beast, the kings of the earth, and their armies,\ngathered together to make war against Him who sat on the horse\nand against His army. 20 Then the beast was captured, and with him\nthe false prophet who worked signs in his presence, by which he\ndeceived those who received the mark of the beast and those who\nworshiped his image. These two were cast alive into the lake of fire\nburning with brimstone. 21 And the rest were killed with the sword\nwhich proceeded from the mouth of Him who sat on the horse. And\nall the birds were filled with their flesh.\n\n5\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":6,"text":"Revelation 20:1-3\nThen I saw an angel coming down from heaven, having the key to\nthe bottomless pit and a great chain in his hand. 2 He laid hold of the\ndragon, that serpent of old, who is the Devil and Satan, and bound\nhim for a thousand years; 3 and he cast him into the bottomless pit,\nand shut him up, and set a seal on him, so that he should deceive\nthe nations no more till the thousand years were finished. But after\nthese things he must be released for a little while.\n\nLesson 12\n\nKey #1: The Antichrist and his army\nwill be defeated by Jesus at His second\ncoming.\n\nC\n\nMILLENNIUM KINGDOM OF GOD\nRefer to Chart L12.2-3\n\nJesus will set up His kingdom on earth for one\nthousand years.\n\nRevelation 20:4\nAnd I saw thrones, and they sat on them, and judgment was\ncommitted to them. Then I saw the souls of those who had been\nbeheaded for their witness to Jesus and for the word of God, who\nhad not worshiped the beast or his image, and had not received\nhis mark on their foreheads or on their hands. And they lived and\nreigned with Christ for a thousand years.\n\n6\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":7,"text":"Lesson 12\n\nDescription of the millennium kingdom\n- Eden recreated (Zechariah 8:12; Isaiah 35:1. 6-7;\nRevelation 22:2-3)\n- Animal natures changed (Isaiah 11:6-8, 65:25)\n- Health restored (Isaiah 33:24; 35:5-6)\n- Human life extended (Isaiah 65:20; Zechariah\n8:4)\n- One language (Zephaniah 3:9)\n- One religion (Jeremiah 31:31-36; Zechariah 14:9)\n- Peace and justice (Isaiah 2:4; Micah 4:3)\n- Jerusalem becomes headquarters (Zechariah\n14:16-17)\nReigning in the Kingdom Age\n-\n\nJesus Christ shall reign as the King of Kings and\nthe Lord of Lords\nVarious ranks and positions of authority (Rev\n1:6, 5:10; Jeremiah 30:21; 1 Cor 6:2)\nSubjects in the Kingdom (Zechariah 14:16)\n\nSatan’s Final Rebellion\nRevelation 20:7-9\nNow when the thousand years have expired, Satan will be released\nfrom his prison 8 and will go out to deceive the nations which are\nin the four corners of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them\ntogether to battle, whose number is as the sand of the sea. 9 They\nwent up on the breadth of the earth and surrounded the camp of\nthe saints and the beloved city. And fire came down from God out of\nheaven and devoured them.\n\nNote to Teacher: Refer to Man in the Garden of\nEden and how a perfect environment cannot\nproduce a perfect heart. Although there is no sin\non the outside, Man still have a sinful nature on\nthe inside.\n\nKey #2: Our choices determine where\nwe will end up in eternity\n7\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":8,"text":"D\n\nJUDGEMENTS OF GOD\n\nLesson 12\nHebrews 9:27\nAnd as it is appointed for men to die once, but after this the judgment\n\nThe Bible speaks about two types of judgments\nthat different groups of people must face.\nJudgement Seat of Christ\nWhile the Great White Throne is for the\njudgment of sin, the Judgement Seat of Christ is\na Judgement for the service of the believer.\n\nRomans 14:10-12\nBut why do you judge your brother? Or why do you show contempt for\nyour brother? For we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ.\n11\nFor it is written: “As I live, says the LORD, every knee shall bow to Me,\nAnd every tongue shall confess to God.” 12 So then each of us shall give\naccount of himself to God.\n2 Corinthians 5:10\nFor we must all appear before the judgment seat of Christ, that each\none may receive the things done in the body, according to what he has\ndone, whether good or bad.\n\nAt the Judgement seat, believers are rewarded\nbased on how faithfully they served Christ. The\nBible talks about believers receiving crowns (see\n2 Timothy 2:5, 2 Timothy 4:8, James 1:12, 1 Peter\n5:4, and Revelation 2:10).\n\n8\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":9,"text":"1 Corinthians 3:12-15\n\nLesson 12\n\nNow if anyone builds on this foundation with gold, silver, precious\nstones, wood, hay, straw, 13 each one’s work will become clear; for the\nDay will declare it, because it will be revealed by fire; and the fire will\ntest each one’s work, of what sort it is. 14 If anyone’s work which he\nhas built on it endures, he will receive a reward. 15 If anyone’s work\nis burned, he will suffer loss; but he himself will be saved, yet so as\nthrough fire.\n\nThis judgment will not determine whether we are\nsaved or lost. Calvary and the grace of God have\nassured our salvation. This is a testing of works to\ndetermine the reward, position, and rank of every\nsaint in the new administration.\nGreat White Throne Judgement\n\nRevelation 20:11-13\nThen I saw a great white throne and Him who sat on it, from whose\nface the earth and the heaven fled away. And there was found no place\nfor them. 12 And I saw the dead, small and great, standing before God,\nand books were opened. And another book was opened, which is the\nBook of Life. And the dead were judged according to their works, by\nthe things which were written in the books. 13 The sea gave up the dead\nwho were in it, and Death and Hades delivered up the dead who were\nin them. And they were judged, each one according to his works.\n\nThe wicked and unrighteous in the Old\nTestament and those who choose to reject Christ\nand His gospel will stand at the Great Throne\nJudgement. They will be judged for their sins.\n\n9\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":10,"text":"Humanity will be judged by the following:\nLesson 12\n\n1.\n\nThe Word of God\n\nJohn 12:48\nHe who rejects Me, and does not receive My words, has that which\njudges him--the word that I have spoken will judge him in the last day.\n\n2.\n\nThoughts and Motives\n\nRomans 2:16\nin the day when God will judge the secrets of men by Jesus Christ,\naccording to my gospel.\n\n3.\n\nIdle Word\n\nMatthew 12:36\nBut I say to you that for every idle word men may speak, they will give\naccount of it in the day of judgment.\n\nKey #3: The Word of God will judge us\n\n10\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":11,"text":"E\nLesson 12\n\nETERNITY\nThere are generally two places we can go at the end of\nour lives. The Bible calls the first place “The Lake of Fire”\nand the other “Heaven”.\nThe Lake of Fire\n\nRevelation 20:14-15\nThen Death and Hades were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second\ndeath. 15 And anyone not found written in the Book of Life was cast into\nthe lake of fire.\n\nThe lake of fire was originally designed to judge the\ndevil and his fallen angels. However, those who chose\nto follow satan and not Jesus have henceforth decided\nto go there also.\nDescription of hell/lake of fire\n• a place of unquenchable fire (Mark 9:44)\n• a place of consciousness (Luke 16:23-24)\n• a place of unbearable eternal torment (Luke 16:28)\n• a place of darkness (Matthew 8:12)\n• a place of intense weeping (Matthew 13:42)\n• a place of separation from loved ones (Luke 13:28)\n• a place with no hope of release (Matthew 25:46)\n• a place where memories will torment (Luke 16:28)\nSomeone once said that God doesn’t force anyone to\ngo to hell as much as He doesn’t force anyone to go to\nheaven. Along the road to the lake of fire, God came\ndown and placed Himself on the cross to save you.\nThere are also the prayers of parents, pastors, Sunday\nschool teachers, and all the other things God brings\ninto our lives to stop us on our selfish way and bring\nus to our Savior. A person must wander past all that\nto put themselves there.\n\n11\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":12,"text":"John 3:16\n\nLesson 12\n\nFor God so loved the world that He gave His only begotten Son, that\nwhoever believes in Him should not perish but have everlasting life.\n\nKey #4: The Lake of fire is the destination for\nthose who choose not to be saved.\n\nA new heaven and earth\nRevelation 21:2\nAnd I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God\nout of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.\nRevelation 21:10-27\nAnd he carried me away in the Spirit to a great and high mountain,\nand showed me the great city, the holy Jerusalem, descending out\nof heaven from God, 11 having the glory of God. Her light was like\na most precious stone, like a jasper stone, clear as crystal. 12 Also\nshe had a great and high wall with twelve gates, and twelve angels\nat the gates, and names written on them, which are the names of\nthe twelve tribes of the children of Israel: 13 three gates on the east,\nthree gates on the north, three gates on the south, and three gates\non the west. 14 Now the wall of the city had twelve foundations,\nand on them were the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb. 15\nAnd he who talked with me had a gold reed to measure the city, its\ngates, and its wall. 16 The city is laid out as a square; its length is as\ngreat as its breadth. And he measured the city with the reed: twelve\nthousand furlongs. Its length, breadth, and height are equal. 17 Then\nhe measured its wall: one hundred and forty-four cubits, according\nto the measure of a man, that is, of an angel. 18 The construction of\nits wall was of jasper; and the city was pure gold, like clear glass. 19\nThe foundations of the wall of the city were adorned with all kinds\nof precious stones: the first foundation was jasper, the second\nsapphire, the third chalcedony, the fourth emerald, 20 the fifth\nsardonyx, the sixth sardius, the seventh chrysolite, the eighth beryl,\nthe ninth topaz, the tenth chrysoprase, the eleventh jacinth, and\nthe twelfth amethyst. 21 The twelve gates were twelve pearls: each\nindividual gate was of one pearl. And the street of the city was pure\ngold, like transparent glass. 22 But I saw no temple in it, for the Lord\nGod Almighty and the Lamb are its temple. 23 The city had no need of\nthe sun or of the moon to shine in it, for the glory of God illuminated\nit. The Lamb is its light. 24 And the nations of those who are saved\nshall walk in its light, and the kings of the earth bring their glory and\nhonor into it. 25 Its gates shall not be shut at all by day (there shall be\nno night there). 26 And they shall bring the glory and the honor of the\nnations into it. 27 But there shall by no means enter it anything that\ndefiles, or causes an abomination or a lie, but only those who are\nwritten in the Lamb’s Book of Life.\n\n12\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":13,"text":"Reversal of the curse in original Eden\nLesson 12\n\nRevelation 22:1-6\nAnd he showed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal,\nproceeding from the throne of God and of the Lamb. 2 In the middle\nof its street, and on either side of the river, was the tree of life, which\nbore twelve fruits, each tree yielding its fruit every month. The leaves\nof the tree were for the healing of the nations. 3 And there shall be\nno more curse, but the throne of God and of the Lamb shall be in it,\nand His servants shall serve Him. 4 They shall see His face, and His\nname shall be on their foreheads. 5 There shall be no night there:\nThey need no lamp nor light of the sun, for the Lord God gives them\nlight. And they shall reign forever and ever. 6 Then he said to me,\n“These words are faithful and true.” And the Lord God of the holy\nprophets sent His angel to show His servants the things which must\nshortly take place.\n\nContrasts between Genesis & Revelation\nGenesis\n\nRevelation\n\nFirst Paradise Closed (3:23)\n\nNew Paradise Opened\n(21:25)\n\nDispossessed through Sin\n(3:24)\n\nRepossessed through Grace\n(21:24)\n\nCurse Imposed (3:17)\n\nCurse Lifted (22:3)\n\nTree of Life Lost (3:24)\n\nTree of Life Regained (22:14)\n\nBeginning of Sorrow and\nDeath (3:16)\n\nEnd of Sorrow and Death\n(21:4)\n\nA Garden where defilement\nentered (3:6-7)\n\nA city where nothing defiled\ncan enter (21:27)\n\nDominion Forfeited in Adam\n(3:19)\n\nDominion Restored in Christ\n(22:5)\n\nEvil Triumph in Serpent (3:13) Lamb Triumphs over Serpent\n(20:10)\n\n13\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":14,"text":"Revelation 22:12-17\n\nLesson 12\n\n“And behold, I am coming quickly, and My reward is with Me, to give\nto every one according to his work. 13 I am the Alpha and the Omega,\nthe Beginning and the End, the First and the Last.” 14 Blessed are\nthose who do His commandments, that they may have the right to\nthe tree of life, and may enter through the gates into the city. 15 But\noutside are dogs and sorcerers and sexually immoral and murderers\nand idolaters, and whoever loves and practices a lie. 16 “I, Jesus, have\nsent My angel to testify to you these things in the churches. I am\nthe Root and the Offspring of David, the Bright and Morning Star.” 17\nAnd the Spirit and the bride say, “Come!” And let him who hears say,\n“Come!” And let him who thirsts come. Whoever desires, let him take\nthe water of life freely.\nRevelation 22:18-21\nFor I testify to everyone who hears the words of the prophecy of\nthis book: If anyone adds to these things, God will add to him the\nplagues that are written in this book; and if anyone takes away from\nthe words of the book of this prophecy, God shall take away his part\nfrom the Book of Life, from the holy city, and from the things which\nare written in this book. He who testifies to these things says, “Surely\nI am coming quickly.” Amen. Even so, come, Lord Jesus! The grace of\nour Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen.\n\nKey #5: Heaven is the destination for those who\nchoose to love, obey and follow Jesus.\n\n14\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":15,"text":"Summary of Lesson\nLesson 12\n\nRefer to Chart L12.3-3\n1. The Antichrist and his army will be defeated\nby Jesus at His second coming.\n2. Our choices determine where we will end\nup in eternity.\n3. The Word of God will judge us.\n4. The Lake of fire is the destination for those\nwho choose not to be saved.\n5. Heaven is the destination for those who\nchoose to love, obey and follow Jesus.\n\nReflection Questions\n1. What stood out to you in this lesson?\n\n2. What is one personal action step you would like to take\nafter this lesson?\n\n15\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":16,"text":"Charts\nLesson 12\n\n16\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"},{"page":17,"text":"Charts\nLesson 12\n\n17\n\nTeacher’s Notes © 2018 Tabernacle of Joy Singapore"}]}};
